insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 15, 'The sons of Caleb son of Jephunneh: Iru, Elah, and Naam. The son of Elah: Kenaz.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 16, 'The sons of Jehallelel: Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, and Asarel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 17, 'The sons of Ezrah: Jether, Mered, Epher, and Jalon.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 18, 'And Mered’s wife Bithiah gave birth to Miriam, Shammai, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa. These were the children of Pharaoh’s daughter Bithiah. Mered also took a Judean wife, who gave birth to Jered the father of Gedor, Heber the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 19, 'The sons of Hodiah’s wife, the sister of Naham, were the fathers of Keilah the Garmite and of Eshtemoa the Maacathite.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 20, 'The sons of Shimon: Amnon, Rinnah, Ben-hanan, and Tilon. The descendants of Ishi: Zoheth and Ben-zoheth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 21, 'The sons of Shelah son of Judah:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 22, 'Er the father of Lecah, Laadah the father of Mareshah and the clans of the linen workers at Beth-ashbea, Jokim, the men of Cozeba, and Joash and Saraph, who ruled in Moab and Jashubi-lehem. (These names are from ancient records.)'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 23, 'These were the potters who lived at Netaim and Gederah. They lived there in the service of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 24, 'The descendants of Simeon: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, and Shaul.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 25, 'The sons of Shaul: Shallum, Mibsam, and Mishma.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 26, 'The sons of Mishma: Hammuel, Zaccur, and Shimei.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 27, 'Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters, but his brothers did not have many children, so their whole clan did not become as numerous as the sons of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 28, 'They lived in Beersheba, Moladah, Hazar-shual,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 29, 'Bilhah, Ezem, Tolad,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 30, 'Bethuel, Hormah, Ziklag,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 31, 'Beth-marcaboth, Hazar-susim, Beth-biri, and Shaaraim. These were their cities until the reign of David.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 32, 'And their villages were Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashan—five towns—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 33, 'and all their surrounding villages as far as Baal. These were their settlements, and they kept a genealogical record:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 34, 'Meshobab, Jamlech, Joshah son of Amaziah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 35, 'Joel, Jehu son of Joshibiah (son of Seraiah, son of Asiel),'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 36, 'Elioenai, Jaakobah, Jeshohaiah, Asaiah, Adiel, Jesimiel, Benaiah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 37, 'and Ziza son of Shiphi (son of Allon, son of Jedaiah, son of Shimri, son of Shemaiah).'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 38, 'These men listed by name were the leaders of their clans. Their families increased greatly,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 39, 'and they journeyed to the entrance of Gedor, to the east side of the valley, in search of pasture for their flocks.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 40, 'There they found rich, good pasture, and the land was spacious, peaceful, and quiet; for some Hamites had lived there formerly.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 41, 'These who were noted by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah. They attacked the Hamites and Meunites there in their dwellings, devoting them to destruction even to this day. Then they settled in their place, because there was pasture for their flocks.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 42, 'And five hundred of these Simeonites led by Pelatiah, Neariah, Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi, went to Mount Seir'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 4, 43, 'and struck down the remnant of the Amalekites who had escaped. And they have lived there to this day.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 1, 'These were the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel. Though he was the firstborn, his birthright was given to the sons of Joseph son of Israel, because Reuben defiled his father’s bed. So he is not reckoned according to birthright.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 2, 'And though Judah prevailed over his brothers and a ruler came from him, the birthright belonged to Joseph.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 3, 'The sons of Reuben, the firstborn of Israel: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 4, 'The descendants of Joel:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 5, 'Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son, Micah his son, Reaiah his son, Baal his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 6, 'and Beerah his son, whom Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria carried into exile.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 7, 'Beerah was a leader of the Reubenites. His relatives by their clans are recorded in their genealogy:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 8, 'Jeiel the chief, Zechariah, and Bela son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel. They settled in Aroer and as far as Nebo and Baal-meon.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 9, 'They also settled in the east as far as the edge of the desert that extends to the Euphrates River, because their livestock had increased in the land of Gilead.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 10, 'During the days of Saul they waged war against the Hagrites, who were defeated at their hands, and they occupied the homes of the Hagrites throughout the region east of Gilead.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 11, 'The descendants of Gad lived next to the Reubenites in the land of Bashan, as far as Salecah:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 12, 'Joel was the chief, Shapham the second, then Jaanai and Shaphat, who lived in Bashan.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 13, 'Their kinsmen by families were Michael, Meshullam, Sheba, Jorai, Jacan, Zia, and Eber—seven in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 14, 'These were the sons of Abihail son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 15, 'Ahi son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, was head of their family.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 16, 'They lived in Gilead, in Bashan and its towns, and throughout the pasturelands of Sharon.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 17, 'All of them were reckoned in the genealogies during the reigns of Jotham king of Judah and Jeroboam king of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 18, 'The Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh had 44,760 warriors—valiant men who carried the shield and sword, drew the bow, and were trained for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 19, 'They waged war against the Hagrites, as well as Jetur, Naphish, and Nodab.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 20, 'And because they cried out to God in battle, they were helped against their enemies, and the Hagrites and all their allies were delivered into their hands. Because they put their trust in God, He answered their prayers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 21, 'They seized the livestock of the Hagrites—50,000 camels, 250,000 sheep, and 2,000 donkeys. They also took 100,000 captives,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 22, 'and many others fell slain, because the battle belonged to God. And they occupied the land until the exile.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 23, 'Now the people of the half-tribe of Manasseh were numerous. They settled in the land from Bashan to Baal-hermon (that is, Senir, also known as Mount Hermon).'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 24, 'These were the heads of their families: Epher, Ishi, Eliel, Azriel, Jeremiah, Hodaviah, and Jahdiel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 25, 'They were mighty men of valor, famous men, and heads of their families. But they were unfaithful to the God of their fathers, and they prostituted themselves with the gods of the peoples of the land, whom God had destroyed before them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 5, 26, 'So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria (that is, Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria) to take the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh into exile. And he brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and the river of Gozan, where they remain to this day.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 1, 'The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 2, 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 3, 'The children of Amram: Aaron, Moses, and Miriam. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 4, 'Eleazar was the father of Phinehas, Phinehas was the father of Abishua,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 5, 'Abishua was the father of Bukki, Bukki was the father of Uzzi,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 6, 'Uzzi was the father of Zerahiah, Zerahiah was the father of Meraioth,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 7, 'Meraioth was the father of Amariah, Amariah was the father of Ahitub,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 8, 'Ahitub was the father of Zadok, Zadok was the father of Ahimaaz,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 9, 'Ahimaaz was the father of Azariah, Azariah was the father of Johanan,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 10, 'Johanan was the father of Azariah, who served as priest in the temple that Solomon built in Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 11, 'Azariah was the father of Amariah, Amariah was the father of Ahitub,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 12, 'Ahitub was the father of Zadok, Zadok was the father of Shallum,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 13, 'Shallum was the father of Hilkiah, Hilkiah was the father of Azariah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 14, 'Azariah was the father of Seraiah, and Seraiah was the father of Jehozadak.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 15, 'Jehozadak went into captivity when the LORD sent Judah and Jerusalem into exile by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 16, 'The sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath, and Merari.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 17, 'These are the names of the sons of Gershom: Libni and Shimei.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 18, 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 19, 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. These are the clans of the Levites listed according to their fathers:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 20, 'Of Gershom:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 21, 'Libni his son, Jahath his son, Zimmah his son, Joah his son, Iddo his son, Zerah his son, and Jeatherai his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 22, 'The descendants of Kohath:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 23, 'Amminadab his son, Korah his son, Assir his son, Elkanah his son, Ebiasaph his son, Assir his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 24, 'Tahath his son, Uriel his son, Uzziah his son, and Shaul his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 25, 'The descendants of Elkanah:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 26, 'Amasai, Ahimoth, Elkanah his son, Zophai his son, Nahath his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 27, 'Eliab his son, Jeroham his son, and Elkanah his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 28, 'The sons of Samuel: Joel his firstborn and Abijah his second son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 29, 'The descendants of Merari:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 30, 'Mahli, Libni his son, Shimei his son, Uzzah his son, Shimea his son, Haggiah his son, and Asaiah his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 31, 'These are the men David put in charge of the music in the house of the LORD after the ark rested there.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 32, 'They ministered with song before the tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting, until Solomon built the house of the LORD in Jerusalem. And they performed their duties according to the regulations given them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 33, 'These are the men who served, together with their sons. From the Kohathites:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 34, 'Heman the singer, the son of Joel, the son of Samuel, the son of Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son of Toah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 35, 'the son of Zuph, the son of Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son of Amasai,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 36, 'the son of Elkanah, the son of Joel, the son of Azariah, the son of Zephaniah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 37, 'the son of Tahath, the son of Assir, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 38, 'the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 39, 'Heman’s kinsman was Asaph, who served at his right hand:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 40, 'Asaph the son of Berechiah, the son of Shimea, the son of Michael, the son of Baaseiah, the son of Malchijah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 41, 'the son of Ethni, the son of Zerah, the son of Adaiah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 42, 'the son of Ethan, the son of Zimmah, the son of Shimei,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 43, 'the son of Jahath, the son of Gershom, the son of Levi.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 44, 'On the left were their kinsmen, the sons of Merari:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 45, 'Ethan the son of Kishi, the son of Abdi, the son of Malluch, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Amaziah, the son of Hilkiah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 46, 'the son of Amzi, the son of Bani, the son of Shemer,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 47, 'the son of Mahli, the son of Mushi, the son of Merari, the son of Levi.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 48, 'Their fellow Levites were assigned to every kind of service of the tabernacle, the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 49, 'But Aaron and his sons did all the work of the Most Holy Place. They presented the offerings on the altar of burnt offering and on the altar of incense to make atonement for Israel, according to all that Moses the servant of God had commanded.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 50, 'These were the descendants of Aaron:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 51, 'Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son, Abishua his son, Bukki his son, Uzzi his son, Zerahiah his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 52, 'Meraioth his son, Amariah his son, Ahitub his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 53, 'Zadok his son, and Ahimaaz his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 54, 'Now these were the territories assigned to the descendants of Aaron from the Kohathite clan for their settlements, because the first lot fell to them:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 55, 'They were given Hebron in the land of Judah and its surrounding pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 56, 'But the fields and villages around the city were given to Caleb son of Jephunneh.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 57, 'So the descendants of Aaron were given Hebron (a city of refuge), Libnah, Jattir, Eshtemoa,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 58, 'Hilen, Debir,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 59, 'Ashan, Juttah, and Beth-shemesh, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 60, 'And from the tribe of Benjamin they were given Gibeon, Geba, Alemeth, and Anathoth, together with their pasturelands. So they had thirteen cities in all among their families.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 61, 'To the rest of the Kohathites, ten cities were allotted from the half-tribe of Manasseh.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 62, 'The Gershomites, according to their clans, were allotted thirteen cities from the tribes of Issachar, Asher, Naphtali, and Manasseh in Bashan.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 63, 'The Merarites, according to their families, were allotted twelve cities from the tribes of Reuben, Gad, and Zebulun.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 64, 'So the Israelites gave to the Levites these cities and their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 65, 'They assigned by lot the cities named above from the tribes of Judah, Simeon, and Benjamin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 66, 'And some of the clans of the Kohathites were given cities from the tribe of Ephraim for their territory:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 67, 'They were given Shechem (a city of refuge) with its pasturelands in the hill country of Ephraim, and Gezer,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 68, 'Jokmeam, Beth-horon,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 69, 'Aijalon, and Gath-rimmon, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 70, 'And from the half-tribe of Manasseh the remaining clans of the Kohathites were given Aner and Bileam, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 71, 'The Gershomites received the following: From the clan of the half-tribe of Manasseh they were given Golan in Bashan and also Ashtaroth, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 72, 'From the tribe of Issachar they were given Kedesh, Daberath,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 73, 'Ramoth, and Anem, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 74, 'From the tribe of Asher they were given Mashal, Abdon,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 75, 'Hukok, and Rehob, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 76, 'And from the tribe of Naphtali they were given Kedesh in Galilee, Hammon, and Kiriathaim, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 77, 'The Merarites (the rest of the Levites) received the following: From the tribe of Zebulun they were given Rimmono and Tabor, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 78, 'From the tribe of Reuben east of the Jordan opposite Jericho they were given Bezer in the wilderness, Jahzah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 79, 'Kedemoth, and Mephaath, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 80, 'And from the tribe of Gad they were given Ramoth in Gilead, Mahanaim,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 6, 81, 'Heshbon, and Jazer, together with their pasturelands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 1, 'The sons of Issachar: Tola, Puah, Jashub, and Shimron—four in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 2, 'The sons of Tola: Uzzi, Rephaiah, Jeriel, Jahmai, Ibsam, and Shemuel, the heads of their families. In the days of David, 22,600 descendants of Tola were numbered in their genealogies as mighty men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 3, 'The son of Uzzi: Izrahiah. The sons of Izrahiah:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 4, 'Michael, Obadiah, Joel, and Isshiah. All five of them were chiefs. In addition to them, according to their genealogy, they had 36,000 troops for battle, for they had many wives and children.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 5, 'Their kinsmen belonging to all the families of Issachar who were mighty men of valor totaled 87,000, as listed in their genealogies.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 6, 'The three sons of Benjamin: Bela, Becher, and Jediael.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 7, 'The sons of Bela: Ezbon, Uzzi, Uzziel, Jerimoth, and Iri, heads of their families—five in all. There were 22,034 mighty men of valor listed in their genealogies.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 8, 'The sons of Becher:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 9, 'Zemirah, Joash, Eliezer, Elioenai, Omri, Jeremoth, Abijah, Anathoth, and Alemeth; all these were Becher’s sons. Their genealogies were recorded according to the heads of their families—20,200 mighty men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 10, 'The son of Jediael: Bilhan. The sons of Bilhan:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 11, 'Jeush, Benjamin, Ehud, Chenaanah, Zethan, Tarshish, and Ahishahar. All these sons of Jediael were heads of their families, mighty men of valor; there were 17,200 fit for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 12, 'The Shuppites and Huppites were descendants of Ir, and the Hushites were descendants of Aher.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 13, 'The sons of Naphtali: Jahziel, Guni, Jezer, and Shallum—the descendants of Bilhah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 14, 'The descendants of Manasseh: Through his Aramean concubine, Asriel, as well as Machir the father of Gilead.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 15, 'Machir took a wife from among the Huppites and Shuppites. The name of his sister was Maacah. Another descendant was named Zelophehad, who had only daughters.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 16, 'Machir’s wife Maacah gave birth to a son, and she named him Peresh. His brother was named Sheresh, and his sons were Ulam and Rekem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 17, 'The son of Ulam: Bedan.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 18, 'These were the sons of Gilead son of Machir, the son of Manasseh. His sister Hammolecheth gave birth to Ishhod, Abiezer, and Mahlah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 19, 'And these were the sons of Shemida: Ahian, Shechem, Likhi, and Aniam.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 20, 'The descendants of Ephraim:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 21, 'Shuthelah, Bered his son, Tahath his son, Eleadah his son, Tahath his son, Zabad his son, and Shuthelah his son. Ezer and Elead were killed by the natives of Gath, because they went down to steal their livestock.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 22, 'Their father Ephraim mourned for many days, and his relatives came to comfort him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 23, 'And again he slept with his wife, and she conceived and gave birth to a son. So he named him Beriah, because tragedy had come upon his house.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 24, 'His daughter was Sheerah, who built Lower and Upper Beth-horon, as well as Uzzen-sheerah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 25, 'Additionally, Rephah was his son, Resheph his son, Telah his son, Tahan his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 26, 'Ladan his son, Ammihud his son, Elishama his son,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 27, 'Nun his son, and Joshua his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 28, 'Their holdings and settlements included Bethel and its villages, Naaran to the east, Gezer and its villages to the west, and Shechem and its villages as far as Ayyah and its villages.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 29, 'And along the borders of Manasseh were Beth-shean, Taanach, Megiddo, and Dor, together with their villages. The descendants of Joseph son of Israel lived in these towns.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 30, 'The children of Asher: Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, Beriah, and their sister Serah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 31, 'The sons of Beriah: Heber, as well as Malchiel, who was the father of Birzaith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 32, 'Heber was the father of Japhlet, Shomer, and Hotham, and of their sister Shua.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 33, 'The sons of Japhlet: Pasach, Bimhal, and Ashvath. These were Japhlet’s sons.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 34, 'The sons of Shemer: Ahi, Rohgah, Hubbah, and Aram.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 35, 'The sons of his brother Helem: Zophah, Imna, Shelesh, and Amal.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 36, 'The sons of Zophah:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 37, 'Suah, Harnepher, Shual, Beri, Imrah, Bezer, Hod, Shamma, Shilshah, Ithran, and Beera.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 38, 'The sons of Jether: Jephunneh, Pispa, and Ara.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 39, 'The sons of Ulla: Arah, Hanniel, and Rizia.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 7, 40, 'All these were the descendants of Asher—heads of their families, choice and mighty men of valor, and chiefs among the leaders. The number of men fit for battle, recorded in their genealogies, was 26,000.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 1, 'Benjamin was the father of Bela, his firstborn; Ashbel was the second born, Aharah the third,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 2, 'Nohah the fourth, and Rapha the fifth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 3, 'The sons of Bela:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 4, 'Addar, Gera, Abihud, Abishua, Naaman, Ahoah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 5, 'Gera, Shephuphan, and Huram.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 6, 'These were the descendants of Ehud who were the heads of the families living in Geba and were exiled to Manahath:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 7, 'Naaman, Ahijah, and Gera, who carried them into exile and who was the father of Uzza and Ahihud.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 8, 'Shaharaim had sons in the country of Moab after he had divorced his wives Hushim and Baara.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 9, 'His sons by his wife Hodesh:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 10, 'Jobab, Zibia, Mesha, Malcam, Jeuz, Sachia, and Mirmah. These were his sons, heads of families.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 11, 'He also had sons by Hushim: Abitub and Elpaal.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 12, 'The sons of Elpaal:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 13, 'Eber, Misham, Shemed (who built Ono and Lod with its villages), and Beriah and Shema (who were the heads of families of the inhabitants of Aijalon and who drove out the inhabitants of Gath).'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 14, 'Ahio, Shashak, Jeremoth,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 15, 'Zebadiah, Arad, Eder,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 16, 'Michael, Ishpah, and Joha were the sons of Beriah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 17, 'Zebadiah, Meshullam, Hizki, Heber,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 18, 'Ishmerai, Izliah, and Jobab were the sons of Elpaal.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 19, 'Jakim, Zichri, Zabdi,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 20, 'Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 21, 'Adaiah, Beraiah, and Shimrath were the sons of Shimei.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 22, 'Ishpan, Eber, Eliel,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 23, 'Abdon, Zichri, Hanan,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 24, 'Hananiah, Elam, Anthothijah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 25, 'Iphdeiah, and Penuel were the sons of Shashak.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 26, 'Shamsherai, Shehariah, Athaliah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 27, 'Jaareshiah, Elijah, and Zichri were the sons of Jeroham.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 28, 'All these were heads of families, the chiefs according to their genealogies, and they lived in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 29, 'Jeiel the father of Gibeon lived in Gibeon. His wife’s name was Maacah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 30, 'and Abdon was his firstborn son, then Zur, Kish, Baal, Nadab,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 31, 'Gedor, Ahio, Zecher,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 32, 'and Mikloth, who was the father of Shimeah. These also lived alongside their relatives in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 33, 'Ner was the father of Kish, Kish was the father of Saul, and Saul was the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Esh-baal.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 34, 'The son of Jonathan: Merib-baal, and Merib-baal was the father of Micah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 35, 'The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tarea, and Ahaz.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 36, 'Ahaz was the father of Jehoaddah, Jehoaddah was the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri, and Zimri was the father of Moza.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 37, 'Moza was the father of Binea. Raphah was his son, Eleasah his son, and Azel his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 38, 'Azel had six sons, and these were their names: Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. All these were the sons of Azel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 39, 'The sons of his brother Eshek:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 8, 40, 'Ulam was his firstborn, Jeush second, and Eliphelet third. The sons of Ulam were mighty men of valor, archers, and they had many sons and grandsons—150 in all. All these were the descendants of Benjamin.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 1, 'So all Israel was recorded in the genealogies written in the Book of the Kings of Israel. But Judah was exiled to Babylon because of their unfaithfulness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 2, 'Now the first to resettle their own property in their cities were Israelites, priests, Levites, and temple servants.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 3, 'These were some of the descendants of Judah, Benjamin, Ephraim, and Manasseh who lived in Jerusalem:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 4, 'Uthai son of Ammihud, the son of Omri, the son of Imri, the son of Bani, a descendant of Perez son of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 5, 'From the Shilonites: Asaiah the firstborn and his sons.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 6, 'From the Zerahites: Jeuel and 690 relatives.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 7, 'From the Benjamites: Sallu son of Meshullam, the son of Hodaviah, the son of Hassenuah;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 8, 'Ibneiah son of Jeroham; Elah son of Uzzi, the son of Michri; Meshullam son of Shephatiah, the son of Reuel, the son of Ibnijah;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 9, 'and 956 of their relatives according to their genealogy. All these men were heads of their families.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 10, 'From the priests: Jedaiah, Jehoiarib, and Jachin;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 11, 'Azariah son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the chief official of God’s temple;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 12, 'Adaiah son of Jeroham, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; Maasai son of Adiel, the son of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Meshillemith, the son of Immer;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 13, 'and 1,760 of their relatives, the heads of their families, able men for the work of the service of the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 14, 'From the Levites: Shemaiah son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, a descendant of Merari;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 15, 'Bakbakkar, Heresh, Galal, and Mattaniah son of Mica, the son of Zichri, the son of Asaph;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 16, 'Obadiah son of Shemaiah, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun; and Berechiah son of Asa, the son of Elkanah, who lived in the villages of the Netophathites.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 17, 'These were the gatekeepers: Shallum, Akkub, Talmon, Ahiman, and their relatives.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 18, 'Shallum was their chief; he was previously stationed at the King’s Gate on the east side. These were the gatekeepers from the camp of the Levites.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 19, 'Shallum son of Kore, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah, and his relatives from the Korahites were assigned to guard the thresholds of the Tent, just as their fathers had been assigned to guard the entrance to the dwelling of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 20, 'In earlier times Phinehas son of Eleazar had been in charge of the gatekeepers, and the LORD was with him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 21, 'Zechariah son of Meshelemiah was the gatekeeper at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 22, 'The number of those chosen to be gatekeepers at the thresholds was 212. They were registered by genealogy in their villages. David and Samuel the seer had appointed them to their positions of trust.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 23, 'So they and their descendants were assigned to guard the gates of the house of the LORD—the house called the Tent.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 24, 'The gatekeepers were stationed on the four sides: east, west, north, and south.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 25, 'Their relatives came from their villages at fixed times to serve with them for seven-day periods.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 26, 'But the four chief gatekeepers, who were Levites, were entrusted with the rooms and the treasuries of the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 27, 'They would spend the night stationed around the house of God, because they were responsible for guarding it and opening it every morning.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 28, 'Some of them were in charge of the articles used in worship, to count them whenever they were brought in or taken out.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 29, 'Others were put in charge of the furnishings and other articles of the sanctuary, as well as the fine flour, wine, oil, frankincense, and spices.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 30, 'And some of the sons of the priests mixed the spices.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 31, 'A Levite named Mattithiah, the firstborn son of Shallum the Korahite, was entrusted with baking the bread.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 32, 'Some of their Kohathite brothers were responsible for preparing the rows of the showbread every Sabbath.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 33, 'Those who were musicians, the heads of Levite families, stayed in the temple chambers and were exempt from other duties because they were on duty day and night.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 34, 'All these were heads of Levite families, chiefs according to their genealogies, and they lived in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 35, 'Jeiel the father of Gibeon lived in Gibeon. His wife’s name was Maacah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 36, 'Abdon was his firstborn son, then Zur, Kish, Baal, Ner, Nadab,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 37, 'Gedor, Ahio, Zechariah, and Mikloth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 38, 'Mikloth was the father of Shimeam. They too lived alongside their relatives in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 39, 'Ner was the father of Kish, Kish was the father of Saul, and Saul was the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Esh-baal.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 40, 'The son of Jonathan: Merib-baal, who was the father of Micah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 41, 'The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tahrea, and Ahaz.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 42, 'Ahaz was the father of Jarah; Jarah was the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri; and Zimri was the father of Moza.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 43, 'Moza was the father of Binea. Rephaiah was his son, Elasah his son, and Azel his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 9, 44, 'And Azel had six sons, and these were their names: Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. These were the sons of Azel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 1, 'Now the Philistines fought against Israel, and the men of Israel fled before them, and many fell slain on Mount Gilboa.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 2, 'The Philistines followed hard after Saul and his sons, and they killed Saul’s sons Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 3, 'When the battle intensified against Saul, the archers overtook him and wounded him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 4, 'Then Saul said to his armor-bearer, “Draw your sword and run it through me, or these uncircumcised men will come and torture me!” But his armor-bearer was terrified and refused to do it. So Saul took his own sword and fell on it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 5, 'When his armor-bearer saw that Saul was dead, he too fell on his own sword and died.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 6, 'So Saul died together with his three sons and all his house.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 7, 'When all the Israelites in the valley saw that the army had fled and that Saul and his sons had died, they abandoned their cities and ran away. So the Philistines came and occupied their cities.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 8, 'The next day, when the Philistines came to strip the dead, they found Saul and his sons fallen on Mount Gilboa.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 9, 'They stripped Saul, cut off his head, took his armor, and sent messengers throughout the land of the Philistines to proclaim the news in the temple of their idols and among their people.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 10, 'They put his armor in the temple of their gods and hung his head in the temple of Dagon.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 11, 'When the people of Jabesh-gilead heard about everything the Philistines had done to Saul,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 12, 'all their men of valor set out and retrieved the bodies of Saul and his sons and brought them to Jabesh. And they buried their bones under the oak in Jabesh and fasted seven days.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 13, 'So Saul died for his unfaithfulness to the LORD, because he did not keep the word of the LORD and even consulted a medium for guidance,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 10, 14, 'and he failed to inquire of the LORD. So the LORD put him to death and turned the kingdom over to David son of Jesse.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 1, 'Then all Israel came together to David at Hebron and said, “Here we are, your own flesh and blood.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 2, 'Even in times past, while Saul was king, you were the one who led Israel out and brought them back. And the LORD your God said, ‘You will shepherd My people Israel, and you will be ruler over them.’”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 3, 'So all the elders of Israel came to the king at Hebron, where David made a covenant with them before the LORD. And they anointed him king over Israel, according to the word of the LORD through Samuel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 4, 'Then David and all the Israelites marched to Jerusalem (that is, Jebus), where the Jebusites inhabited the land.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 5, 'The people of Jebus said to David, “You will never get in here.” Nevertheless, David captured the fortress of Zion (that is, the City of David).'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 6, 'Now David had said, “Whoever is the first to strike down a Jebusite will become chief commander.” And Joab son of Zeruiah went up first, and he became the chief.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 7, 'So David took up residence in the fortress; that is why it was called the City of David.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 8, 'He built up the city around it, from the supporting terraces to the surrounding wall, while Joab restored the rest of the city.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 9, 'And David became greater and greater, for the LORD of Hosts was with him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 10, 'Now these were the chiefs of David’s mighty men, who, together with all Israel, bolstered and strengthened his kingdom, according to the word of the LORD concerning Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 11, 'This is the list of David’s mighty men: Jashobeam son of Hachmoni was chief of the officers; he wielded his spear against three hundred men, whom he killed at one time.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 12, 'Next in command was Eleazar son of Dodo the Ahohite, one of the three mighty men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 13, 'He was with David at Pas-dammim when the Philistines gathered there for battle. At the place with a field full of barley, the troops fled from the Philistines.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 14, 'But Eleazar and David stationed themselves in the middle of the field and defended it. They struck down the Philistines, and the LORD brought about a great victory.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 15, 'Three of the thirty chief men went down to David, to the rock at the cave of Adullam, while a company of Philistines was encamped in the Valley of Rephaim.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 16, 'At that time David was in the stronghold, and the garrison of the Philistines was at Bethlehem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 17, 'David longed for water and said, “Oh, that someone would get me a drink of water from the well near the gate of Bethlehem!”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 18, 'So the Three broke through the Philistine camp, drew water from the well at the gate of Bethlehem, and brought it back to David. But he refused to drink it; instead, he poured it out to the LORD,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 19, 'saying, “Far be it from me, my God, to do this! How can I drink the blood of these men who risked their lives?” Because they had brought it at the risk of their lives, David refused to drink it. Such were the exploits of the three mighty men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 20, 'Now Abishai, the brother of Joab, was chief of the Three, and he lifted his spear against three hundred men, killed them, and won a name along with the Three.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 21, 'He was doubly honored above the Three, and he became their commander, even though he was not included among the Three.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 22, 'And Benaiah son of Jehoiada was a man of valor from Kabzeel, a man of many exploits. He struck down two champions of Moab, and on a snowy day he went down into a pit and killed a lion.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 23, 'He also killed an Egyptian, a huge man five cubits tall. Although the Egyptian had a spear like a weaver’s beam in his hand, Benaiah went against him with a club, snatched the spear from his hand, and killed the Egyptian with his own spear.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 24, 'These were the exploits of Benaiah son of Jehoiada, who won a name alongside the three mighty men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 25, 'He was most honored among the Thirty, but he did not become one of the Three. And David appointed him over his guard.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 26, 'Now these were the mighty men: Asahel the brother of Joab, Elhanan son of Dodo of Bethlehem,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 27, 'Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the Pelonite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 28, 'Ira son of Ikkesh the Tekoite, Abiezer the Anathothite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 29, 'Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the Ahohite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 30, 'Maharai the Netophathite, Heled son of Baanah the Netophathite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 31, 'Ithai son of Ribai from Gibeah of the Benjamites, Benaiah the Pirathonite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 32, 'Hurai from the brooks of Gaash, Abiel the Arbathite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 33, 'Azmaveth the Baharumite, Eliahba the Shaalbonite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 34, 'the sons of Hashem the Gizonite, Jonathan son of Shagee the Hararite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 35, 'Ahiam son of Sachar the Hararite, Eliphal son of Ur,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 36, 'Hepher the Mecherathite, Ahijah the Pelonite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 37, 'Hezro the Carmelite, Naarai son of Ezbai,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 38, 'Joel the brother of Nathan, Mibhar son of Hagri,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 39, 'Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the Beerothite, the armor-bearer of Joab son of Zeruiah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 40, 'Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 41, 'Uriah the Hittite, Zabad son of Ahlai,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 42, 'Adina son of Shiza the Reubenite, chief of the Reubenites, and the thirty with him,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 43, 'Hanan son of Maacah, Joshaphat the Mithnite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 44, 'Uzzia the Ashterathite, Shama and Jeiel the sons of Hotham the Aroerite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 45, 'Jediael son of Shimri and his brother Joha the Tizite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 46, 'Eliel the Mahavite, Jeribai and Joshaviah, the sons of Elnaam, Ithmah the Moabite,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 11, 47, 'Eliel, Obed, and Jaasiel the Mezobaite.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 1, 'Now these were the men who came to David at Ziklag, while he was still banished from the presence of Saul son of Kish (they were among the mighty men who helped him in battle;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 2, 'they were archers using both the right and left hands to sling stones and shoot arrows; and they were Saul’s kinsmen from Benjamin):'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 3, 'Ahiezer their chief and Joash, who were the sons of Shemaah the Gibeathite; Jeziel and Pelet, the sons of Azmaveth; Beracah; Jehu the Anathothite;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 4, 'Ishmaiah the Gibeonite, a mighty man among the Thirty and a leader over the Thirty; Jeremiah, Jahaziel, Johanan, and Jozabad the Gederathite;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 5, 'Eluzai, Jerimoth, Bealiah, Shemariah, and Shephatiah the Haruphite;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 6, 'Elkanah, Isshiah, Azarel, Joezer, and Jashobeam, who were Korahites;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 7, 'and Joelah and Zebadiah, the sons of Jeroham from Gedor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 8, 'Some Gadites defected to David at his stronghold in the desert. They were mighty men of valor, trained for battle, experts with the shield and spear, whose faces were like the faces of lions and who were as swift as gazelles on the mountains:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 9, 'Ezer the chief, Obadiah the second in command, Eliab the third,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 10, 'Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the fifth,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 11, 'Attai the sixth, Eliel the seventh,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 12, 'Johanan the eighth, Elzabad the ninth,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 13, 'Jeremiah the tenth, and Machbanai the eleventh.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 14, 'These Gadites were army commanders, the least of whom was a match for a hundred, and the greatest for a thousand.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 15, 'These are the ones who crossed the Jordan in the first month when it was overflowing all its banks, and they put to flight all those in the valleys, both to the east and to the west.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 16, 'Other Benjamites and some men from Judah also came to David in his stronghold.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 17, 'And David went out to meet them, saying, “If you have come to me in peace to help me, my heart will be united with you; but if you have come to betray me to my enemies when my hands are free of violence, may the God of our fathers see it and judge you.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 18, 'Then the Spirit came upon Amasai, the chief of the Thirty, and he said: “We are yours, O David! We are with you, O son of Jesse! Peace, peace to you, and peace to your helpers, for your God helps you.” So David received them and made them leaders of his troops.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 19, 'Some from Manasseh defected to David when he went with the Philistines to fight against Saul. (They did not help the Philistines because the Philistine rulers consulted and sent David away, saying, “It will cost us our heads if he defects to his master Saul.”)'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 20, 'When David went to Ziklag, these men of Manasseh defected to him: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zillethai, chiefs of thousands in Manasseh.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 21, 'They helped David against the raiders, for they were all mighty men of valor and commanders in the army.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 22, 'For at that time men came to David day after day to help him, until he had a great army, like the army of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 23, 'Now these are the numbers of men armed for battle who came to David at Hebron to turn Saul’s kingdom over to him, in accordance with the word of the LORD:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 24, 'From Judah: 6,800 armed troops bearing shields and spears.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 25, 'From Simeon: 7,100 mighty men of valor, ready for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 26, 'From Levi: 4,600,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 27, 'including Jehoiada, leader of the house of Aaron, with 3,700 men,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 28, 'and Zadok, a mighty young man of valor, with 22 commanders from his own family.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 29, 'From Benjamin, the kinsmen of Saul: 3,000, most of whom had remained loyal to the house of Saul up to that time.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 30, 'From Ephraim: 20,800 mighty men of valor, famous among their own clans.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 31, 'From the half-tribe of Manasseh: 18,000 designated by name to come and make David king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 32, 'From Issachar, men who understood the times and knew what Israel should do: 200 chiefs with all their kinsmen at their command.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 33, 'From Zebulun: 50,000 fit for service, trained for battle with all kinds of weapons of war, who with one purpose were devoted to David.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 34, 'From Naphtali: 1,000 commanders, accompanied by 37,000 men with shield and spear.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 35, 'From Dan: 28,600 prepared for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 36, 'From Asher: 40,000 fit for service, prepared for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 37, 'And from east of the Jordan, from Reuben, Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh there: 120,000 armed with every kind of weapon of war.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 38, 'All these men of war, arrayed for battle, came to Hebron fully determined to make David king over all Israel. And all the rest of the Israelites were of one mind to make David king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 39, 'They spent three days there eating and drinking with David, for their relatives had provided for them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 12, 40, 'And their neighbors from as far away as Issachar, Zebulun, and Naphtali came bringing food on donkeys, camels, mules, and oxen—abundant supplies of flour, fig cakes and raisin cakes, wine and oil, oxen and sheep. Indeed, there was joy in Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 1, 'Then David conferred with all his leaders, the commanders of hundreds and of thousands.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 2, 'And he said to the whole assembly of Israel, “If it seems good to you, and if this is of the LORD our God, let us send word far and wide to the rest of our brothers in all the land of Israel, and also to the priests and Levites in their cities and pasturelands, so that they may join us.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 3, 'Then let us bring back the ark of our God, for we did not inquire of Him in the days of Saul.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 4, 'And because this proposal seemed right to all the people, the whole assembly agreed to it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 5, 'So David assembled all Israel, from the River Shihor in Egypt to Lebo-hamath, to bring the ark of God from Kiriath-jearim.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 6, 'David and all Israel went up to Baalah of Judah (that is, Kiriath-jearim) to bring up from there the ark of God the LORD, who is enthroned between the cherubim—the ark that is called by the Name.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 7, 'So they carried the ark of God from the house of Abinadab on a new cart, with Uzzah and Ahio guiding the cart.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 8, 'David and all the Israelites were celebrating before God with all their might, with songs and on harps and lyres, with tambourines, cymbals, and trumpets.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 9, 'When they came to the threshing floor of Chidon, Uzzah reached out and took hold of the ark, because the oxen had stumbled.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 10, 'And the anger of the LORD burned against Uzzah, and He struck him down because he had put his hand on the ark. So he died there before God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 11, 'Then David became angry because the LORD had burst forth against Uzzah; so he named that place Perez-uzzah, as it is called to this day.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 12, 'That day David feared God and asked, “How can I ever bring the ark of God to me?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 13, 'So he did not move the ark with him to the City of David; instead, he took it aside to the house of Obed-edom the Gittite.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 13, 14, 'Thus the ark of God remained with the family of Obed-edom in his house for three months, and the LORD blessed his household and everything he owned.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 1, 'Now Hiram king of Tyre sent envoys to David, along with cedar logs, stonemasons, and carpenters, to build a palace for him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 2, 'And David realized that the LORD had established him as king over Israel and had highly exalted his kingdom for the sake of His people Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 3, 'And David took more wives in Jerusalem and became the father of more sons and daughters.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 4, 'These are the names of the children born to him in Jerusalem: Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 5, 'Ibhar, Elishua, Elpelet,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 6, 'Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 7, 'Elishama, Beeliada, and Eliphelet.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 8, 'When the Philistines heard that David had been anointed king over all Israel, they all went in search of him; but David learned of this and went out to face them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 9, 'Now the Philistines had come and raided the Valley of Rephaim.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 10, 'So David inquired of God, “Should I go up against the Philistines? Will You deliver them into my hand?” “Go,” replied the LORD, “for I will deliver them into your hand.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 11, 'So David and his men went up to Baal-perazim, where he defeated the Philistines and said, “Like a bursting flood, God has burst out against my enemies by my hand.” So they called that place Baal-perazim.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 12, 'There the Philistines abandoned their gods, and David ordered that they be burned in the fire.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 13, 'Once again the Philistines raided the valley.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 14, 'So David again inquired of God, who answered him, “Do not march up after them, but circle around them and attack them in front of the balsam trees.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 15, 'As soon as you hear the sound of marching in the tops of the balsam trees, move out to battle, because this will mean that God has marched out before you to strike the camp of the Philistines.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 16, 'So David did as God had commanded him, and they struck down the army of the Philistines all the way from Gibeon to Gezer.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 14, 17, 'And David’s fame went out into every land, and the LORD caused all nations to fear him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 1, 'David constructed buildings for himself in the City of David, and he prepared a place for the ark of God and pitched a tent for it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 2, 'Then David said, “No one but the Levites may carry the ark of God, because the LORD has chosen them to carry the ark of the LORD and to minister before Him forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 3, 'And David assembled all Israel in Jerusalem to bring up the ark of the LORD to the place he had prepared for it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 4, 'Then he gathered together the descendants of Aaron and the Levites:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 5, 'From the Kohathites, Uriel the chief and 120 of his relatives;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 6, 'from the Merarites, Asaiah the chief and 220 of his relatives;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 7, 'from the Gershomites, Joel the chief and 130 of his relatives;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 8, 'from the Elizaphanites, Shemaiah the chief and 200 of his relatives;');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 9, 'from the Hebronites, Eliel the chief and 80 of his relatives;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 10, 'and from the Uzzielites, Amminadab the chief and 112 of his relatives.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 11, 'David summoned the priests Zadok and Abiathar and the Levites Uriel, Asaiah, Joel, Shemaiah, Eliel, and Amminadab.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 12, 'And he said to them, “You are the heads of the Levitical families. You and your relatives must consecrate yourselves so that you may bring the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel, to the place I have prepared for it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 13, 'It was because you Levites were not with us the first time that the LORD our God burst forth in anger against us. For we did not consult Him about the proper order.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 14, 'So the priests and Levites consecrated themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 15, 'And the Levites carried the ark of God on their shoulders with the poles, as Moses had commanded in accordance with the word of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 16, 'David also told the leaders of the Levites to appoint their relatives as singers to lift up their voices with joy, accompanied by musical instruments—harps, lyres, and cymbals.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 17, 'So the Levites appointed Heman son of Joel; from his brothers, Asaph son of Berechiah; from their brothers the Merarites, Ethan son of Kushaiah;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 18, 'and with them their brothers next in rank: Zechariah, Jaaziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, and the gatekeepers Obed-edom and Jeiel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 19, 'The musicians Heman, Asaph, and Ethan were to sound the bronze cymbals.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 20, 'Zechariah, Aziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Maaseiah, and Benaiah were to play the harps according to Alamoth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 21, 'And Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah were to lead the music with lyres according to Sheminith.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 22, 'Chenaniah the head Levite was the director of the music because he was highly skilled.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 23, 'Berechiah and Elkanah were to be guardians of the ark.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 24, 'Shebaniah, Joshaphat, Nethanel, Amasai, Zechariah, Benaiah, and Eliezer—the priests—were to blow the trumpets before the ark of God. Obed-edom and Jehiah were also to be guardians of the ark.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 25, 'So David, the elders of Israel, and the commanders of thousands went with rejoicing to bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD from the house of Obed-edom.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 26, 'And because God helped the Levites who were carrying the ark of the covenant of the LORD, they sacrificed seven bulls and seven rams.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 27, 'Now David was dressed in a robe of fine linen, as were all the Levites who were carrying the ark, as well as the singers and Chenaniah, the director of music for the singers. David also wore a linen ephod.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 28, 'So all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the LORD with shouting, with the sounding of rams’ horns and trumpets, and with cymbals and the music of harps and lyres.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 15, 29, 'As the ark of the covenant of the LORD was entering the City of David, Saul’s daughter Michal looked down from a window and saw King David dancing and celebrating, and she despised him in her heart.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 1, 'So they brought the ark of God and placed it inside the tent that David had pitched for it. And they presented burnt offerings and peace offerings before God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 2, 'When David had finished sacrificing the burnt offerings and peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 3, 'Then he distributed to every man and woman of Israel a loaf of bread, a date cake, and a raisin cake.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 4, 'David appointed some of the Levites to minister before the ark of the LORD, to celebrate, to give thanks, and to praise the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 5, 'Asaph was the chief, Zechariah was second, then Jeiel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-edom, and Jeiel. They were to play the harps and lyres, while Asaph sounded the cymbals'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 6, 'and the priests Benaiah and Jahaziel blew the trumpets regularly before the ark of the covenant of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 7, 'On that day David first committed to Asaph and his brothers this song of thanksgiving to the LORD:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 8, '“Give thanks to the LORD; call upon His name; make known His deeds among the nations.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 9, 'Sing to Him, sing praises to Him; tell of all His wonders.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 10, 'Glory in His holy name; let the hearts of those who seek the LORD rejoice.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 11, 'Seek out the LORD and His strength; seek His face always.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 12, 'Remember the wonders He has done, His marvels, and the judgments He has pronounced,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 13, 'O offspring of His servant Israel, O sons of Jacob, His chosen ones.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 14, 'He is the LORD our God; His judgments carry throughout the earth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 15, 'Remember His covenant forever, the word He ordained for a thousand generations—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 16, 'the covenant He made with Abraham, and the oath He swore to Isaac.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 17, 'He confirmed it to Jacob as a decree, to Israel as an everlasting covenant:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 18, '‘I will give you the land of Canaan as the portion of your inheritance.’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 19, 'When they were few in number, few indeed, and strangers in the land,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 20, 'they wandered from nation to nation, from one kingdom to another.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 21, 'He let no man oppress them; He rebuked kings on their behalf:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 22, '‘Do not touch My anointed ones! Do no harm to My prophets!’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 23, 'Sing to the LORD, all the earth. Proclaim His salvation day after day.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 24, 'Declare His glory among the nations, His wonderful deeds among all peoples.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 25, 'For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised; He is to be feared above all gods.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 26, 'For all the gods of the nations are idols, but it is the LORD who made the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 27, 'Splendor and majesty are before Him; strength and joy fill His dwelling.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 28, 'Ascribe to the LORD, O families of the nations, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 29, 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due His name; bring an offering and come before Him. Worship the LORD in the splendor of His holiness;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 30, 'tremble before Him, all the earth. The world is firmly established; it cannot be moved.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 31, 'Let the heavens be glad, and the earth rejoice. Let them say among the nations, ‘The LORD reigns!’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 32, 'Let the sea resound, and all that fills it; let the fields exult, and all that is in them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 33, 'Then the trees of the forest will sing for joy before the LORD, for He is coming to judge the earth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 34, 'Give thanks to the LORD, for He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 35, 'Then cry out: ‘Save us, O God of our salvation; gather and deliver us from the nations, that we may give thanks to Your holy name, that we may glory in Your praise.’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 36, 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting.” Then all the people said, “Amen!” and “Praise the LORD!”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 37, 'So David left Asaph and his brothers there before the ark of the covenant of the LORD, to minister there regularly according to the daily requirements,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 38, 'along with Obed-edom and his sixty-eight relatives. Obed-edom son of Jeduthun, and also Hosah, were to be gatekeepers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 39, 'And David left Zadok the priest and his fellow priests before the tabernacle of the LORD at the high place in Gibeon'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 40, 'to regularly present burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of burnt offerings, morning and evening, according to all that was written in the Law of the LORD, which He had commanded Israel to keep.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 41, 'With them were Heman, Jeduthun, and the rest of those chosen and designated by name to give thanks to the LORD, for “His loving devotion endures forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 42, 'Heman and Jeduthun had with them trumpets and cymbals for the music and instruments for the songs of God. And the sons of Jeduthun were stationed at the gate.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 16, 43, 'Then all the people departed for their homes, and David returned home to bless his household.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 1, 'After David had settled into his palace, he said to Nathan the prophet, “Here I am, living in a house of cedar, while the ark of the covenant of the LORD is under a tent.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 2, 'And Nathan replied to David, “Do all that is in your heart, for God is with you.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 3, 'But that night the word of God came to Nathan, saying,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 4, '“Go and tell My servant David that this is what the LORD says: You are not the one to build Me a house in which to dwell.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 5, 'For I have not dwelt in a house from the day I brought Israel up out of Egypt until this day, but I have moved from tent to tent and dwelling to dwelling.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 6, 'In all My journeys with all the Israelites, have I ever asked any of the leaders I appointed to shepherd My people, ‘Why haven’t you built Me a house of cedar?’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 7, 'Now then, you are to tell My servant David that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: I took you from the pasture, from following the flock, to be the ruler over My people Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 8, 'I have been with you wherever you have gone, and I have cut off all your enemies from before you. Now I will make for you a name like the greatest in the land.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 9, 'And I will provide a place for My people Israel and will plant them so that they may dwell in a place of their own and be disturbed no more. No longer will the sons of wickedness oppress them as they did at the beginning'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 10, 'and have done since the day I appointed judges over My people Israel. And I will subdue all your enemies. Moreover, I declare to you that the LORD will build a house for you.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 11, 'And when your days are fulfilled and you go to be with your fathers, I will raise up your descendant after you, one of your own sons, and I will establish his kingdom.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 12, 'He will build a house for Me, and I will establish his throne forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 13, 'I will be his Father, and he will be My son. And I will never remove My loving devotion from him as I removed it from your predecessor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 14, 'But I will set him over My house and My kingdom forever, and his throne will be established forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 15, 'So Nathan relayed to David all the words of this entire vision.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 16, 'Then King David went in, sat before the LORD, and said, “Who am I, O LORD God, and what is my house, that You have brought me this far?'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 17, 'And as if this was a small thing in Your eyes, O God, You have spoken about the future of the house of Your servant and have regarded me as a man of great distinction, O LORD God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 18, 'What more can David say to You for so honoring Your servant? For You know Your servant,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 19, 'O LORD. For the sake of Your servant and according to Your own heart, You have accomplished this great thing and revealed all Your greatness.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 20, 'O LORD, there is none like You, and there is no God but You, according to everything we have heard with our own ears.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 21, 'And who is like Your people Israel—the one nation on earth whom God went out to redeem as a people for Himself? You made a name for Yourself through great and awesome wonders by driving out nations from before Your people, whom You redeemed from Egypt.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 22, 'For You have made Your people Israel Your very own forever, and You, O LORD, have become their God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 23, 'And now, O LORD, let the word You have spoken concerning Your servant and his house be established forever. Do as You have promised,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 24, 'so that Your name will be established and magnified forever when it is said, ‘The LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, is God over Israel.’ And may the house of Your servant David be established before You.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 25, 'For You, my God, have revealed to Your servant that You will build a house for him. Therefore Your servant has found the courage to pray before You.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 26, 'And now, O LORD, You are God! And You have promised this goodness to Your servant.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 17, 27, 'So now You have been pleased to bless the house of Your servant, that it may continue forever before You. For You, O LORD, have blessed it, and it will be blessed forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 1, 'Some time later, David defeated the Philistines, subdued them, and took Gath and its villages from the hand of the Philistines.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 2, 'David also defeated the Moabites, and they became subject to David and brought him tribute.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 3, 'As far as Hamath, David also defeated King Hadadezer of Zobah, who had marched out to establish his dominion along the Euphrates River.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 4, 'David captured from him a thousand chariots, seven thousand charioteers, and twenty thousand foot soldiers, and he hamstrung all the horses except a hundred he kept for the chariots.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 5, 'When the Arameans of Damascus came to help King Hadadezer of Zobah, David struck down twenty-two thousand men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 6, 'Then he placed garrisons in Aram of Damascus, and the Arameans became subject to David and brought him tribute. So the LORD made David victorious wherever he went.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 7, 'And David took the gold shields that belonged to the officers of Hadadezer and brought them to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 8, 'And from Tibhath and Cun, cities of Hadadezer, David took a large amount of bronze, with which Solomon made the bronze Sea, the pillars, and various bronze articles.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 9, 'When King Tou of Hamath heard that David had defeated the entire army of Hadadezer king of Zobah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 10, 'he sent his son Hadoram to greet King David and bless him for fighting and defeating Hadadezer, who had been at war with Tou. Hadoram brought all kinds of articles of gold and silver and bronze,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 11, 'and King David dedicated these to the LORD, along with the silver and gold he had carried off from all these nations—from Edom and Moab, and from the Ammonites, Philistines, and Amalekites.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 12, 'Moreover, Abishai son of Zeruiah struck down eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 13, 'He placed garrisons in Edom, and all the Edomites were subject to David. So the LORD made David victorious wherever he went.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 14, 'Thus David reigned over all Israel and administered justice and righteousness for all his people:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 15, 'Joab son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was the recorder;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 16, 'Zadok son of Ahitub and Ahimelech son of Abiathar were priests; Shavsha was the scribe;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 18, 17, 'Benaiah son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and Pelethites; and David’s sons were chief officials at the king’s side.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 1, 'Some time later, Nahash king of the Ammonites died and was succeeded by his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 2, 'And David said, “I will show kindness to Hanun son of Nahash, because his father showed kindness to me.” So David sent messengers to console Hanun concerning his father. But when David’s servants arrived in the land of the Ammonites to console him,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 3, 'the princes of the Ammonites said to Hanun, “Just because David has sent you comforters, do you really believe he is showing respect for your father? Have not his servants come to you to explore the land, spy it out, and overthrow it?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 4, 'So Hanun took David’s servants, shaved their beards, cut off their garments at the hips, and sent them away.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 5, 'When someone came and told David about his men, he sent messengers to meet them, since the men had been thoroughly humiliated. The king told them, “Stay in Jericho until your beards have grown back, and then return.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 6, 'When the Ammonites realized that they had become a stench to David, Hanun and the Ammonites sent a thousand talents of silver to hire for themselves chariots and horsemen from Aram-naharaim, Aram-maacah, and Zobah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 7, 'So they hired for themselves thirty-two thousand chariots, as well as the king of Maacah with his troops, who came and camped near Medeba while the Ammonites came from their cities and marched out for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 8, 'On hearing this, David sent Joab and the entire army of mighty men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 9, 'The Ammonites marched out and arrayed themselves for battle at the entrance to the city, while the kings who had come stayed by themselves in the open country.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 10, 'When Joab saw the battle lines before him and behind him, he selected some of the best men of Israel and arrayed them against the Arameans.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 11, 'And he placed the rest of the forces under the command of his brother Abishai, who arrayed them against the Ammonites.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 12, '“If the Arameans are too strong for me,” said Joab, “then you will come to my rescue. And if the Ammonites are too strong for you, then I will come to your rescue.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 13, 'Be strong and let us fight bravely for our people and for the cities of our God. May the LORD do what is good in His sight.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 14, 'So Joab and his troops advanced to fight the Arameans, who fled before him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 15, 'When the Ammonites saw that the Arameans had fled, they too fled before Joab’s brother Abishai, and they entered the city. So Joab went back to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 16, 'When the Arameans saw that they had been defeated by Israel, they sent messengers to bring more Arameans from beyond the Euphrates, with Shophach the commander of Hadadezer’s army leading them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 17, 'When this was reported to David, he gathered all Israel, crossed the Jordan, advanced toward the Arameans, and arrayed for battle against them. When David lined up to engage them in battle, they fought against him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 18, 'But the Arameans fled before Israel, and David killed seven thousand of their charioteers and forty thousand foot soldiers. He also killed Shophach the commander of their army.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 19, 19, 'When Hadadezer’s subjects saw that they had been defeated by Israel, they made peace with David and became subject to him. So the Arameans were unwilling to help the Ammonites anymore.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 1, 'In the spring, at the time when kings march out to war, Joab led out the army and ravaged the land of the Ammonites. He came to Rabbah and besieged it, but David remained in Jerusalem. And Joab attacked Rabbah and demolished it.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 2, 'Then David took the crown from the head of their king. It was found to weigh a talent of gold and was set with precious stones, and it was placed on David’s head. And David took a great amount of plunder from the city.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 3, 'David brought out the people who were there and put them to work with saws, iron picks, and axes. And he did the same to all the Ammonite cities. Then David and all his troops returned to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 4, 'Some time later, war broke out with the Philistines at Gezer. At that time Sibbecai the Hushathite killed Sippai, a descendant of the Rephaim, and the Philistines were subdued.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 5, 'Once again there was a battle with the Philistines, and Elhanan son of Jair killed Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the shaft of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 6, 'And there was still another battle at Gath, where there was a man of great stature with six fingers on each hand and six toes on each foot—twenty-four in all. He too was descended from Rapha,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 7, 'and when he taunted Israel, Jonathan the son of David’s brother Shimei killed him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 20, 8, 'So these descendants of Rapha in Gath fell at the hands of David and his servants.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 1, 'Then Satan rose up against Israel and incited David to take a census of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 2, 'So David said to Joab and the commanders of the troops, “Go and count the Israelites from Beersheba to Dan and bring me a report, so that I may know their number.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 3, 'But Joab replied, “May the LORD multiply His troops a hundred times over. My lord the king, are they not all servants of my lord? Why does my lord want to do this? Why should he bring guilt on Israel?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 4, 'Nevertheless, the king’s word prevailed against Joab. So Joab departed and traveled throughout Israel, and then he returned to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 5, 'And Joab reported to David the total number of the troops. In all Israel there were 1,100,000 men who drew the sword, including 470,000 in Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 6, 'But Joab did not include Levi and Benjamin in the count, because the king’s command was detestable to him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 7, 'This command was also evil in the sight of God; so He struck Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 8, 'Then David said to God, “I have sinned greatly because I have done this thing. Now I beg You to take away the iniquity of Your servant, for I have acted very foolishly.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 9, 'And the LORD instructed Gad, David’s seer,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 10, '“Go and tell David that this is what the LORD says: ‘I am offering you three options. Choose one of them, and I will carry it out against you.’”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 11, 'So Gad went and said to David, “This is what the LORD says: ‘You must choose'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 12, 'between three years of famine, three months of being swept away before your enemies and overtaken by their swords, or three days of the sword of the LORD—days of plague upon the land, with the angel of the LORD ravaging every part of Israel.’ Now then, decide how I should reply to Him who sent me.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 13, 'David answered Gad, “I am deeply distressed. Please, let me fall into the hand of the LORD, for His mercies are very great; but do not let me fall into the hands of men.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 14, 'So the LORD sent a plague upon Israel, and seventy thousand men of Israel fell dead.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 15, 'Then God sent an angel to destroy Jerusalem, but as the angel was doing so, the LORD saw it and relented from the calamity, and He said to the angel who was destroying the people, “Enough! Withdraw your hand now!” At that time the angel of the LORD was standing by the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 16, 'When David lifted up his eyes and saw the angel of the LORD standing between heaven and earth, with a drawn sword in his hand stretched out over Jerusalem, David and the elders, clothed in sackcloth, fell facedown.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 17, 'And David said to God, “Was it not I who gave the order to count the people? I am the one who has sinned and acted wickedly. But these sheep, what have they done? O LORD my God, please let Your hand fall upon me and my father’s house, but do not let this plague remain upon Your people.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 18, 'Then the angel of the LORD ordered Gad to tell David to go up and build an altar to the LORD on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 19, 'So David went up at the word that Gad had spoken in the name of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 20, 'Now Ornan was threshing wheat when he turned and saw the angel; and his four sons who were with him hid themselves.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 21, 'David came to Ornan, and when Ornan looked out and saw David, he left the threshing floor and bowed facedown before David.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 22, 'Then David said to Ornan, “Grant me the site of this threshing floor, that I may build an altar to the LORD. Sell it to me for the full price, so that the plague upon the people may be halted.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 23, 'Ornan said to David, “My lord the king may take whatever seems good. Look, I will give the oxen for the burnt offerings, the threshing sledges for the wood, and the wheat for the grain offering—I will give it all.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 24, '“No,” replied King David, “I insist on paying the full price, for I will not take for the LORD what belongs to you, nor will I offer burnt offerings that cost me nothing.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 25, 'So David paid Ornan six hundred shekels of gold for the site.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 26, 'And there he built an altar to the LORD and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. He called upon the LORD, who answered him with fire from heaven on the altar of burnt offering.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 27, 'Then the LORD spoke to the angel, who put his sword back into its sheath.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 28, 'At that time, when David saw that the LORD had answered him at the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite, he offered sacrifices there.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 29, 'For the tabernacle of the LORD that Moses had made in the wilderness and the altar of burnt offering were presently at the high place in Gibeon,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 21, 30, 'but David could not go before it to inquire of God, because he was afraid of the sword of the angel of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 1, 'Then David said, “Here shall be the house of the LORD God, as well as the altar of burnt offering for Israel.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 2, 'So David gave orders to gather the foreigners in the land of Israel, from whom he appointed stonecutters to prepare finished stones for building the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 3, 'David provided a large quantity of iron to make the nails for the doors of the gateways and for the fittings, together with more bronze than could be weighed'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 4, 'and more cedar logs than could be counted; for the Sidonians and Tyrians had brought a large quantity of cedar logs to David.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 5, 'And David said, “My son Solomon is young and inexperienced, and the house to be built for the LORD must be exceedingly magnificent—famous and glorious throughout all lands. Therefore I must make preparations for it.” So David made lavish preparations before his death.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 6, 'Then David called for his son Solomon and instructed him to build a house for the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 7, '“My son,” said David to Solomon, “it was in my heart to build a house for the Name of the LORD my God,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 8, 'but this word of the LORD came to me: ‘You have shed much blood and waged great wars. You are not to build a house for My Name because you have shed so much blood on the ground before Me.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 9, 'But a son will be born to you who will be a man of rest. I will give him rest from all his enemies on every side; for his name will be Solomon, and I will grant to Israel peace and quiet during his reign.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 10, 'He is the one who will build a house for My Name. He will be My son, and I will be his Father. And I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel forever.’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 11, 'Now, my son, may the LORD be with you, and may you succeed in building the house of the LORD your God, as He said you would.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 12, 'Above all, may the LORD give you insight and understanding when He puts you in command over Israel, so that you may keep the Law of the LORD your God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 13, 'Then you will succeed, if you carefully follow the statutes and ordinances that the LORD commanded Moses for Israel. Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid or discouraged.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 14, 'Now behold, I have taken great pains to provide for the house of the LORD—100,000 talents of gold, 1,000,000 talents of silver, and bronze and iron too great to be weighed. I have also provided timber and stone, and you may add to them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 15, 'You also have many workers: stonecutters, masons, carpenters, and men skilled in every kind of work—'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 16, 'in gold and silver, bronze and iron—craftsmen beyond number. Now begin the work, and may the LORD be with you.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 17, 'Then David ordered all the leaders of Israel to help his son Solomon:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 18, '“Is not the LORD your God with you, and has He not granted you rest on every side? For He has given the inhabitants of the land into my hand, and the land has been subdued before the LORD and His people.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 22, 19, 'Now set your heart and soul to seek the LORD your God. Get started building the sanctuary of the LORD God, so that you may bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD and the holy articles of God into the temple that will be built for the Name of the LORD.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 1, 'When David was old and full of years, he installed his son Solomon as king over Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 2, 'Then he gathered all the leaders of Israel, as well as the priests and Levites.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 3, 'The Levites thirty years of age or older were counted, and the total number of men was 38,000.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 4, '“Of these,” said David, “24,000 are to oversee the work of the house of the LORD, 6,000 are to be officers and judges,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 5, '4,000 are to be gatekeepers, and 4,000 are to praise the LORD with the instruments I have made for giving praise.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 6, 'Then David divided the Levites into divisions according to the sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath, and Merari.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 7, 'The Gershonites: Ladan and Shimei.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 8, 'The sons of Ladan: Jehiel the first, Zetham, and Joel—three in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 9, 'The sons of Shimei: Shelomoth, Haziel, and Haran—three in all. These were the heads of the families of Ladan.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 10, 'And the sons of Shimei: Jahath, Zina, Jeush, and Beriah. These were the sons of Shimei—four in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 11, 'Jahath was the first and Zizah was the second; but Jeush and Beriah did not have many sons, so they were counted as one family and received a single assignment.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 12, 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel—four in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 13, 'The sons of Amram: Aaron and Moses. Aaron and his descendants were set apart forever to consecrate the most holy things, to burn incense before the LORD, to minister before Him, and to pronounce blessings in His name forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 14, 'As for Moses the man of God, his sons were named among the tribe of Levi.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 15, 'The sons of Moses: Gershom and Eliezer.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 16, 'The descendants of Gershom: Shebuel was the first.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 17, 'The descendants of Eliezer: Rehabiah was the first. Eliezer did not have any other sons, but the sons of Rehabiah were very numerous.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 18, 'The sons of Izhar: Shelomith was the first.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 19, 'The sons of Hebron: Jeriah was the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 20, 'The sons of Uzziel: Micah was the first and Isshiah the second.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 21, 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 22, 'The sons of Mahli: Eleazar and Kish. Eleazar died without having any sons; he had only daughters. Their cousins, the sons of Kish, married them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 23, 'The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jeremoth—three in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 24, 'These were the descendants of Levi by their families—the heads of families, registered individually by name—those twenty years of age or older who worked in the service of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 25, 'For David had said, “The LORD, the God of Israel, has given rest to His people and has come to dwell in Jerusalem forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 26, 'So now the Levites no longer need to carry the tabernacle or any of the articles for its service.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 27, 'For according to the final instructions of David, the Levites twenty years of age or older were counted,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 28, 'but their duty was to assist the descendants of Aaron with the service of the house of the LORD, being responsible for the courts and chambers, the purification of all the holy things, and the work of the service of the house of God,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 29, 'as well as for the rows of the showbread, the fine flour for the grain offering, the wafers of unleavened bread, the baking, the mixing, and all measurements of quantity and size.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 30, 'They were also to stand every morning to give thanks and praise to the LORD, and likewise in the evening.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 31, 'Whenever burnt offerings were presented to the LORD on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts, they were to serve regularly before the LORD in the numbers prescribed for them.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 23, 32, 'So the Levites were to carry out the responsibilities for the Tent of Meeting and the Holy Place, and, under their brothers the descendants of Aaron, the service of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 1, 'These were the divisions of the descendants of Aaron. The sons of Aaron were Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 2, 'But Nadab and Abihu died before their father did, and they had no sons; so Eleazar and Ithamar served as priests.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 3, 'With the help of Eleazar’s descendant Zadok and Ithamar’s descendant Ahimelech, David divided them according to the offices of their service.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 4, 'Since more leaders were found among Eleazar’s descendants than those of Ithamar, they were divided accordingly. There were sixteen heads of families from the descendants of Eleazar and eight from the descendants of Ithamar.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 5, 'Thus they were divided by lot, for there were officers of the sanctuary and officers of God among both Eleazar’s and Ithamar’s descendants.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 6, 'The scribe, Shemaiah son of Nethanel, a Levite, recorded their names in the presence of the king and of the officers: Zadok the priest, Ahimelech son of Abiathar, and the heads of families of the priests and the Levites—one family being taken from Eleazar, and then one from Ithamar.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 7, 'The first lot fell to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 8, 'the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 9, 'the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 10, 'the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 11, 'the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 12, 'the eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 13, 'the thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 14, 'the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 15, 'the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 16, 'the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezkel,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 17, 'the twenty-first to Jachin, the twenty-second to Gamul,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 18, 'the twenty-third to Delaiah, and the twenty-fourth to Maaziah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 19, 'This was their appointed order for service when they entered the house of the LORD, according to the regulations prescribed for them by their forefather Aaron, as the LORD, the God of Israel, had commanded him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 20, 'Now these were the remaining descendants of Levi: From the sons of Amram: Shubael; from the sons of Shubael: Jehdeiah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 21, 'As for Rehabiah, from his sons: The first was Isshiah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 22, 'From the Izharites: Shelomoth; from the sons of Shelomoth: Jahath.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 23, 'From the sons of Hebron: Jeriah was the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 24, 'From the sons of Uzziel: Micah; from the sons of Micah: Shamir.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 25, 'The brother of Micah: Isshiah; from the sons of Isshiah: Zechariah.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 26, 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The son of Jaaziah: Beno.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 27, 'The descendants of Merari from Jaaziah: Beno, Shoham, Zaccur, and Ibri.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 28, 'From Mahli: Eleazar, who had no sons.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 29, 'From Kish: Jerahmeel the son of Kish.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 30, 'And the sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites, according to their families.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 24, 31, 'As their brothers the descendants of Aaron did, they also cast lots in the presence of King David and of Zadok, Ahimelech, and the heads of the families of the priests and Levites—the family heads and their younger brothers alike.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 1, 'Additionally, David and the commanders of the army set apart some of the sons of Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun to prophesy with the accompaniment of lyres, harps, and cymbals. The following is the list of the men who performed this service:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 2, 'From the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, Joseph, Nethaniah, and Asarelah. These sons of Asaph were under the direction of Asaph, who prophesied under the direction of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 3, 'From the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Shimei, Hashabiah, and Mattithiah—six in all—under the direction of their father Jeduthun, who prophesied with the harp, giving thanks and praise to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 4, 'From the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 5, 'All these sons of Heman the king’s seer were given him through the promises of God to exalt him, for God had given Heman fourteen sons and three daughters.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 6, 'All these were under the direction of their fathers for the music of the house of the LORD with cymbals, harps, and lyres, for the service of the house of God. Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman were under the direction of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 7, 'Together with their relatives, who were all trained and skillful in the songs of the LORD, they numbered 288.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 8, 'They cast lots for their duties, young and old alike, teacher as well as pupil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 9, 'The first lot, which was for Asaph, fell to Joseph, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all; the second to Gedaliah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 10, 'the third to Zaccur, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 11, 'the fourth to Izri, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 12, 'the fifth to Nethaniah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 13, 'the sixth to Bukkiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 14, 'the seventh to Jesarelah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 15, 'the eighth to Jeshaiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 16, 'the ninth to Mattaniah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 17, 'the tenth to Shimei, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 18, 'the eleventh to Azarel, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 19, 'the twelfth to Hashabiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 20, 'the thirteenth to Shubael, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 21, 'the fourteenth to Mattithiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 22, 'the fifteenth to Jeremoth, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 23, 'the sixteenth to Hananiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 24, 'the seventeenth to Joshbekashah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 25, 'the eighteenth to Hanani, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 26, 'the nineteenth to Mallothi, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 27, 'the twentieth to Eliathah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 28, 'the twenty-first to Hothir, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 29, 'the twenty-second to Giddalti, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 30, 'the twenty-third to Mahazioth, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 25, 31, 'and the twenty-fourth to Romamti-ezer, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 1, 'These were the divisions of the gatekeepers: From the Korahites: Meshelemiah son of Kore, one of the sons of Asaph.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 2, 'Meshelemiah had sons: Zechariah the firstborn, Jediael the second, Zebadiah the third, Jathniel the fourth,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 3, 'Elam the fifth, Jehohanan the sixth, and Eliehoenai the seventh.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 4, 'And Obed-edom also had sons: Shemaiah the firstborn, Jehozabad the second, Joah the third, Sachar the fourth, Nethanel the fifth,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 5, 'Ammiel the sixth, Issachar the seventh, and Peullethai the eighth. For God had blessed Obed-edom.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 6, 'Also to his son Shemaiah were born sons who ruled over their families because they were strong, capable men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 7, 'Shemaiah’s sons were Othni, Rephael, Obed, and Elzabad; his brothers were Elihu and Semachiah, also capable men.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 8, 'All these were descendants of Obed-edom; they and their sons and brothers were capable men with strength to do the work—62 in all from Obed-edom.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 9, 'Meshelemiah also had sons and brothers who were capable men—18 in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 10, 'Hosah the Merarite also had sons: Shimri the first (although he was not the firstborn, his father had appointed him as the first),'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 11, 'Hilkiah the second, Tebaliah the third, and Zechariah the fourth. The sons and brothers of Hosah numbered 13 in all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 12, 'These divisions of the gatekeepers, through their chief men, had duties for ministering in the house of the LORD, just as their brothers did.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 13, 'They cast lots for each gate, according to their families, young and old alike.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 14, 'The lot for the East Gate fell to Shelemiah. Then lots were cast for his son Zechariah, a wise counselor, and the lot for the North Gate fell to him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 15, 'The lot for the South Gate fell to Obed-edom, and the lot for the storehouses to his sons.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 16, 'The lots for the West Gate and the Shallecheth Gate on the ascending highway fell to Shuppim and Hosah. There were guards stationed at every watch.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 17, 'Each day there were six Levites on the east, four on the north, four on the south, and two pairs at the storehouse.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 18, 'As for the court on the west, there were four at the highway and two at the court.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 19, 'These were the divisions of the gatekeepers who were descendants of Korah and Merari.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 20, 'Now their fellow Levites were in charge of the treasuries of the house of God and the treasuries of the dedicated things.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 21, 'From the descendants of Ladan, who were Gershonites through Ladan and heads of the families of Ladan the Gershonite, were Jehieli,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 22, 'the sons of Jehieli, Zetham, and his brother Joel. They were in charge of the treasuries of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 23, 'From the Amramites, the Izharites, the Hebronites, and the Uzzielites:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 24, 'Shebuel, a descendant of Gershom son of Moses, was the officer in charge of the treasuries.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 25, 'His relatives through Eliezer included Rehabiah his son, Jeshaiah his son, Joram his son, Zichri his son, and Shelomith his son.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 26, 'This Shelomith and his brothers were in charge of all the treasuries for the things dedicated by King David, by the heads of families who were the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and by the army commanders.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 27, 'They had dedicated some of the plunder from their battles to the repair of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 28, 'Everything that had been dedicated by Samuel the seer, Saul son of Kish, Abner son of Ner, and Joab son of Zeruiah, along with everything else that was dedicated, was under the care of Shelomith and his brothers.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 29, 'From the Izharites, Chenaniah and his sons had the outside duties as officers and judges over Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 30, 'From the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his relatives, 1,700 capable men, had charge of the affairs of Israel west of the Jordan for all the work of the LORD and for the service of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 31, 'As for the Hebronites, Jerijah was the chief of the Hebronites, according to the genealogies of his ancestors. In the fortieth year of David’s reign the records were searched, and strong, capable men were found among the Hebronites at Jazer in Gilead.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 26, 32, 'Among Jerijah’s relatives there were 2,700 capable men who were heads of families. King David appointed them over the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh for every matter pertaining to God and to the affairs of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 1, 'This is the list of the Israelites—the heads of families, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and their officers who served the king in every matter concerning the divisions on rotating military duty each month throughout the year. There were 24,000 men in each division:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 2, 'Jashobeam son of Zabdiel was in charge of the first division, which was assigned the first month. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 3, 'He was a descendant of Perez and chief of all the army commanders for the first month.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 4, 'Dodai the Ahohite was in charge of the division for the second month, and Mikloth was the leader. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 5, 'The third army commander, as chief for the third month, was Benaiah son of Jehoiada the priest. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 6, 'This Benaiah was mighty among the Thirty and was over the Thirty, and his son Ammizabad was in charge of his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 7, 'The fourth, for the fourth month, was Joab’s brother Asahel, and his son Zebadiah was commander after him. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 8, 'The fifth, for the fifth month, was the commander Shamhuth the Izrahite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 9, 'The sixth, for the sixth month, was Ira son of Ikkesh the Tekoite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 10, 'The seventh, for the seventh month, was Helez the Pelonite, an Ephraimite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 11, 'The eighth, for the eighth month, was Sibbecai the Hushathite, a Zerahite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 12, 'The ninth, for the ninth month, was Abiezer the Anathothite, a Benjamite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 13, 'The tenth, for the tenth month, was Maharai the Netophathite, a Zerahite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 14, 'The eleventh, for the eleventh month, was Benaiah the Pirathonite, an Ephraimite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 15, 'The twelfth, for the twelfth month, was Heldai the Netophathite, from the family of Othniel. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 16, 'These officers were in charge of the tribes of Israel: Over the Reubenites was Eliezer son of Zichri; over the Simeonites was Shephatiah son of Maacah;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 17, 'over Levi was Hashabiah son of Kemuel; over Aaron was Zadok;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 18, 'over Judah was Elihu, one of David’s brothers; over Issachar was Omri son of Michael;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 19, 'over Zebulun was Ishmaiah son of Obadiah; over Naphtali was Jerimoth son of Azriel;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 20, 'over the Ephraimites was Hoshea son of Azaziah; over one of the half-tribes of Manasseh was Joel son of Pedaiah;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 21, 'over the half-tribe of Manasseh in Gilead was Iddo son of Zechariah; over Benjamin was Jaasiel son of Abner;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 22, 'and over Dan was Azarel son of Jeroham. These were the leaders of the tribes of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 23, 'David did not count the men aged twenty or under, because the LORD had said that He would make Israel as numerous as the stars of the sky.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 24, 'Joab son of Zeruiah began to count the men but did not finish. For because of this census wrath came upon Israel, and the number was not entered in the Book of the Chronicles of King David.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 25, 'Azmaveth son of Adiel was in charge of the royal storehouses. Jonathan son of Uzziah was in charge of the storehouses in the country, in the cities, in the villages, and in the fortresses.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 26, 'Ezri son of Chelub was in charge of the workers in the fields who tilled the soil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 27, 'Shimei the Ramathite was in charge of the vineyards. Zabdi the Shiphmite was in charge of the produce of the vineyards for the wine vats.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 28, 'Baal-hanan the Gederite was in charge of the olive and sycamore trees in the foothills. Joash was in charge of the stores of olive oil.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 29, 'Shitrai the Sharonite was in charge of the herds grazing in Sharon. Shaphat son of Adlai was in charge of the herds in the valleys.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 30, 'Obil the Ishmaelite was in charge of the camels. Jehdeiah the Meronothite was in charge of the donkeys.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 31, 'Jaziz the Hagrite was in charge of the flocks. All these officials were in charge of King David’s property.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 32, 'David’s uncle Jonathan was a counselor; he was a man of insight and a scribe. Jehiel son of Hachmoni attended to the sons of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 33, 'Ahithophel was the king’s counselor. Hushai the Archite was the king’s friend.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 27, 34, 'Ahithophel was succeeded by Jehoiada son of Benaiah, then by Abiathar. Joab was the commander of the king’s army.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 1, 'Now David summoned all the leaders of Israel to Jerusalem: the leaders of the tribes, the leaders of the divisions in the king’s service, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and the officials in charge of all the property and cattle of the king and his sons, along with the court officials and mighty men—every mighty man of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 2, 'Then King David rose to his feet and said, “Listen to me, my brothers and my people. It was in my heart to build a house as a resting place for the ark of the covenant of the LORD and as a footstool for our God. I had made preparations to build it,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 3, 'but God said to me, ‘You are not to build a house for My Name, because you are a man of war who has spilled blood.’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 4, 'Yet the LORD, the God of Israel, chose me out of all my father’s house to be king over Israel forever. For He chose Judah as leader, and from the house of Judah He chose my father’s household, and from my father’s sons He was pleased to make me king over all Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 5, 'And of all my sons—for the LORD has given me many sons—He has chosen Solomon my son to sit on the throne of the kingdom of the LORD over Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 6, 'And He said to me, ‘Solomon your son is the one who will build My house and My courts, for I have chosen him as My son, and I will be his Father.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 7, 'I will establish his kingdom forever, if he resolutely carries out My commandments and ordinances, as is being done this day.’'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 8, 'So now in the sight of all Israel, the assembly of the LORD, and in the hearing of our God, keep and seek out all the commandments of the LORD your God, so that you may possess this good land and leave it as an inheritance to your descendants forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 9, 'As for you, Solomon my son, know the God of your father and serve Him wholeheartedly and with a willing mind, for the LORD searches every heart and understands the intent of every thought. If you seek Him, He will be found by you; but if you forsake Him, He will reject you forever.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 10, 'Consider now that the LORD has chosen you to build a house for the sanctuary. Be strong and do it.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 11, 'Then David gave his son Solomon the plans for the portico of the temple, its buildings, storehouses, upper rooms, inner rooms, and the room for the mercy seat.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 12, 'The plans contained everything David had in mind for the courts of the house of the LORD, for all the surrounding rooms, for the treasuries of the house of God and of the dedicated things,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 13, 'for the divisions of the priests and Levites, for all the work of service in the house of the LORD, and for all the articles of service in the house of the LORD:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 14, 'the weight of all the gold articles for every kind of service; the weight of all the silver articles for every kind of service;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 15, 'the weight of the gold lampstands and their lamps, including the weight of each lampstand and its lamps; the weight of each silver lampstand and its lamps, according to the use of each lampstand;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 16, 'the weight of gold for each table of showbread, and of silver for the silver tables;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 17, 'the weight of the pure gold for the forks, sprinkling bowls, and pitchers; the weight of each gold dish; the weight of each silver bowl;'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 18, 'the weight of the refined gold for the altar of incense; and the plans for the chariot of the gold cherubim that spread their wings and overshadowed the ark of the covenant of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 19, '“All this,” said David, “all the details of this plan, the LORD has made clear to me in writing by His hand upon me.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 20, 'David also said to Solomon his son, “Be strong and courageous, and do it. Do not be afraid or discouraged, for the LORD God, my God, is with you. He will neither fail you nor forsake you before all the work for the service of the house of the LORD is finished.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 28, 21, 'The divisions of the priests and Levites are ready for all the service of the house of God, and every willing man of every skill will be at your disposal for the work. The officials and all the people are fully at your command.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 1, 'Then King David said to the whole assembly, “My son Solomon, the one whom God has chosen, is young and inexperienced. The task is great because this palace is not for man, but for the LORD God.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 2, 'Now with all my ability I have made provision for the house of my God—gold for the gold articles, silver for the silver, bronze for the bronze, iron for the iron, and wood for the wood, as well as onyx for the settings, turquoise, stones of various colors, all kinds of precious stones, and slabs of marble—all in abundance.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 3, 'Moreover, because of my delight in the house of my God, I now give for it my personal treasures of gold and silver, over and above all that I have provided for this holy temple:'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 4, 'three thousand talents of gold (the gold of Ophir) and seven thousand talents of refined silver, to overlay the walls of the buildings,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 5, 'for the gold work and the silver work, and for all the work to be done by the craftsmen. Now who will volunteer to consecrate himself to the LORD today?”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 6, 'Then the leaders of the households, the officers of the tribes of Israel, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and the officials in charge of the king’s work gave willingly.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 7, 'Toward the service of God’s house they gave 5,000 talents and 10,000 darics of gold, 10,000 talents of silver, 18,000 talents of bronze, and 100,000 talents of iron.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 8, 'Whoever had precious stones gave them to the treasury of the house of the LORD, under the care of Jehiel the Gershonite.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 9, 'And the people rejoiced at the willing response of their leaders, for they had given to the LORD freely and wholeheartedly. And King David also rejoiced greatly.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 10, 'Then David blessed the LORD in the sight of all the assembly and said: “May You be blessed, O LORD, God of our father Israel, from everlasting to everlasting.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 11, 'Yours, O LORD, is the greatness and the power and the glory and the splendor and the majesty, for everything in heaven and on earth belongs to You. Yours, O LORD, is the kingdom, and You are exalted as head over all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 12, 'Both riches and honor come from You, and You are the ruler over all. In Your hands are power and might to exalt and give strength to all.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 13, 'Now therefore, our God, we give You thanks, and we praise Your glorious name.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 14, 'But who am I, and who are my people, that we should be able to give as generously as this? For everything comes from You, and from Your own hand we have given to You.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 15, 'For we are foreigners and strangers in Your presence, as were all our forefathers. Our days on earth are like a shadow, without hope.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 16, 'O LORD our God, from Your hand comes all this abundance that we have provided to build You a house for Your holy Name, and all of it belongs to You.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 17, 'I know, my God, that You test the heart and delight in uprightness. All these things I have given willingly and with an upright heart, and now I have seen Your people who are present here giving joyfully and willingly to You.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 18, 'O LORD, God of our fathers Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, keep this desire forever in the intentions of the hearts of Your people, and direct their hearts toward You.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 19, 'And give my son Solomon a whole heart to keep and carry out all Your commandments, decrees, and statutes, and to build Your palace for which I have made provision.”'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 20, 'Then David said to the whole assembly, “Blessed be the LORD your God.” So the whole assembly blessed the LORD, the God of their fathers. They bowed down and paid homage to the LORD and to the king.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 21, 'The next day they offered sacrifices and presented burnt offerings to the LORD: a thousand bulls, a thousand rams, and a thousand lambs, along with their drink offerings, and other sacrifices in abundance for all Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 22, 'That day they ate and drank with great joy in the presence of the LORD. Then, for a second time, they designated David’s son Solomon as king, anointing him before the LORD as ruler, and Zadok as the priest.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 23, 'So Solomon sat on the throne of the LORD as king in place of his father David. He prospered, and all Israel obeyed him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 24, 'All the officials and mighty men, as well as all of King David’s sons, pledged their allegiance to King Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 25, 'The LORD highly exalted Solomon in the sight of all Israel and bestowed on him royal majesty such as had not been bestowed on any king in Israel before him.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 26, 'David son of Jesse was king over all Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 27, 'The length of David’s reign over Israel was forty years—seven years in Hebron and thirty-three years in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 28, 'He died at a ripe old age, full of years, riches, and honor, and his son Solomon reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 29, 'Now the acts of King David, from first to last, are indeed written in the Chronicles of Samuel the Seer, the Chronicles of Nathan the Prophet, and the Chronicles of Gad the Seer,'),
  ('BSB', '1 Chronicles', 13, 29, 30, 'together with all the details of his reign, his might, and the circumstances that came upon him and Israel and all the kingdoms of the lands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 1, 'Now Solomon son of David established himself securely over his kingdom, and the LORD his God was with him and highly exalted him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 2, 'Then Solomon spoke to all Israel, to the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, to the judges, and to every leader in all Israel—the heads of the families.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 3, 'And Solomon and the whole assembly went to the high place at Gibeon because it was the location of God’s Tent of Meeting, which Moses the servant of the LORD had made in the wilderness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 4, 'Now David had brought the ark of God from Kiriath-jearim to the place he had prepared for it, because he had pitched a tent for it in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 5, 'But the bronze altar made by Bezalel son of Uri, the son of Hur, was in Gibeon before the tabernacle of the LORD. So Solomon and the assembly inquired of Him there.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 6, 'Solomon offered sacrifices there before the LORD on the bronze altar in the Tent of Meeting, where he offered a thousand burnt offerings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 7, 'That night God appeared to Solomon and said, “Ask, and I will give it to you!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 8, 'Solomon replied to God: “You have shown much loving devotion to my father David, and You have made me king in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 9, 'Now, O LORD God, let Your promise to my father David be fulfilled. For You have made me king over a people as numerous as the dust of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 10, 'Now grant me wisdom and knowledge, so that I may lead this people. For who is able to govern this great people of Yours?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 11, 'God said to Solomon, “Since this was in your heart instead of requesting riches or wealth or glory for yourself or death for your enemies—and since you have not even requested long life but have asked for wisdom and knowledge to govern My people over whom I have made you king—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 12, 'therefore wisdom and knowledge have been granted to you. And I will also give you riches and wealth and honor unlike anything given to the kings before you or after you.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 13, 'So Solomon went to Jerusalem from the high place in Gibeon before the Tent of Meeting, and he reigned over Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 14, 'Solomon accumulated 1,400 chariots and 12,000 horses, which he stationed in the chariot cities and also with him in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 15, 'The king made silver and gold as common in Jerusalem as stones, and cedar as abundant as sycamore in the foothills.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 16, 'Solomon’s horses were imported from Egypt and Kue; the royal merchants purchased them from Kue.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 1, 17, 'A chariot could be imported from Egypt for six hundred shekels of silver, and a horse for a hundred and fifty. Likewise, they exported them to all the kings of the Hittites and to the kings of Aram.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 1, 'Now Solomon purposed to build a house for the Name of the LORD and a royal palace for himself.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 2, 'So he conscripted 70,000 porters, 80,000 stonecutters in the mountains, and 3,600 supervisors.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 3, 'Then Solomon sent word to Hiram king of Tyre: “Do for me as you did for my father David when you sent him cedars to build himself a house to live in.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 4, 'Behold, I am about to build a house for the Name of the LORD my God to dedicate to Him for burning fragrant incense before Him, for displaying the showbread continuously, and for making burnt offerings every morning and evening as well as on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts of the LORD our God. This is ordained for Israel forever.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 5, 'The house that I am building will be great, for our God is greater than all gods.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 6, 'But who is able to build a house for Him, since the heavens, even the highest heavens, cannot contain Him? Who then am I, that I should build a house for Him, except as a place to burn sacrifices before Him?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 7, 'Send me, therefore, a craftsman skilled in engraving to work with gold and silver, with bronze and iron, and with purple, crimson, and blue yarn. He will work with my craftsmen in Judah and Jerusalem, whom my father David provided.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 8, 'Send me also cedar, cypress, and algum logs from Lebanon, for I know that your servants have skill to cut timber there. And indeed, my servants will work with yours'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 9, 'to prepare for me timber in abundance, because the temple I am building will be great and wonderful.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 10, 'I will pay your servants, the woodcutters, 20,000 cors of ground wheat, 20,000 cors of barley, 20,000 baths of wine, and 20,000 baths of olive oil.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 11, 'Then Hiram king of Tyre wrote a letter in reply to Solomon: “Because the LORD loves His people, He has set you over them as king.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 12, 'And Hiram added: “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who made the heavens and the earth! He has given King David a wise son with insight and understanding, who will build a temple for the LORD and a royal palace for himself.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 13, 'So now I am sending you Huram-abi, a skillful man endowed with creativity.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 14, 'He is the son of a woman from the daughters of Dan, and his father is a man of Tyre. He is skilled in work with gold and silver, bronze and iron, stone and wood, purple, blue, and crimson yarn, and fine linen. He is experienced in every kind of engraving and can execute any design that is given him. He will work with your craftsmen and with those of my lord, your father David.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 15, 'Now let my lord send to his servants the wheat, barley, olive oil, and wine he promised.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 16, 'We will cut logs from Lebanon, as many as you need, and we will float them to you as rafts by sea down to Joppa. Then you can take them up to Jerusalem.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 17, 'Solomon numbered all the foreign men in the land of Israel following the census his father David had conducted, and there were found to be 153,600 in all.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 2, 18, 'Solomon made 70,000 of them porters, 80,000 stonecutters in the mountains, and 3,600 supervisors.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 1, 'Then Solomon began to build the house of the LORD in Jerusalem on Mount Moriah, where the LORD had appeared to his father David. This was the place that David had prepared on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 2, 'Solomon began construction on the second day of the second month in the fourth year of his reign.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 3, 'The foundation that Solomon laid for the house of God was sixty cubits long and twenty cubits wide, according to the old standard.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 4, 'The portico at the front, extending across the width of the temple, was twenty cubits long and twenty cubits high. He overlaid the inside with pure gold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 5, 'He paneled the main room with cypress, which he overlaid with fine gold and decorated with palm trees and chains.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 6, 'He adorned the temple with precious stones for beauty, and its gold was from Parvaim.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 7, 'He overlaid its beams, thresholds, walls, and doors with gold, and he carved cherubim on the walls.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 8, 'Then he made the Most Holy Place; its length corresponded to the width of the temple—twenty cubits long and twenty cubits wide. And he overlaid the inside with six hundred talents of fine gold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 9, 'The weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold. He also overlaid the upper area with gold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 10, 'In the Most Holy Place he made two cherubim of sculptured work, and he overlaid them with gold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 11, 'The total wingspan of the cherubim was twenty cubits. One wing of the first cherub was five cubits long and touched the wall of the temple, and its other wing was five cubits long and touched the wing of the other cherub.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 12, 'The wing of the second cherub also measured five cubits and touched the wall of the temple, while its other wing measured five cubits and touched the wing of the first cherub.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 13, 'So the total wingspan of these cherubim was twenty cubits. They stood on their feet, facing the main room.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 14, 'He made the veil of blue, purple, and crimson yarn and fine linen, with cherubim woven into it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 15, 'In front of the temple he made two pillars, which together were thirty-five cubits high, each with a capital on top measuring five cubits.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 16, 'He made interwoven chains and put them on top of the pillars. He made a hundred pomegranates and fastened them into the chainwork.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 3, 17, 'Then he set up the pillars in front of the temple, one on the south and one on the north. The pillar on the south he named Jachin, and the pillar on the north he named Boaz.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 1, 'He made a bronze altar twenty cubits long, twenty cubits wide, and ten cubits high.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 2, 'He also made the Sea of cast metal. It was circular in shape, measuring ten cubits from rim to rim, five cubits in height, and thirty cubits in circumference.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 3, 'Below the rim, figures of oxen encircled it, ten per cubit all the way around the Sea, cast in two rows as a part of the Sea.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 4, 'The Sea stood on twelve oxen, three facing north, three facing west, three facing south, and three facing east. The Sea rested on them, with all their hindquarters toward the center.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 5, 'It was a handbreadth thick, and its rim was fashioned like the brim of a cup, like a lily blossom. It could hold three thousand baths.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 6, 'He also made ten basins for washing and placed five on the south side and five on the north. The parts of the burnt offering were rinsed in them, but the priests used the Sea for washing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 7, 'He made ten gold lampstands according to their specifications and placed them in the temple, five on the south side and five on the north.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 8, 'Additionally, he made ten tables and placed them in the temple, five on the south side and five on the north. He also made a hundred gold bowls.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 9, 'He made the courtyard of the priests and the large court with its doors, and he overlaid the doors with bronze.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 10, 'He put the Sea on the south side, at the southeast corner.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 11, 'Additionally, Huram made the pots, shovels, and sprinkling bowls. So Huram finished the work that he had undertaken for King Solomon in the house of God:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 12, 'the two pillars; the two bowl-shaped capitals atop the pillars; the two sets of network covering both bowls of the capitals atop the pillars;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 13, 'the four hundred pomegranates for the two sets of network (two rows of pomegranates for each network covering both the bowl-shaped capitals atop the pillars);'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 14, 'the stands; the basins on the stands;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 15, 'the Sea; the twelve oxen underneath the Sea;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 16, 'and the pots, shovels, meat forks, and all the other articles. All these objects that Huram-abi made for King Solomon for the house of the LORD were of polished bronze.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 17, 'The king had them cast in clay molds in the plain of the Jordan between Succoth and Zeredah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 18, 'Solomon made all these articles in such great abundance that the weight of the bronze could not be determined.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 19, 'Solomon also made all the furnishings for the house of God: the golden altar; the tables on which was placed the Bread of the Presence;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 20, 'the lampstands of pure gold and their lamps, to burn in front of the inner sanctuary as prescribed;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 21, 'the flowers, lamps, and tongs of gold—of purest gold;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 4, 22, 'the wick trimmers, sprinkling bowls, ladles, and censers of purest gold; and the gold doors of the temple: the inner doors to the Most Holy Place as well as the doors of the main hall.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 1, 'So all the work that Solomon had performed for the house of the LORD was completed. Then Solomon brought in the items his father David had dedicated—the silver, the gold, and all the furnishings—and he placed them in the treasuries of the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 2, 'At that time Solomon assembled in Jerusalem the elders of Israel—all the tribal heads and family leaders of the Israelites—to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD from Zion, the City of David.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 3, 'So all the men of Israel came together to the king at the feast in the seventh month.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 4, 'When all the elders of Israel had arrived, the Levites took up the ark,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 5, 'and they brought up the ark and the Tent of Meeting with all its sacred furnishings. The Levitical priests carried them up.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 6, 'There, before the ark, King Solomon and the whole congregation of Israel who had assembled with him sacrificed so many sheep and oxen that they could not be counted or numbered.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 7, 'Then the priests brought the ark of the covenant of the LORD to its place in the inner sanctuary of the temple, the Most Holy Place, beneath the wings of the cherubim.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 8, 'For the cherubim spread their wings over the place of the ark and overshadowed the ark and its poles.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 9, 'The poles of the ark extended far enough that their ends were visible from in front of the inner sanctuary, but not from outside the Holy Place; and they are there to this day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 10, 'There was nothing in the ark except the two tablets that Moses had placed in it at Horeb, where the LORD had made a covenant with the Israelites after they had come out of Egypt.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 11, 'Now all the priests who were present had consecrated themselves regardless of their divisions. And when the priests came out of the Holy Place,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 12, 'all the Levitical singers—Asaph, Heman, Jeduthun, and their sons and relatives—stood on the east side of the altar, dressed in fine linen and playing cymbals, harps, and lyres, accompanied by 120 priests sounding trumpets.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 13, 'The trumpeters and singers joined together to praise and thank the LORD with one voice. They lifted up their voices, accompanied by trumpets, cymbals, and musical instruments, in praise to the LORD: “For He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.” And the temple, the house of the LORD, was filled with a cloud'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 5, 14, 'so that the priests could not stand there to minister because of the cloud; for the glory of the LORD filled the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 1, 'Then Solomon declared: “The LORD has said that He would dwell in the thick cloud;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 2, 'and I have built You an exalted house, a place for You to dwell forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 3, 'And as the whole assembly of Israel stood there, the king turned around and blessed them all'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 4, 'and said: “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who has fulfilled with His own hand what He spoke with His mouth to my father David, saying,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 5, '‘Since the day I brought My people out of the land of Egypt, I have not chosen a city from any tribe of Israel in which to build a house so that My Name would be there, nor have I chosen anyone to be ruler over My people Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 6, 'But now I have chosen Jerusalem for My Name to be there, and I have chosen David to be over My people Israel.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 7, 'Now it was in the heart of my father David to build a house for the Name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 8, 'But the LORD said to my father David, ‘Since it was in your heart to build a house for My Name, you have done well to have this in your heart.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 9, 'Nevertheless, you are not the one to build it; but your son, your own offspring, will build the house for My Name.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 10, 'Now the LORD has fulfilled the word that He spoke. I have succeeded my father David, and I sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised. I have built the house for the Name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 11, 'And there I have provided a place for the ark, which contains the covenant of the LORD that He made with the children of Israel.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 12, 'Then Solomon stood before the altar of the LORD in front of the whole assembly of Israel and spread out his hands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 13, 'Now Solomon had made a bronze platform five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high, and had placed it in the middle of the courtyard. He stood on it, knelt down before the whole assembly of Israel, spread out his hands toward heaven,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 14, 'and said: “O LORD, God of Israel, there is no God like You in heaven or on earth, keeping Your covenant of loving devotion with Your servants who walk before You with all their hearts.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 15, 'You have kept Your promise to Your servant, my father David. What You spoke with Your mouth You have fulfilled with Your hand this day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 16, 'Therefore now, O LORD, God of Israel, keep for Your servant, my father David, what You promised when You said: ‘You will never fail to have a man to sit before Me on the throne of Israel, if only your descendants guard their way to walk in My law as you have walked before Me.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 17, 'And now, O LORD, God of Israel, please confirm what You promised to Your servant David.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 18, 'But will God indeed dwell with man upon the earth? Even heaven, the highest heaven, cannot contain You, much less this temple I have built.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 19, 'Yet regard the prayer and plea of Your servant, O LORD my God, so that You may hear the cry and the prayer that Your servant is praying before You.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 20, 'May Your eyes be open toward this temple day and night, toward the place where You said You would put Your Name, so that You may hear the prayer that Your servant prays toward this place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 21, 'Hear the plea of Your servant and of Your people Israel when they pray toward this place. May You hear from heaven, Your dwelling place. May You hear and forgive.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 22, 'When a man sins against his neighbor and is required to take an oath, and he comes to take an oath before Your altar in this temple,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 23, 'then may You hear from heaven and act. May You judge Your servants, condemning the wicked man by bringing down on his own head what he has done, and justifying the righteous man by rewarding him according to his righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 24, 'When Your people Israel are defeated before an enemy because they have sinned against You, and they return to You and confess Your name, praying and pleading before You in this temple,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 25, 'then may You hear from heaven and forgive the sin of Your people Israel. May You restore them to the land You gave to them and their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 26, 'When the skies are shut and there is no rain because Your people have sinned against You, and they pray toward this place and confess Your name, and they turn from their sins because You have afflicted them,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 27, 'then may You hear from heaven and forgive the sin of Your servants, Your people Israel, so that You may teach them the good way in which they should walk. May You send rain on the land that You gave Your people as an inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 28, 'When famine or plague comes upon the land, or blight or mildew or locusts or grasshoppers, or when their enemies besiege them in their cities, whatever plague or sickness may come,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 29, 'then may whatever prayer or petition Your people Israel make—each knowing his own afflictions and spreading out his hands toward this temple—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 30, 'be heard by You from heaven, Your dwelling place. And may You forgive and repay each man according to all his ways, since You know his heart—for You alone know the hearts of men—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 31, 'so that they may fear You and walk in Your ways all the days they live in the land that You gave to our fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 32, 'And as for the foreigner who is not of Your people Israel but has come from a distant land because of Your great name and Your mighty hand and outstretched arm—when he comes and prays toward this temple,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 33, 'then may You hear from heaven, Your dwelling place, and do according to all for which the foreigner calls to You. Then all the peoples of the earth will know Your name and fear You, as do Your people Israel, and they will know that this house I have built is called by Your Name.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 34, 'When Your people go to war against their enemies, wherever You send them, and when they pray to You in the direction of the city You have chosen and the house I have built for Your Name,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 35, 'then may You hear from heaven their prayer and their plea, and may You uphold their cause.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 36, 'When they sin against You—for there is no one who does not sin—and You become angry with them and deliver them to an enemy who takes them as captives to a land far or near,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 37, 'and when they come to their senses in the land to which they were taken, and they repent and plead with You in the land of their captors, saying, ‘We have sinned and done wrong; we have acted wickedly,’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 38, 'and when they return to You with all their heart and soul in the land of the enemies who took them captive, and when they pray in the direction of the land that You gave to their fathers, the city You have chosen, and the house I have built for Your Name,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 39, 'then may You hear from heaven, Your dwelling place, their prayer and petition, and may You uphold their cause. May You forgive Your people who sinned against You.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 40, 'Now, my God, may Your eyes be open and Your ears attentive to the prayer offered in this place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 41, 'Now therefore, arise, O LORD God, and enter Your resting place, You and the ark of Your might. May Your priests, O LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and may Your godly ones rejoice in goodness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 6, 42, 'O LORD God, do not reject Your anointed one. Remember Your loving devotion to Your servant David.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 1, 'When Solomon had finished praying, fire came down from heaven and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices, and the glory of the LORD filled the temple.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 2, 'The priests were unable to enter the house of the LORD, because the glory of the LORD had filled it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 3, 'When all the Israelites saw the fire coming down and the glory of the LORD above the temple, they bowed down on the pavement with their faces to the ground, and they worshiped and gave thanks to the LORD: “For He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 4, 'Then the king and all the people offered sacrifices before the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 5, 'And King Solomon offered a sacrifice of 22,000 oxen and 120,000 sheep. So the king and all the people dedicated the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 6, 'The priests stood at their posts, as did the Levites with the musical instruments of the LORD, which King David had made for giving thanks to the LORD and with which David had offered praise, saying, “For His loving devotion endures forever.” Across from the Levites, the priests sounded trumpets, and all the Israelites were standing.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 7, 'Then Solomon consecrated the middle of the courtyard in front of the house of the LORD, and there he offered the burnt offerings and the fat of the peace offerings, since the bronze altar he had made could not contain all these offerings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 8, 'So at that time Solomon and all Israel with him—a very great assembly of people from Lebo-hamath to the Brook of Egypt—kept the feast for seven days.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 9, 'On the eighth day they held a solemn assembly, for the dedication of the altar had lasted seven days, and the feast seven days more.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 10, 'On the twenty-third day of the seventh month, Solomon sent the people away to their homes, joyful and glad of heart for the good things that the LORD had done for David, for Solomon, and for His people Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 11, 'When Solomon had finished the house of the LORD and the royal palace, successfully carrying out all that was in his heart to do for the house of the LORD and for his own palace,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 12, 'the LORD appeared to him at night and said to him: “I have heard your prayer and have chosen this place for Myself as a house of sacrifice.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 13, 'If I close the sky so there is no rain, or if I command the locust to devour the land, or if I send a plague among My people,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 14, 'and if My people who are called by My name humble themselves and pray and seek My face and turn from their wicked ways, then I will hear from heaven, forgive their sin, and heal their land.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 15, 'Now My eyes will be open and My ears attentive to the prayers offered in this place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 16, 'For I have now chosen and consecrated this temple so that My Name may be there forever. My eyes and My heart will be there for all time.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 17, 'And as for you, if you walk before Me as your father David walked, doing all I have commanded you, and if you keep My statutes and ordinances,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 18, 'then I will establish your royal throne, as I covenanted with your father David when I said, ‘You will never fail to have a man to rule over Israel.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 19, 'But if you turn away and forsake the statutes and commandments I have set before you, and if you go off to serve and worship other gods,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 20, 'then I will uproot Israel from the soil I have given them, and I will banish from My presence this temple I have sanctified for My Name. I will make it an object of scorn and ridicule among all the peoples.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 21, 'And when this temple has become a heap of rubble, all who pass by it will be appalled and say, ‘Why has the LORD done such a thing to this land and to this temple?’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 7, 22, 'And others will answer, ‘Because they have forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers, who brought them out of the land of Egypt, and have embraced other gods, worshiping and serving them—because of this, He has brought all this disaster upon them.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 1, 'Now at the end of the twenty years during which Solomon had built the house of the LORD and his own palace,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 2, 'Solomon rebuilt the cities Hiram had given him and settled Israelites there.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 3, 'Then Solomon went to Hamath-zobah and captured it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 4, 'He built Tadmor in the wilderness, in addition to all the store cities that he had built in Hamath.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 5, 'He rebuilt Upper and Lower Beth-horon as fortified cities with walls, gates, and bars,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 6, 'as well as Baalath, all the store cities that belonged to Solomon, and all the cities for his chariots and horses—whatever he desired to build in Jerusalem, Lebanon, and throughout the land of his dominion.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 7, 'As for all the people who remained of the Hittites, Amorites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites (the people who were not Israelites)—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 8, 'their descendants who remained in the land, those whom the Israelites were unable to destroy—Solomon conscripted these people to be forced laborers, as they are to this day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 9, 'But Solomon did not consign any of the Israelites to slave labor, because they were his men of war, his officers and captains, and the commanders of his chariots and cavalry.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 10, 'They were also the chief officers for King Solomon: 250 supervisors.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 11, 'Solomon brought the daughter of Pharaoh up from the City of David to the palace he had built for her. For he said, “My wife must not live in the house of David king of Israel, because the places the ark of the LORD has entered are holy.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 12, 'At that time Solomon offered burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of the LORD he had built in front of the portico.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 13, 'He observed the daily requirement for offerings according to the commandment of Moses for Sabbaths, New Moons, and the three annual appointed feasts—the Feast of Unleavened Bread, the Feast of Weeks, and the Feast of Tabernacles.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 14, 'In keeping with the ordinances of his father David, Solomon appointed the divisions of the priests over their service, and the Levites for their duties to offer praise and to minister before the priests according to the daily requirement. He also appointed gatekeepers by their divisions at each gate, for this had been the command of David, the man of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 15, 'They did not turn aside from the king’s command regarding the priests or the Levites or any matter concerning the treasuries.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 16, 'Thus all the work of Solomon was carried out, from the day the foundation was laid for the house of the LORD until it was finished. So the house of the LORD was completed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 17, 'Then Solomon went to Ezion-geber and to Eloth on the coast of Edom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 8, 18, 'So Hiram sent him ships captained by his servants, along with crews of experienced sailors. They went with Solomon’s servants to Ophir and acquired from there 450 talents of gold, which they delivered to King Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 1, 'Now when the queen of Sheba heard about the fame of Solomon, she came to test him with difficult questions. She arrived in Jerusalem with a very large caravan—with camels bearing spices, gold in abundance, and precious stones. So she came to Solomon and spoke with him about all that was on her mind.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 2, 'And Solomon answered all her questions; nothing was too difficult for him to explain.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 3, 'When the queen of Sheba saw the wisdom of Solomon, the palace he had built,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 4, 'the food at his table, the seating of his servants, the service and attire of his attendants and cupbearers, and the burnt offerings he presented at the house of the LORD, it took her breath away.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 5, 'She said to the king, “The report I heard in my own country about your words and wisdom is true.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 6, 'But I did not believe the reports until I came and saw with my own eyes. Indeed, not half of the greatness of your wisdom was told to me. You have far exceeded the report I heard.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 7, 'How blessed are your men! How blessed are these servants of yours who stand continually before you and hear your wisdom!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 8, 'Blessed be the LORD your God, who has delighted in you to set you on His throne to be king for the LORD your God. Because your God loved Israel enough to establish them forever, He has made you king over them to carry out justice and righteousness.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 9, 'Then she gave the king 120 talents of gold, a great quantity of spices, and precious stones. There had never been such spices as those the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 10, '(The servants of Hiram and of Solomon who brought gold from Ophir also brought algum wood and precious stones.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 11, 'The king made the algum wood into steps for the house of the LORD and for the king’s palace, and into lyres and harps for the singers. Never before had anything like them been seen in the land of Judah.)'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 12, 'King Solomon gave the queen of Sheba all she desired—whatever she asked—far more than she had brought the king. Then she left and returned to her own country, along with her servants.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 13, 'The weight of gold that came to Solomon each year was 666 talents,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 14, 'not including the revenue from the merchants and traders. And all the Arabian kings and governors of the land also brought gold and silver to Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 15, 'King Solomon made two hundred large shields of hammered gold; six hundred shekels of hammered gold went into each shield.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 16, 'He also made three hundred small shields of hammered gold; three hundred shekels of gold went into each shield. And the king put them in the House of the Forest of Lebanon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 17, 'Additionally, the king made a great throne of ivory and overlaid it with pure gold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 18, 'The throne had six steps, and a footstool of gold was attached to it. There were armrests on both sides of the seat, with a lion standing beside each armrest.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 19, 'Twelve lions stood on the six steps, one at either end of each step. Nothing like this had ever been made for any kingdom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 20, 'All King Solomon’s drinking cups were gold, and all the utensils of the House of the Forest of Lebanon were pure gold. There was no silver, because it was accounted as nothing in the days of Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 21, 'For the king had the ships of Tarshish that went with Hiram’s servants, and once every three years the ships of Tarshish would arrive bearing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 22, 'So King Solomon surpassed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 23, 'All the kings of the earth sought an audience with Solomon to hear the wisdom that God had put in his heart.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 24, 'Year after year, each visitor would bring his tribute: articles of silver and gold, clothing, weapons, spices, horses, and mules.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 25, 'Solomon had 4,000 stalls for horses and chariots, and 12,000 horses, which he stationed in the chariot cities and also with him in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 26, 'He reigned over all the kings from the Euphrates to the land of the Philistines, as far as the border of Egypt.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 27, 'The king made silver as common in Jerusalem as stones, and cedar as abundant as sycamore in the foothills.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 28, 'Solomon’s horses were imported from Egypt and from all the lands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 29, 'As for the rest of the acts of Solomon, from beginning to end, are they not written in the Records of Nathan the Prophet, in the Prophecy of Ahijah the Shilonite, and in the Visions of Iddo the Seer concerning Jeroboam son of Nebat?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 30, 'Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel forty years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 9, 31, 'And Solomon rested with his fathers and was buried in the city of his father David. And his son Rehoboam reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 1, 'Then Rehoboam went to Shechem, for all Israel had gone there to make him king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 2, 'When Jeroboam son of Nebat heard about this, he returned from Egypt, where he had fled from King Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 3, 'So they sent for Jeroboam, and he and all Israel came to Rehoboam and said,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 4, '“Your father put a heavy yoke on us. But now you should lighten the burden of your father’s service and the heavy yoke he put on us, and we will serve you.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 5, 'Rehoboam answered, “Come back to me in three days.” So the people departed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 6, 'Then King Rehoboam consulted with the elders who had served his father Solomon during his lifetime. “How do you advise me to respond to these people?” he asked.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 7, 'They replied, “If you will be kind to these people and please them by speaking kind words to them, they will be your servants forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 8, 'But Rehoboam rejected the advice of the elders; instead, he consulted the young men who had grown up with him and served him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 9, 'He asked them, “What message do you advise that we send back to these people who have spoken to me, saying, ‘Lighten the yoke your father put on us’?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 10, 'The young men who had grown up with him replied, “This is how you should answer these people who said to you, ‘Your father made our yoke heavy, but you should make it lighter.’ This is what you should tell them: ‘My little finger is thicker than my father’s waist!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 11, 'Whereas my father burdened you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke. Whereas my father scourged you with whips, I will scourge you with scorpions.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 12, 'After three days, Jeroboam and all the people returned to Rehoboam, since the king had said, “Come back to me on the third day.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 13, 'And the king answered them harshly. King Rehoboam rejected the advice of the elders'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 14, 'and spoke to them as the young men had advised, saying, “Whereas my father made your yoke heavy, I will add to your yoke. Whereas my father scourged you with whips, I will scourge you with scorpions.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 15, 'So the king did not listen to the people, and indeed this turn of events was from God, in order that the LORD might fulfill the word that He had spoken through Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam son of Nebat.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 16, 'When all Israel saw that the king had refused to listen to them, they answered the king: “What portion do we have in David, and what inheritance in the son of Jesse? To your tents, O Israel! Look now to your own house, O David!” So all the Israelites went home,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 17, 'but Rehoboam still reigned over the Israelites living in the cities of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 18, 'Then King Rehoboam sent out Hadoram, who was in charge of the forced labor, but the Israelites stoned him to death. And King Rehoboam mounted his chariot in haste and escaped to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 10, 19, 'So to this day Israel has been in rebellion against the house of David.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 1, 'When Rehoboam arrived in Jerusalem, he mobilized the house of Judah and Benjamin—180,000 chosen warriors—to fight against Israel and restore the kingdom to Rehoboam.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 2, 'But the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah the man of God:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 3, '“Tell Rehoboam son of Solomon king of Judah and all the Israelites in Judah and Benjamin'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 4, 'that this is what the LORD says: ‘You are not to go up and fight against your brothers. Each of you must return home, for this word is from Me.’” So they listened to the words of the LORD and turned back from going against Jeroboam.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 5, 'Rehoboam continued to live in Jerusalem, and he built up cities for defense in Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 6, 'He built up Bethlehem, Etam, Tekoa,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 7, 'Beth-zur, Soco, Adullam,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 8, 'Gath, Mareshah, Ziph,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 9, 'Adoraim, Lachish, Azekah,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 10, 'Zorah, Aijalon, and Hebron, the fortified cities in Judah and Benjamin.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 11, 'He strengthened their fortresses and put officers in them, with supplies of food, oil, and wine.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 12, 'He also put shields and spears in all the cities and strengthened them greatly. So Judah and Benjamin belonged to him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 13, 'Moreover, the priests and Levites from all their districts throughout Israel stood with Rehoboam.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 14, 'For the Levites left their pasturelands and their possessions and went to Judah and Jerusalem, because Jeroboam and his sons had rejected them as priests of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 15, 'And Jeroboam appointed his own priests for the high places and for the goat demons and calf idols he had made.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 16, 'Those from every tribe of Israel who had set their hearts to seek the LORD their God followed the Levites to Jerusalem to sacrifice to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 17, 'So they strengthened the kingdom of Judah and supported Rehoboam son of Solomon for three years, because they walked for three years in the way of David and Solomon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 18, 'And Rehoboam married Mahalath, who was the daughter of David’s son Jerimoth and of Abihail, the daughter of Jesse’s son Eliab.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 19, 'She bore sons to him: Jeush, Shemariah, and Zaham.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 20, 'After her, he married Maacah daughter of Absalom, and she bore to him Abijah, Attai, Ziza, and Shelomith.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 21, 'Rehoboam loved Maacah daughter of Absalom more than all his wives and concubines. In all, he had eighteen wives and sixty concubines, and he was the father of twenty-eight sons and sixty daughters.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 22, 'Rehoboam appointed Abijah son of Maacah as chief prince among his brothers, intending to make him king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 11, 23, 'Rehoboam also acted wisely by dispersing some of his sons throughout the districts of Judah and Benjamin, and to all the fortified cities. He gave them abundant provisions and sought many wives for them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 1, 'After Rehoboam had established his sovereignty and royal power, he and all Israel with him forsook the Law of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 2, 'In the fifth year of Rehoboam’s reign, because they had been unfaithful to the LORD, Shishak king of Egypt came up and attacked Jerusalem'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 3, 'with 1,200 chariots, 60,000 horsemen, and countless troops who came with him out of Egypt—Libyans, Sukkites, and Cushites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 4, 'He captured the fortified cities of Judah and came as far as Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 5, 'Then Shemaiah the prophet came to Rehoboam and the leaders of Judah who had gathered at Jerusalem because of Shishak, and he said to them, “This is what the LORD says: ‘You have forsaken Me; therefore, I have forsaken you into the hand of Shishak.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 6, 'So the leaders of Israel and the king humbled themselves and said, “The LORD is righteous.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 7, 'When the LORD saw that they had humbled themselves, the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah, saying, “They have humbled themselves; I will not destroy them, but will soon grant them deliverance. My wrath will not be poured out on Jerusalem through Shishak.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 8, 'Nevertheless, they will become his servants, so that they may learn the difference between serving Me and serving the kings of other lands.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 9, 'So King Shishak of Egypt attacked Jerusalem and seized the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the royal palace. He took everything, including the gold shields that Solomon had made.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 10, 'Then King Rehoboam made bronze shields in their place and committed them to the care of the captains of the guard on duty at the entrance to the royal palace.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 11, 'And whenever the king entered the house of the LORD, the guards would go with him, bearing the shields, and later they would return them to the guardroom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 12, 'Because Rehoboam humbled himself, the anger of the LORD turned away from him, and He did not destroy him completely. Indeed, conditions were good in Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 13, 'Thus King Rehoboam established himself in Jerusalem. He was forty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city the LORD had chosen from all the tribes of Israel in which to put His Name. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonite.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 14, 'And Rehoboam did evil because he did not set his heart to seek the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 15, 'Now the acts of Rehoboam, from first to last, are they not written in the records of Shemaiah the Prophet and of Iddo the Seer concerning the genealogies? There was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam throughout their days.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 12, 16, 'And Rehoboam rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David. And his son Abijah reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 1, 'In the eighteenth year of Jeroboam’s reign, Abijah became king of Judah,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 2, 'and he reigned in Jerusalem three years. His mother’s name was Micaiah daughter of Uriel; she was from Gibeah. And there was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 3, 'Abijah went into battle with an army of 400,000 chosen men, while Jeroboam drew up in formation against him with 800,000 chosen and mighty men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 4, 'Then Abijah stood on Mount Zemaraim in the hill country of Ephraim and said, “Hear me, O Jeroboam and all Israel!'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 5, 'Do you not know that the LORD, the God of Israel, has given the kingship of Israel to David and his descendants forever by a covenant of salt?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 6, 'Yet Jeroboam son of Nebat, a servant of Solomon son of David, rose up and rebelled against his master.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 7, 'Then worthless and wicked men gathered around him to resist Rehoboam son of Solomon when he was young, inexperienced, and unable to resist them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 8, 'And now you think you can resist the kingdom of the LORD, which is in the hands of David’s descendants. You are indeed a vast army, and you have with you the golden calves that Jeroboam made for you as gods.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 9, 'But did you not drive out the priests of the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites? And did you not make priests for yourselves as do the peoples of other lands? Now whoever comes to consecrate himself with a young bull and seven rams can become a priest of things that are not gods.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 10, 'But as for us, the LORD is our God. We have not forsaken Him; the priests who minister to the LORD are sons of Aaron, and the Levites attend to their duties.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 11, 'Every morning and every evening they present burnt offerings and fragrant incense to the LORD. They set out the rows of showbread on the ceremonially clean table, and every evening they light the lamps of the gold lampstand. We are carrying out the requirements of the LORD our God, while you have forsaken Him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 12, 'Now behold, God Himself is with us as our head, and His priests with their trumpets sound the battle call against you. O children of Israel, do not fight against the LORD, the God of your fathers, for you will not succeed.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 13, 'Now Jeroboam had sent troops around to ambush from the rear, so that while he was in front of Judah, the ambush was behind them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 14, 'When Judah turned and discovered that the battle was both before and behind them, they cried out to the LORD. Then the priests blew the trumpets,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 15, 'and the men of Judah raised the battle cry. And when they raised the cry, God routed Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 16, 'So the Israelites fled before Judah, and God delivered them into their hands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 17, 'Then Abijah and his people struck them with a mighty blow, and 500,000 chosen men of Israel fell slain.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 18, 'Thus the Israelites were subdued at that time, and the men of Judah prevailed because they relied on the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 19, 'Abijah pursued Jeroboam and captured some cities from him: Bethel, Jeshanah, and Ephron, along with their villages.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 20, 'Jeroboam did not again recover his power during the days of Abijah, and the LORD struck him down and he died.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 21, 'But Abijah grew strong, married fourteen wives, and became the father of twenty-two sons and sixteen daughters.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 13, 22, 'Now the rest of the acts of Abijah, along with his ways and his words, are written in the Treatise of the Prophet Iddo.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 1, 'Then Abijah rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David. And his son Asa reigned in his place, and in his days the land was at peace for ten years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 2, 'And Asa did what was good and right in the eyes of the LORD his God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 3, 'He removed the foreign altars and high places, shattered the sacred pillars, and chopped down the Asherah poles.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 4, 'He commanded the people of Judah to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, and to observe the law and the commandments.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 5, 'He also removed the high places and incense altars from all the cities of Judah, and under him the kingdom was at peace.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 6, 'Because the land was at peace, Asa built fortified cities in Judah. In those days no one made war with him, because the LORD had given him rest.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 7, 'So he said to the people of Judah, “Let us build these cities and surround them with walls and towers, with doors and bars. The land is still ours because we have sought the LORD our God. We have sought Him and He has given us rest on every side.” So they built and prospered.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 8, 'Asa had an army of 300,000 men from Judah bearing large shields and spears, and 280,000 men from Benjamin bearing small shields and drawing the bow. All these were mighty men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 9, 'Then Zerah the Cushite came against them with an army of 1,000,000 men and 300 chariots, and they advanced as far as Mareshah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 10, 'So Asa marched out against him and lined up in battle formation in the Valley of Zephathah near Mareshah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 11, 'Then Asa cried out to the LORD his God: “O LORD, there is no one besides You to help the powerless against the mighty. Help us, O LORD our God, for we rely on You, and in Your name we have come against this multitude. O LORD, You are our God. Do not let a mere mortal prevail against You.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 12, 'So the LORD struck down the Cushites before Asa and Judah, and the Cushites fled.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 13, 'Then Asa and his army pursued them as far as Gerar. The Cushites fell and could not recover, for they were crushed before the LORD and His army. So the people of Judah carried off a great amount of plunder'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 14, 'and attacked all the cities around Gerar, because the terror of the LORD had fallen upon them. They plundered all the cities, since there was much plunder there.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 14, 15, 'They also attacked the tents of the herdsmen and carried off many sheep and camels. Then they returned to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 1, 'Now the Spirit of God came upon Azariah son of Oded.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 2, 'So he went out to meet Asa and said to him, “Listen to me, Asa and all Judah and Benjamin. The LORD is with you when you are with Him. If you seek Him, He will be found by you, but if you forsake Him, He will forsake you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 3, 'For many years Israel has been without the true God, without a priest to instruct them, and without the law.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 4, 'But in their distress they turned to the LORD, the God of Israel, and sought Him, and He was found by them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 5, 'In those days there was no safety for travelers, because the residents of the lands had many conflicts.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 6, 'Nation was crushed by nation, and city by city, for God afflicted them with all kinds of adversity.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 7, 'But as for you, be strong; do not be discouraged, for your work will be rewarded.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 8, 'When Asa heard these words and the prophecy of Azariah son of Oded the prophet, he took courage and removed the detestable idols from the whole land of Judah and Benjamin and from the cities he had captured in the hill country of Ephraim. He then restored the altar of the LORD that was in front of the portico of the LORD’s temple.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 9, 'And he assembled all Judah and Benjamin, along with those from the tribes of Ephraim, Manasseh, and Simeon who had settled among them, for great numbers had come over to him from Israel when they saw that the LORD his God was with him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 10, 'So they gathered together in Jerusalem in the third month of the fifteenth year of Asa’s reign.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 11, 'At that time they sacrificed to the LORD seven hundred oxen and seven thousand sheep from all the plunder they had brought back.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 12, 'Then they entered into a covenant to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, with all their heart and soul.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 13, 'And whoever would not seek the LORD, the God of Israel, would be put to death, whether young or old, man or woman.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 14, 'They took an oath to the LORD with a loud voice, with shouting, trumpets, and rams’ horns.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 15, 'And all Judah rejoiced over the oath, for they had sworn it with all their heart. They had sought Him earnestly, and He was found by them. So the LORD gave them rest on every side.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 16, 'King Asa also removed his grandmother Maacah from her position as queen mother because she had made a detestable Asherah pole. Asa chopped down the pole, crushed it, and burned it in the Kidron Valley.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 17, 'The high places were not removed from Israel, but Asa’s heart was fully devoted all his days.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 18, 'And he brought into the house of God the silver and gold articles that he and his father had dedicated.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 15, 19, 'And there was no war until the thirty-fifth year of Asa’s reign.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 1, 'In the thirty-sixth year of Asa’s reign, Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah and fortified Ramah to prevent anyone from leaving or entering the territory of Asa king of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 2, 'So Asa withdrew the silver and gold from the treasuries of the house of the LORD and the royal palace, and he sent it with this message to Ben-hadad king of Aram, who was ruling in Damascus:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 3, '“Let there be a treaty between me and you, between my father and your father. See, I have sent you silver and gold. Now go and break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, so that he will withdraw from me.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 4, 'And Ben-hadad listened to King Asa and sent the commanders of his armies against the cities of Israel, conquering Ijon, Dan, Abel-maim, and all the store cities of Naphtali.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 5, 'When Baasha learned of this, he stopped fortifying Ramah and abandoned his work.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 6, 'Then King Asa brought all the men of Judah, and they carried away the stones of Ramah and the timbers Baasha had used for building. And with these materials he built up Geba and Mizpah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 7, 'At that time Hanani the seer came to King Asa of Judah and told him, “Because you have relied on the king of Aram and not on the LORD your God, the army of the king of Aram has escaped from your hand.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 8, 'Were not the Cushites and Libyans a vast army with many chariots and horsemen? Yet because you relied on the LORD, He delivered them into your hand.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 9, 'For the eyes of the LORD roam to and fro over all the earth, to show Himself strong on behalf of those whose hearts are fully devoted to Him. You have acted foolishly in this matter. From now on, therefore, you will be at war.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 10, 'Asa was angry with the seer and became so enraged over this matter that he put the man in prison. And at the same time Asa oppressed some of the people.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 11, 'Now the rest of the acts of Asa, from beginning to end, are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 12, 'In the thirty-ninth year of his reign, Asa became diseased in his feet, and his malady became increasingly severe. Yet even in his illness he did not seek the LORD, but only the physicians.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 13, 'So in the forty-first year of his reign, Asa died and rested with his fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 16, 14, 'And he was buried in the tomb that he had cut out for himself in the City of David. They laid him on a bier that was full of spices and various blended perfumes; then they made a great fire in his honor.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 1, 'Asa’s son Jehoshaphat reigned in his place, and he strengthened himself against Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 2, 'He stationed troops in every fortified city of Judah and put garrisons in the land of Judah and in the cities of Ephraim that his father Asa had captured.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 3, 'Now the LORD was with Jehoshaphat because he walked in the earlier ways of his father David. He did not seek out the Baals,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 4, 'but he sought the God of his father and walked by His commandments rather than the practices of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 5, 'So the LORD established the kingdom in his hand, and all Judah brought him tribute, so that he had an abundance of riches and honor.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 6, 'And his heart took delight in the ways of the LORD; furthermore, he removed the high places and Asherah poles from Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 7, 'In the third year of his reign, Jehoshaphat sent his officials Ben-hail, Obadiah, Zechariah, Nethanel, and Micaiah to teach in the cities of Judah,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 8, 'accompanied by certain Levites—Shemaiah, Nethaniah, Zebadiah, Asahel, Shemiramoth, Jehonathan, Adonijah, Tobijah, and Tob-adonijah—along with the priests Elishama and Jehoram.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 9, 'They taught throughout Judah, taking with them the Book of the Law of the LORD. They went throughout the towns of Judah and taught the people.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 10, 'And the dread of the LORD fell upon all the kingdoms of the lands that surrounded Judah, so that they did not make war against Jehoshaphat.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 11, 'Some Philistines also brought gifts and silver as tribute to Jehoshaphat, and the Arabs brought him 7,700 rams and 7,700 goats from their flocks.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 12, 'Jehoshaphat grew stronger and stronger, and he built fortresses and store cities in Judah'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 13, 'and kept vast supplies in the cities of Judah. He also had warriors in Jerusalem who were mighty men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 14, 'These are their numbers according to the houses of their fathers: From Judah, the commanders of thousands: Adnah the commander, and with him 300,000 mighty men of valor;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 15, 'next to him, Jehohanan the commander, and with him 280,000;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 16, 'and next to him, Amasiah son of Zichri, the volunteer for the LORD, and with him 200,000 mighty men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 17, 'From Benjamin: Eliada, a mighty man of valor, and with him 200,000 armed with bows and shields;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 18, 'and next to him, Jehozabad, and with him 180,000 armed for battle.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 17, 19, 'These were the men who served the king, besides those he stationed in the fortified cities throughout Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 1, 'Now Jehoshaphat had riches and honor in abundance, and he allied himself with Ahab by marriage.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 2, 'And some years later he went down to visit Ahab in Samaria, where Ahab sacrificed many sheep and cattle for him and the people with him, and urged him to march up to Ramoth-gilead.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 3, 'Ahab king of Israel asked Jehoshaphat king of Judah, “Will you go with me against Ramoth-gilead?” And Jehoshaphat replied, “I am like you, and my people are your people; we will join you in the war.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 4, 'But Jehoshaphat also said to the king of Israel, “Please inquire first for the word of the LORD.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 5, 'So the king of Israel assembled the prophets, four hundred men, and asked them, “Should we go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should we refrain?” “Go up,” they replied, “and God will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 6, 'But Jehoshaphat asked, “Is there not still a prophet of the LORD here of whom we can inquire?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 7, 'The king of Israel answered, “There is still one man who can ask the LORD, but I hate him because he never prophesies anything good for me, but only bad. He is Micaiah son of Imlah.” “The king should not say that!” Jehoshaphat replied.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 8, 'So the king of Israel called one of his officials and said, “Bring Micaiah son of Imlah at once.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 9, 'Dressed in royal attire, the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah were sitting on their thrones at the threshing floor by the entrance of the gate of Samaria, with all the prophets prophesying before them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 10, 'Now Zedekiah son of Chenaanah had made for himself iron horns and declared, “This is what the LORD says: ‘With these you shall gore the Arameans until they are finished off.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 11, 'And all the prophets were prophesying the same, saying, “Go up to Ramoth-gilead and prosper, for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 12, 'Then the messenger who had gone to call Micaiah instructed him, “Behold, with one accord the words of the prophets are favorable to the king. So please let your words be like theirs, and speak favorably.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 13, 'But Micaiah said, “As surely as the LORD lives, I will speak whatever my God tells me.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 14, 'When Micaiah arrived, the king asked him, “Micaiah, should we go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should we refrain?” “Go up and triumph,” Micaiah replied, “for they will be given into your hand.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 15, 'But the king said to him, “How many times must I make you swear not to tell me anything but the truth in the name of the LORD?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 16, 'So Micaiah declared: “I saw all Israel scattered on the hills like sheep without a shepherd. And the LORD said, ‘These people have no master; let each one return home in peace.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 17, 'Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “Did I not tell you that he never prophesies good for me, but only bad?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 18, 'Micaiah continued, “Therefore hear the word of the LORD: I saw the LORD sitting on His throne, and all the host of heaven standing on His right and on His left.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 19, 'And the LORD said, ‘Who will entice Ahab king of Israel to march up and fall at Ramoth-gilead?’ And one suggested this, and another that.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 20, 'Then a spirit came forward, stood before the LORD, and said, ‘I will entice him.’ ‘By what means?’ asked the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 21, 'And he replied, ‘I will go out and be a lying spirit in the mouths of all his prophets.’ ‘You will surely entice him and prevail,’ said the LORD. ‘Go and do it.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 22, 'So you see, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouths of these prophets of yours, and the LORD has pronounced disaster against you.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 23, 'Then Zedekiah son of Chenaanah went up, struck Micaiah in the face, and demanded, “Which way did the Spirit of the LORD go when He departed from me to speak with you?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 24, 'Micaiah replied, “You will soon see, on that day when you go and hide in an inner room.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 25, 'And the king of Israel declared, “Take Micaiah and return him to Amon the governor of the city and to Joash the king’s son,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 26, 'and tell them that this is what the king says: ‘Put this man in prison and feed him only bread and water until I return safely.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 27, 'But Micaiah replied, “If you ever return safely, the LORD has not spoken through me.” Then he added, “Take heed, all you people!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 28, 'So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah went up to Ramoth-gilead.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 29, 'And the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “I will disguise myself and go into battle, but you wear your royal robes.” So the king of Israel disguised himself and went into battle.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 30, 'Now the king of Aram had ordered his chariot commanders, “Do not fight with anyone, small or great, except the king of Israel.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 31, 'When the chariot commanders saw Jehoshaphat, they said, “This is the king of Israel!” So they turned to fight against him, but Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD helped him. God drew them away from him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 32, 'And when the chariot commanders saw that he was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 33, 'However, a certain man drew his bow without taking special aim, and he struck the king of Israel between the joints of his armor. So the king said to his charioteer, “Turn around and take me out of the battle, for I am badly wounded!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 18, 34, 'The battle raged throughout that day, and the king of Israel propped himself up in his chariot facing the Arameans until evening. And at sunset he died.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 1, 'When Jehoshaphat king of Judah had returned safely to his home in Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 2, 'Jehu son of Hanani the seer went out to confront him and said to King Jehoshaphat, “Should you help the wicked and love those who hate the LORD? Because of this, the wrath of the LORD is upon you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 3, 'However, some good is found in you, for you have removed the Asherah poles from the land and have set your heart on seeking God.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 4, 'Jehoshaphat lived in Jerusalem, and once again he went out among the people from Beersheba to the hill country of Ephraim and turned them back to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 5, 'He appointed judges in the land, in each of the fortified cities of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 6, 'Then he said to the judges, “Consider carefully what you do, for you are not judging for man, but for the LORD, who is with you when you render judgment.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 7, 'And now, may the fear of the LORD be upon you. Be careful what you do, for with the LORD our God there is no injustice or partiality or bribery.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 8, 'Moreover, Jehoshaphat appointed in Jerusalem some of the Levites, priests, and heads of the Israelite families to judge on behalf of the LORD and to settle disputes. And they lived in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 9, 'He commanded them, saying, “You must serve faithfully and wholeheartedly in the fear of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 10, 'For every dispute that comes before you from your brothers who dwell in their cities—whether it regards bloodshed or some other violation of law, commandments, statutes, or ordinances—you are to warn them, so that they will not incur guilt before the LORD and wrath will not come upon you and your brothers. Do this, and you will not incur guilt.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 19, 11, 'Note that Amariah, the chief priest, will be over you in all that pertains to the LORD, and Zebadiah son of Ishmael, the ruler of the house of Judah, in all that pertains to the king. And the Levites will serve as officers before you. Act resolutely; may the LORD be with the upright!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 1, 'After this, the Moabites and Ammonites, together with some of the Meunites, came to make war against Jehoshaphat.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 2, 'Then some men came and told Jehoshaphat, “A vast army is coming against you from Edom, from beyond the Sea; they are already in Hazazon-tamar” (that is, En-gedi).'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 3, 'Jehoshaphat was alarmed and set his face to seek the LORD. And he proclaimed a fast throughout Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 4, 'So the people of Judah gathered to seek the LORD, and indeed, they came from all the cities of Judah to seek Him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 5, 'Then Jehoshaphat stood in the assembly of Judah and Jerusalem in the house of the LORD in front of the new courtyard'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 6, 'and said, “O LORD, God of our fathers, are You not the God who is in heaven, and do You not rule over all the kingdoms of the nations? Power and might are in Your hand, and no one can stand against You.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 7, 'Our God, did You not drive out the inhabitants of this land before Your people Israel and give it forever to the descendants of Abraham Your friend?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 8, 'They have lived in the land and have built in it a sanctuary for Your Name, saying,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 9, '‘If disaster comes upon us—whether sword or judgment, plague or famine—we will stand before this temple and before You, for Your Name is in this temple. We will cry out to You in our distress, and You will hear us and save us.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 10, 'And now, here are the men of Ammon, Moab, and Mount Seir, whom You did not let Israel invade when they came out of the land of Egypt; but Israel turned away from them and did not destroy them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 11, 'See how they are repaying us by coming to drive us out of the possession that You gave us as an inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 12, 'Our God, will You not judge them? For we are powerless before this vast army that comes against us. We do not know what to do, but our eyes are upon You.”');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 13, 'Meanwhile all the men of Judah, with their wives and children and little ones, were standing before the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 14, 'Then the Spirit of the LORD came upon Jahaziel son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, a Levite from Asaph’s descendants, as he stood in the midst of the assembly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 15, 'And he said, “Listen, all you people of Judah and Jerusalem! Listen, King Jehoshaphat! This is what the LORD says: ‘Do not be afraid or discouraged because of this vast army, for the battle does not belong to you, but to God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 16, 'Tomorrow you are to march down against them. You will see them coming up the Ascent of Ziz, and you will find them at the end of the valley facing the Wilderness of Jeruel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 17, 'You need not fight this battle. Take up your positions, stand firm, and see the salvation of the LORD on your behalf, O Judah and Jerusalem. Do not be afraid or discouraged. Go out and face them tomorrow, for the LORD is with you.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 18, 'Then Jehoshaphat bowed facedown, and all the people of Judah and Jerusalem fell down before the LORD to worship Him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 19, 'And the Levites from the Kohathites and Korahites stood up to praise the LORD, the God of Israel, shouting in a very loud voice.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 20, 'Early in the morning they got up and left for the Wilderness of Tekoa. As they set out, Jehoshaphat stood up and said, “Hear me, O people of Judah and Jerusalem. Believe in the LORD your God, and you will be upheld; believe in His prophets, and you will succeed.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 21, 'Then Jehoshaphat consulted with the people and appointed those who would sing to the LORD and praise the splendor of His holiness. As they went out before the army, they were singing: “Give thanks to the LORD, for His loving devotion endures forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 22, 'The moment they began their shouts and praises, the LORD set ambushes against the men of Ammon, Moab, and Mount Seir who had come against Judah, and they were defeated.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 23, 'The Ammonites and Moabites rose up against the inhabitants of Mount Seir, devoting them to destruction. And when they had made an end to the inhabitants of Seir, they helped to destroy one another.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 24, 'When the men of Judah came to a place overlooking the wilderness, they looked for the vast army, but there were only corpses lying on the ground; no one had escaped.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 25, 'Then Jehoshaphat and his people went to carry off the plunder, and they found on the bodies an abundance of goods and valuables—more than they could carry away. They were gathering the plunder for three days because there was so much.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 26, 'On the fourth day they assembled in the Valley of Beracah, where they blessed the LORD. Therefore that place is called the Valley of Beracah to this day.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 27, 'Then all the men of Judah and Jerusalem, with Jehoshaphat at their head, returned joyfully to Jerusalem, for the LORD had made them rejoice over their enemies.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 28, 'So they entered Jerusalem and went into the house of the LORD with harps, lyres, and trumpets.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 29, 'And the fear of God came upon all the kingdoms of the lands when they heard that the LORD had fought against the enemies of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 30, 'Then Jehoshaphat’s kingdom was at peace, for his God had given him rest on every side.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 31, 'So Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah. He was thirty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-five years. His mother’s name was Azubah daughter of Shilhi.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 32, 'And Jehoshaphat walked in the way of his father Asa and did not turn away from it; he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 33, 'The high places, however, were not removed; the people had not yet set their hearts on the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 34, 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, from beginning to end, they are indeed written in the Chronicles of Jehu son of Hanani, which are recorded in the Book of the Kings of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 35, 'Later, Jehoshaphat king of Judah made an alliance with Ahaziah king of Israel, who acted wickedly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 36, 'They agreed to make ships to go to Tarshish, and these were built in Ezion-geber.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 20, 37, 'Then Eliezer son of Dodavahu of Mareshah prophesied against Jehoshaphat, saying, “Because you have allied yourself with Ahaziah, the LORD has destroyed your works.” So the ships were wrecked and were unable to sail to Tarshish.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 1, 'And Jehoshaphat rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David. And his son Jehoram reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 2, 'Jehoram’s brothers, the sons of Jehoshaphat, were Azariah, Jehiel, Zechariah, Azariah, Michael, and Shephatiah; these were all sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 3, 'Their father had given them many gifts of silver and gold and precious things, as well as the fortified cities in Judah; but he gave the kingdom to Jehoram because he was the firstborn.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 4, 'When Jehoram had established himself over his father’s kingdom, he strengthened himself by putting to the sword all his brothers along with some of the princes of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 5, 'Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 6, 'And Jehoram walked in the ways of the kings of Israel, just as the house of Ahab had done. For he married a daughter of Ahab and did evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 7, 'Yet the LORD was unwilling to destroy the house of David, because of the covenant He had made with David, and since He had promised to maintain a lamp for David and his descendants forever.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 8, 'In the days of Jehoram, Edom rebelled against the hand of Judah and appointed their own king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 9, 'So Jehoram crossed into Edom with his officers and all his chariots. When the Edomites surrounded him and his chariot commanders, he rose up and attacked by night.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 10, 'So to this day Edom has been in rebellion against the hand of Judah. Likewise, Libnah rebelled against his rule at the same time, because Jehoram had forsaken the LORD, the God of his fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 11, 'Jehoram had also built high places on the hills of Judah; he had caused the people of Jerusalem to prostitute themselves and had led Judah astray.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 12, 'Then a letter came to Jehoram from Elijah the prophet, which stated: “This is what the LORD, the God of your father David, says: ‘You have not walked in the ways of your father Jehoshaphat or of Asa king of Judah,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 13, 'but you have walked in the ways of the kings of Israel and have caused Judah and the people of Jerusalem to prostitute themselves, just as the house of Ahab prostituted itself. You have also killed your brothers, your father’s family, who were better than you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 14, 'So behold, the LORD is about to strike your people, your sons, your wives, and all your possessions with a serious blow.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 15, 'And day after day you yourself will suffer from a severe illness, a disease of your bowels, until it causes your bowels to come out.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 16, 'Then the LORD stirred against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines and Arabs who lived near the Cushites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 17, 'So they went to war against Judah, invaded it, and carried off all the possessions found in the king’s palace, along with his sons and wives; not a son was left to him except Jehoahaz, his youngest.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 18, 'After all this, the LORD afflicted Jehoram with an incurable disease of the bowels.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 19, 'This continued day after day until two full years had passed. Finally, his intestines came out because of his disease, and he died in severe pain. And his people did not make a fire in his honor as they had done for his fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 21, 20, 'Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years. He died, to no one’s regret, and was buried in the City of David, but not in the tombs of the kings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 1, 'Then the people of Jerusalem made Ahaziah, the youngest son of Jehoram, king in his place, since the raiders who had come into the camp with the Arabs had killed all the older sons. So Ahaziah son of Jehoram became king of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 2, 'Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem one year. His mother’s name was Athaliah, the granddaughter of Omri.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 3, 'Ahaziah also walked in the ways of the house of Ahab, for his mother was his counselor in wickedness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 4, 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as the house of Ahab had done, for to his destruction they were his counselors after the death of his father.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 5, 'Ahaziah also followed their counsel and went with Joram son of Ahab king of Israel to fight against Hazael king of Aram at Ramoth-gilead. But the Arameans wounded Joram;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 6, 'so he returned to Jezreel to recover from the wounds they had inflicted on him at Ramah when he fought against Hazael king of Aram. Then Ahaziah son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to Jezreel to visit Joram son of Ahab, because Joram had been wounded.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 7, 'Ahaziah’s downfall came from God when he went to visit Joram. When Ahaziah arrived, he went out with Joram to meet Jehu son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to destroy the house of Ahab.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 8, 'So while Jehu was executing judgment on the house of Ahab, he found the rulers of Judah and the sons of Ahaziah’s brothers who were serving Ahaziah, and he killed them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 9, 'Then Jehu looked for Ahaziah, and Jehu’s soldiers captured him while he was hiding in Samaria. So Ahaziah was brought to Jehu and put to death. They buried him, for they said, “He is the grandson of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart.” So no one was left from the house of Ahaziah with the strength to rule the kingdom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 10, 'When Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she proceeded to annihilate all the royal heirs of the house of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 11, 'But Jehoshabeath daughter of King Jehoram took Joash son of Ahaziah and stole him away from among the sons of the king who were being murdered, and she put him and his nurse in a bedroom. Because Jehoshabeath, the daughter of King Jehoram and the wife of Jehoiada the priest, was Ahaziah’s sister, she hid Joash from Athaliah so that she could not kill him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 22, 12, 'And Joash remained hidden with them in the house of God for six years while Athaliah ruled the land.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 1, 'Then in the seventh year, Jehoiada strengthened himself and made a covenant with the commanders of hundreds—with Azariah son of Jeroham, Ishmael son of Jehohanan, Azariah son of Obed, Maaseiah son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat son of Zichri.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 2, 'So they went throughout Judah and gathered the Levites from all the cities of Judah and the heads of the families of Israel. And when they came to Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 3, 'the whole assembly made a covenant with the king in the house of God. “Behold, the king’s son!” said Jehoiada. “He must reign, just as the LORD promised concerning the descendants of David.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 4, 'This is what you are to do: A third of you priests and Levites who come on duty on the Sabbath shall keep watch at the doors,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 5, 'a third shall be at the royal palace, and a third at the Foundation Gate, while all the others are in the courtyards of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 6, 'No one is to enter the house of the LORD except the priests and those Levites who serve; they may enter because they are consecrated, but all the people are to obey the requirement of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 7, 'The Levites must surround the king with weapons in hand, and anyone who enters the temple must be put to death. You must stay close to the king wherever he goes.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 8, 'So the Levites and all Judah did everything that Jehoiada the priest had ordered. Each of them took his men—those coming on duty on the Sabbath and those going off duty—for Jehoiada the priest had not released any of the divisions.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 9, 'Then Jehoiada the priest gave to the commanders of hundreds the spears and the large and small shields of King David that were in the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 10, 'He stationed all the troops, with their weapons in hand, surrounding the king by the altar and the temple, from the south side to the north side of the temple.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 11, 'Then Jehoiada and his sons brought out the king’s son, put the crown on him, presented him with the Testimony, and proclaimed him king. They anointed him and shouted, “Long live the king!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 12, 'When Athaliah heard the noise of the people running and cheering the king, she went out to them in the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 13, 'And she looked out and saw the king standing by his pillar at the entrance. The officers and trumpeters were beside the king, and all the people of the land were rejoicing and blowing trumpets, while the singers with musical instruments were leading the praises. Then Athaliah tore her clothes and screamed, “Treason, treason!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 14, 'And Jehoiada the priest sent out the commanders of hundreds in charge of the army, saying, “Bring her out between the ranks, and put to the sword anyone who follows her.” For the priest had said, “She must not be put to death in the house of the LORD.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 15, 'So they seized Athaliah as she reached the entrance of the Horse Gate to the palace grounds, and there they put her to death.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 16, 'Then Jehoiada made a covenant between himself and the king and the people that they would be the LORD’s people.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 17, 'So all the people went to the temple of Baal and tore it down. They smashed the altars and idols to pieces and killed Mattan the priest of Baal in front of the altars.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 18, 'Moreover, Jehoiada put the oversight of the house of the LORD into the hands of the Levitical priests, whom David had appointed over the house of the LORD, to offer burnt offerings to the LORD as is written in the Law of Moses, with rejoicing and song, as ordained by David.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 19, 'He stationed gatekeepers at the gates of the house of the LORD, so that nothing unclean could enter for any reason.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 20, 'He also took with him the commanders of hundreds, the nobles, the rulers of the people, and all the people of the land, and they brought the king down from the house of the LORD and entered the royal palace through the Upper Gate. They seated King Joash on the royal throne,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 23, 21, 'and all the people of the land rejoiced. And the city was quiet, because Athaliah had been put to the sword.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 1, 'Joash was seven years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem forty years. His mother’s name was Zibiah; she was from Beersheba.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 2, 'And Joash did what was right in the eyes of the LORD all the days of Jehoiada the priest.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 3, 'Jehoiada took for him two wives, and he had sons and daughters.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 4, 'Some time later, Joash set his heart on repairing the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 5, 'So he gathered the priests and Levites and said, “Go out to the cities of Judah and collect the money due annually from all Israel, to repair the house of your God. Do it quickly.” The Levites, however, did not make haste.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 6, 'So the king called Jehoiada the high priest and said, “Why have you not required the Levites to bring from Judah and Jerusalem the tax imposed by Moses the servant of the LORD and by the assembly of Israel for the Tent of the Testimony?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 7, 'For the sons of that wicked woman Athaliah had broken into the house of God and had even used the sacred objects of the house of the LORD for the Baals.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 8, 'At the king’s command a chest was made and placed outside, at the gate of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 9, 'And a proclamation was issued in Judah and Jerusalem that they were to bring to the LORD the tax imposed by Moses the servant of God on Israel in the wilderness.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 10, 'All the officers and all the people rejoiced and brought their contributions, and they dropped them in the chest until it was full.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 11, 'Whenever the chest was brought by the Levites to the king’s overseers and they saw that there was a large amount of money, the royal scribe and the officer of the high priest would come and empty the chest and carry it back to its place. They did this daily and gathered the money in abundance.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 12, 'Then the king and Jehoiada would give the money to those who supervised the labor on the house of the LORD to hire stonecutters and carpenters to restore the house of the LORD, as well as workers in iron and bronze to repair the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 13, 'So the workmen labored, and in their hands the repair work progressed. They restored the house of God according to its specifications, and they reinforced it.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 14, 'When they were finished, they brought the rest of the money to the king and Jehoiada to make with it the articles for the house of the LORD—utensils for the service and for the burnt offerings, dishes, and other objects of gold and silver. Throughout the days of Jehoiada, burnt offerings were presented regularly in the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 15, 'When Jehoiada was old and full of years, he died at the age of 130.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 16, 'And Jehoiada was buried with the kings in the City of David, because he had done what was good in Israel for God and His temple.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 17, 'After the death of Jehoiada, however, the officials of Judah came and paid homage to the king, and he listened to them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 18, 'They abandoned the house of the LORD, the God of their fathers, and served the Asherah poles and idols. So wrath came upon Judah and Jerusalem for this guilt of theirs.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 19, 'Nevertheless, the LORD sent prophets to bring the people back to Him and to testify against them; but they would not listen.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 20, 'Then the Spirit of God came upon Zechariah son of Jehoiada the priest, who stood up before the people and said to them, “This is what God says: ‘Why do you transgress the commandments of the LORD so that you cannot prosper? Because you have forsaken the LORD, He has forsaken you.’”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 21, 'But they conspired against Zechariah, and by order of the king, they stoned him in the courtyard of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 22, 'Thus King Joash failed to remember the kindness that Zechariah’s father Jehoiada had extended to him. Instead, Joash killed Jehoiada’s son. As he lay dying, Zechariah said, “May the LORD see this and call you to account.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 23, 'In the spring, the army of Aram went to war against Joash. They entered Judah and Jerusalem and destroyed all the leaders of the people, and they sent all the plunder to their king in Damascus.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 24, 'Although the Aramean army had come with only a few men, the LORD delivered into their hand a very great army. Because Judah had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers, judgment was executed on Joash.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 25, 'And when the Arameans had withdrawn, they left Joash severely wounded. His own servants conspired against him for shedding the blood of the son of Jehoiada the priest, and they killed him on his bed. So he died and was buried in the City of David, but not in the tombs of the kings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 26, 'Those who conspired against Joash were Zabad son of Shimeath the Ammonitess and Jehozabad son of Shimrith the Moabitess.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 24, 27, 'The accounts of the sons of Joash, as well as the many pronouncements about him and about the restoration of the house of God, are indeed written in the Treatise of the Book of the Kings. And his son Amaziah reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 1, 'Amaziah was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-nine years. His mother’s name was Jehoaddan; she was from Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 2, 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, but not wholeheartedly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 3, 'As soon as the kingdom was firmly in his grasp, Amaziah executed the servants who had murdered his father the king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 4, 'Yet he did not put their sons to death, but acted according to what is written in the Law, in the Book of Moses, where the LORD commanded: “Fathers must not be put to death for their children, and children must not be put to death for their fathers; each is to die for his own sin.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 5, 'Then Amaziah gathered the people of Judah and assigned them according to their families to commanders of thousands and of hundreds. And he numbered those twenty years of age or older throughout Judah and Benjamin and found 300,000 chosen men able to serve in the army, bearing the spear and shield.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 6, 'He also hired 100,000 mighty warriors from Israel for a hundred talents of silver.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 7, 'But a man of God came to him and said, “O king, do not let the army of Israel go with you, for the LORD is not with Israel—not with any of the Ephraimites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 8, 'Even if you go and fight bravely in battle, God will make you stumble before the enemy, for God has power to help and power to overthrow.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 9, 'Amaziah asked the man of God, “What should I do about the hundred talents I have given to the army of Israel?” And the man of God replied, “The LORD is able to give you much more than this.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 10, 'So Amaziah dismissed the troops who had come to him from Ephraim and sent them home. And they were furious with Judah and returned home in great anger.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 11, 'Amaziah, however, summoned his strength and led his troops to the Valley of Salt, where he struck down 10,000 men of Seir,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 12, 'and the army of Judah also captured 10,000 men alive. They took them to the top of a cliff and threw them down so that all were dashed to pieces.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 13, 'Meanwhile the troops that Amaziah had dismissed from battle raided the cities of Judah, from Samaria to Beth-horon. They struck down 3,000 people and carried off a great deal of plunder.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 14, 'When Amaziah returned from the slaughter of the Edomites, he brought back the gods of the Seirites, set them up as his own gods, bowed before them, and burned sacrifices to them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 15, 'Therefore the anger of the LORD burned against Amaziah, and He sent him a prophet, who said, “Why have you sought this people’s gods, which could not deliver them from your hand?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 16, 'While he was still speaking, the king asked, “Have we made you the counselor to the king? Stop! Why be struck down?” So the prophet stopped, but he said, “I know that God has determined to destroy you, because you have done this and have not heeded my advice.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 17, 'Then Amaziah king of Judah took counsel and sent word to the king of Israel Jehoash son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu. “Come, let us meet face to face,” he said.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 18, 'But Jehoash king of Israel replied to Amaziah king of Judah: “A thistle in Lebanon sent a message to a cedar in Lebanon, saying, ‘Give your daughter to my son in marriage.’ Then a wild beast in Lebanon came along and trampled the thistle.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 19, 'You have said, ‘Look, I have defeated Edom,’ and your heart has become proud and boastful. Now stay at home. Why should you stir up trouble so that you fall—you and Judah with you?”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 20, 'But Amaziah would not listen, for this had come from God in order to deliver them into the hand of Jehoash, because they had sought the gods of Edom.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 21, 'So Jehoash king of Israel advanced, and he and Amaziah king of Judah faced each other at Beth-shemesh in Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 22, 'And Judah was routed before Israel, and every man fled to his own home.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 23, 'There at Beth-shemesh, Jehoash king of Israel captured Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash, the son of Jehoahaz. Then Jehoash brought him to Jerusalem and broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the Ephraim Gate to the Corner Gate—a section of four hundred cubits.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 24, 'He took all the gold and silver and all the articles found in the house of God with Obed-edom and in the treasuries of the royal palace, as well as some hostages. Then he returned to Samaria.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 25, 'Amaziah son of Joash king of Judah lived for fifteen years after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 26, 'As for the rest of the acts of Amaziah, from beginning to end, are they not written in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 27, 'From the time that Amaziah turned from following the LORD, a conspiracy was formed against him in Jerusalem, and he fled to Lachish. But men were sent after him to Lachish, and they killed him there.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 25, 28, 'They carried him back on horses and buried him with his fathers in the City of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 1, 'All the people of Judah took Uzziah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in place of his father Amaziah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 2, 'Uzziah was the one who rebuilt Eloth and restored it to Judah after King Amaziah rested with his fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 3, 'Uzziah was sixteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem fifty-two years. His mother’s name was Jecoliah; she was from Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 4, 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father Amaziah had done.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 5, 'He sought God throughout the days of Zechariah, who instructed him in the fear of God. And as long as he sought the LORD, God gave him success.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 6, 'Uzziah went out to wage war against the Philistines, and he tore down the walls of Gath, Jabneh, and Ashdod. Then he built cities near Ashdod and among the Philistines.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 7, 'God helped him against the Philistines, against the Arabs living in Gur-baal, and against the Meunites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 8, 'The Ammonites brought tribute to Uzziah, and his fame spread as far as the border of Egypt, for he had become exceedingly powerful.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 9, 'Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the Corner Gate, the Valley Gate, and the angle in the wall, and he fortified them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 10, 'Since he had much livestock in the foothills and in the plain, he built towers in the desert and dug many cisterns. And since he was a lover of the soil, he had farmers and vinedressers in the hill country and in the fertile fields.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 11, 'Uzziah had an army ready for battle that went out to war by assigned divisions, as recorded by Jeiel the scribe and Maaseiah the officer under the direction of Hananiah, one of the royal officers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 12, 'The total number of family leaders of the mighty men of valor was 2,600.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 13, 'Under their authority was an army of 307,500 trained for war, a powerful force to support the king against his enemies.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 14, 'Uzziah supplied the entire army with shields, spears, helmets, armor, bows, and slingstones.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 15, 'And in Jerusalem he made skillfully designed devices to shoot arrows and catapult large stones from the towers and corners. So his fame spread far and wide, for he was helped tremendously so that he became powerful.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 16, 'But when Uzziah grew powerful, his arrogance led to his own destruction. He was unfaithful to the LORD his God, for he entered the temple of the LORD to burn incense on the altar of incense.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 17, 'Then Azariah the priest, along with eighty brave priests of the LORD, went in after him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 18, 'They took their stand against King Uzziah and said, “Uzziah, you have no right to offer incense to the LORD. Only the priests, the descendants of Aaron, are consecrated to burn incense. Leave the sanctuary, for you have acted unfaithfully; you will not receive honor from the LORD God.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 19, 'Uzziah, with a censer in his hand to offer incense, was enraged. But while he raged against the priests in their presence in the house of the LORD before the altar of incense, leprosy broke out on his forehead.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 20, 'When Azariah the chief priest and all the priests turned to him and saw his leprous forehead, they rushed him out. Indeed, he himself hurried to get out, because the LORD had afflicted him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 21, 'So King Uzziah was a leper until the day of his death. He lived in isolation, leprous and cut off from the house of the LORD, while his son Jotham had charge of the royal palace to govern the people of the land.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 22, 'As for the rest of the acts of Uzziah, from beginning to end, they are recorded by the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 26, 23, 'And Uzziah rested with his fathers and was buried near them in a field of burial that belonged to the kings; for the people said, “He was a leper.” And his son Jotham reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 1, 'Jotham was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years. His mother’s name was Jerushah daughter of Zadok.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 2, 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father Uzziah had done. In addition, he did not enter the temple of the LORD. But the people still behaved corruptly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 3, 'Jotham rebuilt the Upper Gate of the house of the LORD, and he worked extensively on the wall at the hill of Ophel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 4, 'He also built cities in the hill country of Judah and fortresses and towers in the forests.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 5, 'Jotham waged war against the king of the Ammonites and defeated them, and that year they gave him a hundred talents of silver, ten thousand cors of wheat, and ten thousand cors of barley. They paid him the same in the second and third years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 6, 'So Jotham grew powerful because he ordered his ways before the LORD his God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 7, 'As for the rest of the acts of Jotham, along with all his wars and his ways, they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Israel and Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 8, 'He was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 27, 9, 'And Jotham rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David. And his son Ahaz reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 1, 'Ahaz was twenty years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years. And unlike David his father, he did not do what was right in the eyes of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 2, 'Instead, he walked in the ways of the kings of Israel and even made cast images of the Baals.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 3, 'Moreover, Ahaz burned incense in the Valley of Hinnom and sacrificed his sons in the fire, according to the abominations of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 4, 'And he sacrificed and burned incense on the high places, on the hills, and under every green tree.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 5, 'So the LORD his God delivered Ahaz into the hand of the king of Aram, who attacked him and took many captives to Damascus. Ahaz was also delivered into the hand of the king of Israel, who struck him with great force.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 6, 'For in one day Pekah son of Remaliah killed 120,000 valiant men in Judah. This happened because they had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 7, 'Zichri, a mighty man of Ephraim, killed Maaseiah the son of the king, Azrikam the governor of the palace, and Elkanah the second to the king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 8, 'Then the Israelites took 200,000 captives from their kinsmen—women, sons, and daughters. They also carried off a great deal of plunder and brought it to Samaria.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 9, 'But a prophet of the LORD named Oded was there, and he went out to meet the army that returned to Samaria. “Look,” he said to them, “because of His wrath against Judah, the LORD, the God of your fathers, has delivered them into your hand. But you have slaughtered them in a rage that reaches up to heaven.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 10, 'And now you intend to reduce to slavery the men and women of Judah and Jerusalem. But are you not also guilty before the LORD your God?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 11, 'Now therefore, listen to me and return the captives you took from your kinsmen, for the fierce anger of the LORD is upon you.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 12, 'Then some of the leaders of the Ephraimites—Azariah son of Jehohanan, Berechiah son of Meshillemoth, Jehizkiah son of Shallum, and Amasa son of Hadlai—stood in opposition to those arriving from the war.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 13, '“You must not bring the captives here,” they said, “for you are proposing to bring guilt upon us from the LORD and to add to our sins and our guilt. For our guilt is great, and fierce anger is upon Israel.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 14, 'So the armed men left the captives and the plunder before the leaders and all the assembly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 15, 'Then the men who were designated by name arose, took charge of the captives, and provided from the plunder clothing for the naked. They clothed them, gave them sandals and food and drink, anointed their wounds, and put all the feeble on donkeys. So they brought them to Jericho, the City of Palms, to their brothers. Then they returned to Samaria.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 16, 'At that time King Ahaz sent for help from the king of Assyria.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 17, 'The Edomites had again come and attacked Judah and carried away captives.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 18, 'The Philistines had also raided the cities of the foothills and the Negev of Judah, capturing and occupying Beth-shemesh, Aijalon, and Gederoth, as well as Soco, Timnah, and Gimzo with their villages.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 19, 'For the LORD humbled Judah because Ahaz king of Israel had thrown off restraint in Judah and had been most unfaithful to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 20, 'Then Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria came to Ahaz but afflicted him rather than strengthening him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 21, 'Although Ahaz had taken a portion from the house of the LORD, from the royal palace, and from the princes and had presented it to the king of Assyria, it did not help him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 22, 'In the time of his distress, King Ahaz became even more unfaithful to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 23, 'Since Damascus had defeated him, he sacrificed to their gods and said, “Because the gods of the kings of Aram have helped them, I will sacrifice to them that they may help me.” But these gods were the downfall of Ahaz and of all Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 24, 'Then Ahaz gathered up the articles of the house of God, cut them into pieces, shut the doors of the house of the LORD, and set up altars of his own on every street corner in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 25, 'In every city of Judah he built high places to offer incense to other gods, and so he provoked the LORD, the God of his fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 26, 'As for the rest of the acts of Ahaz and all his ways, from beginning to end, they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 28, 27, 'And Ahaz rested with his fathers and was buried in the city of Jerusalem, but he was not placed in the tombs of the kings of Israel. And his son Hezekiah reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 1, 'Hezekiah was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-nine years. His mother’s name was Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 2, 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father David had done.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 3, 'In the first month of the first year of his reign, Hezekiah opened and repaired the doors of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 4, 'Then he brought in the priests and Levites and gathered them in the square on the east side.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 5, '“Listen to me, O Levites,” he said. “Consecrate yourselves now and consecrate the house of the LORD, the God of your fathers. Remove from the Holy Place every impurity.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 6, 'For our fathers were unfaithful and did evil in the sight of the LORD our God. They abandoned Him, turned their faces away from the dwelling place of the LORD, and turned their backs on Him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 7, 'They also shut the doors of the portico and extinguished the lamps. They did not burn incense or present burnt offerings in the Holy Place of the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 8, 'Therefore, the wrath of the LORD has fallen upon Judah and Jerusalem, and He has made them an object of terror, horror, and mockery, as you can see with your own eyes.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 9, 'For behold, this is why our fathers have fallen by the sword, and our sons and daughters and wives are in captivity.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 10, 'Now it is in my heart to make a covenant with the LORD, the God of Israel, so that His fierce anger will turn away from us.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 11, 'Now, my sons, do not be negligent, for the LORD has chosen you to stand before Him, to serve Him, to minister before Him, and to burn incense.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 12, 'Then the Levites set to work: Mahath son of Amasai and Joel son of Azariah from the Kohathites; Kish son of Abdi and Azariah son of Jehallelel from the Merarites; Joah son of Zimmah and Eden son of Joah from the Gershonites;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 13, 'Shimri and Jeuel from the Elizaphanites; Zechariah and Mattaniah from the Asaphites;'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 14, 'Jehiel and Shimei from the Hemanites; and Shemaiah and Uzziel from the Jeduthunites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 15, 'When they had assembled their brothers and consecrated themselves, they went in to cleanse the house of the LORD, according to the command of the king by the words of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 16, 'So the priests went inside the house of the LORD to cleanse it, and they brought out to the courtyard all the unclean things that they found in the temple of the LORD. Then the Levites took these things and carried them out to the Kidron Valley.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 17, 'They began the consecration on the first day of the first month, and on the eighth day of the month they reached the portico of the LORD. For eight more days they consecrated the house of the LORD itself, finishing on the sixteenth day of the first month.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 18, 'Then they went in to King Hezekiah and reported, “We have cleansed the entire house of the LORD, the altar of burnt offering with all its utensils, and the table of the showbread with all its utensils.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 19, 'Moreover, we have prepared and consecrated all the articles that King Ahaz in his unfaithfulness cast aside during his reign. They are now in front of the altar of the LORD.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 20, 'Early the next morning King Hezekiah gathered the city officials and went up to the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 21, 'They brought seven bulls, seven rams, seven lambs, and seven male goats as a sin offering for the kingdom, for the sanctuary, and for Judah. And the king commanded the priests, the descendants of Aaron, to offer them on the altar of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 22, 'So they slaughtered the bulls, and the priests took the blood and sprinkled it on the altar. They slaughtered the rams and sprinkled the blood on the altar. And they slaughtered the lambs and sprinkled the blood on the altar.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 23, 'Then they brought the goats for the sin offering before the king and the assembly, who laid their hands on them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 24, 'And the priests slaughtered the goats and put their blood on the altar for a sin offering, to make atonement for all Israel, because the king had ordered the burnt offering and the sin offering for all Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 25, 'Hezekiah stationed the Levites in the house of the LORD with cymbals, harps, and lyres according to the command of David, of Gad the king’s seer, and of Nathan the prophet. For the command had come from the LORD through His prophets.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 26, 'The Levites stood with the instruments of David, and the priests with the trumpets.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 27, 'And Hezekiah ordered that the burnt offering be sacrificed on the altar. When the burnt offering began, the song of the LORD and the trumpets began as well, accompanied by the instruments of David king of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 28, 'The whole assembly was worshiping, the singers were singing, and the trumpeters were playing. All this continued until the burnt offering was completed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 29, 'When the offerings were completed, the king and all those present with him bowed down and worshiped.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 30, 'Then King Hezekiah and his officials ordered the Levites to sing praises to the LORD in the words of David and of Asaph the seer. So they sang praises with gladness and bowed their heads and worshiped.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 31, 'Then Hezekiah said, “Now that you have consecrated yourselves to the LORD, come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings to the house of the LORD.” So the assembly brought sacrifices and thank offerings, and all whose hearts were willing brought burnt offerings.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 32, 'The number of burnt offerings the assembly brought was seventy bulls, a hundred rams, and two hundred lambs; all these were for a burnt offering to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 33, 'And the consecrated offerings were six hundred bulls and three thousand sheep.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 34, 'However, since there were not enough priests to skin all the burnt offerings, their Levite brothers helped them until the work was finished and until the priests had been consecrated. For the Levites had been more diligent in consecrating themselves than the priests had been.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 35, 'Furthermore, the burnt offerings were abundant, along with the fat of the peace offerings and the drink offerings for the burnt offerings. So the service of the house of the LORD was established.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 29, 36, 'Then Hezekiah and all the people rejoiced at what God had prepared for the people, because everything had been accomplished so quickly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 1, 'Then Hezekiah sent word throughout all Israel and Judah, and he also wrote letters to Ephraim and Manasseh inviting them to come to the house of the LORD in Jerusalem to keep the Passover of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 2, 'For the king and his officials and the whole assembly in Jerusalem had decided to keep the Passover in the second month,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 3, 'since they had been unable to observe it at the regular time, because not enough priests had consecrated themselves and the people had not been gathered in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 4, 'This proposal pleased the king and the whole assembly.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 5, 'So they established a decree to circulate a proclamation throughout Israel, from Beersheba to Dan, that the people should come to keep the Passover of the LORD, the God of Israel, in Jerusalem. For they had not observed it as a nation as prescribed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 6, 'So the couriers went throughout Israel and Judah with letters from the king and his officials, which read: “Children of Israel, return to the LORD, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, so that He may return to those of you who remain, who have escaped the grasp of the kings of Assyria.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 7, 'Do not be like your fathers and brothers who were unfaithful to the LORD, the God of their fathers, so that He made them an object of horror, as you can see.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 8, 'Now do not stiffen your necks as your fathers did. Submit to the LORD and come to His sanctuary, which He has consecrated forever. Serve the LORD your God, so that His fierce anger will turn away from you.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 9, 'For if you return to the LORD, your brothers and sons will receive mercy in the presence of their captors and will return to this land. For the LORD your God is gracious and merciful; He will not turn His face away from you if you return to Him.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 10, 'And the couriers traveled from city to city through the land of Ephraim and Manasseh as far as Zebulun; but the people scorned and mocked them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 11, 'Nevertheless, some from Asher, Manasseh, and Zebulun humbled themselves and came to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 12, 'Moreover, the power of God was on the people in Judah to give them one heart to obey the command of the king and his officials according to the word of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 13, 'In the second month, a very great assembly gathered in Jerusalem to celebrate the Feast of Unleavened Bread.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 14, 'They proceeded to remove the altars in Jerusalem and to take away the incense altars and throw them into the Kidron Valley.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 15, 'And on the fourteenth day of the second month they slaughtered the Passover lamb. The priests and Levites were ashamed, and they consecrated themselves and brought burnt offerings to the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 16, 'They stood at their prescribed posts, according to the Law of Moses the man of God. The priests sprinkled the blood, which they received from the hand of the Levites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 17, 'Since there were many in the assembly who had not consecrated themselves, the Levites were in charge of slaughtering the Passover lambs for every unclean person to consecrate the lambs to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 18, 'A large number of the people—many from Ephraim, Manasseh, Issachar, and Zebulun—had not purified themselves, yet they ate the Passover, contrary to what was written. But Hezekiah interceded for them, saying, “May the LORD, who is good, provide atonement for everyone'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 19, 'who sets his heart on seeking God—the LORD, the God of his fathers—even if he is not cleansed according to the purification rules of the sanctuary.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 20, 'And the LORD heard Hezekiah and healed the people.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 21, 'The Israelites who were present in Jerusalem celebrated the Feast of Unleavened Bread for seven days with great joy, and the Levites and priests praised the LORD day after day, accompanied by loud instruments of praise to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 22, 'And Hezekiah encouraged all the Levites who performed skillfully before the LORD. For seven days they ate their assigned portion, sacrificing fellowship offerings and giving thanks to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 23, 'The whole assembly agreed to observe seven more days, so they observed seven days with joy.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 24, 'For Hezekiah king of Judah contributed a thousand bulls and seven thousand sheep for the assembly, and the officials contributed a thousand bulls and ten thousand sheep for the assembly, and a great number of priests consecrated themselves.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 25, 'Then the whole assembly of Judah rejoiced along with the priests and Levites and the whole assembly that had come from Israel, including the foreigners who had come from Israel and those who lived in Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 26, 'So there was great rejoicing in Jerusalem, for nothing like this had happened there since the days of Solomon son of David king of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 30, 27, 'Then the priests and the Levites stood to bless the people, and God heard their voice, and their prayer came into His holy dwelling place in heaven.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 1, 'When all this had ended, the Israelites in attendance went out to the cities of Judah and broke up the sacred pillars, chopped down the Asherah poles, and tore down the high places and altars throughout Judah and Benjamin, as well as in Ephraim and Manasseh, until they had utterly destroyed them all. Then all the Israelites returned to their cities, each to his own property.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 2, 'Hezekiah reestablished the divisions of the priests and Levites—each of them according to their duties as priests or Levites—for the burnt offerings and peace offerings, for ministry, for giving thanks, and for singing praises at the gates of the LORD’s dwelling.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 3, 'The king contributed from his own possessions for the regular morning and evening burnt offerings and for the burnt offerings on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts, as written in the Law of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 4, 'Moreover, he commanded the people living in Jerusalem to make a contribution for the priests and Levites so that they could devote themselves to the Law of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 5, 'As soon as the order went out, the Israelites generously provided the firstfruits of the grain, new wine, oil, and honey, and of all the produce of the field, and they brought in an abundance—a tithe of everything.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 6, 'And the Israelites and Judahites who lived in the cities of Judah also brought a tithe of their herds and flocks and a tithe of the holy things consecrated to the LORD their God, and they laid them in large heaps.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 7, 'In the third month they began building up the heaps, and they finished in the seventh month.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 8, 'When Hezekiah and his officials came and viewed the heaps, they blessed the LORD and His people Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 9, 'Then Hezekiah questioned the priests and Levites about the heaps,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 10, 'and Azariah, the chief priest of the household of Zadok, answered him, “Since the people began to bring their contributions into the house of the LORD, we have had enough to eat and there is plenty left over, because the LORD has blessed His people; this great abundance is what is left over.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 11, 'Then Hezekiah commanded them to prepare storerooms in the house of the LORD, and they did so.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 12, 'And they faithfully brought in the contributions, tithes, and dedicated gifts. Conaniah the Levite was the officer in charge of them, and his brother Shimei was second.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 13, 'Jehiel, Azaziah, Nahath, Asahel, Jerimoth, Jozabad, Eliel, Ismachiah, Mahath, and Benaiah were overseers under the authority of Conaniah and his brother Shimei, by appointment of King Hezekiah and of Azariah the chief official of the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 14, 'Kore son of Imnah the Levite, the keeper of the East Gate, was in charge of the freewill offerings given to God, distributing the contributions to the LORD and the consecrated gifts.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 15, 'Under his authority, Eden, Miniamin, Jeshua, Shemaiah, Amariah, and Shecaniah faithfully distributed portions to their fellow priests in their cities, according to their divisions, old and young alike.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 16, 'In addition, they distributed portions to the males registered by genealogy who were three years of age or older—to all who would enter the house of the LORD for their daily duties for service in the responsibilities of their divisions—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 17, 'and to the priests enrolled according to their families in the genealogy, as well as to the Levites twenty years of age or older, according to their duties and divisions.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 18, 'The genealogy included all the little ones, wives, sons, and daughters in the whole assembly. For they had faithfully consecrated themselves as holy.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 19, 'As for the priests, the descendants of Aaron, who lived on the farmlands around each of their cities or in any other city, men were designated by name to distribute a portion to every male among the priests and to every Levite listed by the genealogies.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 20, 'So this is what Hezekiah did throughout Judah. He did what was good and upright and true before the LORD his God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 31, 21, 'He was diligent in every work that he began in the service of the house of God, and in the law and the commandments, in order to seek his God. And so he prospered.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 1, 'After all these acts of faithfulness, Sennacherib king of Assyria came and invaded Judah. He laid siege to the fortified cities, intending to conquer them for himself.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 2, 'When Hezekiah saw that Sennacherib had come to make war against Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 3, 'he consulted with his leaders and commanders about stopping up the waters of the springs outside the city, and they helped him carry it out.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 4, 'Many people assembled and stopped up all the springs and the stream that flowed through the land. “Why should the kings of Assyria come and find plenty of water?” they said.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 5, 'Then Hezekiah worked resolutely to rebuild all the broken sections of the wall and to raise up towers on it. He also built an outer wall and reinforced the supporting terraces of the City of David, and he produced an abundance of weapons and shields.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 6, 'Hezekiah appointed military commanders over the people and gathered the people in the square of the city gate. Then he encouraged them, saying,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 7, '“Be strong and courageous! Do not be afraid or discouraged before the king of Assyria and the vast army with him, for there is a greater One with us than with him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 8, 'With him is only the arm of flesh, but with us is the LORD our God to help us and to fight our battles.” So the people were strengthened by the words of Hezekiah king of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 9, 'Later, as Sennacherib king of Assyria and all his forces besieged Lachish, he sent his servants to Jerusalem with a message for King Hezekiah of Judah and all the people of Judah who were in Jerusalem:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 10, '“This is what Sennacherib king of Assyria says: What is the basis of your confidence, that you remain in Jerusalem under siege?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 11, 'Is not Hezekiah misleading you to give you over to death by famine and thirst when he says, ‘The LORD our God will deliver us from the hand of the king of Assyria?’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 12, 'Did not Hezekiah himself remove His high places and His altars and say to Judah and Jerusalem, ‘You must worship before one altar, and on it you shall burn sacrifices’?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 13, 'Do you not know what I and my fathers have done to all the peoples of the lands? Have the gods of these nations ever been able to deliver their land from my hand?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 14, 'Who among all the gods of these nations that my fathers devoted to destruction has been able to deliver his people from my hand? How then can your God deliver you from my hand?'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 15, 'So now, do not let Hezekiah deceive you, and do not let him mislead you like this. Do not believe him, for no god of any nation or kingdom has been able to deliver his people from my hand or from the hand of my fathers. How much less will your God deliver you from my hand!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 16, 'And the servants of Sennacherib spoke further against the LORD God and against His servant Hezekiah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 17, 'He also wrote letters mocking the LORD, the God of Israel, and saying against Him: “Just as the gods of the nations did not deliver their people from my hand, so the God of Hezekiah will not deliver His people from my hand.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 18, 'Then the Assyrians called out loudly in Hebrew to the people of Jerusalem who were on the wall, to frighten and terrify them in order to capture the city.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 19, 'They spoke against the God of Jerusalem as they had spoken against the gods of the peoples of the earth—the work of human hands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 20, 'In response, King Hezekiah and the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz cried out to heaven in prayer,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 21, 'and the LORD sent an angel who annihilated every mighty man of valor and every leader and commander in the camp of the king of Assyria. So he withdrew to his own land in disgrace. And when he entered the temple of his god, some of his own sons struck him down with the sword.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 22, 'So the LORD saved Hezekiah and the people of Jerusalem from the hands of King Sennacherib of Assyria and all the others, and He gave them rest on every side.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 23, 'Many brought offerings to Jerusalem for the LORD and valuable gifts for Hezekiah king of Judah, and from then on he was exalted in the eyes of all nations.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 24, 'In those days Hezekiah became mortally ill. So he prayed to the LORD, who spoke to him and gave him a sign.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 25, 'But because his heart was proud, Hezekiah did not repay the favor shown to him. Therefore wrath came upon him and upon Judah and Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 26, 'Then Hezekiah humbled the pride of his heart—he and the people of Jerusalem—so that the wrath of the LORD did not come upon them during the days of Hezekiah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 27, 'Hezekiah had very great riches and honor, and he made treasuries for his silver, gold, precious stones, spices, shields, and all kinds of valuable articles.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 28, 'He also made storehouses for the harvest of grain and new wine and oil, stalls for all kinds of livestock, and pens for the flocks.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 29, 'He made cities for himself, and he acquired herds of sheep and cattle in abundance, for God gave him very great wealth.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 30, 'It was Hezekiah who blocked the upper outlet of the Spring of Gihon and channeled it down to the west side of the City of David. And Hezekiah prospered in all that he did.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 31, 'And so when ambassadors of the rulers of Babylon were sent to him to inquire about the wonder that had happened in the land, God left him alone to test him, that He might know all that was in Hezekiah’s heart.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 32, 'As for the rest of the acts of Hezekiah and his deeds of loving devotion, they are indeed written in the vision of the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 32, 33, 'And Hezekiah rested with his fathers and was buried in the upper tombs of David’s descendants. All Judah and the people of Jerusalem paid him honor at his death. And his son Manasseh reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 1, 'Manasseh was twelve years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem fifty-five years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 2, 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD by following the abominations of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 3, 'For he rebuilt the high places that his father Hezekiah had torn down, and he raised up altars for the Baals and made Asherah poles. And he worshiped and served all the host of heaven.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 4, 'Manasseh also built altars in the house of the LORD, of which the LORD had said, “My Name will remain in Jerusalem forever.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 5, 'In both courtyards of the house of the LORD, he built altars to all the host of heaven.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 6, 'He sacrificed his sons in the fire in the Valley of Hinnom. He practiced sorcery, divination, and witchcraft, and consulted mediums and spiritists. He did great evil in the sight of the LORD, provoking Him to anger.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 7, 'Manasseh even took the carved image he had made and set it up in the house of God, of which God had said to David and his son Solomon, “In this temple and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will establish My Name forever.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 8, 'I will never again cause the feet of the Israelites to leave the land that I assigned to your fathers, if only they are careful to do all that I have commanded them through Moses—all the laws, statutes, and judgments.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 9, 'So Manasseh led the people of Judah and Jerusalem astray, so that they did greater evil than the nations that the LORD had destroyed before the Israelites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 10, 'And the LORD spoke to Manasseh and his people, but they did not listen.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 11, 'So the LORD brought against them the military commanders of the king of Assyria, who captured Manasseh, put a hook in his nose, bound him with bronze shackles, and took him to Babylon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 12, 'And in his distress, Manasseh sought the favor of the LORD his God and earnestly humbled himself before the God of his fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 13, 'And when he prayed to Him, the LORD received his plea and heard his petition; so He brought him back to Jerusalem and to his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the LORD is God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 14, 'After this, Manasseh rebuilt the outer wall of the City of David from west of Gihon in the valley to the entrance of the Fish Gate, and he brought it around the hill of Ophel and heightened it considerably. He also stationed military commanders in all the fortified cities of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 15, 'He removed the foreign gods and the idol from the house of the LORD, along with all the altars he had built on the temple mount and in Jerusalem, and he dumped them outside the city.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 16, 'Then he restored the altar of the LORD and sacrificed peace offerings and thank offerings on it, and he told Judah to serve the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 17, 'Nevertheless, the people still sacrificed at the high places, but only to the LORD their God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 18, 'As for the rest of the acts of Manasseh, along with his prayer to his God and the words of the seers who spoke to him in the name of the LORD, the God of Israel, they are indeed written in the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 19, 'His prayer and how God received his plea, as well as all his sin and unfaithfulness, and the sites where he built high places and set up Asherah poles and idols before he humbled himself, they are indeed written in the Records of the Seers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 20, 'And Manasseh rested with his fathers and was buried at his palace. And his son Amon reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 21, 'Amon was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem two years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 22, 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as his father Manasseh had done. Amon served and sacrificed to all the idols that his father Manasseh had made,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 23, 'but he did not humble himself before the LORD as his father Manasseh had done; instead, Amon increased his guilt.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 24, 'Then the servants of Amon conspired against him and killed him in his palace.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 33, 25, 'But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon, and they made his son Josiah king in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 1, 'Josiah was eight years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem thirty-one years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 2, 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD and walked in the ways of his father David; he did not turn aside to the right or to the left.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 3, 'In the eighth year of his reign, while he was still young, Josiah began to seek the God of his father David, and in the twelfth year he began to cleanse Judah and Jerusalem of the high places, the Asherah poles, the carved idols, and the cast images.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 4, 'Then in his presence the altars of the Baals were torn down, and he cut to pieces the incense altars that were above them. He shattered the Asherah poles, the carved idols, and the cast images, crushed them to dust, and scattered them over the graves of those who had sacrificed to them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 5, 'Then he burned the bones of the priests on their altars. So he cleansed Judah and Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 6, 'Josiah did the same in the cities of Manasseh, Ephraim, and Simeon, as far as Naphtali, and in the ruins around them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 7, 'He tore down the altars and Asherah poles, crushed the idols to powder, and cut to pieces all the incense altars throughout the land of Israel. Then he returned to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 8, 'Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, in order to cleanse the land and the temple, Josiah sent Shaphan son of Azaliah, Maaseiah the governor of the city, and Joah son of Joahaz, the recorder, to repair the house of the LORD his God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 9, 'So they went to Hilkiah the high priest and gave him the money that had been brought into the house of God, which the Levites at the doors had collected from the people of Manasseh and Ephraim, from all the remnant of Israel, Judah, and Benjamin, and from the people of Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 10, 'They put it into the hands of the supervisors of those doing the work of the house of the LORD, who in turn gave it to the workmen restoring and repairing the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 11, 'They also gave money to the carpenters and builders to buy dressed stone, as well as timbers for couplings and beams for the buildings that the kings of Judah had allowed to deteriorate.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 12, 'And the men did the work faithfully. The Levites overseeing them were Jahath and Obadiah, descendants of Merari, and Zechariah and Meshullam, descendants of Kohath. Other Levites, all skilled with musical instruments,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 13, 'were over the laborers and supervised all who did the work, task by task. Some of the Levites were secretaries, officers, and gatekeepers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 14, 'While they were bringing out the money that had been taken into the house of the LORD, Hilkiah the priest found the Book of the Law of the LORD written by Moses.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 15, 'And Hilkiah said to Shaphan the scribe, “I have found the Book of the Law in the house of the LORD!” And he gave it to Shaphan.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 16, 'Then Shaphan brought the book to the king and reported, “Your servants are doing all that has been placed in their hands.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 17, 'They have paid out the money that was found in the house of the LORD and have put it into the hands of the supervisors and workers.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 18, 'Moreover, Shaphan the scribe told the king, “Hilkiah the priest has given me a book.” And Shaphan read it in the presence of the king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 19, 'When the king heard the words of the Law, he tore his clothes'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 20, 'and commanded Hilkiah, Ahikam son of Shaphan, Abdon son of Micah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the servant of the king:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 21, '“Go and inquire of the LORD for me and for those remaining in Israel and Judah concerning the words in the book that has been found. For great is the wrath of the LORD that has been poured out on us because our fathers have not kept the word of the LORD by doing all that is written in this book.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 22, 'So Hilkiah and those the king had designated went and spoke to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum son of Tokhath, the son of Hasrah, the keeper of the wardrobe. She lived in Jerusalem, in the Second District.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 23, 'And Huldah said to them, “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Tell the man who sent you'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 24, 'that this is what the LORD says: I am about to bring calamity on this place and on its people, according to all the curses written in the book that has been read in the presence of the king of Judah,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 25, 'because they have forsaken Me and burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke Me to anger with all the works of their hands. My wrath will be poured out upon this place and will not be quenched.’'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 26, 'But as for the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, tell him that this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘As for the words that you heard,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 27, 'because your heart was tender and you humbled yourself before God when you heard His words against this place and against its people, and because you have humbled yourself before Me and you have torn your clothes and wept before Me, I have heard you,’ declares the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 28, '‘Now I will indeed gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes will not see all the calamity that I will bring on this place and on its inhabitants.’” So they brought her answer back to the king.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 29, 'Then the king summoned all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 30, 'And he went up to the house of the LORD with all the people of Judah and Jerusalem, as well as the priests and the Levites—all the people small and great—and in their hearing he read all the words of the Book of the Covenant that had been found in the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 31, 'So the king stood by the pillar and made a covenant before the LORD to follow the LORD and to keep His commandments, decrees, and statutes with all his heart and all his soul, and to carry out the words of this covenant that were written in this book.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 32, 'Then he had everyone in Jerusalem and Benjamin take a stand in agreement to it. So all the people of Jerusalem carried out the covenant of God, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 34, 33, 'And Josiah removed all the abominations from all the lands belonging to the Israelites, and he required everyone in Israel to serve the LORD their God. Throughout his reign they did not turn aside from following the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 1, 'Then Josiah celebrated the Passover to the LORD in Jerusalem, and the Passover lamb was slaughtered on the fourteenth day of the first month.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 2, 'He appointed the priests to their duties and encouraged them in the service of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 3, 'To the Levites who taught all Israel and were holy to the LORD, Josiah said: “Put the holy ark in the temple built by Solomon son of David king of Israel. It is not to be carried around on your shoulders. Now serve the LORD your God and His people Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 4, 'Prepare yourselves by families in your divisions, according to the instructions written by David king of Israel and Solomon his son.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 5, 'Moreover, stand in the Holy Place by the divisions of the families of your kinsmen the lay people, and by the divisions of the families of the Levites.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 6, 'Slaughter the Passover lambs, consecrate yourselves, and make preparations for your fellow countrymen to carry out the word of the LORD given by Moses.”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 7, 'From his own flocks and herds Josiah contributed 30,000 lambs and goats plus 3,000 bulls for the Passover offerings for all the people who were present.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 8, 'His officials also contributed willingly to the people and priests and Levites. Hilkiah, Zechariah, and Jehiel, the administrators of the house of God, gave the priests 2,600 Passover offerings and 300 bulls.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 9, 'Additionally, Conaniah and his brothers Shemaiah and Nethanel, as well as Hashabiah, Jeiel, and Jozabad, officers of the Levites, donated to the Levites 5,000 Passover offerings and 500 bulls.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 10, 'So the service was prepared; the priests stood in their places and the Levites in their divisions according to the king’s command.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 11, 'And they slaughtered the Passover lambs, while the priests sprinkled the blood handed to them and the Levites skinned the animals.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 12, 'They set aside the burnt offerings to be given to the divisions of the families of the people to offer to the LORD, as is written in the Book of Moses; and they did the same with the bulls.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 13, 'They roasted the Passover animals on the fire according to the regulation, and they boiled the other holy offerings in pots, kettles, and bowls and quickly brought them to all the people.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 14, 'Afterward, they made preparations for themselves and for the priests, since the priests, the descendants of Aaron, were offering up burnt offerings and fat until nightfall. So the Levites made preparations for themselves and for the priests, the descendants of Aaron.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 15, 'The singers, the descendants of Asaph, were at their stations according to the command of David, Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun the king’s seer. And the gatekeepers at each gate did not need to leave their position, because their fellow Levites made preparations for them.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 16, 'So on that day the entire service of the LORD was carried out for celebrating the Passover and offering burnt offerings on the altar of the LORD, according to the command of King Josiah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 17, 'The Israelites who were present also observed the Passover at that time, as well as the Feast of Unleavened Bread for seven days.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 18, 'No such Passover had been observed in Israel since the days of Samuel the prophet. None of the kings of Israel ever observed a Passover like the one that Josiah observed with the priests, the Levites, all Judah, the Israelites who were present, and the people of Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 19, 'In the eighteenth year of Josiah’s reign, this Passover was observed.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 20, 'After all this, when Josiah had set the temple in order, Neco king of Egypt marched up to fight at Carchemish by the Euphrates, and Josiah went out to confront him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 21, 'But Neco sent messengers to him, saying, “What is the issue between you and me, O king of Judah? I have not come against you today, but I am fighting another dynasty. God told me to hurry; so stop opposing God, who is with me, or He will destroy you!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 22, 'Josiah, however, did not turn away from him; instead, in order to engage him in battle, he disguised himself. He did not listen to Neco’s words from the mouth of God, but went to fight him on the Plain of Megiddo.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 23, 'There the archers shot King Josiah, who said to his servants, “Take me away, for I am badly wounded!”'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 24, 'So his servants took him out of his chariot, put him in his second chariot, and brought him to Jerusalem, where he died. And Josiah was buried in the tomb of his fathers, and all Judah and Jerusalem mourned for him.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 25, 'Then Jeremiah lamented over Josiah, and to this day all the choirs of men and women sing laments over Josiah. They established them as a statute for Israel, and indeed they are written in the Book of Laments.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 26, 'As for the rest of the acts of Josiah, along with his deeds of loving devotion according to what is written in the Law of the LORD—'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 35, 27, 'his acts from beginning to end—they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Israel and Judah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 1, 'Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz son of Josiah and made him king in Jerusalem in place of his father.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 2, 'Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 3, 'And the king of Egypt dethroned him in Jerusalem and imposed on Judah a levy of a hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 4, 'Then Neco king of Egypt made Eliakim brother of Jehoahaz king over Judah and Jerusalem, and he changed Eliakim’s name to Jehoiakim. But Neco took Eliakim’s brother Jehoahaz and carried him off to Egypt.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 5, 'Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. And he did evil in the sight of the LORD his God.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 6, 'Then Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up against Jehoiakim and bound him with bronze shackles to take him to Babylon.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 7, 'Nebuchadnezzar also took to Babylon some of the articles from the house of the LORD, and he put them in his temple in Babylon.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 8, 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, the abominations he committed, and all that was found against him, they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Israel and Judah. And his son Jehoiachin reigned in his place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 9, 'Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months and ten days. And he did evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 10, 'In the spring, King Nebuchadnezzar summoned Jehoiachin and brought him to Babylon, along with the articles of value from the house of the LORD. And he made Jehoiachin’s relative Zedekiah king over Judah and Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 11, 'Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 12, 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD his God and did not humble himself before Jeremiah the prophet, who spoke for the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 13, 'He also rebelled against King Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him swear by God. But Zedekiah stiffened his neck and hardened his heart against turning to the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 14, 'Furthermore, all the leaders of the priests and the people multiplied their unfaithful deeds, following all the abominations of the nations, and they defiled the house of the LORD, which He had consecrated in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 15, 'Again and again the LORD, the God of their fathers, sent word to His people through His messengers because He had compassion on them and on His dwelling place.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 16, 'But they mocked the messengers of God, despising His words and scoffing at His prophets, until the wrath of the LORD against His people was stirred up beyond remedy.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 17, 'So He brought up against them the king of the Chaldeans, who put their young men to the sword in the sanctuary, sparing neither young men nor young women, neither elderly nor infirm. God gave them all into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar,'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 18, 'who carried off everything to Babylon—all the articles of the house of God, both large and small, and the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the king and his officials.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 19, 'Then the Chaldeans set fire to the house of God and broke down the wall of Jerusalem. They burned down all the palaces and destroyed every article of value.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 20, 'Those who escaped the sword were carried by Nebuchadnezzar into exile in Babylon, and they became servants to him and his sons until the kingdom of Persia came to power.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 21, 'So the land enjoyed its Sabbath rest all the days of the desolation, until seventy years were completed, in fulfillment of the word of the LORD through Jeremiah.'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 22, 'In the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, to fulfill the word of the LORD spoken through Jeremiah, the LORD stirred the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia to send a proclamation throughout his kingdom and to put it in writing as follows:'),
  ('BSB', '2 Chronicles', 14, 36, 23, '“This is what Cyrus king of Persia says: ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, who has given me all the kingdoms of the earth, has appointed me to build a house for Him at Jerusalem in Judah. Whoever among you belongs to His people, may the LORD his God be with him, and may he go up.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 1, 'In the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, to fulfill the word of the LORD spoken through Jeremiah, the LORD stirred the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia to send a proclamation throughout his kingdom and to put it in writing as follows:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 2, '“This is what Cyrus king of Persia says: ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, who has given me all the kingdoms of the earth, has appointed me to build a house for Him at Jerusalem in Judah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 3, 'Whoever among you belongs to His people, may his God be with him, and may he go to Jerusalem in Judah and build the house of the LORD, the God of Israel; He is the God who is in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 4, 'And let every survivor, wherever he lives, be assisted by the men of that region with silver, gold, goods, and livestock, along with a freewill offering for the house of God in Jerusalem.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 5, 'So the family heads of Judah and Benjamin, along with the priests and Levites—everyone whose spirit God had stirred—prepared to go up and rebuild the house of the LORD in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 6, 'And all their neighbors supported them with articles of silver and gold, with goods and livestock, and with valuables, in addition to all their freewill offerings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 7, 'King Cyrus also brought out the articles belonging to the house of the LORD that Nebuchadnezzar had carried away from Jerusalem and placed in the temple of his gods.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 8, 'Cyrus king of Persia had them brought out by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, who counted them out to Sheshbazzar the prince of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 9, 'This was the inventory: 30 gold dishes, 1,000 silver dishes, 29 silver utensils,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 10, '30 gold bowls, 410 matching silver bowls, and 1,000 other articles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 1, 11, 'In all, there were 5,400 gold and silver articles. Sheshbazzar brought all these along when the exiles went up from Babylon to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 1, 'Now these are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 2, 'accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah. This is the count of the men of Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 3, 'the descendants of Parosh, 2,172;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 4, 'the descendants of Shephatiah, 372;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 5, 'the descendants of Arah, 775;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 6, 'the descendants of Pahath-moab (through the line of Jeshua and Joab), 2,812;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 7, 'the descendants of Elam, 1,254;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 8, 'the descendants of Zattu, 945;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 9, 'the descendants of Zaccai, 760;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 10, 'the descendants of Bani, 642;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 11, 'the descendants of Bebai, 623;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 12, 'the descendants of Azgad, 1,222;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 13, 'the descendants of Adonikam, 666;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 14, 'the descendants of Bigvai, 2,056;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 15, 'the descendants of Adin, 454;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 16, 'the descendants of Ater (through Hezekiah), 98;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 17, 'the descendants of Bezai, 323;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 18, 'the descendants of Jorah, 112;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 19, 'the descendants of Hashum, 223;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 20, 'the descendants of Gibbar, 95;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 21, 'the men of Bethlehem, 123;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 22, 'the men of Netophah, 56;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 23, 'the men of Anathoth, 128;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 24, 'the descendants of Azmaveth, 42;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 25, 'the men of Kiriath-jearim, Chephirah, and Beeroth, 743;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 26, 'the men of Ramah and Geba, 621;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 27, 'the men of Michmash, 122;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 28, 'the men of Bethel and Ai, 223;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 29, 'the descendants of Nebo, 52;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 30, 'the descendants of Magbish, 156;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 31, 'the descendants of the other Elam, 1,254;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 32, 'the descendants of Harim, 320;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 33, 'the men of Lod, Hadid, and Ono, 725;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 34, 'the men of Jericho, 345;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 35, 'and the descendants of Senaah, 3,630.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 36, 'The priests: The descendants of Jedaiah (through the house of Jeshua), 973;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 37, 'the descendants of Immer, 1,052;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 38, 'the descendants of Pashhur, 1,247;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 39, 'and the descendants of Harim, 1,017.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 40, 'The Levites: the descendants of Jeshua and Kadmiel (through the line of Hodaviah), 74.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 41, 'The singers: the descendants of Asaph, 128.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 42, 'The gatekeepers: the descendants of Shallum, the descendants of Ater, the descendants of Talmon, the descendants of Akkub, the descendants of Hatita, and the descendants of Shobai, 139 in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 43, 'The temple servants: the descendants of Ziha, the descendants of Hasupha, the descendants of Tabbaoth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 44, 'the descendants of Keros, the descendants of Siaha, the descendants of Padon,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 45, 'the descendants of Lebanah, the descendants of Hagabah, the descendants of Akkub,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 46, 'the descendants of Hagab, the descendants of Shalmai, the descendants of Hanan,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 47, 'the descendants of Giddel, the descendants of Gahar, the descendants of Reaiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 48, 'the descendants of Rezin, the descendants of Nekoda, the descendants of Gazzam,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 49, 'the descendants of Uzza, the descendants of Paseah, the descendants of Besai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 50, 'the descendants of Asnah, the descendants of Meunim, the descendants of Nephusim,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 51, 'the descendants of Bakbuk, the descendants of Hakupha, the descendants of Harhur,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 52, 'the descendants of Bazluth, the descendants of Mehida, the descendants of Harsha,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 53, 'the descendants of Barkos, the descendants of Sisera, the descendants of Temah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 54, 'the descendants of Neziah, and the descendants of Hatipha.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 55, 'The descendants of the servants of Solomon: the descendants of Sotai, the descendants of Sophereth, the descendants of Peruda,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 56, 'the descendants of Jaala, the descendants of Darkon, the descendants of Giddel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 57, 'the descendants of Shephatiah, the descendants of Hattil, the descendants of Pochereth-hazzebaim, and the descendants of Ami.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 58, 'The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 59, 'The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer, but could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 60, 'the descendants of Delaiah, the descendants of Tobiah, and the descendants of Nekoda, 652 in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 61, 'And from among the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai (who had married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 62, 'These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 63, 'The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest to consult the Urim and Thummim.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 64, 'The whole assembly numbered 42,360,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 65, 'in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 200 male and female singers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 66, 'They had 736 horses, 245 mules,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 67, '435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 68, 'When they arrived at the house of the LORD in Jerusalem, some of the heads of the families gave freewill offerings to rebuild the house of God on its original site.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 69, 'According to their ability, they gave to the treasury for this work 61,000 darics of gold, 5,000 minas of silver, and 100 priestly garments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 2, 70, 'So the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, along with some of the people, settled in their own towns; and the rest of the Israelites settled in their towns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 1, 'By the seventh month, the Israelites had settled in their towns, and the people assembled as one man in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 2, 'Then Jeshua son of Jozadak and his fellow priests, along with Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and his associates, began to build the altar of the God of Israel to sacrifice burnt offerings on it, as it is written in the Law of Moses the man of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 3, 'They set up the altar on its foundation and sacrificed burnt offerings on it to the LORD—both the morning and evening burnt offerings—even though they feared the people of the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 4, 'They also celebrated the Feast of Tabernacles in accordance with what is written, and they offered burnt offerings daily based on the number prescribed for each day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 5, 'After that, they presented the regular burnt offerings and those for New Moons and for all the appointed sacred feasts of the LORD, as well as all the freewill offerings brought to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 6, 'On the first day of the seventh month, the Israelites began to offer burnt offerings to the LORD, although the foundation of the temple of the LORD had not been laid.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 7, 'They gave money to the masons and carpenters, and food and drink and oil to the people of Sidon and Tyre to bring cedar logs from Lebanon to Joppa by sea, as authorized by Cyrus king of Persia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 8, 'In the second month of the second year after they had arrived at the house of God in Jerusalem, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, Jeshua son of Jozadak, and the rest of their associates including the priests, the Levites, and all who had returned to Jerusalem from the captivity, began the work. They appointed Levites twenty years of age or older to supervise the construction of the house of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 9, 'So Jeshua and his sons and brothers, Kadmiel and his sons (descendants of Yehudah), and the sons of Henadad and their sons and brothers—all Levites—joined together to supervise those working on the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 10, 'When the builders had laid the foundation of the temple of the LORD, the priests in their apparel with trumpets, and the Levites (the sons of Asaph) with cymbals, took their positions to praise the LORD, as David king of Israel had prescribed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 11, 'And they sang responsively with praise and thanksgiving to the LORD: “For He is good; for His loving devotion to Israel endures forever.” Then all the people gave a great shout of praise to the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD had been laid.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 12, 'But many of the older priests, Levites, and family heads who had seen the first temple wept loudly when they saw the foundation of this temple. Still, many others shouted joyfully.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 3, 13, 'The people could not distinguish the shouts of joy from the sound of weeping, because the people were making so much noise. And the sound was heard from afar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 1, 'When the enemies of Judah and Benjamin heard that the exiles were building a temple for the LORD, the God of Israel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 2, 'they approached Zerubbabel and the heads of the families, saying, “Let us build with you because, like you, we seek your God and have been sacrificing to Him since the time of King Esar-haddon of Assyria, who brought us here.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 3, 'But Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and the other heads of the families of Israel replied, “You have no part with us in building a house for our God, since we alone must build it for the LORD, the God of Israel, as Cyrus king of Persia has commanded us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 4, 'Then the people of the land set out to discourage the people of Judah and make them afraid to build.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 5, 'They hired counselors against them to frustrate their plans throughout the reign of Cyrus king of Persia and down to the reign of Darius king of Persia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 6, 'At the beginning of the reign of Xerxes, an accusation was lodged against the people of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 7, 'And in the days of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of his associates wrote a letter to Artaxerxes. It was written in Aramaic and then translated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 8, 'Rehum the commander and Shimshai the scribe wrote the letter against Jerusalem to King Artaxerxes as follows:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 9, 'From Rehum the commander, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of their associates—the judges and officials over Tripolis, Persia, Erech and Babylon, the Elamites of Susa,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 10, 'and the rest of the peoples whom the great and honorable Ashurbanipal deported and settled in the cities of Samaria and elsewhere west of the Euphrates.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 11, '(This is the text of the letter they sent to him.) To King Artaxerxes, From your servants, the men west of the Euphrates:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 12, 'Let it be known to the king that the Jews who came from you to us have returned to Jerusalem. And they are rebuilding that rebellious and wicked city, restoring its walls, and repairing its foundations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 13, 'Let it now be known to the king that if that city is rebuilt and its walls are restored, they will not pay tribute, duty, or toll, and the royal treasury will suffer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 14, 'Now because we are in the service of the palace and it is not fitting for us to allow the king to be dishonored, we have sent to inform the king'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 15, 'that a search should be made of the record books of your fathers. In these books you will discover and verify that the city is a rebellious city, harmful to kings and provinces, inciting sedition from ancient times. That is why this city was destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 16, 'We advise the king that if this city is rebuilt and its walls are restored, you will have no dominion west of the Euphrates.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 17, 'Then the king sent this reply: To Rehum the commander, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of your associates living in Samaria and elsewhere in the region west of the Euphrates: Greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 18, 'The letter you sent us has been translated and read in my presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 19, 'I issued a decree, and a search was conducted. It was discovered that this city has revolted against kings from ancient times, engaging in rebellion and sedition.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 20, 'And mighty kings have ruled over Jerusalem and exercised authority over the whole region west of the Euphrates; and tribute, duty, and toll were paid to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 21, 'Now, therefore, issue an order for these men to stop, so that this city will not be rebuilt until I so order.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 22, 'See that you do not neglect this matter. Why allow this threat to increase and the royal interests to suffer?'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 23, 'When the text of the letter from King Artaxerxes was read to Rehum, Shimshai the scribe, and their associates, they went immediately to the Jews in Jerusalem and forcibly stopped them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 4, 24, 'Thus the construction of the house of God in Jerusalem ceased, and it remained at a standstill until the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 1, 'Later, the prophets Haggai and Zechariah son of Iddo prophesied to the Jews in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, who was over them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 2, 'Then Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and Jeshua son of Jozadak rose up and began to rebuild the house of God in Jerusalem. And the prophets of God were with them, helping them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 3, 'At that time Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates went to the Jews and asked, “Who authorized you to rebuild this temple and restore this structure?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 4, 'They also asked, “What are the names of the men who are constructing this building?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 5, 'But the eye of their God was on the elders of the Jews, so that they were not stopped until a report was sent to Darius and written instructions about this matter were returned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 6, 'This is the text of the letter that Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates, the officials in the region, sent to King Darius.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 7, 'The report they sent him read as follows: To King Darius: All peace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 8, 'Let it be known to the king that we went into the province of Judah, to the house of the great God. The people are rebuilding it with large stones, and placing timbers in the walls. This work is being carried out diligently and is prospering in their hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 9, 'So we questioned the elders and asked, “Who authorized you to rebuild this temple and restore this structure?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 10, 'We also asked for their names, so that we could write down the names of their leaders for your information.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 11, 'And this is the answer they returned: “We are servants of the God of heaven and earth, and we are rebuilding the temple that was built many years ago, which a great king of Israel built and completed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 12, 'But since our fathers angered the God of heaven, He delivered them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, the Chaldean who destroyed this temple and carried away the people to Babylon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 13, 'In his first year, however, Cyrus king of Babylon issued a decree to rebuild this house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 14, 'He also removed from the temple of Babylon the gold and silver articles belonging to the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar had taken and carried there from the temple in Jerusalem. King Cyrus gave these articles to a man named Sheshbazzar, whom he appointed governor'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 15, 'and instructed, ‘Take these articles, put them in the temple in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be rebuilt on its original site.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 16, 'So this Sheshbazzar came and laid the foundation of the house of God in Jerusalem, and from that time until now it has been under construction, but it has not yet been completed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 5, 17, 'Now, therefore, if it pleases the king, let a search be made of the royal archives in Babylon to see if King Cyrus did indeed issue a decree to rebuild the house of God in Jerusalem. Then let the king send us his decision in this matter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 1, 'Thus King Darius ordered a search of the archives stored in the treasury of Babylon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 2, 'And a scroll was found in the fortress of Ecbatana, in the province of Media, with the following written on it: Memorandum:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 3, 'In the first year of King Cyrus, he issued a decree concerning the house of God in Jerusalem: Let the house be rebuilt as a place for offering sacrifices, and let its foundations be firmly laid. It is to be sixty cubits high and sixty cubits wide,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 4, 'with three layers of cut stones and one of timbers. The costs are to be paid from the royal treasury.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 5, 'Furthermore, the gold and silver articles of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took from the temple in Jerusalem and carried to Babylon, must also be returned to the temple in Jerusalem and deposited in the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 6, 'Therefore Darius decreed: To Tattenai governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and your associates and officials in the region: You must stay away from that place!'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 7, 'Leave this work on the house of God alone. Let the governor and elders of the Jews rebuild this house of God on its original site.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 8, 'I hereby decree what you must do for these elders of the Jews who are rebuilding this house of God: The cost is to be paid in full to these men from the royal treasury out of the taxes of the provinces west of the Euphrates, so that the work will not be hindered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 9, 'Whatever is needed—young bulls, rams, and lambs for burnt offerings to the God of heaven, as well as wheat, salt, wine, and oil, as requested by the priests in Jerusalem—must be given to them daily without fail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 10, 'Then they will be able to offer sacrifices of a sweet aroma to the God of heaven and to pray for the lives of the king and his sons.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 11, 'I also decree that if any man interferes with this directive, a beam is to be torn from his house and raised up, and he is to be impaled on it. And his own house shall be made a pile of rubble for this offense.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 12, 'May God, who has caused His Name to dwell there, overthrow any king or people who lifts a hand to alter this decree or to destroy this house of God in Jerusalem. I, Darius, have issued the decree. Let it be carried out with diligence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 13, 'In response, Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates diligently carried out what King Darius had decreed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 14, 'So the Jewish elders built and prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah son of Iddo. They finished building according to the command of the God of Israel and the decrees of Cyrus, Darius, and Artaxerxes, kings of Persia.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 15, 'And this temple was completed on the third day of the month of Adar, in the sixth year of the reign of King Darius.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 16, 'Then the people of Israel—the priests, the Levites, and the rest of the exiles—celebrated the dedication of the house of God with joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 17, 'For the dedication of the house of God they offered a hundred bulls, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs, and a sin offering for all Israel of twelve male goats, one for each tribe of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 18, 'They also appointed the priests by their divisions and the Levites by their groups to the service of God in Jerusalem, according to what is written in the Book of Moses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 19, 'On the fourteenth day of the first month, the exiles kept the Passover.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 20, 'All the priests and Levites had purified themselves and were ceremonially clean. And the Levites slaughtered the Passover lamb for all the exiles, for their priestly brothers, and for themselves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 21, 'The Israelites who had returned from exile ate it, together with all who had separated themselves from the uncleanness of the peoples of the land to seek the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 6, 22, 'For seven days they kept the Feast of Unleavened Bread with joy, because the LORD had made them joyful and turned the heart of the king of Assyria toward them to strengthen their hands in the work on the house of the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 1, 'Many years later, during the reign of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra son of Seraiah, the son of Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 2, 'the son of Shallum, the son of Zadok, the son of Ahitub,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 3, 'the son of Amariah, the son of Azariah, the son of Meraioth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 4, 'the son of Zerahiah, the son of Uzzi, the son of Bukki,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 5, 'the son of Abishua, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the chief priest—'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 6, 'this Ezra came up from Babylon. He was a scribe skilled in the Law of Moses, which the LORD, the God of Israel, had given. The king had granted Ezra all his requests, for the hand of the LORD his God was upon him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 7, 'So in the seventh year of King Artaxerxes, he went up to Jerusalem with some of the Israelites, including priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, and temple servants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 8, 'Ezra arrived in Jerusalem in the fifth month of the seventh year of the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 9, 'He had begun the journey from Babylon on the first day of the first month, and he arrived in Jerusalem on the first day of the fifth month, for the gracious hand of his God was upon him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 10, 'For Ezra had set his heart to study the Law of the LORD, to practice it, and to teach its statutes and ordinances in Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 11, 'This is the text of the letter King Artaxerxes had given to Ezra the priest and scribe, an expert in the commandments and statutes of the LORD to Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 12, 'Artaxerxes, king of kings. To Ezra the priest, the scribe of the Law of the God of heaven: Greetings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 13, 'I hereby decree that any volunteers among the Israelites in my kingdom, including the priests and Levites, may go up with you to Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 14, 'You are sent by the king and his seven counselors to evaluate Judah and Jerusalem according to the Law of your God, which is in your hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 15, 'Moreover, you are to take with you the silver and gold that the king and his counselors have freely offered to the God of Israel, whose dwelling is in Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 16, 'together with all the silver and gold you may find in all the province of Babylon, as well as the freewill offerings of the people and priests to the house of their God in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 17, 'With this money, therefore, you are to buy as many bulls, rams, and lambs as needed, together with their grain offerings and drink offerings, and offer them on the altar at the house of your God in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 18, 'You and your brothers may do whatever seems best with the rest of the silver and gold, according to the will of your God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 19, 'You must deliver to the God of Jerusalem all the articles given to you for the service of the house of your God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 20, 'And if anything else is needed for the house of your God that you may have occasion to supply, you may pay for it from the royal treasury.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 21, 'I, King Artaxerxes, decree to all the treasurers west of the Euphrates: Whatever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the Law of the God of heaven, may require of you, it must be provided promptly,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 22, 'up to a hundred talents of silver, a hundred cors of wheat, a hundred baths of wine, a hundred baths of olive oil, and salt without limit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 23, 'Whatever is commanded by the God of heaven must be done diligently for His house. For why should wrath fall on the realm of the king and his sons?'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 24, 'And be advised that you have no authority to impose tribute, duty, or toll on any of the priests, Levites, singers, doorkeepers, temple servants, or other servants of this house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 25, 'And you, Ezra, according to the wisdom of your God which you possess, are to appoint magistrates and judges to judge all the people west of the Euphrates—all who know the laws of your God. And you are to teach these laws to anyone who does not know them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 26, 'If anyone does not keep the law of your God and the law of the king, let a strict judgment be executed against him, whether death, banishment, confiscation of property, or imprisonment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 27, 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of our fathers, who has put into the heart of the king to so honor the house of the LORD in Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 7, 28, 'and who has shown me favor before the king, his counselors, and all his powerful officials. And because the hand of the LORD my God was upon me, I took courage and gathered the leaders of Israel to return with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 1, 'These are the family heads and genealogical records of those who returned with me from Babylon during the reign of King Artaxerxes:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 2, 'from the descendants of Phinehas, Gershom; from the descendants of Ithamar, Daniel;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 3, 'from the descendants of David, Hattush of the descendants of Shecaniah; from the descendants of Parosh, Zechariah, and with him were registered 150 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 4, 'from the descendants of Pahath-Moab, Eliehoenai son of Zerahiah, and with him 200 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 5, 'from the descendants of Zattu, Shecaniah son of Jahaziel, and with him 300 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 6, 'from the descendants of Adin, Ebed son of Jonathan, and with him 50 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 7, 'from the descendants of Elam, Jeshaiah son of Athaliah, and with him 70 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 8, 'from the descendants of Shephatiah, Zebadiah son of Michael, and with him 80 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 9, 'from the descendants of Joab, Obadiah son of Jehiel, and with him 218 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 10, 'from the descendants of Bani, Shelomith son of Josiphiah, and with him 160 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 11, 'from the descendants of Bebai, Zechariah son of Bebai, and with him 28 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 12, 'from the descendants of Azgad, Johanan son of Hakkatan, and with him 110 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 13, 'from the later descendants of Adonikam, these were their names: Eliphelet, Jeiel, and Shemaiah, and with them 60 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 14, 'and from the descendants of Bigvai, both Uthai and Zaccur, and with them 70 men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 15, 'Now I assembled these exiles at the canal that flows to Ahava, and we camped there three days. And when I searched among the people and priests, I found no Levites there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 16, 'Then I summoned the leaders: Eliezer, Ariel, Shemaiah, Elnathan, Jarib, Elnathan, Nathan, Zechariah, and Meshullam, as well as the teachers Joiarib and Elnathan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 17, 'And I sent them to Iddo, the leader at Casiphia, with a message for him and his kinsmen, the temple servants at Casiphia, that they should bring to us ministers for the house of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 18, 'And since the gracious hand of our God was upon us, they brought us Sherebiah—a man of insight from the descendants of Mahli son of Levi, the son of Israel—along with his sons and brothers, 18 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 19, 'also Hashabiah, together with Jeshaiah, from the descendants of Merari, and his brothers and their sons, 20 men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 20, 'They also brought 220 of the temple servants, all designated by name. David and the officials had appointed them to assist the Levites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 21, 'And there by the Ahava Canal I proclaimed a fast, so that we might humble ourselves before our God and ask Him for a safe journey for us and our children, with all our possessions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 22, 'For I was ashamed to ask the king for an escort of soldiers and horsemen to protect us from our enemies on the road, since we had told him, “The hand of our God is gracious to all who seek Him, but His great anger is against all who forsake Him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 23, 'So we fasted and petitioned our God about this, and He granted our request.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 24, 'Then I set apart twelve of the leading priests, together with Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brothers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 25, 'and I weighed out to them the contribution of silver and gold and the articles that the king, his counselors, his leaders, and all the Israelites there had offered for the house of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 26, 'I weighed out into their hands 650 talents of silver, articles of silver weighing 100 talents, 100 talents of gold,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 27, '20 gold bowls valued at 1,000 darics, and two articles of fine polished bronze, as precious as gold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 28, 'Then I told them, “You are holy to the LORD, and these articles are holy. The silver and gold are a freewill offering to the LORD, the God of your fathers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 29, 'Guard them carefully until you weigh them out in the chambers of the house of the LORD in Jerusalem before the leading priests, Levites, and heads of the Israelite families.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 30, 'So the priests and Levites took charge of the silver and gold and sacred articles that had been weighed out to be taken to the house of our God in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 31, 'On the twelfth day of the first month we set out from the Ahava Canal to go to Jerusalem, and the hand of our God was upon us to protect us from the hands of the enemies and bandits along the way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 32, 'So we arrived at Jerusalem and rested there for three days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 33, 'On the fourth day, in the house of our God, we weighed out the silver and gold and sacred articles into the hand of Meremoth son of Uriah, the priest. Eleazar son of Phinehas was with him, along with the Levites Jozabad son of Jeshua and Noadiah son of Binnui.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 34, 'Everything was verified by number and weight, and the total weight was recorded at that time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 35, 'Then the exiles who had returned from captivity sacrificed burnt offerings to the God of Israel: 12 bulls for all Israel, 96 rams, 77 lambs, and a sin offering of 12 male goats. All this was a burnt offering to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 8, 36, 'They also delivered the king’s edicts to the royal satraps and governors of the region west of the Euphrates, who proceeded to assist the people and the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 1, 'After these things had been accomplished, the leaders approached me and said, “The people of Israel, including the priests and Levites, have not kept themselves separate from the surrounding peoples whose abominations are like those of the Canaanites, Hittites, Perizzites, Jebusites, Ammonites, Moabites, Egyptians, and Amorites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 2, 'Indeed, the Israelites have taken some of their daughters as wives for themselves and their sons, so that the holy seed has been mixed with the people of the land. And the leaders and officials have taken the lead in this unfaithfulness!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 3, 'When I heard this report, I tore my tunic and cloak, pulled out some hair from my head and beard, and sat down in horror.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 4, 'Then everyone who trembled at the words of the God of Israel gathered around me because of the unfaithfulness of the exiles, while I sat there in horror until the evening offering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 5, 'At the evening offering, I got up from my humiliation with my tunic and cloak torn, and I fell on my knees, spread out my hands to the LORD my God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 6, 'and said: “O my God, I am ashamed and embarrassed to lift up my face to You, my God, because our iniquities are higher than our heads, and our guilt has reached the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 7, 'From the days of our fathers to this day, our guilt has been great. Because of our iniquities, we and our kings and priests have been delivered into the hands of the kings of the earth and put to the sword and captivity, to pillage and humiliation, as we are this day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 8, 'But now, for a brief moment, grace has come from the LORD our God to preserve for us a remnant and to give us a stake in His holy place. Even in our bondage, our God has given us new life and light to our eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 9, 'Though we are slaves, our God has not forsaken us in our bondage, but He has extended to us grace in the sight of the kings of Persia, giving us new life to rebuild the house of our God and repair its ruins, and giving us a wall of protection in Judah and Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 10, 'And now, our God, what can we say after this? For we have forsaken the commandments'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 11, 'that You gave through Your servants the prophets, saying: ‘The land that you are entering to possess is a land polluted by the impurity of its peoples and the abominations with which they have filled it from end to end.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 12, 'Now, therefore, do not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters for your sons. Never seek their peace or prosperity, so that you may be strong and may eat the good things of the land, leaving it as an inheritance to your sons forever.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 13, 'After all that has come upon us because of our evil deeds and our great guilt (though You, our God, have punished us less than our iniquities deserve and have given us such a remnant as this),'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 14, 'shall we again break Your commandments and intermarry with the peoples who commit these abominations? Would You not become so angry with us as to wipe us out, leaving no remnant or survivor?'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 9, 15, 'O LORD, God of Israel, You are righteous! For we remain this day as a remnant. Here we are before You in our guilt, though because of it no one can stand before You.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 1, 'While Ezra prayed and made this confession, weeping and falling facedown before the house of God, a very large assembly of Israelites—men, women, and children—gathered around him, and the people wept bitterly as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 2, 'Then Shecaniah son of Jehiel, an Elamite, said to Ezra: “We have been unfaithful to our God by marrying foreign women from the people of the land, yet in spite of this, there is hope for Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 3, 'So now let us make a covenant before our God to send away all the foreign wives and their children, according to the counsel of my lord and of those who tremble at the command of our God. Let it be done according to the Law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 4, 'Get up, for this matter is your responsibility, and we will support you. Be strong and take action!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 5, 'So Ezra got up and made the leading priests, Levites, and all Israel take an oath to do what had been said. And they took the oath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 6, 'Then Ezra withdrew from before the house of God and walked to the chamber of Jehohanan son of Eliashib. And while he stayed there, he ate no food and drank no water, because he was mourning over the unfaithfulness of the exiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 7, 'And a proclamation was issued throughout Judah and Jerusalem that all the exiles should gather at Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 8, 'Whoever failed to appear within three days would forfeit all his property, according to the counsel of the leaders and elders, and would himself be expelled from the assembly of the exiles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 9, 'So within the three days, all the men of Judah and Benjamin assembled in Jerusalem, and on the twentieth day of the ninth month, all the people sat in the square at the house of God, trembling regarding this matter and because of the heavy rain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 10, 'Then Ezra the priest stood up and said to them, “You have been unfaithful by marrying foreign women, adding to the guilt of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 11, 'Now, therefore, make a confession to the LORD, the God of your fathers, and do His will. Separate yourselves from the people of the land and from your foreign wives.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 12, 'And the whole assembly responded in a loud voice: “Truly we must do as you say!'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 13, 'But there are many people here, and it is the rainy season. We are not able to stay out in the open. Nor is this the work of one or two days, for we have transgressed greatly in this matter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 14, 'Let our leaders represent the whole assembly. Then let everyone in our towns who has married a foreign woman come at an appointed time, together with the elders and judges of each town, until the fierce anger of our God in this matter is turned away from us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 15, '(Only Jonathan son of Asahel and Jahzeiah son of Tikvah, supported by Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite, opposed this plan.)'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 16, 'So the exiles did as proposed. Ezra the priest selected men who were family heads, each of them identified by name, to represent their families. On the first day of the tenth month they launched the investigation,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 17, 'and by the first day of the first month they had dealt with all the men who had married foreign women.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 18, 'Among the descendants of the priests who had married foreign women were found these descendants of Jeshua son of Jozadak and his brothers:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 19, 'Maaseiah, Eliezer, Jarib, and Gedaliah. They pledged to send their wives away, and for their guilt they presented a ram from the flock as a guilt offering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 20, 'From the descendants of Immer: Hanani and Zebadiah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 21, 'From the descendants of Harim: Maaseiah, Elijah, Shemaiah, Jehiel, and Uzziah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 22, 'From the descendants of Pashhur: Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael, Nethanel, Jozabad, and Elasah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 23, 'Among the Levites: Jozabad, Shimei, Kelaiah (that is, Kelita), Pethahiah, Judah, and Eliezer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 24, 'From the singers: Eliashib. From the gatekeepers: Shallum, Telem, and Uri.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 25, 'And among the other Israelites, from the descendants of Parosh: Ramiah, Izziah, Malchijah, Mijamin, Eleazar, Malchijah, and Benaiah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 26, 'From the descendants of Elam: Mattaniah, Zechariah, Jehiel, Abdi, Jeremoth, and Elijah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 27, 'From the descendants of Zattu: Elioenai, Eliashib, Mattaniah, Jeremoth, Zabad, and Aziza.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 28, 'From the descendants of Bebai: Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, and Athlai.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 29, 'From the descendants of Bani: Meshullam, Malluch, Adaiah, Jashub, Sheal, and Jeremoth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 30, 'From the descendants of Pahath-moab: Adna, Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattaniah, Bezalel, Binnui, and Manasseh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 31, 'From the descendants of Harim:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 32, 'Eliezer, Isshijah, Malchijah, Shemaiah, Shimeon, Benjamin, Malluch, and Shemariah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 33, 'From the descendants of Hashum: Mattenai, Mattattah, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jeremai, Manasseh, and Shimei.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 34, 'From the descendants of Bani:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 35, 'Maadai, Amram, Uel, Benaiah, Bedeiah, Cheluhi,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 36, 'Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 37, 'Mattaniah, Mattenai, and Jaasu.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 38, 'From the descendants of Binnui:'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 39, 'Shimei, Shelemiah, Nathan, Adaiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 40, 'Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 41, 'Azarel, Shelemiah, Shemariah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 42, 'Shallum, Amariah, and Joseph.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 43, 'And from the descendants of Nebo: Jeiel, Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Jaddai, Joel, and Benaiah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Ezra', 15, 10, 44, 'All these men had married foreign women, and some of them had children by these wives.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 1, 'These are the words of Nehemiah son of Hacaliah: In the month of Chislev, in the twentieth year, while I was in the citadel of Susa,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 2, 'Hanani, one of my brothers, arrived with men from Judah. So I questioned them about the remnant of the Jews who had survived the exile, and also about Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 3, 'And they told me, “The remnant who survived the exile are there in the province, in great trouble and disgrace. The wall of Jerusalem is broken down, and its gates are burned with fire.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 4, 'When I heard these words, I sat down and wept. I mourned for days, fasting and praying before the God of heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 5, 'Then I said: “O LORD, God of heaven, the great and awesome God who keeps His covenant of loving devotion with those who love Him and keep His commandments,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 6, 'let Your eyes be open and Your ears attentive to hear the prayer that I, Your servant, now pray before You day and night for Your servants, the Israelites. I confess the sins that we Israelites have committed against You. Both I and my father’s house have sinned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 7, 'We have behaved corruptly against You and have not kept the commandments, statutes, and ordinances that You gave Your servant Moses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 8, 'Remember, I pray, the word that You commanded Your servant Moses when You said, ‘If you are unfaithful, I will scatter you among the nations,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 9, 'but if you return to Me and keep and practice My commandments, then even if your exiles have been banished to the farthest horizon, I will gather them from there and bring them to the place I have chosen as a dwelling for My Name.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 10, 'They are Your servants and Your people. You redeemed them by Your great power and mighty hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 1, 11, 'O Lord, may Your ear be attentive to my prayer and to the prayers of Your servants who delight to revere Your name. Give Your servant success this day, I pray, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man.” (At that time I was the cupbearer to the king.)'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 1, 'Now in the month of Nisan, in the twentieth year of King Artaxerxes, when wine was set before him, I took the wine and gave it to the king. I had never been sad in his presence,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 2, 'so the king said to me, “Why is your face sad, though you are not ill? This could only be sadness of the heart.” I was overwhelmed with fear'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 3, 'and replied to the king, “May the king live forever! Why should I not be sad when the city where my fathers are buried lies in ruins, and its gates have been destroyed by fire?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 4, '“What is your request?” replied the king. So I prayed to the God of heaven'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 5, 'and answered the king, “If it pleases the king, and if your servant has found favor in your sight, I ask that you send me to Judah, to the city where my fathers are buried, so that I may rebuild it.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 6, 'Then the king, with the queen seated beside him, asked me, “How long will your journey take, and when will you return?” So it pleased the king to send me, and I set a time.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 7, 'I also said to him, “If it pleases the king, may letters be given to me for the governors west of the Euphrates, so that they will grant me safe passage until I reach Judah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 8, 'And may I have a letter to Asaph, keeper of the king’s forest, so that he will give me timber to make beams for the gates of the citadel to the temple, for the city wall, and for the house I will occupy.” And because the gracious hand of my God was upon me, the king granted my requests.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 9, 'Then I went to the governors west of the Euphrates and gave them the king’s letters. The king had also sent army officers and cavalry with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 10, 'But when Sanballat the Horonite and Tobiah the Ammonite official heard about this, they were deeply disturbed that someone had come to seek the well-being of the Israelites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 11, 'After I had arrived in Jerusalem and had been there three days,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 12, 'I set out at night with a few men. I did not tell anyone what my God had laid on my heart to do for Jerusalem. The only animal with me was the one on which I was riding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 13, 'So I went out at night through the Valley Gate toward the Well of the Serpent and the Dung Gate, and I inspected the walls of Jerusalem that had been broken down and the gates that had been destroyed by fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 14, 'Then I went on to the Fountain Gate and the King’s Pool, but there was no room for the animal under me to get through;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 15, 'so I went up the valley by night and inspected the wall. Then I headed back and reentered through the Valley Gate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 16, 'The officials did not know where I had gone or what I was doing, for I had not yet told the Jews or priests or nobles or officials or any other workers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 17, 'Then I said to them, “You see the trouble we are in. Jerusalem lies in ruins, and its gates have been burned down. Come, let us rebuild the wall of Jerusalem, so that we will no longer be a disgrace.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 18, 'I also told them about the gracious hand of my God upon me, and what the king had said to me. “Let us start rebuilding,” they replied, and they set their hands to this good work.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 19, 'But when Sanballat the Horonite, Tobiah the Ammonite official, and Geshem the Arab heard about this, they mocked us and ridiculed us, saying, “What is this you are doing? Are you rebelling against the king?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 2, 20, 'So I answered them and said, “The God of heaven is the One who will grant us success. We, His servants, will start rebuilding, but you have no portion, right, or claim in Jerusalem.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 1, 'At the Sheep Gate, Eliashib the high priest and his fellow priests began rebuilding. They dedicated it and installed its doors. After building as far as the Tower of the Hundred and the Tower of Hananel, they dedicated the wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 2, 'The men of Jericho built next to Eliashib, and Zaccur son of Imri built next to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 3, 'The Fish Gate was rebuilt by the sons of Hassenaah. They laid its beams and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 4, 'Next to them, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, made repairs. Next to him, Meshullam son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabel, made repairs; and next to him, Zadok son of Baana made repairs as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 5, 'Next to him, the Tekoites made repairs, but their nobles did not put their shoulders to the work under their supervisors.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 6, 'The Jeshanah Gate was repaired by Joiada son of Paseah and Meshullam son of Besodeiah. They laid its beams and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 7, 'Next to them, repairs were made by Melatiah the Gibeonite, Jadon the Meronothite, and the men of Gibeon and Mizpah, who were under the authority of the governor of the region west of the Euphrates.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 8, 'Next to them, Uzziel son of Harhaiah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs, and next to him, Hananiah son of the perfumer made repairs. They fortified Jerusalem as far as the Broad Wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 9, 'Next to them, Rephaiah son of Hur, ruler of a half-district of Jerusalem, made repairs;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 10, 'next to him, Jedaiah son of Harumaph made repairs across from his house; and next to him, Hattush son of Hashabneiah made repairs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 11, 'Malchijah son of Harim and Hasshub son of Pahath-moab repaired another section, as well as the Tower of the Ovens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 12, 'And next to them, Shallum son of Hallohesh, ruler of the other half-district of Jerusalem, made repairs, with the help of his daughters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 13, 'The Valley Gate was repaired by Hanun and the residents of Zanoah. They rebuilt it, installed its doors, bolts, and bars, and repaired a thousand cubits of the wall as far as the Dung Gate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 14, 'The Dung Gate was repaired by Malchijah son of Rechab, ruler of the district of Beth-haccherem. He rebuilt it and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 15, 'The Fountain Gate was repaired by Shallun son of Col-hozeh, ruler of the district of Mizpah. He rebuilt it, roofed it, and installed its doors, bolts, and bars. He also repaired the wall of the Pool of Shelah near the king’s garden, as far as the stairs that descend from the City of David.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 16, 'Beyond him, Nehemiah son of Azbuk, ruler of a half-district of Beth-zur, made repairs up to a point opposite the tombs of David, as far as the artificial pool and the House of the Mighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 17, 'Next to him, the Levites made repairs under Rehum son of Bani, and next to him, Hashabiah, ruler of a half-district of Keilah, made repairs for his district.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 18, 'Next to him, their countrymen made repairs under Binnui son of Henadad, ruler of the other half-district of Keilah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 19, 'And next to him, Ezer son of Jeshua, ruler of Mizpah, repaired another section opposite the Ascent to the Armory, near the angle in the wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 20, 'Next to him, Baruch son of Zabbai diligently repaired another section, from the angle to the doorway of the house of Eliashib the high priest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 21, 'Next to him, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, repaired another section, from the doorway of the house of Eliashib to the end of the house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 22, 'And next to him, the priests from the surrounding area made repairs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 23, 'Beyond them, Benjamin and Hasshub made repairs in front of their house, and next to them, Azariah son of Maaseiah, the son of Ananiah, made repairs beside his house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 24, 'After him, Binnui son of Henadad repaired another section, from the house of Azariah to the angle and the corner,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 25, 'and Palal son of Uzai made repairs opposite the angle and the tower that juts out from the upper palace of the king near the courtyard of the guard. Next to him, Pedaiah son of Parosh'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 26, 'and the temple servants living on the hill of Ophel made repairs opposite the Water Gate toward the east and the tower that juts out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 27, 'And next to them, the Tekoites repaired another section, from a point opposite the great tower that juts out to the wall of Ophel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 28, 'Above the Horse Gate, each of the priests made repairs in front of his own house.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 29, 'Next to them, Zadok son of Immer made repairs opposite his house, and next to him, Shemaiah son of Shecaniah, the guard of the East Gate, made repairs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 30, 'Next to him, Hananiah son of Shelemiah, as well as Hanun the sixth son of Zalaph, repaired another section. Next to them, Meshullam son of Berechiah made repairs opposite his own quarters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 31, 'Next to him, Malchijah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs as far as the house of the temple servants and the merchants, opposite the Inspection Gate, and as far as the upper room above the corner.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 3, 32, 'And between the upper room above the corner and the Sheep Gate, the goldsmiths and merchants made repairs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 1, 'Now when Sanballat heard that we were rebuilding the wall, he was furious and filled with indignation. He ridiculed the Jews'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 2, 'before his associates and the army of Samaria, saying, “What are these feeble Jews doing? Can they restore the wall by themselves? Will they offer sacrifices? Will they complete it in a day? Can they bring these burnt stones back to life from the mounds of rubble?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 3, 'Then Tobiah the Ammonite, who was beside him, said, “If even a fox were to climb up on what they are building, it would break down their wall of stones!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 4, 'Hear us, O God, for we are despised. Turn their scorn back upon their own heads, and let them be taken as plunder to a land of captivity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 5, 'Do not cover up their iniquity or let their sin be blotted out from Your sight, for they have provoked the builders.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 6, 'So we rebuilt the wall until all of it was joined together up to half its height, for the people had a mind to work.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 7, 'When Sanballat and Tobiah, together with the Arabs, Ammonites, and Ashdodites, heard that the repair to the walls of Jerusalem was progressing and that the gaps were being closed, they were furious,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 8, 'and all of them conspired to come and fight against Jerusalem and create a hindrance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 9, 'So we prayed to our God and posted a guard against them day and night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 10, 'Meanwhile, the people of Judah said: “The strength of the laborer fails, and there is so much rubble that we will never be able to rebuild the wall.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 11, 'And our enemies said, “Before they know or see a thing, we will come into their midst, kill them, and put an end to the work.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 12, 'At that time the Jews who lived nearby came and told us ten times over, “Wherever you turn, they will attack us.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 13, 'So I stationed men behind the lowest sections of the wall, at the vulnerable areas. I stationed them by families with their swords, spears, and bows.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 14, 'After I had made an inspection, I stood up and said to the nobles, the officials, and the rest of the people, “Do not be afraid of them. Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your brothers, your sons and your daughters, your wives and your homes.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 15, 'When our enemies heard that we were aware of their scheme and that God had frustrated it, each of us returned to his own work on the wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 16, 'And from that day on, half of my servants did the work while the other half held spears, shields, bows, and armor. The officers stationed themselves behind all the people of Judah'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 17, 'who were rebuilding the wall. The laborers who carried materials worked with one hand and held a weapon with the other.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 18, 'And each of the builders worked with his sword strapped at his side. But the trumpeter stayed beside me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 19, 'Then I said to the nobles, the officials, and the rest of the people: “The work is great and extensive, and we are spread out far from one another along the wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 20, 'Wherever you hear the sound of the horn, rally to us there. Our God will fight for us!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 21, 'So we continued the work, while half of the men held spears from the break of dawn until the stars came out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 22, 'At that time I also said to the people, “Let every man and his servant spend the night inside Jerusalem, so that they can stand guard by night and work by day.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 4, 23, 'So neither I nor my brothers nor my servants nor the guards with me changed out of our clothes; each carried his weapon, even to go for water.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 1, 'About that time there was a great outcry from the people and their wives against their fellow Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 2, 'Some were saying, “We and our sons and daughters are numerous. We must get grain in order to eat and stay alive.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 3, 'Others were saying, “We are mortgaging our fields, our vineyards, and our homes to get grain during the famine.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 4, 'Still others were saying, “We have borrowed money to pay the king’s tax on our fields and vineyards.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 5, 'We and our children are just like our countrymen and their children, yet we are subjecting our sons and daughters to slavery. Some of our daughters are already enslaved, but we are powerless to redeem them because our fields and vineyards belong to others.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 6, 'When I heard their outcry and these complaints, I became extremely angry,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 7, 'and after serious thought I rebuked the nobles and officials, saying, “You are exacting usury from your own brothers!” So I called a large assembly against them'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 8, 'and said, “We have done our best to buy back our Jewish brothers who were sold to foreigners, but now you are selling your own brothers, that they may be sold back to us!” But they remained silent, for they could find nothing to say.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 9, 'So I continued, “What you are doing is not right. Shouldn’t you walk in the fear of our God to avoid the reproach of our foreign enemies?'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 10, 'I, as well as my brothers and my servants, have been lending the people money and grain. Please, let us stop this usury.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 11, 'Please restore to them immediately their fields, vineyards, olive groves, and houses, along with the percentage of the money, grain, new wine, and oil that you have been assessing them.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 12, '“We will restore it,” they replied, “and will require nothing more from them. We will do as you say.” So I summoned the priests and required of the nobles and officials an oath that they would do what they had promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 13, 'I also shook out the folds of my robe and said, “May God likewise shake out of His house and possession every man who does not keep this promise. May such a man be shaken out and have nothing!” The whole assembly said, “Amen,” and they praised the LORD. And the people did as they had promised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 14, 'Furthermore, from the day King Artaxerxes appointed me to be their governor in the land of Judah, from his twentieth year until his thirty-second year (twelve years total), neither I nor my brothers ate the food allotted to the governor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 15, 'The governors before me had heavily burdened the people, taking from them bread and wine plus forty shekels of silver. Their servants also oppressed the people, but I did not do this because of my fear of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 16, 'Instead, I devoted myself to the construction of the wall, and all my servants were gathered there for the work; we did not acquire any land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 17, 'There were 150 Jews and officials at my table, besides the guests from the surrounding nations.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 18, 'Each day one ox, six choice sheep, and some fowl were prepared for me, and once every ten days an abundance of all kinds of wine was provided. But I did not demand the food allotted to the governor, because the burden on the people was so heavy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 5, 19, 'Remember me favorably, O my God, for all that I have done for this people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 1, 'When Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem the Arab, and the rest of our enemies heard that I had rebuilt the wall and not a gap was left—though to that time I had not yet installed the doors in the gates—'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 2, 'Sanballat and Geshem sent me this message: “Come, let us meet together in one of the villages on the plain of Ono.” But they were planning to harm me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 3, 'So I sent messengers to them, saying, “I am doing a great work and cannot come down. Why should the work stop while I leave it to go down to you?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 4, 'Four times they sent me the same message, and each time I gave the same reply.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 5, 'The fifth time, Sanballat sent me this same message by his young servant, who had in his hand an unsealed letter'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 6, 'that read: “It is reported among the nations—and Geshem agrees—that you and the Jews are plotting to revolt, and this is why you are building the wall. According to these reports, you are to become their king,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 7, 'and you have even appointed prophets in Jerusalem to proclaim on your behalf: ‘There is a king in Judah.’ Soon these rumors will reach the ears of the king. So come, let us confer together.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 8, 'Then I sent him this reply: “There is nothing to these rumors you are spreading; you are inventing them in your own mind.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 9, 'For they were all trying to frighten us, saying, “Their hands will be weakened in the work, and it will never be finished.” But now, my God, strengthen my hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 10, 'Later, I went to the house of Shemaiah son of Delaiah, the son of Mehetabel, who was confined to his house. He said: “Let us meet at the house of God inside the temple. Let us shut the temple doors because they are coming to kill you— by night they are coming to kill you!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 11, 'But I replied, “Should a man like me run away? Should one like me go into the temple to save his own life? I will not go!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 12, 'I realized that God had not sent him, but that he had uttered this prophecy against me because Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 13, 'He had been hired to intimidate me so that I would sin by doing as he suggested, so they could give me a bad name in order to discredit me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 14, 'O my God, remember Tobiah and Sanballat for what they have done, and also Noadiah the prophetess and the other prophets who tried to intimidate me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 15, 'So the wall was completed in fifty-two days, on the twenty-fifth of Elul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 16, 'When all our enemies heard about this, all the surrounding nations were afraid and disheartened, for they realized that this task had been accomplished by our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 17, 'Also in those days, the nobles of Judah sent many letters to Tobiah, and Tobiah’s letters came back to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 18, 'For many in Judah were bound by oath to him, since he was a son-in-law of Shecaniah son of Arah, and his son Jehohanan had married the daughter of Meshullam son of Berechiah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 6, 19, 'Moreover, these nobles kept reporting to me Tobiah’s good deeds, and they relayed my words to him. And Tobiah sent letters to intimidate me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 1, 'When the wall had been rebuilt and I had set the doors in place, the gatekeepers, singers, and Levites were appointed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 2, 'Then I put my brother Hanani in charge of Jerusalem, along with Hananiah the commander of the fortress, because he was a faithful man who feared God more than most.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 3, 'And I told them, “Do not open the gates of Jerusalem until the sun is hot. While the guards are on duty, keep the doors shut and securely fastened. And appoint the residents of Jerusalem as guards, some at their posts and some at their own homes.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 4, 'Now the city was large and spacious, but there were few people in it, and the houses had not yet been rebuilt.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 5, 'Then my God put it into my heart to assemble the nobles, the officials, and the people to be enrolled by genealogy. I found the genealogical register of those who had first returned, and I found the following written in it:'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 6, 'These are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 7, 'accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, and Baanah. This is the count of the men of Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 8, 'the descendants of Parosh, 2,172;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 9, 'the descendants of Shephatiah, 372;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 10, 'the descendants of Arah, 652;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 11, 'the descendants of Pahath-moab (through the line of Jeshua and Joab), 2,818;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 12, 'the descendants of Elam, 1,254;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 13, 'the descendants of Zattu, 845;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 14, 'the descendants of Zaccai, 760;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 15, 'the descendants of Binnui, 648;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 16, 'the descendants of Bebai, 628;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 17, 'the descendants of Azgad, 2,322;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 18, 'the descendants of Adonikam, 667;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 19, 'the descendants of Bigvai, 2,067;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 20, 'the descendants of Adin, 655;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 21, 'the descendants of Ater (through Hezekiah), 98;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 22, 'the descendants of Hashum, 328;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 23, 'the descendants of Bezai, 324;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 24, 'the descendants of Hariph, 112;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 25, 'the descendants of Gibeon, 95;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 26, 'the men of Bethlehem and Netophah, 188;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 27, 'the men of Anathoth, 128;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 28, 'the men of Beth-azmaveth, 42;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 29, 'the men of Kiriath-jearim, Chephirah, and Beeroth, 743;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 30, 'the men of Ramah and Geba, 621;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 31, 'the men of Michmash, 122;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 32, 'the men of Bethel and Ai, 123;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 33, 'the men of the other Nebo, 52;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 34, 'the descendants of the other Elam, 1,254;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 35, 'the descendants of Harim, 320;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 36, 'the men of Jericho, 345;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 37, 'the men of Lod, Hadid, and Ono, 721;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 38, 'and the descendants of Senaah, 3,930.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 39, 'The priests: the descendants of Jedaiah (through the house of Jeshua), 973;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 40, 'the descendants of Immer, 1,052;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 41, 'the descendants of Pashhur, 1,247;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 42, 'and the descendants of Harim, 1,017.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 43, 'The Levites: the descendants of Jeshua (through Kadmiel, through the line of Hodevah), 74.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 44, 'The singers: the descendants of Asaph, 148.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 45, 'The gatekeepers: the descendants of Shallum, the descendants of Ater, the descendants of Talmon, the descendants of Akkub, the descendants of Hatita, and the descendants of Shobai, 138 in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 46, 'The temple servants: the descendants of Ziha, the descendants of Hasupha, the descendants of Tabbaoth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 47, 'the descendants of Keros, the descendants of Sia, the descendants of Padon,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 48, 'the descendants of Lebanah, the descendants of Hagabah, the descendants of Shalmai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 49, 'the descendants of Hanan, the descendants of Giddel, the descendants of Gahar,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 50, 'the descendants of Reaiah, the descendants of Rezin, the descendants of Nekoda,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 51, 'the descendants of Gazzam, the descendants of Uzza, the descendants of Paseah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 52, 'the descendants of Besai, the descendants of Meunim, the descendants of Nephushesim,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 53, 'the descendants of Bakbuk, the descendants of Hakupha, the descendants of Harhur,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 54, 'the descendants of Bazlith, the descendants of Mehida, the descendants of Harsha,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 55, 'the descendants of Barkos, the descendants of Sisera, the descendants of Temah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 56, 'the descendants of Neziah, and the descendants of Hatipha.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 57, 'The descendants of the servants of Solomon: the descendants of Sotai, the descendants of Sophereth, the descendants of Perida,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 58, 'the descendants of Jaala, the descendants of Darkon, the descendants of Giddel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 59, 'the descendants of Shephatiah, the descendants of Hattil, the descendants of Pochereth-hazzebaim, and the descendants of Amon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 60, 'The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 61, 'The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer, but could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 62, 'the descendants of Delaiah, the descendants of Tobiah, and the descendants of Nekoda, 642 in all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 63, 'And from among the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai (who had married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 64, 'These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 65, 'The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest to consult the Urim and Thummim.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 66, 'The whole assembly numbered 42,360,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 67, 'in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 245 male and female singers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 68, 'They had 736 horses, 245 mules,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 69, '435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 70, 'Some of the heads of the families contributed to the project. The governor gave to the treasury 1,000 darics of gold, 50 bowls, and 530 priestly garments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 71, 'And some of the heads of the families gave to the treasury for the project 20,000 darics of gold and 2,200 minas of silver.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 72, 'The rest of the people gave a total of 20,000 darics of gold, 2,000 minas of silver, and 67 priestly garments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 7, 73, 'So the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, and temple servants, along with some of the people and the rest of the Israelites, settled in their own towns. And by the seventh month the Israelites had settled in their towns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 1, 'At that time all the people gathered together in the square before the Water Gate, and they asked Ezra the scribe to bring out the Book of the Law of Moses, which the LORD had commanded for Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 2, 'On the first day of the seventh month, Ezra the priest brought the Law before the assembly of men and women and all who could listen and understand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 3, 'So Ezra read it aloud from daybreak until noon as he faced the square before the Water Gate, in front of the men and women and those who could understand. And all the people listened attentively to the Book of the Law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 4, 'Ezra the scribe stood on a high wooden platform built for this occasion. At his right side stood Mattithiah, Shema, Anaiah, Uriah, Hilkiah, and Maaseiah, and at his left were Pedaiah, Mishael, Malchijah, Hashum, Hash-baddanah, Zechariah, and Meshullam.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 5, 'Ezra opened the book in full view of all the people, since he was standing above them all, and as he opened it, all the people stood up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 6, 'Then Ezra blessed the LORD, the great God, and with their hands uplifted, all the people said, “Amen, Amen!” Then they bowed down and worshiped the LORD with their faces to the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 7, 'The Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodiah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, and Pelaiah—instructed the people in the Law as they stood in their places.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 8, 'So they read from the Book of the Law of God, explaining it and giving insight, so that the people could understand what was being read.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 9, 'Nehemiah the governor, Ezra the priest and scribe, and the Levites who were instructing the people said to all of them, “This day is holy to the LORD your God. Do not mourn or weep.” For all the people were weeping as they heard the words of the Law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 10, 'Then Nehemiah told them, “Go and eat what is rich, drink what is sweet, and send out portions to those who have nothing prepared, since today is holy to our Lord. Do not grieve, for the joy of the LORD is your strength.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 11, 'And the Levites calmed all the people, saying, “Be still, since today is holy. Do not grieve.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 12, 'Then all the people began to eat and drink, to send out portions, and to rejoice greatly, because they understood the words that had been made known to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 13, 'On the second day of the month, the heads of all the families, along with the priests and Levites, gathered around Ezra the scribe to study the words of the Law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 14, 'And they found written in the Law, which the LORD had commanded through Moses, that the Israelites were to dwell in booths during the feast of the seventh month.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 15, 'So they proclaimed this message and spread it throughout their towns and in Jerusalem, saying, “Go out to the hill country and bring back branches of olive, wild olive, myrtle, palm, and other leafy trees, to make booths, as it is written.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 16, 'And the people went out, brought back branches, and made booths on their own rooftops, in their courtyards, in the court of the house of God, and in the squares by the Water Gate and by the Gate of Ephraim.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 17, 'The whole assembly who had returned from exile made booths and lived in them. From the days of Joshua son of Nun until that day, the Israelites had not celebrated like this. And there was great rejoicing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 8, 18, 'Day after day, from the first day to the last, Ezra read from the Book of the Law of God. The Israelites kept the feast for seven days, and on the eighth day they held an assembly, according to the ordinance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 1, 'On the twenty-fourth day of the same month, the Israelites gathered together, fasting and wearing sackcloth, with dust on their heads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 2, 'Those of Israelite descent separated themselves from all the foreigners, and they stood and confessed their sins and the iniquities of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 3, 'While they stood in their places, they read from the Book of the Law of the LORD their God for a quarter of the day, and they spent another quarter of the day in confession and worship of the LORD their God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 4, 'And the Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani—stood on the raised platform and cried out in a loud voice to the LORD their God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 5, 'Then the Levites—Jeshua, Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabneiah, Sherebiah, Hodiah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah—said, “Stand up and bless the LORD your God from everlasting to everlasting: Blessed be Your glorious name, and may it be exalted above all blessing and praise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 6, 'You alone are the LORD. You created the heavens, the highest heavens with all their host, the earth and all that is on it, the seas and all that is in them. You give life to all things, and the host of heaven worships You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 7, 'You are the LORD, the God who chose Abram, who brought him out of Ur of the Chaldeans and gave him the name Abraham.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 8, 'You found his heart faithful before You, and made a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanites and Hittites, of the Amorites and Perizzites, of the Jebusites and Girgashites— to give it to his descendants. You have kept Your promise, because You are righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 9, 'You saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt; You heard their cry at the Red Sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 10, 'You performed signs and wonders against Pharaoh, all his officials, and all the people of his land, for You knew they had acted with arrogance against our fathers. You made a name for Yourself that endures to this day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 11, 'You divided the sea before them, and they crossed through it on dry ground. You hurled their pursuers into the depths like a stone into raging waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 12, 'You led them with a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night, to light for them the way in which they should travel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 13, 'You came down on Mount Sinai and spoke with them from heaven. You gave them just ordinances, true laws, and good statutes and commandments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 14, 'You revealed to them Your holy Sabbath and gave them commandments and statutes and laws through Your servant Moses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 15, 'In their hunger You gave them bread from heaven; in their thirst You brought them water from the rock. You told them to go in and possess the land which You had sworn to give them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 16, 'But they and our fathers became arrogant and stiff-necked and did not obey Your commandments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 17, 'They refused to listen and failed to remember the wonders You performed among them. They stiffened their necks and appointed a leader to return them to their bondage in Egypt. But You are a forgiving God, gracious and compassionate, slow to anger and rich in loving devotion, and You did not forsake them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 18, 'Even when they cast for themselves an image of a calf and said, ‘This is your God who brought you up out of Egypt,’ and when they committed terrible blasphemies,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 19, 'You in Your great compassion did not forsake them in the wilderness. By day the pillar of cloud never turned away from guiding them on their path; and by the night the pillar of fire illuminated the way they should go.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 20, 'You gave Your good Spirit to instruct them. You did not withhold Your manna from their mouths, and You gave them water for their thirst.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 21, 'For forty years You sustained them in the wilderness, so that they lacked nothing. Their clothes did not wear out and their feet did not swell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 22, 'You gave them kingdoms and peoples and allotted to them every corner of the land. So they took the land of Sihon king of Heshbon and of Og king of Bashan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 23, 'You multiplied their descendants like the stars of heaven and brought them to the land You had told their fathers to enter and possess.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 24, 'So their descendants went in and possessed the land; You subdued before them the Canaanites dwelling in the land. You delivered into their hands the kings and peoples of the land, to do with them as they wished.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 25, 'They captured fortified cities and fertile land and took houses full of all goods, wells already dug, vineyards, olive groves, and fruit trees in abundance. So they ate and were filled; they grew fat and delighted in Your great goodness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 26, 'But they were disobedient and rebelled against You; they flung Your law behind their backs. They killed Your prophets, who had admonished them to return to You. They committed terrible blasphemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 27, 'So You delivered them into the hands of enemies who oppressed them, and in their time of distress they cried out to You. From heaven You heard them, and in Your great compassion You gave them deliverers who saved them from the hands of their enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 28, 'But as soon as they had rest, they again did evil in Your sight. So You abandoned them to the hands of their enemies, who had dominion over them. When they cried out to You again, You heard from heaven, and You delivered them many times in Your compassion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 29, 'You admonished them to turn back to Your law, but they were arrogant and disobeyed Your commandments. They sinned against Your ordinances, by which a man will live if he practices them. They stubbornly shrugged their shoulders; they stiffened their necks and would not obey.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 30, 'You were patient with them for many years, and Your Spirit admonished them through Your prophets. Yet they would not listen, so You gave them into the hands of the neighboring peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 31, 'But in Your great compassion, You did not put an end to them; nor did You forsake them, for You are a gracious and compassionate God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 32, 'So now, our God, the great and mighty and awesome God who keeps His gracious covenant, do not view lightly all the hardship that has come upon us, and upon our kings and leaders, our priests and prophets, our ancestors and all Your people, from the days of the kings of Assyria until today.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 33, 'You are just in all that has befallen us, because You have acted faithfully, while we have acted wickedly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 34, 'Our kings and leaders and priests and fathers did not obey Your law or listen to Your commandments and warnings that You gave them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 35, 'For even while they were in their kingdom, with the abundant goodness that You had given them, and in the spacious and fertile land that You had set before them, they would not serve You or turn from their wicked ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 36, 'So here we are today as slaves in the land You gave our fathers to enjoy its fruit and goodness— here we are as slaves!'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 37, 'Its abundant harvest goes to the kings You have set over us because of our sins. And they rule over our bodies and our livestock as they please. We are in great distress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 9, 38, 'In view of all this, we make a binding agreement, putting it in writing and sealing it with the names of our leaders, Levites, and priests.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 1, 'Now these were the ones who sealed the document: Nehemiah the governor, son of Hacaliah, and also Zedekiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 2, 'Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 3, 'Pashhur, Amariah, Malchijah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 4, 'Hattush, Shebaniah, Malluch,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 5, 'Harim, Meremoth, Obadiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 6, 'Daniel, Ginnethon, Baruch,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 7, 'Meshullam, Abijah, Mijamin,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 8, 'Maaziah, Bilgai, and Shemaiah. These were the priests.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 9, 'The Levites: Jeshua son of Azaniah, Binnui of the sons of Henadad, Kadmiel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 10, 'and their associates: Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, Hanan,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 11, 'Mica, Rehob, Hashabiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 12, 'Zaccur, Sherebiah, Shebaniah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 13, 'Hodiah, Bani, and Beninu.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 14, 'And the leaders of the people: Parosh, Pahath-moab, Elam, Zattu, Bani,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 15, 'Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 16, 'Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 17, 'Ater, Hezekiah, Azzur,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 18, 'Hodiah, Hashum, Bezai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 19, 'Hariph, Anathoth, Nebai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 20, 'Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 21, 'Meshezabel, Zadok, Jaddua,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 22, 'Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 23, 'Hoshea, Hananiah, Hasshub,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 24, 'Hallohesh, Pilha, Shobek,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 25, 'Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 26, 'Ahijah, Hanan, Anan,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 27, 'Malluch, Harim, and Baanah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 28, '“The rest of the people—the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, temple servants, and all who had separated themselves from the people of the land to obey the Law of God—along with their wives and all their sons and daughters who are able to understand,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 29, 'hereby join with their noble brothers and commit themselves with a sworn oath to follow the Law of God given through His servant Moses and to carefully obey all the commandments, ordinances, and statutes of the LORD our Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 30, 'We will not give our daughters in marriage to the people of the land, and we will not take their daughters for our sons.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 31, 'When the people of the land bring merchandise or any kind of grain to sell on the Sabbath day, we will not buy from them on a Sabbath or holy day. Every seventh year we will let the fields lie fallow, and will cancel every debt.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 32, 'We also place ourselves under the obligation to contribute a third of a shekel yearly for the service of the house of our God:'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 33, 'for the showbread, for the regular grain offerings and burnt offerings, for the Sabbath offerings, for the New Moons and appointed feasts, for the holy offerings, for the sin offerings to make atonement for Israel, and for all the duties of the house of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 34, 'We have cast lots among the priests, Levites, and people for the donation of wood by our families at the appointed times each year. They are to bring it to the house of our God to burn on the altar of the LORD our God, as it is written in the Law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 35, 'We will also bring the firstfruits of our land and of every fruit tree to the house of the LORD year by year.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 36, 'And we will bring the firstborn of our sons and our livestock, as it is written in the Law, and will bring the firstborn of our herds and flocks to the house of our God, to the priests who minister in the house of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 37, 'Moreover, we will bring to the priests at the storerooms of the house of our God the firstfruits of our dough, of our grain offerings, of the fruit of all our trees, and of our new wine and oil. A tenth of our produce belongs to the Levites, so that they shall receive tithes in all the towns where we labor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 38, 'A priest of Aaron’s line is to accompany the Levites when they collect the tenth, and the Levites are to bring a tenth of these tithes to the storerooms of the treasury in the house of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 10, 39, 'For the Israelites and the Levites are to bring the contributions of grain, new wine, and oil to the storerooms where the articles of the sanctuary are kept and where the ministering priests, the gatekeepers, and the singers stay. Thus we will not neglect the house of our God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 1, 'Now the leaders of the people settled in Jerusalem, and the rest of the people cast lots to bring one out of ten to live in the holy city of Jerusalem, while the remaining nine were to dwell in their own towns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 2, 'And the people blessed all the men who volunteered to live in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 3, 'These are the heads of the provinces who settled in Jerusalem. (In the villages of Judah, however, each lived on his own property in their towns—the Israelites, priests, Levites, temple servants, and descendants of Solomon’s servants—'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 4, 'while some of the descendants of Judah and Benjamin settled in Jerusalem.) From the descendants of Judah: Athaiah son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalalel, a descendant of Perez;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 5, 'and Maaseiah son of Baruch, the son of Col-hozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, a descendant of Shelah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 6, 'The descendants of Perez who settled in Jerusalem totaled 468 men of valor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 7, 'From the descendants of Benjamin: Sallu son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jeshaiah;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 8, 'and his followers Gabbai and Sallai—928 men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 9, 'Joel son of Zichri was the officer over them, and Judah son of Hassenuah was over the Second District of the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 10, 'From the priests:'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 11, 'Jedaiah son of Joiarib; Jachin; Seraiah son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the chief official of the house of God;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 12, 'and their associates who did the work at the temple—822 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 13, 'Adaiah son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; and his associates, the leaders of families—242 men;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 14, 'Amashai son of Azarel, the son of Ahzai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer; and his associates—128 mighty men of valor. Zabdiel son of Haggedolim was their overseer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 15, 'From the Levites: Shemaiah son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 16, 'Shabbethai and Jozabad, two leaders of the Levites, who supervised the work outside the house of God;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 17, 'Mattaniah son of Mica, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, who led in thanksgiving and prayer; Bakbukiah, second among his associates; and Abda son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 18, 'The Levites in the holy city totaled 284.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 19, 'And the gatekeepers: Akkub, Talmon, and their associates, who kept watch at the gates—172 men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 20, 'The rest of the Israelites, with the priests and Levites, were in all the villages of Judah, each on his own inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 21, 'The temple servants lived on the hill of Ophel, with Ziha and Gishpa over them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 22, 'Now the overseer of the Levites in Jerusalem was Uzzi son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Mica. He was one of Asaph’s descendants, who were the singers in charge of the service of the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 23, 'For there was a command from the king concerning the singers, an ordinance regulating their daily activities.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 24, 'Pethahiah son of Meshezabel, a descendant of Zerah son of Judah, was the king’s agent in every matter concerning the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 25, 'As for the villages with their fields, some of the people of Judah lived in Kiriath-arba, Dibon, Jekabzeel, and their villages;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 26, 'in Jeshua, Moladah, and Beth-pelet;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 27, 'in Hazar-shual; in Beersheba and its villages;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 28, 'in Ziklag; in Meconah and its villages;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 29, 'in En-rimmon, Zorah, Jarmuth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 30, 'Zanoah, Adullam, and their villages; in Lachish and its fields; and in Azekah and its villages. So they settled from Beersheba all the way to the Valley of Hinnom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 31, 'The descendants of Benjamin from Geba lived in Michmash, Aija, and Bethel with its villages;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 32, 'in Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 33, 'Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 34, 'Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 35, 'Lod, and Ono; and in the Valley of the Craftsmen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 11, 36, 'And some divisions of the Levites of Judah settled in Benjamin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 1, 'Now these are the priests and Levites who went up with Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and with Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 2, 'Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 3, 'Shecaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 4, 'Iddo, Ginnethon, Abijah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 5, 'Mijamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 6, 'Shemaiah, Joiarib, Jedaiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 7, 'Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, and Jedaiah. These were the leaders of the priests and their associates in the days of Jeshua.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 8, 'The Levites were Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, and Mattaniah, who, with his associates, led the songs of thanksgiving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 9, 'Bakbukiah and Unni, their associates, stood across from them in the services.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 10, 'Jeshua was the father of Joiakim, Joiakim was the father of Eliashib, Eliashib was the father of Joiada,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 11, 'Joiada was the father of Jonathan, and Jonathan was the father of Jaddua.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 12, 'In the days of Joiakim, these were the heads of the priestly families: of the family of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 13, 'of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 14, 'of Malluchi, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 15, 'of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 16, 'of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 17, 'of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin and of Moadiah, Piltai;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 18, 'of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jonathan;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 19, 'of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 20, 'of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 21, 'of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; and of Jedaiah, Nethanel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 22, 'In the days of Eliashib, Joiada, Johanan, and Jaddua, during the reign of Darius the Persian, the heads of the families of the Levites and priests were recorded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 23, 'As for the descendants of Levi, the family heads up to the days of Johanan son of Eliashib were recorded in the Book of the Chronicles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 24, 'The leaders of the Levites were Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua son of Kadmiel, along with their associates, who stood across from them to give praise and thanksgiving as one section alternated with the other, as prescribed by David the man of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 25, 'Mattaniah, Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, and Akkub were gatekeepers who guarded the storerooms at the gates.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 26, 'They served in the days of Joiakim son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor and Ezra the priest and scribe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 27, 'At the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, the Levites were sought out from all their homes and brought to Jerusalem to celebrate the joyous dedication with thanksgiving and singing, accompanied by cymbals, harps, and lyres.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 28, 'The singers were also assembled from the region around Jerusalem, from the villages of the Netophathites,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 29, 'from Beth-gilgal, and from the fields of Geba and Azmaveth, for they had built villages for themselves around Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 30, 'After the priests and Levites had purified themselves, they purified the people, the gates, and the wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 31, 'Then I brought the leaders of Judah up on the wall, and I appointed two great thanksgiving choirs. One was to proceed along the top of the wall to the right, toward the Dung Gate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 32, 'Hoshaiah and half the leaders of Judah followed,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 33, 'along with Azariah, Ezra, Meshullam,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 34, 'Judah, Benjamin, Shemaiah, Jeremiah,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 35, 'and some of the priests with trumpets, and also Zechariah son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 36, 'and his associates—Shemaiah, Azarel, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethanel, Judah, and Hanani—with the musical instruments prescribed by David the man of God. Ezra the scribe led the procession.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 37, 'At the Fountain Gate they climbed the steps of the City of David on the ascent to the wall and passed above the house of David to the Water Gate on the east.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 38, 'The second thanksgiving choir proceeded to the left, and I followed it with half the people along the top of the wall, past the Tower of the Ovens to the Broad Wall,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 39, 'over the Gate of Ephraim, the Jeshanah Gate, the Fish Gate, the Tower of Hananel, and the Tower of the Hundred, as far as the Sheep Gate. And they stopped at the Gate of the Guard.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 40, 'The two thanksgiving choirs then stood in the house of God, as did I, along with the half of the officials accompanying me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 41, 'as well as the priests with their trumpets—Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Micaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah—'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 42, 'and also Maaseiah, Shemaiah, Eleazar, Uzzi, Jehohanan, Malchijah, Elam, and Ezer. Then the choirs sang out under the direction of Jezrahiah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 43, 'On that day they offered great sacrifices, rejoicing because God had given them great joy. The women and children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard from afar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 44, 'And on that same day men were appointed over the rooms that housed the supplies, contributions, firstfruits, and tithes. The portions specified by the Law for the priests and Levites were gathered into these storerooms from the fields of the villages, because Judah rejoiced over the priests and Levites who were serving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 45, 'They performed the service of their God and the service of purification, along with the singers and gatekeepers, as David and his son Solomon had prescribed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 46, 'For long ago, in the days of David and Asaph, there were directors for the singers and for the songs of praise and thanksgiving to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 12, 47, 'So in the days of Zerubbabel and Nehemiah, all Israel contributed the daily portions for the singers and gatekeepers. They also set aside daily portions for the Levites, and the Levites set aside daily portions for the descendants of Aaron.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 1, 'At that time the Book of Moses was read aloud in the hearing of the people, and in it they found the passage stating that no Ammonite or Moabite should ever enter the assembly of God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 2, 'because they had not met the Israelites with food and water, but had hired Balaam to call down a curse against them (although our God had turned the curse into a blessing).'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 3, 'As soon as the people heard this law, they excluded from Israel all of foreign descent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 4, 'Now before this, Eliashib the priest, a relative of Tobiah, had been put in charge of the storerooms of the house of our God'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 5, 'and had prepared for Tobiah a large room where they had previously stored the grain offerings, the frankincense, the temple articles, and the tithes of grain, new wine, and oil prescribed for the Levites, singers, and gatekeepers, along with the contributions for the priests.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 6, 'While all this was happening, I was not in Jerusalem, because I had returned to Artaxerxes king of Babylon in the thirty-second year of his reign. Some time later I obtained leave from the king'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 7, 'to return to Jerusalem. Then I discovered the evil that Eliashib had done on behalf of Tobiah by providing him a room in the courts of the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 8, 'And I was greatly displeased and threw all of Tobiah’s household goods out of the room.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 9, 'Then I ordered that the rooms be purified, and I had the articles of the house of God restored to them, along with the grain offerings and frankincense.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 10, 'I also learned that because the portions for the Levites had not been given to them, all the Levites and singers responsible for performing the service had gone back to their own fields.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 11, 'So I rebuked the officials and asked, “Why has the house of God been neglected?” Then I gathered the Levites and singers together and stationed them at their posts,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 12, 'and all Judah brought a tenth of the grain, new wine, and oil into the storerooms.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 13, 'I appointed as treasurers over the storerooms Shelemiah the priest, Zadok the scribe, and Pedaiah of the Levites, with Hanan son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah, to assist them, because they were considered trustworthy. They were responsible for distributing the supplies to their fellow Levites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 14, 'Remember me for this, O my God, and do not blot out my deeds of loving devotion for the house of my God and for its services.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 15, 'In those days I saw people in Judah treading winepresses on the Sabbath and bringing in grain and loading it on donkeys, along with wine, grapes, and figs. All kinds of goods were being brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day. So I warned them against selling food on that day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 16, 'Additionally, men of Tyre who lived there were importing fish and all kinds of merchandise and selling them on the Sabbath to the people of Judah in Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 17, 'Then I rebuked the nobles of Judah and asked, “What is this evil you are doing—profaning the Sabbath day?'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 18, 'Did not your forefathers do the same things, so that our God brought all this disaster on us and on this city? And now you are rekindling His wrath against Israel by profaning the Sabbath!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 19, 'When the evening shadows began to fall on the gates of Jerusalem, just before the Sabbath, I ordered that the gates be shut and not opened until after the Sabbath. I posted some of my servants at the gates so that no load could enter on the Sabbath day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 20, 'Once or twice, the merchants and those who sell all kinds of goods camped outside Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 21, 'but I warned them, “Why are you camping in front of the wall? If you do it again, I will lay hands on you.” From that time on, they did not return on the Sabbath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 22, 'Then I instructed the Levites to purify themselves and guard the gates in order to keep the Sabbath day holy. Remember me for this as well, O my God, and show me mercy according to Your abundant loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 23, 'In those days I also saw Jews who had married women from Ashdod, Ammon, and Moab.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 24, 'Half of their children spoke the language of Ashdod or of the other peoples, but could not speak the language of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 25, 'I rebuked them and called down curses on them. I beat some of these men and pulled out their hair. Then I made them take an oath before God and said, “You must not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters as wives for your sons or for yourselves!'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 26, 'Did not King Solomon of Israel sin in matters like this? There was not a king like him among many nations, and he was loved by his God, who made him king over all Israel—yet foreign women drew him into sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 27, 'Must we now hear that you too are doing all this terrible evil and acting unfaithfully against our God by marrying foreign women?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 28, 'Even one of the sons of Jehoiada son of Eliashib the high priest had become a son-in-law to Sanballat the Horonite. Therefore I drove him away from me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 29, 'Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood and the covenant of the priesthood and of the Levites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 30, 'Thus I purified the priests and Levites from everything foreign, and I assigned specific duties to each of the priests and Levites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Nehemiah', 16, 13, 31, 'I also arranged for contributions of wood at the appointed times, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, with favor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 1, 'This is what happened in the days of Xerxes, who reigned over 127 provinces from India to Cush.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 2, 'In those days King Xerxes sat on his royal throne in the citadel of Susa.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 3, 'In the third year of his reign, Xerxes held a feast for all his officials and servants. The military leaders of Persia and Media were there, along with the nobles and princes of the provinces.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 4, 'And for a full 180 days he displayed the glorious riches of his kingdom and the magnificent splendor of his greatness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 5, 'At the end of this time, in the garden court of the royal palace, the king held a seven-day feast for all the people in the citadel of Susa, from the least to the greatest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 6, 'Hangings of white and blue linen were fastened with cords of fine white and purple material to silver rings on the marble pillars. Gold and silver couches were arranged on a mosaic pavement of porphyry, marble, mother-of-pearl, and other costly stones.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 7, 'Beverages were served in an array of goblets of gold, each with a different design, and the royal wine flowed freely, according to the king’s bounty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 8, 'By order of the king, no limit was placed on the drinking, and every official of his household was to serve each man whatever he desired.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 9, 'Queen Vashti also gave a banquet for the women in the royal palace of King Xerxes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 10, 'On the seventh day, when the king’s heart was merry with wine, he ordered the seven eunuchs who served him—Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, Abagtha, Zethar, and Carkas—'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 11, 'to bring Queen Vashti before him, wearing her royal crown, to display her beauty to the people and officials. For she was beautiful to behold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 12, 'Queen Vashti, however, refused to come at the king’s command brought by his eunuchs. And the king became furious, and his anger burned within him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 13, 'Then the king consulted the wise men who knew the times, for it was customary for him to confer with the experts in law and justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 14, 'His closest advisors were Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media who had personal access to the king and ranked highest in the kingdom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 15, '“According to law,” he asked, “what should be done with Queen Vashti, since she refused to obey the command of King Xerxes delivered by the eunuchs?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 16, 'And in the presence of the king and his princes, Memucan replied, “Queen Vashti has wronged not only the king, but all the princes and the peoples in all the provinces of King Xerxes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 17, 'For the conduct of the queen will become known to all women, causing them to despise their husbands and say, ‘King Xerxes ordered Queen Vashti to be brought before him, but she did not come.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 18, 'This very day the noble women of Persia and Media who have heard about the queen’s conduct will say the same thing to all the king’s officials, resulting in much contempt and wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 19, 'So if it pleases the king, let him issue a royal decree, and let it be recorded in the laws of Persia and Media so that it cannot be repealed, that Vashti shall never again enter the presence of King Xerxes, and that her royal position shall be given to a woman better than she.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 20, 'The edict the king issues will be heard throughout his vast kingdom—and so all women, from the least to the greatest, will honor their husbands.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 21, 'The king and his princes were pleased with this counsel; so the king did as Memucan had advised.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 1, 22, 'He sent letters to all the provinces of the kingdom, to each province in its own script and to each people in their own language, proclaiming that every man should be master of his own household.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 1, 'Some time later, when the anger of King Xerxes had subsided, he remembered Vashti and what she had done, and what had been decreed against her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 2, 'Then the king’s attendants proposed, “Let a search be made for beautiful young virgins for the king,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 3, 'and let the king appoint commissioners in each province of his kingdom to assemble all the beautiful young women into the harem at the citadel of Susa. Let them be placed under the care of Hegai, the king’s eunuch in charge of the women, and let them be given beauty treatments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 4, 'Then let the young woman who pleases the king become queen in place of Vashti.” This suggestion pleased the king, and he acted accordingly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 5, 'Now there was at the citadel of Susa a Jewish man from the tribe of Benjamin named Mordecai son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 6, 'He had been carried into exile from Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon among those taken captive with Jeconiah king of Judah.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 7, 'And Mordecai had brought up Hadassah (that is, Esther), the daughter of his uncle, because she did not have a father or mother. The young woman was lovely in form and appearance, and when her father and mother had died, Mordecai had taken her in as his own daughter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 8, 'When the king’s command and edict had been proclaimed, many young women gathered at the citadel of Susa under the care of Hegai. Esther was also taken to the palace and placed under the care of Hegai, the custodian of the women.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 9, 'And the young woman pleased him and obtained his favor, so he quickly provided her with beauty treatments and the special diet. He assigned to her seven select maidservants from the palace and transferred her with them to the best place in the harem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 10, 'Esther did not reveal her people or her lineage, because Mordecai had instructed her not to do so.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 11, 'And every day Mordecai would walk back and forth in front of the court of the harem to learn about Esther’s welfare and what was happening to her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 12, 'In the twelve months before her turn to go to King Xerxes, the harem regulation required each young woman to receive beauty treatments with oil of myrrh for six months, and then with perfumes and cosmetics for another six months.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 13, 'When the young woman would go to the king, she was given whatever she requested to take with her from the harem to the king’s palace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 14, 'She would go there in the evening, and in the morning she would return to a second harem under the care of Shaashgaz, the king’s eunuch in charge of the concubines. She would not return to the king unless he delighted in her and summoned her by name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 15, 'Now Esther was the daughter of Abihail, the uncle from whom Mordecai had adopted her as his own daughter. And when it was her turn to go to the king, she did not ask for anything except what Hegai, the king’s trusted official in charge of the harem, had advised. And Esther found favor in the eyes of everyone who saw her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 16, 'She was taken to King Xerxes in the royal palace in the tenth month, the month of Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 17, 'And the king loved Esther more than all the other women, and she found grace and favor in his sight more than all of the other virgins. So he placed the royal crown upon her head and made her queen in place of Vashti.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 18, 'Then the king held a great banquet, Esther’s banquet, for all his officials and servants. He proclaimed a tax holiday in the provinces and gave gifts worthy of the king’s bounty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 19, 'When the virgins were assembled a second time, Mordecai was sitting at the king’s gate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 20, 'Esther still had not revealed her lineage or her people, just as Mordecai had instructed. She obeyed Mordecai’s command, as she had done under his care.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 21, 'In those days, while Mordecai was sitting at the king’s gate, Bigthan and Teresh, two of the king’s eunuchs who guarded the entrance, grew angry and conspired to assassinate King Xerxes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 22, 'When Mordecai learned of the plot, he reported it to Queen Esther, and she informed the king on Mordecai’s behalf.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 2, 23, 'After the report had been investigated and verified, both officials were hanged on the gallows. And all this was recorded in the Book of the Chronicles in the presence of the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 1, 'After these events, King Xerxes honored Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, elevating him to a position above all the princes who were with him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 2, 'All the royal servants at the king’s gate bowed down and paid homage to Haman, because the king had commanded that this be done for him. But Mordecai would not bow down or pay homage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 3, 'Then the royal servants at the king’s gate asked Mordecai, “Why do you disobey the command of the king?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 4, 'Day after day they warned him, but he would not comply. So they reported it to Haman to see whether Mordecai’s behavior would be tolerated, since he had told them he was a Jew.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 5, 'When Haman saw that Mordecai would not bow down or pay him homage, he was filled with rage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 6, 'And when he learned the identity of Mordecai’s people, he scorned the notion of laying hands on Mordecai alone. Instead, he sought to destroy all of Mordecai’s people, the Jews, throughout the kingdom of Xerxes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 7, 'In the twelfth year of King Xerxes, in the first month, the month of Nisan, the Pur (that is, the lot) was cast before Haman to determine a day and month. And the lot fell on the twelfth month, the month of Adar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 8, 'Then Haman informed King Xerxes, “There is a certain people scattered and dispersed among the peoples of every province of your kingdom. Their laws are different from everyone else’s, and they do not obey the king’s laws. So it is not in the king’s best interest to tolerate them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 9, 'If it pleases the king, let a decree be issued to destroy them, and I will deposit ten thousand talents of silver into the royal treasury to pay those who carry it out.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 10, 'So the king removed the signet ring from his finger and gave it to Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 11, '“Keep your money,” said the king to Haman. “These people are given to you to do with them as you please.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 12, 'On the thirteenth day of the first month, the royal scribes were summoned and the order was written exactly as Haman commanded the royal satraps, the governors of each province, and the officials of each people, in the script of each province and the language of every people. It was written in the name of King Xerxes and sealed with the royal signet ring.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 13, 'And the letters were sent by couriers to each of the royal provinces with the order to destroy, kill, and annihilate all the Jews—young and old, women and children—and to plunder their possessions on a single day, the thirteenth day of Adar, the twelfth month.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 14, 'A copy of the text of the edict was to be issued in every province and published to all the people, so that they would be ready on that day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 3, 15, 'The couriers left, spurred on by the king’s command, and the edict was issued in the citadel of Susa. Then the king and Haman sat down to drink, but the city of Susa was in confusion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 1, 'When Mordecai learned of all that had happened, he tore his clothes, put on sackcloth and ashes, and went out into the middle of the city, wailing loudly and bitterly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 2, 'But he went only as far as the king’s gate, because the law prohibited anyone wearing sackcloth from entering that gate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 3, 'In every province to which the king’s command and edict came, there was great mourning among the Jews. They fasted, wept, and lamented, and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 4, 'When Esther’s maidens and eunuchs came and told her about Mordecai, the queen was overcome with distress. She sent clothes for Mordecai to wear instead of his sackcloth, but he would not accept them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 5, 'Then Esther summoned Hathach, one of the king’s eunuchs appointed to her, and she dispatched him to Mordecai to learn what was troubling him and why.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 6, 'So Hathach went out to Mordecai in the city square in front of the king’s gate,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 7, 'and Mordecai told him all that had happened to him, including the exact amount of money that Haman had promised to pay into the royal treasury in order to destroy the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 8, 'Mordecai also gave Hathach a copy of the written decree issued in Susa for the destruction of the Jews, to show and explain to Esther, urging her to approach the king, implore his favor, and plead before him for her people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 9, 'So Hathach went back and relayed Mordecai’s response to Esther.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 10, 'Then Esther spoke to Hathach and instructed him to tell Mordecai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 11, '“All the royal officials and the people of the king’s provinces know that one law applies to every man or woman who approaches the king in the inner court without being summoned—that he be put to death. Only if the king extends the gold scepter may that person live. But I have not been summoned to appear before the king for the past thirty days.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 12, 'When Esther’s words were relayed to Mordecai,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 13, 'he sent back to her this reply: “Do not imagine that because you are in the king’s palace you alone will escape the fate of all the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 14, 'For if you remain silent at this time, relief and deliverance for the Jews will arise from another place, but you and your father’s house will perish. And who knows if perhaps you have come to the kingdom for such a time as this?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 15, 'Then Esther sent this reply to Mordecai:'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 16, '“Go and assemble all the Jews who can be found in Susa, and fast for me. Do not eat or drink for three days, night or day, and I and my maidens will fast as you do. After that, I will go to the king, even though it is against the law. And if I perish, I perish!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 4, 17, 'So Mordecai went and did all that Esther had instructed him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 1, 'On the third day, Esther put on her royal attire and stood in the inner court of the palace across from the king’s quarters. The king was sitting on his royal throne in the royal courtroom, facing the entrance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 2, 'As soon as the king saw Queen Esther standing in the court, she found favor in his sight. The king extended the gold scepter in his hand toward Esther, and she approached and touched the tip of the scepter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 3, '“What is it, Queen Esther?” the king inquired. “What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be given to you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 4, '“If it pleases the king,” Esther replied, “may the king and Haman come today to the banquet I have prepared for the king.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 5, '“Hurry,” commanded the king, “and bring Haman, so we can do as Esther has requested.” So the king and Haman went to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 6, 'And as they drank their wine, the king said to Esther, “What is your petition? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be fulfilled.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 7, 'Esther replied, “This is my petition and my request:'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 8, 'If I have found favor in the sight of the king, and if it pleases the king to grant my petition and fulfill my request, may the king and Haman come tomorrow to the banquet I will prepare for them. Then I will answer the king’s question.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 9, 'That day Haman went out full of joy and glad of heart. At the king’s gate, however, he saw Mordecai, who did not rise or tremble in fear at his presence. And Haman was filled with rage toward Mordecai.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 10, 'Nevertheless, Haman restrained himself and went home. And calling for his friends and his wife Zeresh,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 11, 'Haman recounted to them his glorious wealth, his many sons, and all the ways the king had honored and promoted him over the other officials and servants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 12, '“What is more,” Haman added, “Queen Esther invited no one but me to join the king at the banquet she prepared, and I am invited back tomorrow along with the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 13, 'Yet none of this satisfies me as long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king’s gate.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 5, 14, 'His wife Zeresh and all his friends told him, “Have them build a gallows fifty cubits high, and ask the king in the morning to have Mordecai hanged on it. Then go to the banquet with the king and enjoy yourself.” The advice pleased Haman, and he had the gallows constructed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 1, 'That night sleep escaped the king; so he ordered the Book of Records, the Chronicles, to be brought in and read to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 2, 'And there it was found recorded that Mordecai had exposed Bigthana and Teresh, two of the eunuchs who guarded the king’s entrance, when they had conspired to assassinate King Xerxes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 3, 'The king inquired, “What honor or dignity has been bestowed on Mordecai for this act?” “Nothing has been done for him,” replied the king’s attendants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 4, '“Who is in the court?” the king asked. Now Haman had just entered the outer court of the palace to ask the king to hang Mordecai on the gallows he had prepared for him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 5, 'So the king’s attendants answered him, “Haman is there, standing in the court.” “Bring him in,” ordered the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 6, 'Haman entered, and the king asked him, “What should be done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor?” Now Haman thought to himself, “Whom would the king be delighted to honor more than me?”');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 7, 'And Haman told the king, “For the man whom the king is delighted to honor,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 8, 'have them bring a royal robe that the king himself has worn and a horse on which the king himself has ridden—one with a royal crest placed on its head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 9, 'Let the robe and the horse be entrusted to one of the king’s most noble princes. Let them array the man the king wants to honor and parade him on the horse through the city square, proclaiming before him, ‘This is what is done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor!’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 10, '“Hurry,” said the king to Haman, “and do just as you proposed. Take the robe and the horse to Mordecai the Jew, who is sitting at the king’s gate. Do not neglect anything that you have suggested.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 11, 'So Haman took the robe and the horse, arrayed Mordecai, and paraded him through the city square, crying out before him, “This is what is done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 12, 'Then Mordecai returned to the king’s gate. But Haman rushed home, with his head covered in grief.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 13, 'Haman told his wife Zeresh and all his friends everything that had happened. His advisers and his wife Zeresh said to him, “Since Mordecai, before whom your downfall has begun, is Jewish, you will not prevail against him—for surely you will fall before him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 6, 14, 'While they were still speaking with Haman, the king’s eunuchs arrived and rushed him to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 1, 'So the king and Haman went to dine with Esther the queen,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 2, 'and as they drank their wine on that second day, the king asked once more, “Queen Esther, what is your petition? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be fulfilled.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 3, 'Queen Esther replied, “If I have found favor in your sight, O king, and if it pleases the king, grant me my life as my petition, and the lives of my people as my request.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 4, 'For my people and I have been sold out to destruction, death, and annihilation. If we had merely been sold as menservants and maidservants, I would have remained silent, because no such distress would justify burdening the king.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 5, 'Then King Xerxes spoke up and asked Queen Esther, “Who is this, and where is the one who would devise such a scheme?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 6, 'Esther replied, “The adversary and enemy is this wicked man—Haman!” And Haman stood in terror before the king and queen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 7, 'In his fury, the king arose from drinking his wine and went to the palace garden, while Haman stayed behind to beg Queen Esther for his life, for he realized that the king was planning a terrible fate for him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 8, 'Just as the king returned from the palace garden to the banquet hall, Haman was falling on the couch where Esther was reclining. The king exclaimed, “Would he actually assault the queen while I am in the palace?” As soon as the words had left the king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 9, 'Then Harbonah, one of the eunuchs attending the king, said: “There is a gallows fifty cubits high at Haman’s house. He had it built for Mordecai, who gave the report that saved the king.” “Hang him on it!” declared the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 7, 10, 'So they hanged Haman on the gallows he had prepared for Mordecai. Then the fury of the king subsided.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 1, 'That same day King Xerxes awarded Queen Esther the estate of Haman, the enemy of the Jews. And Mordecai entered the king’s presence because Esther had revealed his relation to her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 2, 'The king removed the signet ring he had recovered from Haman and presented it to Mordecai. And Esther appointed Mordecai over the estate of Haman.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 3, 'And once again, Esther addressed the king. She fell at his feet weeping and begged him to revoke the evil scheme of Haman the Agagite, which he had devised against the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 4, 'The king extended the gold scepter toward Esther, and she arose and stood before the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 5, '“If it pleases the king,” she said, “and if I have found favor in his sight, and the matter seems proper to the king, and I am pleasing in his sight, may an order be written to revoke the letters that the scheming Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, wrote to destroy the Jews in all the king’s provinces.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 6, 'For how could I bear to see the disaster that would befall my people? How could I bear to see the destruction of my kindred?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 7, 'So King Xerxes said to Esther the Queen and Mordecai the Jew, “Behold, I have given Haman’s estate to Esther, and he was hanged on the gallows because he attacked the Jews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 8, 'Now you may write in the king’s name as you please regarding the Jews, and seal it with the royal signet ring. For a decree that is written in the name of the king and sealed with the royal signet ring cannot be revoked.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 9, 'At once the royal scribes were summoned, and on the twenty-third day of the third month (the month of Sivan), they recorded all of Mordecai’s orders to the Jews and to the satraps, governors, and princes of the 127 provinces from India to Cush—writing to each province in its own script, to every people in their own language, and to the Jews in their own script and language.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 10, 'Mordecai wrote in the name of King Xerxes and sealed it with the royal signet ring. He sent the documents by mounted couriers riding on swift horses bred from the royal mares.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 11, 'By these letters the king permitted the Jews in each and every city the right to assemble and defend themselves, to destroy, kill, and annihilate all the forces of any people or province hostile to them, including women and children, and to plunder their possessions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 12, 'The single day appointed throughout all the provinces of King Xerxes was the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 13, 'A copy of the text of the edict was to be issued in every province and published to all the people, so that the Jews would be ready on that day to avenge themselves on their enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 14, 'The couriers rode out in haste on their royal horses, pressed on by the command of the king. And the edict was also issued in the citadel of Susa.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 15, 'Mordecai went out from the presence of the king in royal garments of blue and white, with a large gold crown and a purple robe of fine linen. And the city of Susa shouted and rejoiced.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 16, 'For the Jews it was a time of light and gladness, of joy and honor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 8, 17, 'In every province and every city, wherever the king’s edict and decree reached, there was joy and gladness among the Jews, with feasting and celebrating. And many of the people of the land themselves became Jews, because the fear of the Jews had fallen upon them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 1, 'On the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar, the king’s command and edict were to be executed. On this day the enemies of the Jews had hoped to overpower them, but their plan was overturned and the Jews overpowered those who hated them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 2, 'In each of the provinces of King Xerxes, the Jews assembled in their cities to attack those who sought to harm them. No man could withstand them, because the fear of them had fallen upon all peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 3, 'And all the officials of the provinces, the satraps, the governors, and the king’s administrators helped the Jews, because the fear of Mordecai had fallen upon them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 4, 'For Mordecai exercised great power in the palace, and his fame spread throughout the provinces as he became more and more powerful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 5, 'The Jews put all their enemies to the sword, killing and destroying them, and they did as they pleased to those who hated them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 6, 'In the citadel of Susa, the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 7, 'including Parshandatha, Dalphon, Aspatha,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 8, 'Poratha, Adalia, Aridatha,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 9, 'Parmashta, Arisai, Aridai, and Vaizatha.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 10, 'They killed these ten sons of Haman son of Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 11, 'On that day the number of those killed in the citadel of Susa was reported to the king,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 12, 'who said to Queen Esther, “In the citadel of Susa the Jews have killed and destroyed five hundred men, including Haman’s ten sons. What have they done in the rest of the royal provinces? Now what is your petition? It will be given to you. And what further do you request? It will be fulfilled.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 13, 'Esther replied, “If it pleases the king, may the Jews in Susa also have tomorrow to carry out today’s edict, and may the bodies of Haman’s ten sons be hanged on the gallows.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 14, 'So the king commanded that this be done. An edict was issued in Susa, and they hanged the ten sons of Haman.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 15, 'On the fourteenth day of the month of Adar, the Jews in Susa came together again and put to death three hundred men there, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 16, 'The rest of the Jews in the royal provinces also assembled to defend themselves and rid themselves of their enemies. They killed 75,000 who hated them, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 17, 'This was done on the thirteenth day of the month of Adar, and on the fourteenth day they rested, making it a day of feasting and joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 18, 'The Jews in Susa, however, had assembled on the thirteenth and the fourteenth days of the month. So they rested on the fifteenth day, making it a day of feasting and joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 19, 'This is why the rural Jews, who live in the villages, observe the fourteenth day of the month of Adar as a day of joy and feasting. It is a holiday for sending gifts to one another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 20, 'Mordecai recorded these events and sent letters to all the Jews in all the provinces of King Xerxes, both near and far,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 21, 'to establish among them an annual celebration on the fourteenth and fifteenth days of the month of Adar'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 22, 'as the days on which the Jews gained rest from their enemies and the month in which their sorrow turned to joy and their mourning into a holiday. He wrote that these were to be days of feasting and joy, of sending gifts to one another and to the poor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 23, 'So the Jews agreed to continue the custom they had started, as Mordecai had written to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 24, 'For Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had plotted against the Jews to destroy them and had cast the Pur (that is, the lot) to crush and destroy them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 25, 'But when it came before the king, he commanded by letter that the wicked scheme which Haman had devised against the Jews should come back upon his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 26, 'Therefore these days are called Purim, from the word Pur. Because of all the instructions in this letter, and because of all they had seen and experienced,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 27, 'the Jews bound themselves to establish the custom that they and their descendants and all who join them should not fail to celebrate these two days at the appointed time each and every year, according to their regulation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 28, 'These days should be remembered and celebrated by every generation, family, province, and city, so that these days of Purim should not fail to be observed among the Jews, nor should the memory of them fade from their descendants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 29, 'So Queen Esther daughter of Abihail, along with Mordecai the Jew, wrote with full authority to confirm this second letter concerning Purim.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 30, 'And Mordecai sent letters with words of peace and truth to all the Jews in the 127 provinces of the kingdom of Xerxes,'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 31, 'in order to confirm these days of Purim at their appointed time, just as Mordecai the Jew and Queen Esther had established them and had committed themselves and their descendants to the times of fasting and lamentation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 9, 32, 'So Esther’s decree confirmed these regulations about Purim, which were written into the record.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 10, 1, 'Now King Xerxes imposed tribute throughout the land, even to its farthest shores.'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 10, 2, 'And all of Mordecai’s powerful and magnificent accomplishments, together with the full account of the greatness to which the king had raised him, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Media and Persia?'),
  ('BSB', 'Esther', 17, 10, 3, 'For Mordecai the Jew was second only to King Xerxes, preeminent among the Jews and highly favored by his many kinsmen, seeking the good of his people and speaking peace to all his countrymen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 1, 'There was a man in the land of Uz whose name was Job. And this man was blameless and upright, fearing God and shunning evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 2, 'He had seven sons and three daughters,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 3, 'and he owned 7,000 sheep, 3,000 camels, 500 yoke of oxen, 500 female donkeys, and a very large number of servants. Job was the greatest man of all the people of the East.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 4, 'Job’s sons would take turns holding feasts in their homes, and they would invite their three sisters to eat and drink with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 5, 'And when the days of feasting were over, Job would send for his children to purify them, rising early in the morning to offer burnt offerings for all of them. For Job thought, “Perhaps my children have sinned and cursed God in their hearts.” This was Job’s regular practice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 6, 'One day the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan also came with them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 7, '“Where have you come from?” said the LORD to Satan. “From roaming through the earth,” he replied, “and walking back and forth in it.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 8, 'Then the LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered My servant Job? For there is no one on earth like him, a man who is blameless and upright, who fears God and shuns evil.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 9, 'Satan answered the LORD, “Does Job fear God for nothing?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 10, 'Have You not placed a hedge on every side around him and his household and all that he owns? You have blessed the work of his hands, and his possessions have increased in the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 11, 'But stretch out Your hand and strike all that he has, and he will surely curse You to Your face.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 12, '“Very well,” said the LORD to Satan. “Everything he has is in your hands, but you must not lay a hand on the man himself.” Then Satan went out from the presence of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 13, 'One day, while Job’s sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 14, 'a messenger came and reported to Job: “While the oxen were plowing and the donkeys were grazing nearby,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 15, 'the Sabeans swooped down and took them away. They put the servants to the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 16, 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “The fire of God fell from heaven. It burned and consumed the sheep and the servants, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 17, 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “The Chaldeans formed three bands, raided the camels, and took them away. They put the servants to the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 18, 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “Your sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 19, 'when suddenly a mighty wind swept in from the desert and struck the four corners of the house. It collapsed on the young people and they are dead, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 20, 'Then Job stood up, tore his robe, and shaved his head. He fell to the ground and worshiped,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 21, 'saying: “Naked I came from my mother’s womb, and naked I will return. The LORD gave, and the LORD has taken away. Blessed be the name of the LORD.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 1, 22, 'In all this, Job did not sin or charge God with wrongdoing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 1, 'On another day the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan also came with them to present himself before Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 2, '“Where have you come from?” said the LORD to Satan. “From roaming through the earth,” he replied, “and walking back and forth in it.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 3, 'Then the LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered My servant Job? For there is no one on earth like him, a man who is blameless and upright, who fears God and shuns evil. He still retains his integrity, even though you incited Me against him to ruin him without cause.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 4, '“Skin for skin!” Satan replied. “A man will give up all he owns in exchange for his life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 5, 'But stretch out Your hand and strike his flesh and bones, and he will surely curse You to Your face.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 6, '“Very well,” said the LORD to Satan. “He is in your hands, but you must spare his life.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 7, 'So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD and infected Job with terrible boils from the soles of his feet to the crown of his head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 8, 'And Job took a piece of broken pottery to scrape himself as he sat among the ashes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 9, 'Then Job’s wife said to him, “Do you still retain your integrity? Curse God and die!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 10, '“You speak as a foolish woman speaks,” he told her. “Should we accept from God only good and not adversity?” In all this, Job did not sin in what he said.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 11, 'Now when Job’s three friends—Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite—heard about all this adversity that had come upon him, each of them came from his home, and they met together to go and sympathize with Job and comfort him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 12, 'When they lifted up their eyes from afar, they could barely recognize Job. They began to weep aloud, and each man tore his robe and threw dust in the air over his head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 2, 13, 'Then they sat on the ground with him for seven days and seven nights, but no one spoke a word to him because they saw how intense his suffering was.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 1, 'After this, Job opened his mouth and cursed the day of his birth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 2, 'And this is what he said:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 3, '“May the day of my birth perish, and the night it was said, ‘A boy is conceived.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 4, 'If only that day had turned to darkness! May God above disregard it; may no light shine upon it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 5, 'May darkness and gloom reclaim it, and a cloud settle over it; may the blackness of the day overwhelm it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 6, 'If only darkness had taken that night away! May it not appear among the days of the year; may it never be entered in any of the months.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 7, 'Behold, may that night be barren; may no joyful voice come into it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 8, 'May it be cursed by those who curse the day— those prepared to rouse Leviathan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 9, 'May its morning stars grow dark; may it wait in vain for daylight; may it not see the breaking of dawn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 10, 'For that night did not shut the doors of the womb to hide the sorrow from my eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 11, 'Why did I not perish at birth; why did I not die as I came from the womb?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 12, 'Why were there knees to receive me, and breasts that I should be nursed?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 13, 'For now I would be lying down in peace; I would be asleep and at rest'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 14, 'with kings and counselors of the earth, who built for themselves cities now in ruins,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 15, 'or with princes who had gold, who filled their houses with silver.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 16, 'Or why was I not hidden like a stillborn child, like an infant who never sees daylight?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 17, 'There the wicked cease from raging, and there the weary find rest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 18, 'The captives enjoy their ease; they do not hear the voice of the oppressor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 19, 'Both small and great are there, and the slave is freed from his master.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 20, 'Why is light given to the miserable, and life to the bitter of soul,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 21, 'who long for death that does not come, and search for it like hidden treasure,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 22, 'who rejoice and greatly exult when they can find the grave?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 23, 'Why is life given to a man whose way is hidden, whom God has hedged in?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 24, 'I sigh when food is put before me, and my groans pour out like water.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 25, 'For the thing I feared has overtaken me, and what I dreaded has befallen me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 3, 26, 'I am not at ease or quiet; I have no rest, for trouble has come.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 1, 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 2, '“If one ventures a word with you, will you be wearied? Yet who can keep from speaking?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 3, 'Surely you have instructed many, and have strengthened their feeble hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 4, 'Your words have steadied those who stumbled; you have braced the knees that were buckling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 5, 'But now trouble has come upon you, and you are weary. It strikes you, and you are dismayed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 6, 'Is your reverence not your confidence, and the uprightness of your ways your hope?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 7, 'Consider now, I plead: Who, being innocent, has ever perished? Or where have the upright been destroyed?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 8, 'As I have observed, those who plow iniquity and those who sow trouble reap the same.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 9, 'By the breath of God they perish, and by the blast of His anger they are consumed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 10, 'The lion may roar, and the fierce lion may growl, yet the teeth of the young lions are broken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 11, 'The old lion perishes for lack of prey, and the cubs of the lioness are scattered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 12, 'Now a word came to me secretly; my ears caught a whisper of it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 13, 'In disquieting visions in the night, when deep sleep falls on men,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 14, 'fear and trembling came over me and made all my bones shudder.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 15, 'Then a spirit glided past my face, and the hair on my body bristled.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 16, 'It stood still, but I could not discern its appearance; a form loomed before my eyes, and I heard a whispering voice:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 17, '‘Can a mortal be more righteous than God, or a man more pure than his Maker?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 18, 'If God puts no trust in His servants, and He charges His angels with error,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 19, 'how much more those who dwell in houses of clay, whose foundations are in the dust, who can be crushed like a moth!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 20, 'They are smashed to pieces from dawn to dusk; unnoticed, they perish forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 4, 21, 'Are not their tent cords pulled up, so that they die without wisdom?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 1, '“Call out if you please, but who will answer? To which of the holy ones will you turn?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 2, 'For resentment kills a fool, and envy slays the simple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 3, 'I have seen a fool taking root, but suddenly his house was cursed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 4, 'His sons are far from safety, crushed in court without a defender.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 5, 'The hungry consume his harvest, taking it even from the thorns, and the thirsty pant after his wealth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 6, 'For distress does not spring from the dust, and trouble does not sprout from the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 7, 'Yet man is born to trouble as surely as sparks fly upward.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 8, 'However, if I were you, I would appeal to God and lay my cause before Him—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 9, 'the One who does great and unsearchable things, wonders without number.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 10, 'He gives rain to the earth and sends water upon the fields.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 11, 'He sets the lowly on high, so that mourners are lifted to safety.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 12, 'He thwarts the schemes of the crafty, so that their hands find no success.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 13, 'He catches the wise in their craftiness, and sweeps away the plans of the cunning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 14, 'They encounter darkness by day and grope at noon as in the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 15, 'He saves the needy from the sword in their mouth and from the clutches of the powerful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 16, 'So the poor have hope, and injustice shuts its mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 17, 'Blessed indeed is the man whom God corrects; so do not despise the discipline of the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 18, 'For He wounds, but He also binds; He strikes, but His hands also heal.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 19, 'He will rescue you from six calamities; no harm will touch you in seven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 20, 'In famine He will redeem you from death, and in battle from the stroke of the sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 21, 'You will be hidden from the scourge of the tongue, and will not fear havoc when it comes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 22, 'You will laugh at destruction and famine, and need not fear the beasts of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 23, 'For you will have a covenant with the stones of the field, and the wild animals will be at peace with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 24, 'You will know that your tent is secure, and find nothing amiss when inspecting your home.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 25, 'You will know that your offspring will be many, your descendants like the grass of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 26, 'You will come to the grave in full vigor, like a sheaf of grain gathered in season.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 5, 27, 'Indeed, we have investigated, and it is true! So hear it and know for yourself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 1, 'Then Job replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 2, '“If only my grief could be weighed and placed with my calamity on the scales.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 3, 'For then it would outweigh the sand of the seas— no wonder my words have been rash.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 4, 'For the arrows of the Almighty have pierced me; my spirit drinks in their poison; the terrors of God are arrayed against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 5, 'Does a wild donkey bray over fresh grass, or an ox low over its fodder?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 6, 'Is tasteless food eaten without salt, or is there flavor in the white of an egg?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 7, 'My soul refuses to touch them; they are loathsome food to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 8, 'If only my request were granted and God would fulfill my hope:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 9, 'that God would be willing to crush me, to unleash His hand and cut me off!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 10, 'It still brings me comfort, and joy through unrelenting pain, that I have not denied the words of the Holy One.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 11, 'What strength do I have, that I should still hope? What is my future, that I should be patient?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 12, 'Is my strength like that of stone, or my flesh made of bronze?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 13, 'Is there any help within me now that success is driven from me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 14, 'A despairing man should have the kindness of his friend, even if he forsakes the fear of the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 15, 'But my brothers are as faithless as wadis, as seasonal streams that overflow,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 16, 'darkened because of the ice and the inflow of melting snow,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 17, 'but ceasing in the dry season and vanishing from their channels in the heat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 18, 'Caravans turn aside from their routes; they go into the wasteland and perish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 19, 'The caravans of Tema look for water; the travelers of Sheba hope to find it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 20, 'They are confounded because they had hoped; their arrival brings disappointment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 21, 'For now you are of no help; you see terror, and you are afraid.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 22, 'Have I ever said, ‘Give me something; offer me a bribe from your wealth;'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 23, 'deliver me from the hand of the enemy; redeem me from the grasp of the ruthless’?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 24, 'Teach me, and I will be silent. Help me understand how I have erred.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 25, 'How painful are honest words! But what does your argument prove?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 26, 'Do you intend to correct my words, and treat as wind my cry of despair?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 27, 'You would even cast lots for an orphan and barter away your friend.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 28, 'But now, please look at me. Would I lie to your face?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 29, 'Reconsider; do not be unjust. Reconsider, for my righteousness is at stake.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 6, 30, 'Is there iniquity on my tongue? Can my mouth not discern malice?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 1, '“Is not man consigned to labor on earth? Are not his days like those of a hired hand?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 2, 'Like a slave he longs for shade; like a hireling he waits for his wages.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 3, 'So I am allotted months of futility, and nights of misery are appointed me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 4, 'When I lie down I think: ‘When will I get up?’ But the night drags on, and I toss and turn until dawn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 5, 'My flesh is clothed with worms and encrusted with dirt; my skin is cracked and festering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 6, 'My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle; they come to an end without hope.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 7, 'Remember that my life is but a breath. My eyes will never again see happiness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 8, 'The eye that beholds me will no longer see me. You will look for me, but I will be no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 9, 'As a cloud vanishes and is gone, so he who goes down to Sheol does not come back up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 10, 'He never returns to his house; his place remembers him no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 11, 'Therefore I will not restrain my mouth; I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 12, 'Am I the sea, or the monster of the deep, that You must keep me under guard?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 13, 'When I think my bed will comfort me and my couch will ease my complaint,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 14, 'then You frighten me with dreams and terrify me with visions,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 15, 'so that I would prefer strangling and death over my life in this body.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 16, 'I loathe my life! I would not live forever. Leave me alone, for my days are but a breath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 17, 'What is man that You should exalt him, that You should set Your heart upon him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 18, 'that You attend to him every morning, and test him every moment?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 19, 'Will You never look away from me, or leave me alone to swallow my spittle?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 20, 'If I have sinned, what have I done to You, O watcher of mankind? Why have You made me Your target, so that I am a burden to You?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 7, 21, 'Why do You not pardon my transgression and take away my iniquity? For soon I will lie down in the dust; You will seek me, but I will be no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 1, 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 2, '“How long will you go on saying such things? The words of your mouth are a blustering wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 3, 'Does God pervert justice? Does the Almighty pervert what is right?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 4, 'When your children sinned against Him, He gave them over to their rebellion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 5, 'But if you would earnestly seek God and ask the Almighty for mercy,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 6, 'if you are pure and upright, even now He will rouse Himself on your behalf and restore your righteous estate.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 7, 'Though your beginnings were modest, your latter days will flourish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 8, 'Please inquire of past generations and consider the discoveries of their fathers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 9, 'For we were born yesterday and know nothing; our days on earth are but a shadow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 10, 'Will they not teach you and tell you, and speak from their understanding?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 11, 'Does papyrus grow where there is no marsh? Do reeds flourish without water?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 12, 'While the shoots are still uncut, they dry up quicker than grass.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 13, 'Such is the destiny of all who forget God; so the hope of the godless will perish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 14, 'His confidence is fragile; his security is in a spider’s web.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 15, 'He leans on his web, but it gives way; he holds fast, but it does not endure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 16, 'He is a well-watered plant in the sunshine, spreading its shoots over the garden.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 17, 'His roots wrap around the rock heap; he looks for a home among the stones.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 18, 'If he is uprooted from his place, it will disown him, saying, ‘I never saw you.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 19, 'Surely this is the joy of his way; yet others will spring from the dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 20, 'Behold, God does not reject the blameless, nor will He strengthen the hand of evildoers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 21, 'He will yet fill your mouth with laughter, and your lips with a shout of joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 8, 22, 'Your enemies will be clothed in shame, and the tent of the wicked will be no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 2, '“Yes, I know that it is so, but how can a mortal be righteous before God?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 3, 'If one wished to contend with God, he could not answer Him one time out of a thousand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 4, 'God is wise in heart and mighty in strength. Who has resisted Him and prospered?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 5, 'He moves mountains without their knowledge and overturns them in His anger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 6, 'He shakes the earth from its place, so that its foundations tremble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 7, 'He commands the sun not to shine; He seals off the stars.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 8, 'He alone stretches out the heavens and treads on the waves of the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 9, 'He is the Maker of the Bear and Orion, of the Pleiades and the constellations of the south.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 10, 'He does great things beyond searching out, and wonders without number.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 11, 'Were He to pass by me, I would not see Him; were He to move, I would not recognize Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 12, 'If He takes away, who can stop Him? Who dares to ask Him, ‘What are You doing?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 13, 'God does not restrain His anger; the helpers of Rahab cower beneath Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 14, 'How then can I answer Him or choose my arguments against Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 15, 'For even if I were right, I could not answer. I could only beg my Judge for mercy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 16, 'If I summoned Him and He answered me, I do not believe He would listen to my voice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 17, 'For He would crush me with a tempest and multiply my wounds without cause.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 18, 'He does not let me catch my breath, but overwhelms me with bitterness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 19, 'If it is a matter of strength, He is indeed mighty! If it is a matter of justice, who can summon Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 20, 'Even if I were righteous, my mouth would condemn me; if I were blameless, it would declare me guilty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 21, 'Though I am blameless, I have no concern for myself; I despise my own life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 22, 'It is all the same, and so I say, ‘He destroys both the blameless and the wicked.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 23, 'When the scourge brings sudden death, He mocks the despair of the innocent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 24, 'The earth is given into the hand of the wicked; He blindfolds its judges. If it is not He, then who is it?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 25, 'My days are swifter than a runner; they flee without seeing good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 26, 'They sweep by like boats of papyrus, like an eagle swooping down on its prey.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 27, 'If I were to say, ‘I will forget my complaint and change my expression and smile,’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 28, 'I would still dread all my sufferings; I know that You will not acquit me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 29, 'Since I am already found guilty, why should I labor in vain?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 30, 'If I should wash myself with snow and cleanse my hands with lye,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 31, 'then You would plunge me into the pit, and even my own clothes would despise me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 32, 'For He is not a man like me, that I can answer Him, that we can take each other to court.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 33, 'Nor is there a mediator between us, to lay his hand upon us both.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 34, 'Let Him remove His rod from me, so that His terror will no longer frighten me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 9, 35, 'Then I would speak without fear of Him. But as it is, I am on my own.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 1, '“I loathe my own life; I will express my complaint and speak in the bitterness of my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 2, 'I will say to God: Do not condemn me! Let me know why You prosecute me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 3, 'Does it please You to oppress me, to reject the work of Your hands and favor the schemes of the wicked?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 4, 'Do You have eyes of flesh? Do You see as man sees?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 5, 'Are Your days like those of a mortal, or Your years like those of a man,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 6, 'that You should seek my iniquity and search out my sin—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 7, 'though You know that I am not guilty, and there is no deliverance from Your hand?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 8, 'Your hands shaped me and altogether formed me. Would You now turn and destroy me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 9, 'Please remember that You molded me like clay. Would You now return me to dust?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 10, 'Did You not pour me out like milk, and curdle me like cheese?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 11, 'You clothed me with skin and flesh, and knit me together with bones and sinews.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 12, 'You have granted me life and loving devotion, and Your care has preserved my spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 13, 'Yet You concealed these things in Your heart, and I know that this was in Your mind:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 14, 'If I sinned, You would take note, and would not acquit me of my iniquity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 15, 'If I am guilty, woe to me! And even if I am righteous, I cannot lift my head. I am full of shame and aware of my affliction.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 16, 'Should I hold my head high, You would hunt me like a lion, and again display Your power against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 17, 'You produce new witnesses against me and multiply Your anger toward me. Hardships assault me in wave after wave.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 18, 'Why then did You bring me from the womb? Oh, that I had died, and no eye had seen me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 19, 'If only I had never come to be, but had been carried from the womb to the grave.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 20, 'Are my days not few? Withdraw from me, that I may have a little comfort,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 21, 'before I go—never to return— to a land of darkness and gloom,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 10, 22, 'to a land of utter darkness, of deep shadow and disorder, where even the light is like darkness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 1, 'Then Zophar the Naamathite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 2, '“Should this stream of words go unanswered and such a speaker be vindicated?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 3, 'Should your babbling put others to silence? Will you scoff without rebuke?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 4, 'You have said, ‘My doctrine is sound, and I am pure in Your sight.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 5, 'But if only God would speak and open His lips against you,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 6, 'and disclose to you the secrets of wisdom, for true wisdom has two sides. Know then that God exacts from you less than your iniquity deserves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 7, 'Can you fathom the deep things of God or discover the limits of the Almighty?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 8, 'They are higher than the heavens—what can you do? They are deeper than Sheol—what can you know?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 9, 'Their measure is longer than the earth and wider than the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 10, 'If He comes along to imprison you, or convenes a court, who can stop Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 11, 'Surely He knows the deceit of men. If He sees iniquity, does He not take note?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 12, 'But a witless man can no more become wise than the colt of a wild donkey can be born a man!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 13, 'As for you, if you direct your heart and lift up your hands to Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 14, 'if you put away the iniquity in your hand, and allow no injustice to dwell in your tents,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 15, 'then indeed you will lift up your face without shame; you will stand firm and unafraid.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 16, 'For you will forget your misery, recalling it only as waters gone by.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 17, 'Your life will be brighter than noonday; its darkness will be like the morning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 18, 'You will be secure, because there is hope, and you will look around and lie down in safety.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 19, 'You will lie down without fear, and many will court your favor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 11, 20, 'But the eyes of the wicked will fail, and escape will elude them; they will hope for their last breath.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 2, '“Truly then you are the people with whom wisdom itself will die!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 3, 'But I also have a mind; I am not inferior to you. Who does not know such things as these?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 4, 'I am a laughingstock to my friends, though I called on God, and He answered. The righteous and upright man is a laughingstock.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 5, 'The one at ease scorns misfortune as the fate of those whose feet are slipping.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 6, 'The tents of robbers are safe, and those who provoke God are secure— those who carry their god in their hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 7, 'But ask the animals, and they will instruct you; ask the birds of the air, and they will tell you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 8, 'Or speak to the earth, and it will teach you; let the fish of the sea inform you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 9, 'Which of all these does not know that the hand of the LORD has done this?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 10, 'The life of every living thing is in His hand, as well as the breath of all mankind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 11, 'Does not the ear test words as the tongue tastes its food?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 12, 'Wisdom is found with the elderly, and understanding comes with long life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 13, 'Wisdom and strength belong to God; counsel and understanding are His.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 14, 'What He tears down cannot be rebuilt; the man He imprisons cannot be released.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 15, 'If He holds back the waters, they dry up, and if He releases them, they overwhelm the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 16, 'True wisdom and power belong to Him. The deceived and the deceiver are His.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 17, 'He leads counselors away barefoot and makes fools of judges.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 18, 'He loosens the bonds placed by kings and fastens a belt around their waists.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 19, 'He leads priests away barefoot and overthrows the established.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 20, 'He deprives the trusted of speech and takes away the discernment of elders.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 21, 'He pours out contempt on nobles and disarms the mighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 22, 'He reveals the deep things of darkness and brings deep shadows into light.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 23, 'He makes nations great and destroys them; He enlarges nations, then disperses them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 24, 'He deprives the earth’s leaders of reason and makes them wander in a trackless wasteland.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 12, 25, 'They grope in the darkness without light; He makes them stagger like drunkards.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 1, '“Indeed, my eyes have seen all this; my ears have heard and understood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 2, 'What you know, I also know; I am not inferior to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 3, 'Yet I desire to speak to the Almighty and argue my case before God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 4, 'You, however, smear with lies; you are all worthless physicians.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 5, 'If only you would remain silent; for that would be your wisdom!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 6, 'Hear now my argument, and listen to the plea of my lips.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 7, 'Will you speak wickedly on God’s behalf or speak deceitfully for Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 8, 'Would you show Him partiality or argue in His defense?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 9, 'Would it be well when He examined you? Could you deceive Him like a man?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 10, 'Surely He would rebuke you if you secretly showed partiality.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 11, 'Would His majesty not terrify you? Would the dread of Him not fall upon you?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 12, 'Your maxims are proverbs of ashes; your defenses are defenses of clay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 13, 'Be silent, and I will speak. Then let come to me what may.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 14, 'Why do I put myself at risk and take my life in my own hands?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 15, 'Though He slay me, I will hope in Him. I will still defend my ways to His face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 16, 'Moreover, this will be my salvation, for no godless man can appear before Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 17, 'Listen carefully to my words; let my declaration ring in your ears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 18, 'Behold, now that I have prepared my case, I know that I will be vindicated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 19, 'Can anyone indict me? If so, I will be silent and die.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 20, 'Only grant these two things to me, so that I need not hide from You:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 21, 'Withdraw Your hand from me, and do not let Your terror frighten me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 22, 'Then call me, and I will answer, or let me speak, and You can reply.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 23, 'How many are my iniquities and sins? Reveal to me my transgression and sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 24, 'Why do You hide Your face and consider me as Your enemy?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 25, 'Would You frighten a windblown leaf? Would You chase after dry chaff?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 26, 'For You record bitter accusations against me and bequeath to me the iniquities of my youth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 27, 'You put my feet in the stocks and stand watch over all my paths; You set a limit for the soles of my feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 13, 28, 'So man wastes away like something rotten, like a moth-eaten garment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 1, '“Man, who is born of woman, is short of days and full of trouble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 2, 'Like a flower, he comes forth, then withers away; like a fleeting shadow, he does not endure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 3, 'Do You open Your eyes to one like this? Will You bring him into judgment before You?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 4, 'Who can bring out clean from unclean? No one!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 5, 'Since his days are determined and the number of his months is with You, and since You have set limits that he cannot exceed,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 6, 'look away from him and let him rest, so he can enjoy his day as a hired hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 7, 'For there is hope for a tree: If it is cut down, it will sprout again, and its tender shoots will not fail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 8, 'If its roots grow old in the ground and its stump dies in the soil,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 9, 'at the scent of water it will bud and put forth twigs like a sapling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 10, 'But a man dies and is laid low; he breathes his last, and where is he?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 11, 'As water disappears from the sea and a river becomes parched and dry,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 12, 'so a man lies down and does not rise. Until the heavens are no more, he will not be awakened or roused from sleep.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 13, 'If only You would hide me in Sheol and conceal me until Your anger has passed! If only You would appoint a time for me and then remember me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 14, 'When a man dies, will he live again? All the days of my hard service I will wait, until my renewal comes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 15, 'You will call, and I will answer; You will desire the work of Your hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 16, 'For then You would count my steps, but would not keep track of my sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 17, 'My transgression would be sealed in a bag, and You would cover over my iniquity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 18, 'But as a mountain erodes and crumbles and a rock is dislodged from its place,');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 19, 'as water wears away the stones and torrents wash away the soil, so You destroy a man’s hope.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 20, 'You forever overpower him, and he passes on; You change his countenance and send him away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 21, 'If his sons receive honor, he does not know it; if they are brought low, he is unaware.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 14, 22, 'He feels only the pain of his own body and mourns only for himself.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 1, 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 2, '“Does a wise man answer with empty counsel or fill his belly with the hot east wind?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 3, 'Should he argue with useless words or speeches that serve no purpose?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 4, 'But you even undermine the fear of God and hinder meditation before Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 5, 'For your iniquity instructs your mouth, and you choose the language of the crafty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 6, 'Your own mouth, not mine, condemns you; your own lips testify against you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 7, 'Were you the first man ever born? Were you brought forth before the hills?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 8, 'Do you listen in on the council of God or limit wisdom to yourself?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 9, 'What do you know that we do not? What do you understand that is not clear to us?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 10, 'Both the gray-haired and the aged are on our side— men much older than your father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 11, 'Are the consolations of God not enough for you, even words spoken gently to you?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 12, 'Why has your heart carried you away, and why do your eyes flash,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 13, 'as you turn your spirit against God and pour such words from your mouth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 14, 'What is man, that he should be pure, or one born of woman, that he should be righteous?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 15, 'If God puts no trust in His holy ones, if even the heavens are not pure in His eyes,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 16, 'how much less man, who is vile and corrupt, who drinks injustice like water?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 17, 'Listen to me and I will inform you. I will describe what I have seen,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 18, 'what was declared by wise men and was not concealed from their fathers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 19, 'to whom alone the land was given when no foreigner passed among them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 20, 'A wicked man writhes in pain all his days; only a few years are reserved for the ruthless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 21, 'Sounds of terror fill his ears; in his prosperity the destroyer attacks him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 22, 'He despairs of his return from darkness; he is marked for the sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 23, 'He wanders about as food for vultures; he knows the day of darkness is at hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 24, 'Distress and anguish terrify him, overwhelming him like a king poised to attack.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 25, 'For he has stretched out his hand against God and has vaunted himself against the Almighty,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 26, 'rushing headlong at Him with a thick, studded shield.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 27, 'Though his face is covered with fat and his waistline bulges with flesh,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 28, 'he will dwell in ruined cities, in abandoned houses destined to become rubble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 29, 'He will no longer be rich; his wealth will not endure. His possessions will not overspread the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 30, 'He will not escape from the darkness; the flame will wither his shoots, and the breath of God’s mouth will carry him away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 31, 'Let him not deceive himself with trust in emptiness, for emptiness will be his reward.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 32, 'It will be paid in full before his time, and his branch will not flourish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 33, 'He will be like a vine stripped of its unripe grapes, like an olive tree that sheds its blossoms.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 34, 'For the company of the godless will be barren, and fire will consume the tents of bribery.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 15, 35, 'They conceive trouble and give birth to evil; their womb is pregnant with deceit.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 2, '“I have heard many things like these; miserable comforters are you all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 3, 'Is there no end to your long-winded speeches? What provokes you to continue testifying?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 4, 'I could also speak like you if you were in my place; I could heap up words against you and shake my head at you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 5, 'But I would encourage you with my mouth, and the consolation of my lips would bring relief.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 6, 'Even if I speak, my pain is not relieved, and if I hold back, how will it go away?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 7, 'Surely He has now exhausted me; You have devastated all my family.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 8, 'You have bound me, and it has become a witness; my frailty rises up and testifies against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 9, 'His anger has torn me and opposed me; He gnashes His teeth at me. My adversary pierces me with His eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 10, 'They open their mouths against me and strike my cheeks with contempt; they join together against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 11, 'God has delivered me to unjust men; He has thrown me to the clutches of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 12, 'I was at ease, but He shattered me; He seized me by the neck and crushed me. He has set me up as His target;'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 13, 'His archers surround me. He pierces my kidneys without mercy and spills my gall on the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 14, 'He breaks me with wound upon wound; He rushes me like a mighty warrior.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 15, 'I have sewn sackcloth over my skin; I have buried my horn in the dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 16, 'My face is red with weeping, and deep shadows ring my eyes;'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 17, 'yet my hands are free of violence and my prayer is pure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 18, 'O earth, do not cover my blood; may my cry for help never be laid to rest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 19, 'Even now my witness is in heaven, and my advocate is on high.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 20, 'My friends are my scoffers as my eyes pour out tears to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 21, 'Oh, that a man might plead with God as he pleads with his neighbor!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 16, 22, 'For when only a few years are past I will go the way of no return.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 1, '“My spirit is broken; my days are extinguished; the grave awaits me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 2, 'Surely mockers surround me, and my eyes must gaze at their rebellion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 3, 'Give me, I pray, the pledge You demand. Who else will be my guarantor?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 4, 'You have closed their minds to understanding; therefore You will not exalt them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 5, 'If a man denounces his friends for a price, the eyes of his children will fail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 6, 'He has made me a byword among the people, a man in whose face they spit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 7, 'My eyes have grown dim with grief, and my whole body is but a shadow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 8, 'The upright are appalled at this, and the innocent are stirred against the godless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 9, 'Yet a righteous one holds to his way, and the one with clean hands grows stronger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 10, 'But come back and try again, all of you. For I will not find a wise man among you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 11, 'My days have passed; my plans are broken off— even the desires of my heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 12, 'They have turned night into day, making light seem near in the face of darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 13, 'If I look for Sheol as my home, if I spread out my bed in darkness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 14, 'and say to corruption, ‘You are my father,’ and to the worm, ‘My mother,’ or ‘My sister,’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 15, 'where then is my hope? Who can see any hope for me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 17, 16, 'Will it go down to the gates of Sheol? Will we go down together into the dust?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 1, 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 2, '“How long until you end these speeches? Show some sense, and then we can talk.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 3, 'Why are we regarded as cattle, as stupid in your sight?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 4, 'You who tear yourself in anger— should the earth be forsaken on your account, or the rocks be moved from their place?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 5, 'Indeed, the lamp of the wicked is extinguished; the flame of his fire does not glow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 6, 'The light in his tent grows dark, and the lamp beside him goes out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 7, 'His vigorous stride is shortened, and his own schemes trip him up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 8, 'For his own feet lead him into a net, and he wanders into its mesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 9, 'A trap seizes his heel; a snare grips him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 10, 'A noose is hidden in the ground, and a trap lies in his path.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 11, 'Terrors frighten him on every side and harass his every step.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 12, 'His strength is depleted, and calamity is ready at his side.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 13, 'It devours patches of his skin; the firstborn of death devours his limbs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 14, 'He is torn from the shelter of his tent and is marched off to the king of terrors.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 15, 'Fire resides in his tent; burning sulfur rains down on his dwelling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 16, 'The roots beneath him dry up, and the branches above him wither away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 17, 'The memory of him perishes from the earth, and he has no name in the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 18, 'He is driven from light into darkness and is chased from the inhabited world.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 19, 'He has no offspring or posterity among his people, no survivor where he once lived.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 20, 'Those in the west are appalled at his fate, while those in the east tremble in horror.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 18, 21, 'Surely such is the dwelling of the wicked and the place of one who does not know God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 2, '“How long will you torment me and crush me with your words?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 3, 'Ten times now you have reproached me; you shamelessly mistreat me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 4, 'Even if I have truly gone astray, my error concerns me alone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 5, 'If indeed you would exalt yourselves above me and use my disgrace against me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 6, 'then understand that it is God who has wronged me and drawn His net around me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 7, 'Though I cry out, ‘Violence!’ I get no response; though I call for help, there is no justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 8, 'He has blocked my way so I cannot pass; He has veiled my paths with darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 9, 'He has stripped me of my honor and removed the crown from my head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 10, 'He tears me down on every side until I am gone; He uproots my hope like a tree.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 11, 'His anger burns against me, and He counts me among His enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 12, 'His troops advance together; they construct a ramp against me and encamp around my tent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 13, 'He has removed my brothers from me; my acquaintances have abandoned me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 14, 'My kinsmen have failed me, and my friends have forgotten me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 15, 'My guests and maidservants count me as a stranger; I am a foreigner in their sight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 16, 'I call for my servant, but he does not answer, though I implore him with my own mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 17, 'My breath is repulsive to my wife, and I am loathsome to my own family.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 18, 'Even little boys scorn me; when I appear, they deride me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 19, 'All my best friends despise me, and those I love have turned against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 20, 'My skin and flesh cling to my bones; I have escaped by the skin of my teeth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 21, 'Have pity on me, my friends, have pity, for the hand of God has struck me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 22, 'Why do you persecute me as God does? Will you never get enough of my flesh?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 23, 'I wish that my words were recorded and inscribed in a book,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 24, 'by an iron stylus on lead, or chiseled in stone forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 25, 'But I know that my Redeemer lives, and in the end He will stand upon the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 26, 'Even after my skin has been destroyed, yet in my flesh I will see God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 27, 'I will see Him for myself; my eyes will behold Him, and not as a stranger. How my heart yearns within me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 28, 'If you say, ‘Let us persecute him, since the root of the matter lies with him,’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 19, 29, 'then you should fear the sword yourselves, because wrath brings punishment by the sword, so that you may know there is a judgment.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 1, 'Then Zophar the Naamathite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 2, '“So my anxious thoughts compel me to answer, because of the turmoil within me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 3, 'I have heard a rebuke that insults me, and my understanding prompts a reply.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 4, 'Do you not know that from antiquity, since man was placed on the earth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 5, 'the triumph of the wicked has been brief and the joy of the godless momentary?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 6, 'Though his arrogance reaches the heavens, and his head touches the clouds,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 7, 'he will perish forever, like his own dung; those who had seen him will ask, ‘Where is he?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 8, 'He will fly away like a dream, never to be found; he will be chased away like a vision in the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 9, 'The eye that saw him will see him no more, and his place will no longer behold him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 10, 'His sons will seek the favor of the poor, for his own hands must return his wealth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 11, 'The youthful vigor that fills his bones will lie down with him in the dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 12, 'Though evil is sweet in his mouth and he conceals it under his tongue,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 13, 'though he cannot bear to let it go and keeps it in his mouth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 14, 'yet in his stomach his food sours into the venom of cobras within him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 15, 'He swallows wealth but vomits it out; God will force it from his stomach.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 16, 'He will suck the poison of cobras; the fangs of a viper will kill him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 17, 'He will not enjoy the streams, the rivers flowing with honey and cream.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 18, 'He must return the fruit of his labor without consuming it; he cannot enjoy the profits of his trading.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 19, 'For he has oppressed and forsaken the poor; he has seized houses he did not build.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 20, 'Because his appetite is never satisfied, he cannot escape with his treasure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 21, 'Nothing is left for him to consume; thus his prosperity will not endure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 22, 'In the midst of his plenty, he will be distressed; the full force of misery will come upon him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 23, 'When he has filled his stomach, God will vent His fury upon him, raining it down on him as he eats.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 24, 'Though he flees from an iron weapon, a bronze-tipped arrow will pierce him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 25, 'It is drawn out of his back, the gleaming point from his liver. Terrors come over him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 26, 'Total darkness is reserved for his treasures. A fire unfanned will consume him and devour what is left in his tent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 27, 'The heavens will expose his iniquity, and the earth will rise up against him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 28, 'The possessions of his house will be removed, flowing away on the day of God’s wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 20, 29, 'This is the wicked man’s portion from God, the inheritance God has appointed him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 2, '“Listen carefully to my words; let this be your consolation to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 3, 'Bear with me while I speak; then, after I have spoken, you may go on mocking.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 4, 'Is my complaint against a man? Then why should I not be impatient?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 5, 'Look at me and be appalled; put your hand over your mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 6, 'When I remember, terror takes hold, and my body trembles in horror.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 7, 'Why do the wicked live on, growing old and increasing in power?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 8, 'Their descendants are established around them, and their offspring before their eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 9, 'Their homes are safe from fear; no rod of punishment from God is upon them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 10, 'Their bulls breed without fail; their cows bear calves and do not miscarry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 11, 'They send forth their little ones like a flock; their children skip about,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 12, 'singing to the tambourine and lyre and making merry at the sound of the flute.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 13, 'They spend their days in prosperity and go down to Sheol in peace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 14, 'Yet they say to God: ‘Leave us alone! For we have no desire to know Your ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 15, 'Who is the Almighty, that we should serve Him, and what would we gain if we pray to Him?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 16, 'Still, their prosperity is not in their own hands, so I stay far from the counsel of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 17, 'How often is the lamp of the wicked put out? Does disaster come upon them? Does God, in His anger, apportion destruction?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 18, 'Are they like straw before the wind, like chaff swept away by a storm?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 19, 'It is said that God lays up one’s punishment for his children. Let God repay the man himself, so he will know it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 20, 'Let his eyes see his own destruction; let him drink for himself the wrath of the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 21, 'For what does he care about his household after him, when the number of his months has run out?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 22, 'Can anyone teach knowledge to God, since He judges those on high?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 23, 'One man dies full of vigor, completely secure and at ease.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 24, 'His body is well nourished, and his bones are rich with marrow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 25, 'Yet another man dies in the bitterness of his soul, having never tasted prosperity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 26, 'But together they lie down in the dust, and worms cover them both.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 27, 'Behold, I know your thoughts full well, the schemes by which you would wrong me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 28, 'For you say, ‘Where now is the nobleman’s house, and where are the tents in which the wicked dwell?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 29, 'Have you never asked those who travel the roads? Do you not accept their reports?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 30, 'Indeed, the evil man is spared from the day of calamity, delivered from the day of wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 31, 'Who denounces his behavior to his face? Who repays him for what he has done?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 32, 'He is carried to the grave, and watch is kept over his tomb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 33, 'The clods of the valley are sweet to him; everyone follows behind him, and those before him are without number.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 21, 34, 'So how can you comfort me with empty words? For your answers remain full of falsehood.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 1, 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 2, '“Can a man be of use to God? Can even a wise man benefit Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 3, 'Does it delight the Almighty that you are righteous? Does He profit if your ways are blameless?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 4, 'Is it for your reverence that He rebukes you and enters into judgment against you?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 5, 'Is not your wickedness great? Are not your iniquities endless?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 6, 'For you needlessly demanded security from your brothers and deprived the naked of their clothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 7, 'You gave no water to the weary and withheld food from the famished,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 8, 'while the land belonged to a mighty man, and a man of honor lived on it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 9, 'You sent widows away empty-handed, and the strength of the fatherless was crushed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 10, 'Therefore snares surround you, and sudden peril terrifies you;'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 11, 'it is so dark you cannot see, and a flood of water covers you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 12, 'Is not God as high as the heavens? Look at the highest stars, how lofty they are!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 13, 'Yet you say: ‘What does God know? Does He judge through thick darkness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 14, 'Thick clouds veil Him so He does not see us as He traverses the vault of heaven.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 15, 'Will you stay on the ancient path that wicked men have trod?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 16, 'They were snatched away before their time, and their foundations were swept away by a flood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 17, 'They said to God, ‘Depart from us. What can the Almighty do to us?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 18, 'But it was He who filled their houses with good things; so I stay far from the counsel of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 19, 'The righteous see it and are glad; the innocent mock them:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 20, '‘Surely our foes are destroyed, and fire has consumed their excess.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 21, 'Reconcile now and be at peace with Him; thereby good will come to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 22, 'Receive instruction from His mouth, and lay up His words in your heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 23, 'If you return to the Almighty, you will be restored. If you remove injustice from your tents'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 24, 'and consign your gold to the dust and the gold of Ophir to the stones of the ravines,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 25, 'then the Almighty will be your gold and the finest silver for you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 26, 'Surely then you will delight in the Almighty and lift up your face to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 27, 'You will pray to Him, and He will hear you, and you will fulfill your vows.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 28, 'Your decisions will be carried out, and light will shine on your ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 29, 'When men are brought low and you say, ‘Lift them up!’ then He will save the lowly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 22, 30, 'He will deliver even one who is not innocent, rescuing him through the cleanness of your hands.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 2, '“Even today my complaint is bitter. His hand is heavy despite my groaning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 3, 'If only I knew where to find Him, so that I could go to His seat.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 4, 'I would plead my case before Him and fill my mouth with arguments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 5, 'I would learn how He would answer, and consider what He would say.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 6, 'Would He contend with me in His great power? No, He would certainly take note of me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 7, 'Then an upright man could reason with Him, and I would be delivered forever from my Judge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 8, 'If I go east, He is not there, and if I go west, I cannot find Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 9, 'When He is at work in the north, I cannot behold Him; when He turns to the south, I cannot see Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 10, 'Yet He knows the way I have taken; when He has tested me, I will come forth as gold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 11, 'My feet have followed in His tracks; I have kept His way without turning aside.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 12, 'I have not departed from the command of His lips; I have treasured the words of His mouth more than my daily bread.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 13, 'But He is unchangeable, and who can oppose Him? He does what He desires.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 14, 'For He carries out His decree against me, and He has many such plans.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 15, 'Therefore I am terrified in His presence; when I consider this, I fear Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 16, 'God has made my heart faint; the Almighty has terrified me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 23, 17, 'Yet I am not silenced by the darkness, by the thick darkness that covers my face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 1, '“Why does the Almighty not reserve times for judgment? Why may those who know Him never see His days?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 2, 'Men move boundary stones; they pasture stolen flocks.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 3, 'They drive away the donkey of the fatherless and take the widow’s ox in pledge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 4, 'They push the needy off the road and force all the poor of the land into hiding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 5, 'Indeed, like wild donkeys in the desert, the poor go to work foraging for food; the wasteland is food for their children.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 6, 'They gather fodder in the fields and glean the vineyards of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 7, 'Without clothing, they spend the night naked; they have no covering against the cold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 8, 'Drenched by mountain rains, they huddle against the rocks for want of shelter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 9, 'The fatherless infant is snatched from the breast; the nursing child of the poor is seized for a debt.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 10, 'Without clothing, they wander about naked. They carry the sheaves, but still go hungry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 11, 'They crush olives within their walls; they tread the winepresses, but go thirsty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 12, 'From the city, men groan, and the souls of the wounded cry out, yet God charges no one with wrongdoing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 13, 'Then there are those who rebel against the light, not knowing its ways or staying on its paths.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 14, 'When daylight is gone, the murderer rises to kill the poor and needy; in the night he is like a thief.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 15, 'The eye of the adulterer watches for twilight. Thinking, ‘No eye will see me,’ he covers his face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 16, 'In the dark they dig through houses; by day they shut themselves in, never to experience the light.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 17, 'For to them, deep darkness is their morning; surely they are friends with the terrors of darkness!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 18, 'They are but foam on the surface of the water; their portion of the land is cursed, so that no one turns toward their vineyards.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 19, 'As drought and heat consume the melting snow, so Sheol steals those who have sinned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 20, 'The womb forgets them; the worm feeds on them; they are remembered no more. So injustice is like a broken tree.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 21, 'They prey on the barren and childless, and show no kindness to the widow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 22, 'Yet by His power, God drags away the mighty; though rising up, they have no assurance of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 23, 'He gives them a sense of security, but His eyes are on their ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 24, 'They are exalted for a moment, then they are gone; they are brought low and gathered up like all others; they are cut off like heads of grain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 24, 25, 'If this is not so, then who can prove me a liar and reduce my words to nothing?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 25, 1, 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 25, 2, '“Dominion and awe belong to God; He establishes harmony in the heights of heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 25, 3, 'Can His troops be numbered? On whom does His light not rise?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 25, 4, 'How then can a man be just before God? How can one born of woman be pure?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 25, 5, 'If even the moon does not shine, and the stars are not pure in His sight,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 25, 6, 'how much less man, who is but a maggot, and the son of man, who is but a worm!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 1, 'Then Job answered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 2, '“How you have helped the powerless and saved the arm that is feeble!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 3, 'How you have counseled the unwise and provided fully sound insight!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 4, 'To whom have you uttered these words? And whose spirit spoke through you?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 5, 'The dead tremble— those beneath the waters and those who dwell in them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 6, 'Sheol is naked before God, and Abaddon has no covering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 7, 'He stretches out the north over empty space; He hangs the earth upon nothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 8, 'He wraps up the waters in His clouds, yet the clouds do not burst under their own weight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 9, 'He covers the face of the full moon, spreading over it His cloud.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 10, 'He has inscribed a horizon on the face of the waters at the boundary between light and darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 11, 'The foundations of heaven quake, astounded at His rebuke.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 12, 'By His power He stirred the sea; by His understanding He shattered Rahab.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 13, 'By His breath the skies were cleared; His hand pierced the fleeing serpent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 26, 14, 'Indeed, these are but the fringes of His ways; how faint is the whisper we hear of Him! Who then can understand the thunder of His power?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 1, 'Job continued his discourse:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 2, '“As surely as God lives, who has deprived me of justice— the Almighty, who has embittered my soul—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 3, 'as long as my breath is still within me and the breath of God remains in my nostrils,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 4, 'my lips will not speak wickedness, and my tongue will not utter deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 5, 'I will never say that you are right; I will maintain my integrity until I die.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 6, 'I will cling to my righteousness and never let go. As long as I live, my conscience will not accuse me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 7, 'May my enemy be like the wicked and my opponent like the unjust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 8, 'For what is the hope of the godless when he is cut off, when God takes away his life?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 9, 'Will God hear his cry when distress comes upon him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 10, 'Will he delight in the Almighty? Will he call upon God at all times?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 11, 'I will instruct you in the power of God. I will not conceal the ways of the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 12, 'Surely all of you have seen it for yourselves. Why then do you keep up this empty talk?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 13, 'This is the wicked man’s portion from God— the heritage the ruthless receive from the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 14, 'Though his sons are many, they are destined for the sword; and his offspring will never have enough food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 15, 'His survivors will be buried by the plague, and their widows will not weep for them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 16, 'Though he heaps up silver like dust and piles up a wardrobe like clay,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 17, 'what he lays up, the righteous will wear, and his silver will be divided by the innocent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 18, 'The house he built is like a moth’s cocoon, like a hut set up by a watchman.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 19, 'He lies down wealthy, but will do so no more; when he opens his eyes, all is gone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 20, 'Terrors overtake him like a flood; a tempest sweeps him away in the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 21, 'The east wind carries him away, and he is gone; it sweeps him out of his place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 22, 'It hurls itself against him without mercy as he flees headlong from its power.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 27, 23, 'It claps its hands at him and hisses him out of his place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 1, '“Surely there is a mine for silver and a place where gold is refined.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 2, 'Iron is taken from the earth, and copper is smelted from ore.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 3, 'Man puts an end to the darkness; he probes the farthest recesses for ore in deepest darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 4, 'Far from human habitation he cuts a shaft in places forgotten by the foot of man. Far from men he dangles and sways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 5, 'Food may come from the earth, but from below it is transformed as by fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 6, 'Its rocks are the source of sapphires, containing flecks of gold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 7, 'No bird of prey knows that path; no falcon’s eye has seen it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 8, 'Proud beasts have never trodden it; no lion has ever prowled over it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 9, 'The miner strikes the flint; he overturns mountains at their base.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 10, 'He hews out channels in the rocks, and his eyes spot every treasure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 11, 'He stops up the sources of the streams to bring what is hidden to light.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 12, 'But where can wisdom be found, and where does understanding dwell?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 13, 'No man can know its value, nor is it found in the land of the living.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 14, 'The ocean depths say, ‘It is not in me,’ while the sea declares, ‘It is not with me.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 15, 'It cannot be bought with gold, nor can its price be weighed out in silver.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 16, 'It cannot be valued in the gold of Ophir, in precious onyx or sapphire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 17, 'Neither gold nor crystal can compare to it, nor jewels of fine gold be exchanged for it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 18, 'Coral and quartz are unworthy of mention; the price of wisdom is beyond rubies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 19, 'Topaz from Cush cannot compare to it, nor can it be valued in pure gold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 20, 'From where then does wisdom come, and where does understanding dwell?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 21, 'It is hidden from the eyes of every living thing and concealed from the birds of the air.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 22, 'Abaddon and Death say, ‘We have heard a rumor about it.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 23, 'But God understands its way, and He knows its place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 24, 'For He looks to the ends of the earth and sees everything under the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 25, 'When God fixed the weight of the wind and measured out the waters,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 26, 'when He set a limit for the rain and a path for the thunderbolt,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 27, 'then He looked at wisdom and appraised it; He established it and searched it out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 28, 28, 'And He said to man, ‘Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom, and to turn away from evil is understanding.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 1, 'And Job continued his discourse:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 2, '“How I long for the months gone by, for the days when God watched over me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 3, 'when His lamp shone above my head, and by His light I walked through the darkness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 4, 'when I was in my prime, when the friendship of God rested on my tent,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 5, 'when the Almighty was still with me and my children were around me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 6, 'when my steps were bathed in cream and the rock poured out for me streams of oil!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 7, 'When I went out to the city gate and took my seat in the public square,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 8, 'the young men saw me and withdrew, and the old men rose to their feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 9, 'The princes refrained from speaking and covered their mouths with their hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 10, 'The voices of the nobles were hushed, and their tongues stuck to the roofs of their mouths.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 11, 'For those who heard me called me blessed, and those who saw me commended me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 12, 'because I rescued the poor who cried out and the fatherless who had no helper.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 13, 'The dying man blessed me, and I made the widow’s heart sing for joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 14, 'I put on righteousness, and it clothed me; justice was my robe and my turban.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 15, 'I served as eyes to the blind and as feet to the lame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 16, 'I was a father to the needy, and I took up the case of the stranger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 17, 'I shattered the fangs of the unjust and snatched the prey from his teeth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 18, 'So I thought: ‘I will die in my nest and multiply my days as the sand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 19, 'My roots will spread out to the waters, and the dew will rest nightly on my branches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 20, 'My glory is ever new within me, and my bow is renewed in my hand.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 21, 'Men listened to me with expectation, waiting silently for my counsel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 22, 'After my words, they spoke no more; my speech settled on them like dew.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 23, 'They waited for me as for rain and drank in my words like spring showers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 24, 'If I smiled at them, they did not believe it; the light of my countenance was precious.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 29, 25, 'I chose their course and presided as chief. So I dwelt as a king among his troops, as a comforter of the mourners.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 1, '“But now they mock me, men younger than I am, whose fathers I would have refused to entrust with my sheep dogs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 2, 'What use to me was the strength of their hands, since their vigor had left them?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 3, 'Gaunt from poverty and hunger, they gnawed the dry land, and the desolate wasteland by night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 4, 'They plucked mallow among the shrubs, and the roots of the broom tree were their food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 5, 'They were banished from among men, shouted down like thieves,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 6, 'so that they lived on the slopes of the wadis, among the rocks and in holes in the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 7, 'They cried out among the shrubs and huddled beneath the nettles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 8, 'A senseless and nameless brood, they were driven off the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 9, 'And now they mock me in song; I have become a byword among them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 10, 'They abhor me and keep far from me; they do not hesitate to spit in my face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 11, 'Because God has unstrung my bow and afflicted me, they have cast off restraint in my presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 12, 'The rabble arises at my right; they lay snares for my feet and build siege ramps against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 13, 'They tear up my path; they profit from my destruction, with no one to restrain them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 14, 'They advance as through a wide breach; through the ruins they keep rolling in.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 15, 'Terrors are turned loose against me; they drive away my dignity as by the wind, and my prosperity has passed like a cloud.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 16, 'And now my soul is poured out within me; days of affliction grip me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 17, 'Night pierces my bones, and my gnawing pains never rest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 18, 'With great force He grasps my garment; He seizes me by the collar of my tunic.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 19, 'He throws me into the mud, and I have become like dust and ashes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 20, 'I cry out to You for help, but You do not answer; when I stand up, You merely look at me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 21, 'You have ruthlessly turned on me; You oppose me with Your strong hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 22, 'You snatch me up into the wind and drive me before it; You toss me about in the storm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 23, 'Yes, I know that You will bring me down to death, to the place appointed for all the living.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 24, 'Yet no one stretches out his hand to a ruined man when he cries for help in his distress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 25, 'Have I not wept for those in trouble? Has my soul not grieved for the needy?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 26, 'But when I hoped for good, evil came; when I looked for light, darkness fell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 27, 'I am churning within and cannot rest; days of affliction confront me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 28, 'I go about blackened, but not by the sun. I stand up in the assembly and cry for help.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 29, 'I have become a brother of jackals, a companion of ostriches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 30, 'My skin grows black and peels, and my bones burn with fever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 30, 31, 'My harp is tuned to mourning and my flute to the sound of weeping.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 1, '“I have made a covenant with my eyes. How then could I gaze with desire at a virgin?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 2, 'For what is the allotment of God from above, or the heritage from the Almighty on high?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 3, 'Does not disaster come to the unjust and calamity to the workers of iniquity?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 4, 'Does He not see my ways and count my every step?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 5, 'If I have walked in falsehood or my foot has rushed to deceit,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 6, 'let God weigh me with honest scales, that He may know my integrity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 7, 'If my steps have turned from the path, if my heart has followed my eyes, or if impurity has stuck to my hands,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 8, 'then may another eat what I have sown, and may my crops be uprooted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 9, 'If my heart has been enticed by my neighbor’s wife, or I have lurked at his door,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 10, 'then may my own wife grind grain for another, and may other men sleep with her.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 11, 'For that would be a heinous crime, an iniquity to be judged.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 12, 'For it is a fire that burns down to Abaddon; it would root out my entire harvest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 13, 'If I have rejected the cause of my manservant or maidservant when they made a complaint against me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 14, 'what will I do when God rises to judge? How will I answer when called to account?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 15, 'Did not He who made me in the womb also make them? Did not the same One form us in the womb?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 16, 'If I have denied the desires of the poor or allowed the widow’s eyes to fail,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 17, 'if I have eaten my morsel alone, not sharing it with the fatherless—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 18, 'though from my youth I reared him as would a father, and from my mother’s womb I guided the widow—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 19, 'if I have seen one perish for lack of clothing, or a needy man without a cloak,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 20, 'if his heart has not blessed me for warming him with the fleece of my sheep,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 21, 'if I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless because I saw that I had support in the gate,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 22, 'then may my arm fall from my shoulder and be torn from its socket.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 23, 'For calamity from God terrifies me, and His splendor I cannot overpower.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 24, 'If I have put my trust in gold or called pure gold my security,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 25, 'if I have rejoiced in my great wealth because my hand had gained so much,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 26, 'if I have beheld the sun in its radiance or the moon moving in splendor,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 27, 'so that my heart was secretly enticed and my hand threw a kiss from my mouth,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 28, 'this would also be an iniquity to be judged, for I would have denied God on high.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 29, 'If I have rejoiced in my enemy’s ruin, or exulted when evil befell him—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 30, 'I have not allowed my mouth to sin by asking for his life with a curse—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 31, 'if the men of my house have not said, ‘Who is there who has not had his fill?’—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 32, 'but no stranger had to lodge on the street, for my door has been open to the traveler—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 33, 'if I have covered my transgressions like Adam by hiding my guilt in my heart,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 34, 'because I greatly feared the crowds and the contempt of the clans terrified me, so that I kept silent and would not go outside—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 35, '(Oh, that I had one to hear me! Here is my signature. Let the Almighty answer me; let my accuser compose an indictment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 36, 'Surely I would carry it on my shoulder and wear it like a crown.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 37, 'I would give account of all my steps; I would approach Him like a prince.)—'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 38, 'if my land cries out against me and its furrows weep together,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 39, 'if I have devoured its produce without payment or broken the spirit of its tenants,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 31, 40, 'then let briers grow instead of wheat and stinkweed instead of barley.” Thus conclude the words of Job.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 1, 'So these three men stopped answering Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 2, 'This kindled the anger of Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite, of the family of Ram. He burned with anger against Job for justifying himself rather than God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 3, 'and he burned with anger against Job’s three friends because they had failed to refute Job, and yet had condemned him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 4, 'Now Elihu had waited to speak to Job because the others were older than he.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 5, 'But when he saw that the three men had no further reply, his anger was kindled.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 6, 'So Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite declared: “I am young in years, while you are old; that is why I was timid and afraid to tell you what I know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 7, 'I thought that age should speak, and many years should teach wisdom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 8, 'But there is a spirit in a man, the breath of the Almighty, that gives him understanding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 9, 'It is not only the old who are wise, or the elderly who understand justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 10, 'Therefore I say, ‘Listen to me; I too will declare what I know.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 11, 'Indeed, I waited while you spoke; I listened to your reasoning; as you searched for words,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 12, 'I paid you full attention. But no one proved Job wrong; not one of you rebutted his arguments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 13, 'So do not claim, ‘We have found wisdom; let God, not man, refute him.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 14, 'But Job has not directed his words against me, and I will not answer him with your arguments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 15, 'Job’s friends are dismayed, with no more to say; words have escaped them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 16, 'Must I wait, now that they are silent, now that they stand and no longer reply?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 17, 'I too will answer; yes, I will declare what I know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 18, 'For I am full of words, and my spirit within me compels me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 19, 'Behold, my belly is like unvented wine; it is about to burst like a new wineskin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 20, 'I must speak and find relief; I must open my lips and respond.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 21, 'I will be partial to no one, nor will I flatter any man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 32, 22, 'For I do not know how to flatter, or my Maker would remove me in an instant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 1, '“But now, O Job, hear my speech, and listen to all my words.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 2, 'Behold, I will open my mouth; my address is on the tip of my tongue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 3, 'My words are from an upright heart, and my lips speak sincerely what I know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 4, 'The Spirit of God has made me, and the breath of the Almighty gives me life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 5, 'Refute me if you can; prepare your case and confront me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 6, 'I am just like you before God; I was also formed from clay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 7, 'Surely no fear of me should terrify you; nor will my hand be heavy upon you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 8, 'Surely you have spoken in my hearing, and I have heard these very words:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 9, '‘I am pure, without transgression; I am clean, with no iniquity in me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 10, 'Yet God finds occasions against me; He counts me as His enemy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 11, 'He puts my feet in the stocks; He watches over all my paths.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 12, 'Behold, you are not right in this matter. I will answer you, for God is greater than man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 13, 'Why do you complain to Him that He answers nothing a man asks?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 14, 'For God speaks in one way and in another, yet no one notices.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 15, 'In a dream, in a vision in the night, when deep sleep falls upon men as they slumber on their beds,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 16, 'He opens their ears and terrifies them with warnings'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 17, 'to turn a man from wrongdoing and keep him from pride,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 18, 'to preserve his soul from the Pit and his life from perishing by the sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 19, 'A man is also chastened on his bed with pain and constant distress in his bones,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 20, 'so that he detests his bread, and his soul loathes his favorite food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 21, 'His flesh wastes away from sight, and his hidden bones protrude.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 22, 'He draws near to the Pit, and his life to the messengers of death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 23, 'Yet if there is a messenger on his side, one mediator in a thousand, to tell a man what is right for him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 24, 'to be gracious to him and say, ‘Spare him from going down to the Pit; I have found his ransom,’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 25, 'then his flesh is refreshed like a child’s; he returns to the days of his youth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 26, 'He prays to God and finds favor; he sees God’s face and shouts for joy, and God restores His righteousness to that man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 27, 'Then he sings before men with these words: ‘I have sinned and perverted what was right; yet I did not get what I deserved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 28, 'He redeemed my soul from going down to the Pit, and I will live to see the light.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 29, 'Behold, all these things God does to a man, two or even three times,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 30, 'to bring back his soul from the Pit, that he may be enlightened with the light of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 31, 'Pay attention, Job, and listen to me; be silent, and I will speak.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 32, 'But if you have something to say, answer me; speak up, for I would like to vindicate you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 33, 33, 'But if not, then listen to me; be quiet, and I will teach you wisdom.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 1, 'Then Elihu continued:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 2, '“Hear my words, O wise men; give ear to me, O men of learning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 3, 'For the ear tests words as the mouth tastes food.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 4, 'Let us choose for ourselves what is right; let us learn together what is good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 5, 'For Job has declared, ‘I am righteous, yet God has deprived me of justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 6, 'Would I lie about my case? My wound is incurable, though I am without transgression.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 7, 'What man is like Job, who drinks up derision like water?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 8, 'He keeps company with evildoers and walks with wicked men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 9, 'For he has said, ‘It profits a man nothing that he should delight in God.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 10, 'Therefore listen to me, O men of understanding. Far be it from God to do wrong, and from the Almighty to act unjustly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 11, 'For according to a man’s deeds He repays him; according to a man’s ways He brings consequences.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 12, 'Indeed, it is true that God does not act wickedly, and the Almighty does not pervert justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 13, 'Who gave Him charge over the earth? Who appointed Him over the whole world?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 14, 'If He were to set His heart to it and withdraw His Spirit and breath,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 15, 'all flesh would perish together and mankind would return to the dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 16, 'If you have understanding, hear this; listen to my words.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 17, 'Could one who hates justice govern? Will you condemn the just and mighty One,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 18, 'who says to kings, ‘You are worthless!’ and to nobles, ‘You are wicked,’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 19, 'who is not partial to princes and does not favor rich over poor? For they are all the work of His hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 20, 'They die in an instant, in the middle of the night. The people convulse and pass away; the mighty are removed without human hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 21, 'For His eyes are on the ways of a man, and He sees his every step.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 22, 'There is no darkness or deep shadow where the workers of iniquity can hide.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 23, 'For God need not examine a man further or have him approach for judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 24, 'He shatters the mighty without inquiry and sets up others in their place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 25, 'Therefore, He recognizes their deeds; He overthrows them in the night and they are crushed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 26, 'He strikes them for their wickedness in full view,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 27, 'because they turned aside from Him and had no regard for any of His ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 28, 'They caused the cry of the poor to come before Him, and He heard the outcry of the afflicted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 29, 'But when He remains silent, who can condemn Him? When He hides His face, who can see Him? Yet He watches over both man and nation,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 30, 'that godless men should not rule or lay snares for the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 31, 'Suppose someone says to God, ‘I have endured my punishment; I will offend no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 32, 'Teach me what I cannot see; if I have done wrong, I will not do it again.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 33, 'Should God repay you on your own terms when you have disavowed His? You must choose, not I; so tell me what you know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 34, 'Men of understanding will declare to me, and the wise men who hear me will say:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 35, '‘Job speaks without knowledge; his words lack insight.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 36, 'If only Job were tried to the utmost for answering like a wicked man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 34, 37, 'For he adds rebellion to his sin; he claps his hands among us and multiplies his words against God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 1, 'And Elihu went on to say:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 2, '“Do you think this is just? You say, ‘I am more righteous than God.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 3, 'For you ask, ‘What does it profit me, and what benefit do I gain apart from sin?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 4, 'I will reply to you and to your friends as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 5, 'Look to the heavens and see; gaze at the clouds high above you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 6, 'If you sin, what do you accomplish against Him? If you multiply your transgressions, what do you do to Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 7, 'If you are righteous, what do you give Him, or what does He receive from your hand?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 8, 'Your wickedness affects only a man like yourself, and your righteousness only a son of man.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 9, 'Men cry out under great oppression; they plead for relief from the arm of the mighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 10, 'But no one asks, ‘Where is God my Maker, who gives us songs in the night,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 11, 'who teaches us more than the beasts of the earth and makes us wiser than the birds of the air?’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 12, 'There they cry out, but He does not answer, because of the pride of evil men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 13, 'Surely God does not listen to empty pleas, and the Almighty does not take note of it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 14, 'How much less, then, when you say that you do not see Him, that your case is before Him and you must wait for Him,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 15, 'and further, that in His anger He has not punished or taken much notice of folly!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 35, 16, 'So Job opens his mouth in vain and multiplies words without knowledge.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 1, 'And Elihu continued:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 2, '“Bear with me a little longer, and I will show you that there is more to be said on God’s behalf.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 3, 'I get my knowledge from afar, and I will ascribe justice to my Maker.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 4, 'For truly my words are free of falsehood; one perfect in knowledge is with you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 5, 'Indeed, God is mighty, but He despises no one; He is mighty in strength of understanding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 6, 'He does not keep the wicked alive, but He grants justice to the afflicted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 7, 'He does not take His eyes off the righteous, but He enthrones them with kings and exalts them forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 8, 'And if men are bound with chains, caught in cords of affliction,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 9, 'then He tells them their deeds and how arrogantly they have transgressed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 10, 'He opens their ears to correction and commands that they turn from iniquity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 11, 'If they obey and serve Him, then they end their days in prosperity and their years in happiness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 12, 'But if they do not obey, then they perish by the sword and die without knowledge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 13, 'The godless in heart harbor resentment; even when He binds them, they do not cry for help.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 14, 'They die in their youth, among the male shrine prostitutes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 15, 'God rescues the afflicted by their affliction and opens their ears in oppression.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 16, 'Indeed, He drew you from the jaws of distress to a spacious and broad place, to a table full of richness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 17, 'But now you are laden with the judgment due the wicked; judgment and justice have seized you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 18, 'Be careful that no one lures you with riches; do not let a large bribe lead you astray.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 19, 'Can your wealth or all your mighty effort keep you from distress?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 20, 'Do not long for the night, when people vanish from their homes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 21, 'Be careful not to turn to iniquity, for this you have preferred to affliction.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 22, 'Behold, God is exalted in His power. Who is a teacher like Him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 23, 'Who has appointed His way for Him, or told Him, ‘You have done wrong’?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 24, 'Remember to magnify His work, which men have praised in song.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 25, 'All mankind has seen it; men behold it from afar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 26, 'Indeed, God is great—beyond our knowledge; the number of His years is unsearchable.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 27, 'For He draws up drops of water which distill the rain from the mist,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 28, 'which the clouds pour out and shower abundantly on mankind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 29, 'Furthermore, who can understand how the clouds spread out, how the thunder roars from His pavilion?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 30, 'See how He scatters His lightning around Him and covers the depths of the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 31, 'For by these He judges the nations and provides food in abundance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 32, 'He fills His hands with lightning and commands it to strike its mark.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 36, 33, 'The thunder declares His presence; even the cattle regard the rising storm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 1, '“At this my heart also pounds and leaps from its place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 2, 'Listen closely to the thunder of His voice and the rumbling that comes from His mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 3, 'He unleashes His lightning beneath the whole sky and sends it to the ends of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 4, 'Then there comes a roaring sound; He thunders with His majestic voice. He does not restrain the lightning when His voice resounds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 5, 'God thunders wondrously with His voice; He does great things we cannot comprehend.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 6, 'For He says to the snow, ‘Fall on the earth,’ and to the gentle rain, ‘Pour out a mighty downpour.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 7, 'He seals up the hand of every man, so that all men may know His work.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 8, 'The wild animals enter their lairs; they settle down in their dens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 9, 'The tempest comes from its chamber, and the cold from the driving north winds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 10, 'By the breath of God the ice is formed and the watery expanses are frozen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 11, 'He loads the clouds with moisture; He scatters His lightning through them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 12, 'They swirl about, whirling at His direction, accomplishing all that He commands over the face of all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 13, 'Whether for punishment or for His land, He accomplishes this in His loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 14, 'Listen to this, O Job; stand still and consider the wonders of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 15, 'Do you know how God dispatches the clouds or makes the lightning flash?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 16, 'Do you understand how the clouds float, those wonders of Him who is perfect in knowledge?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 17, 'You whose clothes get hot when the land lies hushed under the south wind,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 18, 'can you, like Him, spread out the skies to reflect the heat like a mirror of bronze?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 19, 'Teach us what we should say to Him; we cannot draw up our case when our faces are in darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 20, 'Should He be told that I want to speak? Would a man ask to be swallowed up?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 21, 'Now no one can gaze at the sun when it is bright in the skies after the wind has swept them clean.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 22, 'Out of the north He comes in golden splendor; awesome majesty surrounds Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 23, 'The Almighty is beyond our reach; He is exalted in power! In His justice and great righteousness He does not oppress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 37, 24, 'Therefore, men fear Him, for He is not partial to the wise in heart.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 1, 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind and said:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 2, '“Who is this who obscures My counsel by words without knowledge?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 3, 'Now brace yourself like a man; I will question you, and you shall inform Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 4, 'Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth? Tell Me, if you have understanding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 5, 'Who fixed its measurements? Surely you know! Or who stretched a measuring line across it?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 6, 'On what were its foundations set, or who laid its cornerstone,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 7, 'while the morning stars sang together and all the sons of God shouted for joy?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 8, 'Who enclosed the sea behind doors when it burst forth from the womb,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 9, 'when I made the clouds its garment and thick darkness its blanket,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 10, 'when I fixed its boundaries and set in place its bars and doors,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 11, 'and I declared: ‘You may come this far, but no farther; here your proud waves must stop’?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 12, 'In your days, have you commanded the morning or assigned the dawn its place,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 13, 'that it might spread to the ends of the earth and shake the wicked out of it?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 14, 'The earth takes shape like clay under a seal; its hills stand out like the folds of a garment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 15, 'Light is withheld from the wicked, and their upraised arm is broken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 16, 'Have you journeyed to the vents of the sea or walked in the trenches of the deep?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 17, 'Have the gates of death been revealed to you? Have you seen the gates of the shadow of death?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 18, 'Have you surveyed the extent of the earth? Tell Me, if you know all this.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 19, 'Where is the way to the home of light? Do you know where darkness resides,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 20, 'so you can lead it back to its border? Do you know the paths to its home?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 21, 'Surely you know, for you were already born! And the number of your days is great!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 22, 'Have you entered the storehouses of snow or observed the storehouses of hail,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 23, 'which I hold in reserve for times of trouble, for the day of war and battle?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 24, 'In which direction is the lightning dispersed, or the east wind scattered over the earth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 25, 'Who cuts a channel for the flood or clears a path for the thunderbolt,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 26, 'to bring rain on a barren land, on a desert where no man lives,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 27, 'to satisfy the parched wasteland and make it sprout with tender grass?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 28, 'Does the rain have a father? Who has begotten the drops of dew?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 29, 'From whose womb does the ice emerge? Who gives birth to the frost from heaven,'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 30, 'when the waters become hard as stone and the surface of the deep is frozen?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 31, 'Can you bind the chains of the Pleiades or loosen the belt of Orion?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 32, 'Can you bring forth the constellations in their seasons or lead out the Bear and her cubs?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 33, 'Do you know the laws of the heavens? Can you set their dominion over the earth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 34, 'Can you command the clouds so that a flood of water covers you?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 35, 'Can you send the lightning bolts on their way? Do they report to you, ‘Here we are’?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 36, 'Who has put wisdom in the heart or given understanding to the mind?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 37, 'Who has the wisdom to count the clouds? Or who can tilt the water jars of the heavens'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 38, 'when the dust hardens into a mass and the clods of earth stick together?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 39, 'Can you hunt the prey for a lioness or satisfy the hunger of young lions'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 40, 'when they crouch in their dens and lie in wait in the thicket?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 38, 41, 'Who provides food for the raven when its young cry out to God as they wander about for lack of food?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 1, '“Do you know when mountain goats give birth? Have you watched the doe bear her fawn?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 2, 'Can you count the months they are pregnant? Do you know the time they give birth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 3, 'They crouch down and bring forth their young; they deliver their newborn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 4, 'Their young ones thrive and grow up in the open field; they leave and do not return.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 5, 'Who set the wild donkey free? Who released the swift donkey from the harness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 6, 'I made the wilderness his home and the salt flats his dwelling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 7, 'He scorns the tumult of the city and never hears the shouts of a driver.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 8, 'He roams the mountains for pasture, searching for any green thing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 9, 'Will the wild ox consent to serve you? Will he stay by your manger at night?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 10, 'Can you hold him to the furrow with a harness? Will he plow the valleys behind you?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 11, 'Can you rely on his great strength? Will you leave your hard work to him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 12, 'Can you trust him to bring in your grain and gather it to your threshing floor?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 13, 'The wings of the ostrich flap joyfully, but cannot match the pinions and feathers of the stork.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 14, 'For she leaves her eggs on the ground and lets them warm in the sand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 15, 'She forgets that a foot may crush them, or a wild animal may trample them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 16, 'She treats her young harshly, as if not her own, with no concern that her labor was in vain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 17, 'For God has deprived her of wisdom; He has not endowed her with understanding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 18, 'Yet when she proudly spreads her wings, she laughs at the horse and its rider.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 19, 'Do you give strength to the horse or adorn his neck with a mane?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 20, 'Do you make him leap like a locust, striking terror with his proud snorting?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 21, 'He paws in the valley and rejoices in his strength; he charges into battle.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 22, 'He laughs at fear, frightened of nothing; he does not turn back from the sword.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 23, 'A quiver rattles at his side, along with a flashing spear and lance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 24, 'Trembling with excitement, he devours the distance; he cannot stand still when the ram’s horn sounds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 25, 'At the blast of the horn, he snorts with fervor. He catches the scent of battle from afar— the shouts of captains and the cry of war.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 26, 'Does the hawk take flight by your understanding and spread his wings toward the south?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 27, 'Does the eagle soar at your command and make his nest on high?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 28, 'He dwells on a cliff and lodges there; his stronghold is on a rocky crag.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 29, 'From there he spies out food; his eyes see it from afar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 39, 30, 'His young ones feast on blood; and where the slain are, there he is.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 1, 'And the LORD said to Job:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 2, '“Will the faultfinder contend with the Almighty? Let him who argues with God give an answer.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 3, 'Then Job answered the LORD:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 4, '“Behold, I am insignificant. How can I reply to You? I place my hand over my mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 5, 'I have spoken once, but I have no answer— twice, but I have nothing to add.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 6, 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind and said:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 7, '“Now brace yourself like a man; I will question you, and you shall inform Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 8, 'Would you really annul My justice? Would you condemn Me to justify yourself?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 9, 'Do you have an arm like God’s? Can you thunder with a voice like His?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 10, 'Then adorn yourself with majesty and splendor, and clothe yourself with honor and glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 11, 'Unleash the fury of your wrath; look on every proud man and bring him low.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 12, 'Look on every proud man and humble him; trample the wicked where they stand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 13, 'Bury them together in the dust; imprison them in the grave.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 14, 'Then I will confess to you that your own right hand can save you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 15, 'Look at Behemoth, which I made along with you. He feeds on grass like an ox.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 16, 'See the strength of his loins and the power in the muscles of his belly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 17, 'His tail sways like a cedar; the sinews of his thighs are tightly knit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 18, 'His bones are tubes of bronze; his limbs are rods of iron.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 19, 'He is the foremost of God’s works; only his Maker can draw the sword against him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 20, 'The hills yield him their produce, while all the beasts of the field play nearby.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 21, 'He lies under the lotus plants, hidden among the reeds of the marsh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 22, 'The lotus plants conceal him in their shade; the willows of the brook surround him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 23, 'Though the river rages, Behemoth is unafraid; he remains secure, though the Jordan surges to his mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 40, 24, 'Can anyone capture him as he looks on, or pierce his nose with a snare?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 1, '“Can you pull in Leviathan with a hook or tie down his tongue with a rope?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 2, 'Can you put a cord through his nose or pierce his jaw with a hook?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 3, 'Will he beg you for mercy or speak to you softly?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 4, 'Will he make a covenant with you to take him as a slave for life?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 5, 'Can you pet him like a bird or put him on a leash for your maidens?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 6, 'Will traders barter for him or divide him among the merchants?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 7, 'Can you fill his hide with harpoons or his head with fishing spears?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 8, 'If you lay a hand on him, you will remember the battle and never repeat it!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 9, 'Surely hope of overcoming him is false. Is not the sight of him overwhelming?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 10, 'No one is so fierce as to rouse Leviathan. Then who is able to stand against Me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 11, 'Who has given to Me that I should repay him? Everything under heaven is Mine.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 12, 'I cannot keep silent about his limbs, his power and graceful form.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 13, 'Who can strip off his outer coat? Who can approach him with a bridle?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 14, 'Who can open his jaws, ringed by his fearsome teeth?'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 15, 'His rows of scales are his pride, tightly sealed together.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 16, 'One scale is so near to another that no air can pass between them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 17, 'They are joined to one another; they clasp and cannot be separated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 18, 'His snorting flashes with light, and his eyes are like the rays of dawn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 19, 'Firebrands stream from his mouth; fiery sparks shoot forth!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 20, 'Smoke billows from his nostrils as from a boiling pot over burning reeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 21, 'His breath sets coals ablaze, and flames pour from his mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 22, 'Strength resides in his neck, and dismay leaps before him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 23, 'The folds of his flesh are tightly joined; they are firm and immovable.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 24, 'His chest is as hard as a rock, as hard as a lower millstone!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 25, 'When Leviathan rises up, the mighty are terrified; they withdraw before his thrashing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 26, 'The sword that reaches him has no effect, nor does the spear or dart or arrow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 27, 'He regards iron as straw and bronze as rotten wood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 28, 'No arrow can make him flee; slingstones become like chaff to him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 29, 'A club is regarded as straw, and he laughs at the sound of the lance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 30, 'His undersides are jagged potsherds, spreading out the mud like a threshing sledge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 31, 'He makes the depths seethe like a cauldron; he makes the sea like a jar of ointment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 32, 'He leaves a glistening wake behind him; one would think the deep had white hair!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 33, 'Nothing on earth is his equal— a creature devoid of fear!'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 41, 34, 'He looks down on all the haughty; he is king over all the proud.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 1, 'Then Job replied to the LORD:'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 2, '“I know that You can do all things and that no plan of Yours can be thwarted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 3, 'You asked, ‘Who is this who conceals My counsel without knowledge?’ Surely I spoke of things I did not understand, things too wonderful for me to know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 4, 'You said, ‘Listen now, and I will speak. I will question you, and you shall inform Me.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 5, 'My ears had heard of You, but now my eyes have seen You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 6, 'Therefore I retract my words, and I repent in dust and ashes.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 7, 'After the LORD had spoken these words to Job, He said to Eliphaz the Temanite, “My wrath is kindled against you and your two friends. For you have not spoken about Me accurately, as My servant Job has.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 8, 'So now, take seven bulls and seven rams, go to My servant Job, and sacrifice a burnt offering for yourselves. Then My servant Job will pray for you, for I will accept his prayer and not deal with you according to your folly. For you have not spoken accurately about Me, as My servant Job has.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 9, 'So Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite went and did as the LORD had told them; and the LORD accepted Job’s request.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 10, 'After Job had prayed for his friends, the LORD restored his prosperity and doubled his former possessions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 11, 'All his brothers and sisters and prior acquaintances came and dined with him in his house. They consoled him and comforted him over all the adversity that the LORD had brought upon him. And each one gave him a piece of silver and a gold ring.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 12, 'So the LORD blessed Job’s latter days more than his first. He owned 14,000 sheep, 6,000 camels, 1,000 yoke of oxen, and 1,000 female donkeys.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 13, 'And he also had seven sons and three daughters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 14, 'He named his first daughter Jemimah, his second Keziah, and his third Keren-happuch.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 15, 'No women as beautiful as Job’s daughters could be found in all the land, and their father granted them an inheritance among their brothers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 16, 'After this, Job lived 140 years and saw his children and their children to the fourth generation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Job', 18, 42, 17, 'And so Job died, old and full of years.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 1, 1, 'Blessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, or set foot on the path of sinners, or sit in the seat of mockers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 1, 2, 'But his delight is in the Law of the LORD, and on His law he meditates day and night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 1, 3, 'He is like a tree planted by streams of water, yielding its fruit in season, whose leaf does not wither, and who prospers in all he does.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 1, 4, 'Not so the wicked! For they are like chaff driven off by the wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 1, 5, 'Therefore the wicked will not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the assembly of the righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 1, 6, 'For the LORD guards the path of the righteous, but the way of the wicked will perish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 1, 'Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 2, 'The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together, against the LORD and against His Anointed One:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 3, '“Let us break Their chains and cast away Their cords.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 4, 'The One enthroned in heaven laughs; the Lord taunts them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 5, 'Then He rebukes them in His anger, and terrifies them in His fury:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 6, '“I have installed My King on Zion, upon My holy mountain.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 7, 'I will proclaim the decree spoken to Me by the LORD: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 8, 'Ask Me, and I will make the nations Your inheritance, the ends of the earth Your possession.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 9, 'You will break them with an iron scepter; You will shatter them like pottery.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 10, 'Therefore be wise, O kings; be admonished, O judges of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 11, 'Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 2, 12, 'Kiss the Son, lest He be angry and you perish in your rebellion, when His wrath ignites in an instant. Blessed are all who take refuge in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 1, 'O LORD, how my foes have increased! How many rise up against me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 2, 'Many say of me, “God will not deliver him.” Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 3, 'But You, O LORD, are a shield around me, my glory, and the One who lifts my head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 4, 'To the LORD I cry aloud, and He answers me from His holy mountain. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 5, 'I lie down and sleep; I wake again, for the LORD sustains me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 6, 'I will not fear the myriads set against me on every side.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 7, 'Arise, O LORD! Save me, O my God! Strike all my enemies on the jaw; break the teeth of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 3, 8, 'Salvation belongs to the LORD; may Your blessing be on Your people. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 1, 'Answer me when I call, O God of my righteousness! You have relieved my distress; show me grace and hear my prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 2, 'How long, O men, will my honor be maligned? How long will you love vanity and seek after lies? Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 3, 'Know that the LORD has set apart the godly for Himself; the LORD hears when I call to Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 4, 'Be angry, yet do not sin; on your bed, search your heart and be still. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 5, 'Offer the sacrifices of the righteous and trust in the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 6, 'Many ask, “Who can show us the good?” Shine the light of Your face upon us, O LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 7, 'You have filled my heart with more joy than when grain and new wine abound.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 4, 8, 'I will lie down and sleep in peace, for You alone, O LORD, make me dwell in safety.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 1, 'Give ear to my words, O LORD; consider my groaning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 2, 'Attend to the sound of my cry, my King and my God, for to You I pray.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 3, 'In the morning, O LORD, You hear my voice; at daybreak I lay my plea before You and wait in expectation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 4, 'For You are not a God who delights in wickedness; no evil can dwell with You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 5, 'The boastful cannot stand in Your presence; You hate all workers of iniquity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 6, 'You destroy those who tell lies; the LORD abhors the man of bloodshed and deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 7, 'But I will enter Your house by the abundance of Your loving devotion; in reverence I will bow down toward Your holy temple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 8, 'Lead me, O LORD, in Your righteousness because of my enemies; make straight Your way before me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 9, 'For not a word they speak can be trusted; destruction lies within them. Their throats are open graves; their tongues practice deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 10, 'Declare them guilty, O God; let them fall by their own devices. Drive them out for their many transgressions, for they have rebelled against You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 11, 'But let all who take refuge in You rejoice; let them ever shout for joy. May You shelter them, that those who love Your name may rejoice in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 5, 12, 'For surely You, O LORD, bless the righteous; You surround them with the shield of Your favor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 1, 'O LORD, do not rebuke me in Your anger or discipline me in Your wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 2, 'Be merciful to me, O LORD, for I am frail; heal me, O LORD, for my bones are in agony.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 3, 'My soul is deeply distressed. How long, O LORD, how long?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 4, 'Turn, O LORD, and deliver my soul; save me because of Your loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 5, 'For there is no mention of You in death; who can praise You from Sheol?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 6, 'I am weary from groaning; all night I flood my bed with weeping and drench my couch with tears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 7, 'My eyes fail from grief; they grow dim because of all my foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 8, 'Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity, for the LORD has heard my weeping.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 9, 'The LORD has heard my cry for mercy; the LORD accepts my prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 6, 10, 'All my enemies will be ashamed and dismayed; they will turn back in sudden disgrace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 1, 'O LORD my God, I take refuge in You; save me and deliver me from all my pursuers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 2, 'or they will shred my soul like a lion and tear me to pieces with no one to rescue me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 3, 'O LORD my God, if I have done this, if injustice is on my hands,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 4, 'if I have rewarded my ally with evil, if I have plundered my foe without cause,');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 5, 'then may my enemy pursue me and overtake me; may he trample me to the ground and leave my honor in the dust. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 6, 'Arise, O LORD, in Your anger; rise up against the fury of my enemies. Awake, my God, and ordain judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 7, 'Let the assembled peoples gather around You; take Your seat over them on high.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 8, 'The LORD judges the peoples; vindicate me, O LORD, according to my righteousness and integrity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 9, 'Put an end to the evil of the wicked, but establish the righteous, O righteous God who searches hearts and minds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 10, 'My shield is with God, who saves the upright in heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 11, 'God is a righteous judge and a God who feels indignation each day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 12, 'If one does not repent, God will sharpen His sword; He has bent and strung His bow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 13, 'He has prepared His deadly weapons; He ordains His arrows with fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 14, 'Behold, the wicked man travails with evil; he conceives trouble and births falsehood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 15, 'He has dug a hole and hollowed it out; he has fallen into a pit of his own making.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 16, 'His trouble recoils on himself, and his violence falls on his own head.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 7, 17, 'I will thank the LORD for His righteousness and sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 1, 'O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth! You have set Your glory above the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 2, 'From the mouths of children and infants You have ordained praise on account of Your adversaries, to silence the enemy and avenger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 3, 'When I behold Your heavens, the work of Your fingers, the moon and the stars, which You have set in place—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 4, 'what is man that You are mindful of him, or the son of man that You care for him?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 5, 'You made him a little lower than the angels; You crowned him with glory and honor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 6, 'You made him ruler of the works of Your hands; You have placed everything under his feet:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 7, 'all sheep and oxen, and even the beasts of the field,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 8, 'the birds of the air and the fish of the sea, all that swim the paths of the seas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 8, 9, 'O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 1, 'I will give thanks to the LORD with all my heart; I will recount all Your wonders.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 2, 'I will be glad and rejoice in You; I will sing praise to Your name, O Most High.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 3, 'When my enemies retreat, they stumble and perish before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 4, 'For You have upheld my just cause; You sit on Your throne judging righteously.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 5, 'You have rebuked the nations; You have destroyed the wicked; You have erased their name forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 6, 'The enemy has come to eternal ruin, and You have uprooted their cities; the very memory of them has vanished.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 7, 'But the LORD abides forever; He has established His throne for judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 8, 'He judges the world with justice; He governs the people with equity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 9, 'The LORD is a refuge for the oppressed, a stronghold in times of trouble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 10, 'Those who know Your name trust in You, for You, O LORD, have not forsaken those who seek You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 11, 'Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in Zion; proclaim His deeds among the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 12, 'For the Avenger of bloodshed remembers; He does not ignore the cry of the afflicted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 13, 'Be merciful to me, O LORD; see how my enemies afflict me! Lift me up from the gates of death,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 14, 'that I may declare all Your praises— that within the gates of Daughter Zion I may rejoice in Your salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 15, 'The nations have fallen into a pit of their making; their feet are caught in the net they have hidden.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 16, 'The LORD is known by the justice He brings; the wicked are ensnared by the work of their hands. Higgaion Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 17, 'The wicked will return to Sheol— all the nations who forget God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 18, 'For the needy will not always be forgotten; nor the hope of the oppressed forever dashed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 19, 'Rise up, O LORD, do not let man prevail; let the nations be judged in Your presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 9, 20, 'Lay terror upon them, O LORD; let the nations know they are but men. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 1, 'Why, O LORD, do You stand far off? Why do You hide in times of trouble?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 2, 'In pride the wicked pursue the needy; let them be caught in the schemes they devise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 3, 'For the wicked man boasts in the cravings of his heart; he blesses the greedy and reviles the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 4, 'In his pride the wicked man does not seek Him; in all his schemes there is no God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 5, 'He is secure in his ways at all times; Your lofty judgments are far from him; he sneers at all his foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 6, 'He says to himself, “I will not be moved; from age to age I am free of distress.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 7, 'His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and violence; trouble and malice are under his tongue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 8, 'He lies in wait near the villages; in ambush he slays the innocent; his eyes watch in stealth for the helpless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 9, 'He lies in wait like a lion in a thicket; he lurks to seize the oppressed; he catches the lowly in his net.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 10, 'They are crushed and beaten down; the hapless fall prey to his strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 11, 'He says to himself, “God has forgotten; He hides His face and never sees.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 12, 'Arise, O LORD! Lift up Your hand, O God! Do not forget the helpless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 13, 'Why has the wicked man renounced God? He says to himself, “You will never call me to account.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 14, 'But You have regarded trouble and grief; You see to repay it by Your hand. The victim entrusts himself to You; You are the helper of the fatherless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 15, 'Break the arm of the wicked and evildoer; call him to account for his wickedness until none is left to be found.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 16, 'The LORD is King forever and ever; the nations perish from His land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 17, 'You have heard, O LORD, the desire of the humble; You will strengthen their hearts. You will incline Your ear,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 10, 18, 'to vindicate the fatherless and oppressed, that the men of the earth may strike terror no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 1, 'In the LORD I take refuge. How then can you say to me: “Flee like a bird to your mountain!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 2, 'For behold, the wicked bend their bows. They set their arrow on the string to shoot from the shadows at the upright in heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 3, 'If the foundations are destroyed, what can the righteous do?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 4, 'The LORD is in His holy temple; the LORD is on His heavenly throne. His eyes are watching closely; they examine the sons of men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 5, 'The LORD tests the righteous and the wicked; His soul hates the lover of violence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 6, 'On the wicked He will rain down fiery coals and sulfur; a scorching wind will be their portion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 11, 7, 'For the LORD is righteous; He loves justice. The upright will see His face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 1, 'Help, O LORD, for the godly are no more; the faithful have vanished from among men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 2, 'They lie to one another; they speak with flattering lips and a double heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 3, 'May the LORD cut off all flattering lips and every boastful tongue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 4, 'They say, “With our tongues we will prevail. We own our lips—who can be our master?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 5, '“For the cause of the oppressed and for the groaning of the needy, I will now arise,” says the LORD. “I will bring safety to him who yearns.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 6, 'The words of the LORD are flawless, like silver refined in a furnace, like gold purified sevenfold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 7, 'You, O LORD, will keep us; You will forever guard us from this generation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 12, 8, 'The wicked wander freely, and vileness is exalted among men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 13, 1, 'How long, O LORD? Will You forget me forever? How long will You hide Your face from me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 13, 2, 'How long must I wrestle in my soul, with sorrow in my heart each day? How long will my enemy dominate me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 13, 3, 'Consider me and respond, O LORD my God. Give light to my eyes, lest I sleep in death,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 13, 4, 'lest my enemy say, “I have overcome him,” and my foes rejoice when I fall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 13, 5, 'But I have trusted in Your loving devotion; my heart will rejoice in Your salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 13, 6, 'I will sing to the LORD, for He has been good to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 1, 'The fool says in his heart, “There is no God.” They are corrupt; their acts are vile. There is no one who does good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 2, 'The LORD looks down from heaven upon the sons of men to see if any understand, if any seek God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 3, 'All have turned away, they have together become corrupt; there is no one who does good, not even one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 4, 'Will the workers of iniquity never learn? They devour my people like bread; they refuse to call upon the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 5, 'There they are, overwhelmed with dread, for God is in the company of the righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 6, 'You sinners frustrate the plans of the oppressed, yet the LORD is their shelter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 14, 7, 'Oh, that the salvation of Israel would come from Zion! When the LORD restores His captive people, let Jacob rejoice, let Israel be glad!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 15, 1, 'O LORD, who may abide in Your tent? Who may dwell on Your holy mountain?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 15, 2, 'He who walks with integrity and practices righteousness, who speaks the truth from his heart,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 15, 3, 'who has no slander on his tongue, who does no harm to his neighbor, who casts no scorn on his friend,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 15, 4, 'who despises the vile but honors those who fear the LORD, who does not revise a costly oath,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 15, 5, 'who lends his money without interest and refuses a bribe against the innocent. He who does these things will never be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 1, 'Preserve me, O God, for in You I take refuge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 2, 'I said to the LORD, “You are my Lord; apart from You I have no good thing.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 3, 'As for the saints in the land, they are the excellence in whom all my delight resides.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 4, 'Sorrows will multiply to those who chase other gods. I will not pour out their libations of blood, or speak their names with my lips.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 5, 'The LORD is my chosen portion and my cup; You have made my lot secure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 6, 'The lines of my boundary have fallen in pleasant places; surely my inheritance is delightful.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 7, 'I will bless the LORD who counsels me; even at night my conscience instructs me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 8, 'I have set the LORD always before me. Because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 9, 'Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices; my body also will dwell securely.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 10, 'For You will not abandon my soul to Sheol, nor will You let Your Holy One see decay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 16, 11, 'You have made known to me the path of life; You will fill me with joy in Your presence, with eternal pleasures at Your right hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 1, 'Hear, O LORD, my righteous plea; listen to my cry. Give ear to my prayer— it comes from lips free of deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 2, 'May my vindication come from Your presence; may Your eyes see what is right.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 3, 'You have tried my heart; You have visited me in the night. You have tested me and found no evil; I have resolved not to sin with my mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 4, 'As for the deeds of men— by the word of Your lips I have avoided the ways of the violent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 5, 'My steps have held to Your paths; my feet have not slipped.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 6, 'I call on You, O God, for You will answer me. Incline Your ear to me; hear my words.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 7, 'Show the wonders of Your loving devotion, You who save by Your right hand those who seek refuge from their foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 8, 'Keep me as the apple of Your eye; hide me in the shadow of Your wings'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 9, 'from the wicked who assail me, from my mortal enemies who surround me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 10, 'They have closed their callous hearts; their mouths speak with arrogance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 11, 'They have tracked us down, and now surround us; their eyes are set to cast us to the ground,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 12, 'like a lion greedy for prey, like a young lion lurking in ambush.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 13, 'Arise, O LORD, confront them! Bring them to their knees; deliver me from the wicked by Your sword,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 14, 'from such men, O LORD, by Your hand— from men of the world whose portion is in this life. May You fill the bellies of Your treasured ones and satisfy their sons, so they leave their abundance to their children.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 17, 15, 'As for me, I will behold Your face in righteousness; when I awake, I will be satisfied in Your presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 1, 'I love You, O LORD, my strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 2, 'The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer. My God is my rock, in whom I take refuge, my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my stronghold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 3, 'I will call upon the LORD, who is worthy to be praised; so shall I be saved from my enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 4, 'The cords of death encompassed me; the torrents of chaos overwhelmed me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 5, 'The cords of Sheol entangled me; the snares of death confronted me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 6, 'In my distress I called upon the LORD; I cried to my God for help. From His temple He heard my voice, and my cry for His help reached His ears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 7, 'Then the earth shook and quaked, and the foundations of the mountains trembled; they were shaken because He burned with anger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 8, 'Smoke rose from His nostrils, and consuming fire came from His mouth; glowing coals blazed forth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 9, 'He parted the heavens and came down with dark clouds beneath His feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 10, 'He mounted a cherub and flew; He soared on the wings of the wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 11, 'He made darkness His hiding place, and storm clouds a canopy around Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 12, 'From the brightness of His presence His clouds advanced— hailstones and coals of fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 13, 'The LORD thundered from heaven; the voice of the Most High resounded— hailstones and coals of fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 14, 'He shot His arrows and scattered the foes; He hurled lightning and routed them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 15, 'The channels of the sea appeared, and the foundations of the world were exposed, at Your rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of Your nostrils.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 16, 'He reached down from on high and took hold of me; He drew me out of deep waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 17, 'He rescued me from my powerful enemy, from foes too mighty for me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 18, 'They confronted me in my day of calamity, but the LORD was my support.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 19, 'He brought me out into the open; He rescued me because He delighted in me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 20, 'The LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness; He has repaid me according to the cleanness of my hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 21, 'For I have kept the ways of the LORD and have not wickedly departed from my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 22, 'For all His ordinances are before me; I have not disregarded His statutes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 23, 'And I have been blameless before Him and kept myself from iniquity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 24, 'So the LORD has repaid me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in His sight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 25, 'To the faithful You show Yourself faithful, to the blameless You show Yourself blameless;'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 26, 'to the pure You show Yourself pure, but to the crooked You show Yourself shrewd.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 27, 'For You save an afflicted people, but You humble those with haughty eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 28, 'For You, O LORD, light my lamp; my God lights up my darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 29, 'For in You I can charge an army, and with my God I can scale a wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 30, 'As for God, His way is perfect; the word of the LORD is flawless. He is a shield to all who take refuge in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 31, 'For who is God besides the LORD? And who is the Rock except our God?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 32, 'It is God who arms me with strength and makes my way clear.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 33, 'He makes my feet like those of a deer and stations me upon the heights.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 34, 'He trains my hands for battle; my arms can bend a bow of bronze.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 35, 'You have given me Your shield of salvation; Your right hand upholds me, and Your gentleness exalts me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 36, 'You broaden the path beneath me so that my ankles do not give way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 37, 'I pursued my enemies and overtook them; I did not turn back until they were consumed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 38, 'I crushed them so they could not rise; they have fallen under my feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 39, 'You have armed me with strength for battle; You have subdued my foes beneath me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 40, 'You have made my enemies retreat before me; I put an end to those who hated me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 41, 'They cried for help, but there was no one to save them— to the LORD, but He did not answer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 42, 'I ground them as dust in the face of the wind; I trampled them like mud in the streets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 43, 'You have delivered me from the strife of the people; You have made me the head of nations; a people I had not known shall serve me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 44, 'When they hear me, they obey me; foreigners cower before me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 45, 'Foreigners lose heart and come trembling from their strongholds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 46, 'The LORD lives, and blessed be my Rock! And may the God of my salvation be exalted—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 47, 'the God who avenges me and subdues nations beneath me,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 48, 'who delivers me from my enemies. You exalt me above my foes; You rescue me from violent men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 49, 'Therefore I will praise You, O LORD, among the nations; I will sing praises to Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 18, 50, 'Great salvation He brings to His king. He shows loving devotion to His anointed, to David and his descendants forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 1, 'The heavens declare the glory of God; the skies proclaim the work of His hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 2, 'Day after day they pour forth speech; night after night they reveal knowledge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 3, 'Without speech or language, without a sound to be heard,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 4, 'their voice has gone out into all the earth, their words to the ends of the world. In the heavens He has pitched a tent for the sun.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 5, 'Like a bridegroom emerging from his chamber, like a champion rejoicing to run his course,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 6, 'it rises at one end of the heavens and runs its circuit to the other; nothing is deprived of its warmth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 7, 'The Law of the LORD is perfect, reviving the soul; the testimony of the LORD is trustworthy, making wise the simple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 8, 'The precepts of the LORD are right, bringing joy to the heart; the commandments of the LORD are radiant, giving light to the eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 9, 'The fear of the LORD is pure, enduring forever; the judgments of the LORD are true, being altogether righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 10, 'They are more precious than gold, than much pure gold; they are sweeter than honey, than honey from the comb.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 11, 'By them indeed Your servant is warned; in keeping them is great reward.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 12, 'Who can discern his own errors? Cleanse me from my hidden faults.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 13, 'Keep Your servant also from willful sins; may they not rule over me. Then I will be blameless and cleansed of great transgression.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 19, 14, 'May the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be pleasing in Your sight, O LORD, my Rock and my Redeemer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 1, 'May the LORD answer you in the day of trouble; may the name of the God of Jacob protect you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 2, 'May He send you help from the sanctuary and sustain you from Zion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 3, 'May He remember all your gifts and look favorably on your burnt offerings. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 4, 'May He give you the desires of your heart and make all your plans succeed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 5, 'May we shout for joy at your victory and raise a banner in the name of our God. May the LORD grant all your petitions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 6, 'Now I know that the LORD saves His anointed; He answers him from His holy heaven with the saving power of His right hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 7, 'Some trust in chariots and others in horses, but we trust in the name of the LORD our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 8, 'They collapse and fall, but we rise up and stand firm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 20, 9, 'O LORD, save the king. Answer us on the day we call.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 1, 'O LORD, the king rejoices in Your strength. How greatly he exults in Your salvation!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 2, 'You have granted his heart’s desire and have not withheld the request of his lips. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 3, 'For You welcomed him with rich blessings; You placed on his head a crown of pure gold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 4, 'He asked You for life, and You granted it— length of days, forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 5, 'Great is his glory in Your salvation; You bestow on him splendor and majesty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 6, 'For You grant him blessings forever; You cheer him with joy in Your presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 7, 'For the king trusts in the LORD; through the loving devotion of the Most High, he will not be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 8, 'Your hand will apprehend all Your enemies; Your right hand will seize those who hate You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 9, 'You will place them in a fiery furnace at the time of Your appearing. In His wrath the LORD will engulf them, and the fire will consume them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 10, 'You will wipe their descendants from the earth, and their offspring from the sons of men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 11, 'Though they intend You harm, the schemes they devise will not prevail.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 12, 'For You will put them to flight when Your bow is trained upon them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 21, 13, 'Be exalted, O LORD, in Your strength; we will sing and praise Your power.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 1, 'My God, my God, why have You forsaken me? Why are You so far from saving me, so far from my words of groaning?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 2, 'I cry out by day, O my God, but You do not answer, and by night, but I have no rest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 3, 'Yet You are holy, enthroned on the praises of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 4, 'In You our fathers trusted; they trusted and You delivered them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 5, 'They cried out to You and were set free; they trusted in You and were not disappointed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 6, 'But I am a worm and not a man, scorned by men and despised by the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 7, 'All who see me mock me; they sneer and shake their heads:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 8, '“He trusts in the LORD, let the LORD deliver him; let the LORD rescue him, since He delights in him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 9, 'Yet You brought me forth from the womb; You made me secure at my mother’s breast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 10, 'From birth I was cast upon You; from my mother’s womb You have been my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 11, 'Be not far from me, for trouble is near and there is no one to help.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 12, 'Many bulls surround me; strong bulls of Bashan encircle me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 13, 'They open their jaws against me like lions that roar and maul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 14, 'I am poured out like water, and all my bones are disjointed. My heart is like wax; it melts away within me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 15, 'My strength is dried up like a potsherd, and my tongue sticks to the roof of my mouth. You lay me in the dust of death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 16, 'For dogs surround me; a band of evil men encircles me; they have pierced my hands and feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 17, 'I can count all my bones; they stare and gloat over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 18, 'They divide my garments among them and cast lots for my clothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 19, 'But You, O LORD, be not far off; O my Strength, come quickly to help me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 20, 'Deliver my soul from the sword, my precious life from the power of wild dogs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 21, 'Save me from the mouth of the lion; at the horns of the wild oxen You have answered me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 22, 'I will proclaim Your name to my brothers; I will praise You in the assembly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 23, 'You who fear the LORD, praise Him! All descendants of Jacob, honor Him! All offspring of Israel, revere Him!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 24, 'For He has not despised or detested the torment of the afflicted. He has not hidden His face from him, but has attended to his cry for help.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 25, 'My praise for You resounds in the great assembly; I will fulfill my vows before those who fear You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 26, 'The poor will eat and be satisfied; those who seek the LORD will praise Him. May your hearts live forever!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 27, 'All the ends of the earth will remember and turn to the LORD. All the families of the nations will bow down before Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 28, 'For dominion belongs to the LORD and He rules over the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 29, 'All the rich of the earth will feast and worship; all who go down to the dust will kneel before Him— even those unable to preserve their lives.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 30, 'Posterity will serve Him; they will declare the Lord to a new generation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 22, 31, 'They will come and proclaim His righteousness to a people yet unborn— all that He has done.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 23, 1, 'The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 23, 2, 'He makes me lie down in green pastures; He leads me beside quiet waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 23, 3, 'He restores my soul; He guides me in the paths of righteousness for the sake of His name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 23, 4, 'Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil, for You are with me; Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 23, 5, 'You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies. You anoint my head with oil; my cup overflows.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 23, 6, 'Surely goodness and mercy will follow me all the days of my life, and I will dwell in the house of the LORD forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 1, 'The earth is the LORD’s, and the fullness thereof, the world and all who dwell therein.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 2, 'For He has founded it upon the seas and established it upon the waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 3, 'Who may ascend the hill of the LORD? Who may stand in His holy place?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 4, 'He who has clean hands and a pure heart, who does not lift up his soul to an idol or swear deceitfully.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 5, 'He will receive blessing from the LORD and vindication from the God of his salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 6, 'Such is the generation of those who seek Him, who seek Your face, O God of Jacob. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 7, 'Lift up your heads, O gates! Be lifted up, O ancient doors, that the King of Glory may enter!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 8, 'Who is this King of Glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 9, 'Lift up your heads, O gates! Be lifted up, O ancient doors, that the King of Glory may enter!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 24, 10, 'Who is He, this King of Glory? The LORD of Hosts— He is the King of Glory. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 1, 'To You, O LORD, I lift up my soul;'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 2, 'in You, my God, I trust. Do not let me be put to shame; do not let my enemies exult over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 3, 'Surely none who wait for You will be put to shame; but those who are faithless without cause will be disgraced.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 4, 'Show me Your ways, O LORD; teach me Your paths.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 5, 'Guide me in Your truth and teach me, for You are the God of my salvation; all day long I wait for You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 6, 'Remember, O LORD, Your compassion and loving devotion, for they are from age to age.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 7, 'Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my rebellious acts; remember me according to Your loving devotion, because of Your goodness, O LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 8, 'Good and upright is the LORD; therefore He shows sinners the way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 9, 'He guides the humble in what is right and teaches them His way.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 10, 'All the LORD’s ways are loving and faithful to those who keep His covenant and His decrees.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 11, 'For the sake of Your name, O LORD, forgive my iniquity, for it is great.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 12, 'Who is the man who fears the LORD? He will instruct him in the path chosen for him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 13, 'His soul will dwell in prosperity, and his descendants will inherit the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 14, 'The LORD confides in those who fear Him, and reveals His covenant to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 15, 'My eyes are always on the LORD, for He will free my feet from the mesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 16, 'Turn to me and be gracious, for I am lonely and afflicted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 17, 'The troubles of my heart increase; free me from my distress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 18, 'Consider my affliction and trouble, and take away all my sins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 19, 'Consider my enemies, for they are many, and they hate me with vicious hatred.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 20, 'Guard my soul and deliver me; let me not be put to shame, for I take refuge in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 21, 'May integrity and uprightness preserve me, because I wait for You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 25, 22, 'Redeem Israel, O God, from all its distress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 1, 'Vindicate me, O LORD! For I have walked with integrity; I have trusted in the LORD without wavering.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 2, 'Test me, O LORD, and try me; examine my heart and mind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 3, 'For Your loving devotion is before my eyes, and I have walked in Your truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 4, 'I do not sit with deceitful men, nor keep company with hypocrites.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 5, 'I hate the mob of evildoers, and refuse to sit with the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 6, 'I wash my hands in innocence that I may go about Your altar, O LORD,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 7, 'to raise my voice in thanksgiving and declare all Your wonderful works.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 8, 'O LORD, I love the house where You dwell, the place where Your glory resides.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 9, 'Do not take my soul away with sinners, or my life with men of bloodshed,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 10, 'in whose hands are wicked schemes, whose right hands are full of bribes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 11, 'But I will walk with integrity; redeem me and be merciful to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 26, 12, 'My feet stand on level ground; in the congregations I will bless the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 1, 'The LORD is my light and my salvation— whom shall I fear? The LORD is the stronghold of my life— whom shall I dread?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 2, 'When the wicked came upon me to devour my flesh, my enemies and foes stumbled and fell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 3, 'Though an army encamps around me, my heart will not fear; though a war breaks out against me, I will keep my trust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 4, 'One thing I have asked of the LORD; this is what I desire: to dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to gaze on the beauty of the LORD and seek Him in His temple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 5, 'For in the day of trouble He will hide me in His shelter; He will conceal me under the cover of His tent; He will set me high upon a rock.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 6, 'Then my head will be held high above my enemies around me. At His tabernacle I will offer sacrifices with shouts of joy; I will sing and make music to the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 7, 'Hear, O LORD, my voice when I call; be merciful and answer me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 8, 'My heart said, “Seek His face.” Your face, O LORD, I will seek.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 9, 'Hide not Your face from me, nor turn away Your servant in anger. You have been my helper; do not leave me or forsake me, O God of my salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 10, 'Though my father and mother forsake me, the LORD will receive me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 11, 'Teach me Your way, O LORD, and lead me on a level path, because of my oppressors.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 12, 'Do not hand me over to the will of my foes, for false witnesses rise up against me, breathing out violence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 13, 'Still I am certain to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 27, 14, 'Wait patiently for the LORD; be strong and courageous. Wait patiently for the LORD!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 1, 'To You, O LORD, I call; be not deaf to me, O my Rock. For if You remain silent, I will be like those descending to the Pit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 2, 'Hear my cry for mercy when I call to You for help, when I lift up my hands toward Your holy sanctuary.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 3, 'Do not drag me away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity, who speak peace to their neighbors while malice is in their hearts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 4, 'Repay them according to their deeds and for their works of evil. Repay them for what their hands have done; bring back on them what they deserve.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 5, 'Since they show no regard for the works of the LORD or what His hands have done, He will tear them down and never rebuild them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 6, 'Blessed be the LORD, for He has heard my cry for mercy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 7, 'The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart trusts in Him, and I am helped. Therefore my heart rejoices, and I give thanks to Him with my song.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 8, 'The LORD is the strength of His people, a stronghold of salvation for His anointed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 28, 9, 'Save Your people and bless Your inheritance; shepherd them and carry them forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 1, 'Ascribe to the LORD, O heavenly beings, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 2, 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due His name; worship the LORD in the splendor of His holiness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 3, 'The voice of the LORD is over the waters; the God of glory thunders; the LORD is heard over many waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 4, 'The voice of the LORD is powerful; the voice of the LORD is majestic.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 5, 'The voice of the LORD breaks the cedars; the LORD shatters the cedars of Lebanon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 6, 'He makes Lebanon skip like a calf, and Sirion like a young wild ox.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 7, 'The voice of the LORD strikes with flames of fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 8, 'The voice of the LORD shakes the wilderness; the LORD shakes the Wilderness of Kadesh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 9, 'The voice of the LORD twists the oaks and strips the forests bare. And in His temple all cry, “Glory!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 10, 'The LORD sits enthroned over the flood; the LORD is enthroned as King forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 29, 11, 'The LORD gives His people strength; the LORD blesses His people with peace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 1, 'I will exalt You, O LORD, for You have lifted me up and have not allowed my foes to rejoice over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 2, 'O LORD my God, I cried to You for help, and You healed me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 3, 'O LORD, You pulled me up from Sheol; You spared me from descending into the Pit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 4, 'Sing to the LORD, O you His saints, and praise His holy name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 5, 'For His anger is fleeting, but His favor lasts a lifetime. Weeping may stay the night, but joy comes in the morning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 6, 'In prosperity I said, “I will never be shaken.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 7, 'O LORD, You favored me; You made my mountain stand strong. When You hid Your face, I was dismayed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 8, 'To You, O LORD, I called, and I begged my Lord for mercy:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 9, '“What gain is there in my bloodshed, in my descent to the Pit? Will the dust praise You? Will it proclaim Your faithfulness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 10, 'Hear me, O LORD, and have mercy; O LORD, be my helper.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 11, 'You turned my mourning into dancing; You peeled off my sackcloth and clothed me with joy,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 30, 12, 'that my heart may sing Your praises and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 1, 'In You, O LORD, I have taken refuge; let me never be put to shame; save me by Your righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 2, 'Incline Your ear to me; come quickly to my rescue. Be my rock of refuge, the stronghold of my deliverance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 3, 'For You are my rock and my fortress; lead me and guide me for the sake of Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 4, 'You free me from the net laid out for me, for You are my refuge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 5, 'Into Your hands I commit my spirit; You have redeemed me, O LORD, God of truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 6, 'I hate those who cling to worthless idols, but in the LORD I trust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 7, 'I will be glad and rejoice in Your loving devotion, for You have seen my affliction; You have known the anguish of my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 8, 'You have not delivered me to the enemy; You have set my feet in the open.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 9, 'Be merciful to me, O LORD, for I am in distress; my eyes fail from sorrow, my soul and body as well.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 10, 'For my life is consumed with grief and my years with groaning; my iniquity has drained my strength, and my bones are wasting away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 11, 'Among all my enemies I am a disgrace, and among my neighbors even more. I am dreaded by my friends— they flee when they see me on the street.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 12, 'I am forgotten like a dead man, out of mind. I am like a broken vessel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 13, 'For I hear the slander of many; there is terror on every side. They conspire against me and plot to take my life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 14, 'But I trust in You, O LORD; I say, “You are my God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 15, 'My times are in Your hands; deliver me from my enemies and from those who pursue me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 16, 'Make Your face shine on Your servant; save me by Your loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 17, 'O LORD, let me not be ashamed, for I have called on You. Let the wicked be put to shame; let them lie silent in Sheol.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 18, 'May lying lips be silenced— lips that speak with arrogance against the righteous, full of pride and contempt.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 19, 'How great is Your goodness which You have laid up for those who fear You, which You have bestowed before the sons of men on those who take refuge in You!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 20, 'You hide them in the secret place of Your presence from the schemes of men. You conceal them in Your shelter from accusing tongues.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 21, 'Blessed be the LORD, for He has shown me His loving devotion in a city under siege.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 22, 'In my alarm I said, “I am cut off from Your sight!” But You heard my plea for mercy when I called to You for help.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 23, 'Love the LORD, all His saints. The LORD preserves the faithful, but fully repays the arrogant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 31, 24, 'Be strong and courageous, all you who hope in the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 1, 'Blessed is he whose transgressions are forgiven, whose sins are covered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 2, 'Blessed is the man whose iniquity the LORD does not count against him, in whose spirit there is no deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 3, 'When I kept silent, my bones became brittle from my groaning all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 4, 'For day and night Your hand was heavy upon me; my strength was drained as in the summer heat. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 5, 'Then I acknowledged my sin to You and did not hide my iniquity. I said, “I will confess my transgressions to the LORD,” and You forgave the guilt of my sin. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 6, 'Therefore let all the godly pray to You while You may be found. Surely when great waters rise, they will not come near.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 7, 'You are my hiding place. You protect me from trouble; You surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 8, 'I will instruct you and teach you the way you should go; I will give you counsel and watch over you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 9, 'Do not be like the horse or mule, which have no understanding; they must be controlled with bit and bridle to make them come to you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 10, 'Many are the sorrows of the wicked, but loving devotion surrounds him who trusts in the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 32, 11, 'Be glad in the LORD and rejoice, O righteous ones; shout for joy, all you upright in heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 1, 'Rejoice in the LORD, O righteous ones; it is fitting for the upright to praise Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 2, 'Praise the LORD with the harp; make music to Him with ten strings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 3, 'Sing to Him a new song; play skillfully with a shout of joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 4, 'For the word of the LORD is upright, and all His work is trustworthy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 5, 'The LORD loves righteousness and justice; the earth is full of His loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 6, 'By the word of the LORD the heavens were made, and all the stars by the breath of His mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 7, 'He piles up the waters of the sea; He puts the depths into storehouses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 8, 'Let all the earth fear the LORD; let all the people of the world revere Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 9, 'For He spoke, and it came to be; He commanded, and it stood firm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 10, 'The LORD frustrates the plans of the nations; He thwarts the devices of the peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 11, 'The counsel of the LORD stands forever, the purposes of His heart to all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 12, 'Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD, the people He has chosen as His inheritance!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 13, 'The LORD looks down from heaven; He sees all the sons of men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 14, 'From His dwelling place He gazes on all who inhabit the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 15, 'He shapes the hearts of each; He considers all their works.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 16, 'No king is saved by his vast army; no warrior is delivered by his great strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 17, 'A horse is a vain hope for salvation; even its great strength cannot save.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 18, 'Surely the eyes of the LORD are on those who fear Him, on those whose hope is in His loving devotion'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 19, 'to deliver them from death and keep them alive in famine.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 20, 'Our soul waits for the LORD; He is our help and our shield.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 21, 'For our hearts rejoice in Him, since we trust in His holy name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 33, 22, 'May Your loving devotion rest on us, O LORD, as we put our hope in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 1, 'I will bless the LORD at all times; His praise will always be on my lips.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 2, 'My soul boasts in the LORD; let the oppressed hear and rejoice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 3, 'Magnify the LORD with me; let us exalt His name together.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 4, 'I sought the LORD, and He answered me; He delivered me from all my fears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 5, 'Those who look to Him are radiant with joy; their faces shall never be ashamed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 6, 'This poor man called out, and the LORD heard him; He saved him from all his troubles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 7, 'The angel of the LORD encamps around those who fear Him, and he delivers them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 8, 'Taste and see that the LORD is good; blessed is the man who takes refuge in Him!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 9, 'Fear the LORD, you His saints, for those who fear Him lack nothing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 10, 'Young lions go lacking and hungry, but those who seek the LORD lack no good thing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 11, 'Come, children, listen to me; I will teach you the fear of the LORD.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 12, 'Who is the man who delights in life, who desires to see good days?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 13, 'Keep your tongue from evil and your lips from deceitful speech.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 14, 'Turn away from evil and do good; seek peace and pursue it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 15, 'The eyes of the LORD are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their cry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 16, 'But the face of the LORD is against those who do evil, to wipe out all memory of them from the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 17, 'The righteous cry out, and the LORD hears; He delivers them from all their troubles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 18, 'The LORD is near to the brokenhearted; He saves the contrite in spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 19, 'Many are the afflictions of the righteous, but the LORD delivers him from them all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 20, 'He protects all his bones; not one of them will be broken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 21, 'Evil will slay the wicked, and the haters of the righteous will be condemned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 34, 22, 'The LORD redeems His servants, and none who take refuge in Him will be condemned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 1, 'Contend with my opponents, O LORD; fight against those who fight against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 2, 'Take up Your shield and buckler; arise and come to my aid.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 3, 'Draw the spear and javelin against my pursuers; say to my soul: “I am your salvation.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 4, 'May those who seek my life be disgraced and put to shame; may those who plan to harm me be driven back and confounded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 5, 'May they be like chaff in the wind, as the angel of the LORD drives them away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 6, 'May their path be dark and slick, as the angel of the LORD pursues.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 7, 'For without cause they laid their net for me; without reason they dug a pit for my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 8, 'May ruin befall them by surprise; may the net they hid ensnare them; may they fall into the hazard they created.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 9, 'Then my soul will rejoice in the LORD and exult in His salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 10, 'All my bones will exclaim, “Who is like You, O LORD, who delivers the afflicted from the aggressor, the poor and needy from the robber?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 11, 'Hostile witnesses come forward; they make charges I know nothing about.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 12, 'They repay me evil for good, to the bereavement of my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 13, 'Yet when they were ill, I put on sackcloth; I humbled myself with fasting, but my prayers returned unanswered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 14, 'I paced about as for my friend or brother; I was bowed down with grief, like one mourning for his mother.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 15, 'But when I stumbled, they assembled in glee; they gathered together against me. Assailants I did not know slandered me without ceasing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 16, 'Like godless jesters at a feast, they gnashed their teeth at me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 17, 'How long, O Lord, will You look on? Rescue my soul from their ravages, my precious life from these lions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 18, 'Then I will give You thanks in the great assembly; I will praise You among many people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 19, 'Let not my enemies gloat over me without cause, nor those who hate me without reason wink in malice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 20, 'For they do not speak peace, but they devise deceitful schemes against those who live quietly in the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 21, 'They gape at me and say, “Aha, aha! Our eyes have seen!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 22, 'O LORD, You have seen it; be not silent. O Lord, be not far from me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 23, 'Awake and rise to my defense, to my cause, my God and my Lord!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 24, 'Vindicate me by Your righteousness, O LORD my God, and do not let them gloat over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 25, 'Let them not say in their hearts, “Aha, just what we wanted!” Let them not say, “We have swallowed him up!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 26, 'May those who gloat in my distress be ashamed and confounded; may those who exalt themselves over me be clothed in shame and reproach.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 27, 'May those who favor my vindication shout for joy and gladness; may they always say, “Exalted be the LORD who delights in His servant’s well-being.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 35, 28, 'Then my tongue will proclaim Your righteousness and Your praises all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 1, 'An oracle is in my heart regarding the transgression of the wicked man: There is no fear of God before his eyes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 2, 'For his eyes are too full of conceit to detect or hate his own sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 3, 'The words of his mouth are wicked and deceitful; he has ceased to be wise and well-doing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 4, 'Even on his bed he plots wickedness; he sets himself on a path that is not good; he fails to reject evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 5, 'Your loving devotion, O LORD, reaches to the heavens, Your faithfulness to the clouds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 6, 'Your righteousness is like the highest mountains; Your judgments are like the deepest sea. O LORD, You preserve man and beast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 7, 'How precious is Your loving devotion, O God, that the children of men take refuge in the shadow of Your wings!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 8, 'They feast on the abundance of Your house, and You give them drink from Your river of delights.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 9, 'For with You is the fountain of life; in Your light we see light.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 10, 'Extend Your loving devotion to those who know You, and Your righteousness to the upright in heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 11, 'Let not the foot of the proud come against me, nor the hand of the wicked drive me away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 36, 12, 'There the evildoers lie fallen, thrown down and unable to rise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 1, 'Do not fret over those who do evil; do not envy those who do wrong.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 2, 'For they wither quickly like grass and wilt like tender plants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 3, 'Trust in the LORD and do good; dwell in the land and cultivate faithfulness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 4, 'Delight yourself in the LORD, and He will give you the desires of your heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 5, 'Commit your way to the LORD; trust in Him, and He will do it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 6, 'He will bring forth your righteousness like the dawn, your justice like the noonday sun.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 7, 'Be still before the LORD and wait patiently for Him; do not fret when men prosper in their ways, when they carry out wicked schemes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 8, 'Refrain from anger and abandon wrath; do not fret—it can only bring harm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 9, 'For the evildoers will be cut off, but those who hope in the LORD will inherit the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 10, 'Yet a little while, and the wicked will be no more; though you look for them, they will not be found.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 11, 'But the meek will inherit the land and delight in abundant prosperity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 12, 'The wicked scheme against the righteous and gnash their teeth at them,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 13, 'but the Lord laughs, seeing that their day is coming.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 14, 'The wicked have drawn the sword and bent the bow to bring down the poor and needy, to slay those whose ways are upright.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 15, 'But their swords will pierce their own hearts, and their bows will be broken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 16, 'Better is the little of the righteous than the abundance of many who are wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 17, 'For the arms of the wicked will be broken, but the LORD upholds the righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 18, 'The LORD knows the days of the blameless, and their inheritance will last forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 19, 'In the time of evil they will not be ashamed, and in the days of famine they will be satisfied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 20, 'But the wicked and enemies of the LORD will perish like the glory of the fields. They will vanish; like smoke they will fade away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 21, 'The wicked borrow and do not repay, but the righteous are gracious and giving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 22, 'Surely those He blesses will inherit the land, but the cursed will be destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 23, 'The steps of a man are ordered by the LORD who takes delight in his journey.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 24, 'Though he falls, he will not be overwhelmed, for the LORD is holding his hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 25, 'I once was young and now am old, yet never have I seen the righteous abandoned or their children begging for bread.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 26, 'They are ever generous and quick to lend, and their children are a blessing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 27, 'Turn away from evil and do good, so that you will abide forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 28, 'For the LORD loves justice and will not forsake His saints. They are preserved forever, but the offspring of the wicked will be cut off.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 29, 'The righteous will inherit the land and dwell in it forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 30, 'The mouth of the righteous man utters wisdom, and his tongue speaks justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 31, 'The law of his God is in his heart; his steps do not falter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 32, 'Though the wicked lie in wait for the righteous, and seek to slay them,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 33, 'the LORD will not leave them in their power or let them be condemned under judgment.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 34, 'Wait for the LORD and keep His way, and He will raise you up to inherit the land. When the wicked are cut off, you will see it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 35, 'I have seen a wicked, ruthless man flourishing like a well-rooted native tree,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 36, 'yet he passed away and was no more; though I searched, he could not be found.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 37, 'Consider the blameless and observe the upright, for posterity awaits the man of peace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 38, 'But the transgressors will all be destroyed; the future of the wicked will be cut off.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 39, 'The salvation of the righteous is from the LORD; He is their stronghold in time of trouble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 37, 40, 'The LORD helps and delivers them; He rescues and saves them from the wicked, because they take refuge in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 1, 'O LORD, do not rebuke me in Your anger or discipline me in Your wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 2, 'For Your arrows have pierced me deeply, and Your hand has pressed down on me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 3, 'There is no soundness in my body because of Your anger; there is no rest in my bones because of my sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 4, 'For my iniquities have overwhelmed me; they are a burden too heavy to bear.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 5, 'My wounds are foul and festering because of my sinful folly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 6, 'I am bent and brought low; all day long I go about mourning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 7, 'For my loins are full of burning pain, and no soundness remains in my body.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 8, 'I am numb and badly crushed; I groan in anguish of heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 9, 'O Lord, my every desire is before You; my groaning is not hidden from You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 10, 'My heart pounds, my strength fails, and even the light of my eyes has faded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 11, 'My beloved and friends shun my disease, and my kinsmen stand at a distance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 12, 'Those who seek my life lay snares; those who wish me harm speak destruction, plotting deceit all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 13, 'But like a deaf man, I do not hear; and like a mute man, I do not open my mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 14, 'I am like a man who cannot hear, whose mouth offers no reply.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 15, 'I wait for You, O LORD; You will answer, O Lord my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 16, 'For I said, “Let them not gloat over me— those who taunt me when my foot slips.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 17, 'For I am ready to fall, and my pain is ever with me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 18, 'Yes, I confess my iniquity; I am troubled by my sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 19, 'Many are my enemies without cause, and many hate me without reason.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 20, 'Those who repay my good with evil attack me for pursuing the good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 21, 'Do not forsake me, O LORD; be not far from me, O my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 38, 22, 'Come quickly to help me, O Lord my Savior.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 1, 'I said, “I will watch my ways so that I will not sin with my tongue; I will guard my mouth with a muzzle as long as the wicked are present.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 2, 'I was speechless and still; I remained silent, even from speaking good, and my sorrow was stirred.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 3, 'My heart grew hot within me; as I mused, the fire burned. Then I spoke with my tongue:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 4, '“Show me, O LORD, my end and the measure of my days. Let me know how fleeting my life is.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 5, 'You, indeed, have made my days as handbreadths, and my lifetime as nothing before You. Truly each man at his best exists as but a breath. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 6, 'Surely every man goes about like a phantom; surely he bustles in vain; he heaps up riches not knowing who will haul them away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 7, 'And now, O Lord, for what do I wait? My hope is in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 8, 'Deliver me from all my transgressions; do not make me the reproach of fools.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 9, 'I have become mute; I do not open my mouth because of what You have done.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 10, 'Remove Your scourge from me; I am perishing by the force of Your hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 11, 'You discipline and correct a man for his iniquity, consuming like a moth what he holds dear; surely each man is but a vapor. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 12, 'Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear to my cry for help; do not be deaf to my weeping. For I am a foreigner dwelling with You, a stranger like all my fathers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 39, 13, 'Turn Your gaze away from me, that I may again be cheered before I depart and am no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 1, 'I waited patiently for the LORD; He inclined to me and heard my cry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 2, 'He lifted me up from the pit of despair, out of the miry clay; He set my feet upon a rock, and made my footsteps firm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 3, 'He put a new song in my mouth, a hymn of praise to our God. Many will see and fear and put their trust in the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 4, 'Blessed is the man who has made the LORD his trust, who has not turned to the proud, nor to those who lapse into falsehood.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 5, 'Many, O LORD my God, are the wonders You have done, and the plans You have for us— none can compare to You— if I proclaim and declare them, they are more than I can count.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 6, 'Sacrifice and offering You did not desire, but my ears You have opened. Burnt offerings and sin offerings You did not require.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 7, 'Then I said, “Here I am, I have come— it is written about me in the scroll:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 8, 'I delight to do Your will, O my God; Your law is within my heart.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 9, 'I proclaim righteousness in the great assembly; behold, I do not seal my lips, as You, O LORD, do know.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 10, 'I have not covered up Your righteousness in my heart; I have declared Your faithfulness and salvation; I have not concealed Your loving devotion and faithfulness from the great assembly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 11, 'O LORD, do not withhold Your mercy from me; Your loving devotion and faithfulness will always guard me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 12, 'For evils without number surround me; my sins have overtaken me, so that I cannot see. They are more than the hairs of my head, and my heart has failed within me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 13, 'Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me; hurry, O LORD, to help me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 14, 'May those who seek my life be ashamed and confounded; may those who wish me harm be repelled and humiliated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 15, 'May those who say to me, “Aha, aha!” be appalled at their own shame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 16, 'May all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You; may those who love Your salvation always say, “The LORD be magnified!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 40, 17, 'But I am poor and needy; may the Lord think of me. You are my helper and deliverer; O my God, do not delay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 1, 'Blessed is the one who cares for the poor; the LORD will deliver him in the day of trouble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 2, 'The LORD will protect and preserve him; He will bless him in the land and refuse to surrender him to the will of his foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 3, 'The LORD will sustain him on his bed of illness and restore him from his bed of sickness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 4, 'I said, “O LORD, be gracious to me; heal me, for I have sinned against You.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 5, 'My enemies say with malice: “When will he die and be forgotten?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 6, 'My visitor speaks falsehood; he gathers slander in his heart; he goes out and spreads it abroad.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 7, 'All who hate me whisper against me; they imagine the worst for me:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 8, '“A vile disease has been poured into him; he will never get up from where he lies!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 9, 'Even my close friend whom I trusted, the one who shared my bread, has lifted up his heel against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 10, 'But You, O LORD, be gracious to me and raise me up, that I may repay them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 11, 'By this I know that You delight in me, for my enemy does not triumph over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 12, 'In my integrity You uphold me and set me in Your presence forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 41, 13, 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting. Amen and Amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 1, 'As the deer pants for streams of water, so my soul longs after You, O God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 2, 'My soul thirsts for God, the living God. When shall I come and appear in God’s presence?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 3, 'My tears have been my food both day and night, while men ask me all day long, “Where is your God?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 4, 'These things come to mind as I pour out my soul: how I walked with the multitude, leading the procession to the house of God with shouts of joy and praise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 5, 'Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him for the salvation of His presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 6, 'O my God, my soul despairs within me. Therefore I remember You from the land of Jordan and the peaks of Hermon— even from Mount Mizar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 7, 'Deep calls to deep in the roar of Your waterfalls; all Your breakers and waves have rolled over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 8, 'The LORD decrees His loving devotion by day, and at night His song is with me as a prayer to the God of my life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 9, 'I say to God my Rock, “Why have You forgotten me? Why must I walk in sorrow because of the enemy’s oppression?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 10, 'Like the crushing of my bones, my enemies taunt me, while they say to me all day long, “Where is your God?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 42, 11, 'Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him, my Savior and my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 43, 1, 'Vindicate me, O God, and plead my case against an ungodly nation; deliver me from deceitful and unjust men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 43, 2, 'For You are the God of my refuge. Why have You rejected me? Why must I walk in sorrow because of the enemy’s oppression?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 43, 3, 'Send out Your light and Your truth; let them lead me. Let them bring me to Your holy mountain, and to the place where You dwell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 43, 4, 'Then I will go to the altar of God, to God, my greatest joy. I will praise You with the harp, O God, my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 43, 5, 'Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him, my Savior and my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 1, 'We have heard with our ears, O God; our fathers have told us the work You did in their days, in the days of old.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 2, 'With Your hand You drove out the nations and planted our fathers there; You crushed the peoples and cast them out.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 3, 'For it was not by their sword that they took the land; their arm did not bring them victory. It was by Your right hand, Your arm, and the light of Your face, because You favored them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 4, 'You are my King, O God, who ordains victories for Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 5, 'Through You we repel our foes; through Your name we trample our enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 6, 'For I do not trust in my bow, nor does my sword save me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 7, 'For You save us from our enemies; You put those who hate us to shame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 8, 'In God we have boasted all day long, and Your name we will praise forever. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 9, 'But You have rejected and humbled us; You no longer go forth with our armies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 10, 'You have made us retreat from the foe, and those who hate us have plundered us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 11, 'You have given us up as sheep to be devoured; You have scattered us among the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 12, 'You sell Your people for nothing; no profit do You gain from their sale.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 13, 'You have made us a reproach to our neighbors, a mockery and derision to those around us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 14, 'You have made us a byword among the nations, a laughingstock among the peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 15, 'All day long my disgrace is before me, and shame has covered my face,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 16, 'at the voice of the scorner and reviler, because of the enemy, bent on revenge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 17, 'All this has come upon us, though we have not forgotten You or betrayed Your covenant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 18, 'Our hearts have not turned back; our steps have not strayed from Your path.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 19, 'But You have crushed us in the lair of jackals; You have covered us with deepest darkness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 20, 'If we had forgotten the name of our God or spread out our hands to a foreign god,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 21, 'would not God have discovered, since He knows the secrets of the heart?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 22, 'Yet for Your sake we face death all day long; we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 23, 'Wake up, O Lord! Why are You sleeping? Arise! Do not reject us forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 24, 'Why do You hide Your face and forget our affliction and oppression?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 25, 'For our soul has sunk to the dust; our bodies cling to the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 44, 26, 'Rise up; be our help! Redeem us on account of Your loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 1, 'My heart is stirred by a noble theme as I recite my verses to the king; my tongue is the pen of a skillful writer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 2, 'You are the most handsome of men; grace has anointed your lips, since God has blessed you forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 3, 'Strap your sword at your side, O mighty warrior; appear in your majesty and splendor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 4, 'In your splendor ride forth in victory on behalf of truth and humility and justice; may your right hand show your awesome deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 5, 'Your arrows pierce the hearts of the king’s foes; the nations fall beneath your feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 6, 'Your throne, O God, endures forever and ever, and justice is the scepter of Your kingdom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 7, 'You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness; therefore God, your God, has anointed you above your companions with the oil of joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 8, 'All your garments are fragrant with myrrh and aloes and cassia; from palaces of ivory the harps make you glad.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 9, 'The daughters of kings are among your honored women; the queen stands at your right hand, adorned with the gold of Ophir.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 10, 'Listen, O daughter! Consider and incline your ear: Forget your people and your father’s house,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 11, 'and the king will desire your beauty; bow to him, for he is your lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 12, 'The Daughter of Tyre will come with a gift; men of wealth will seek your favor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 13, 'All glorious is the princess in her chamber; her gown is embroidered with gold.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 14, 'In colorful garments she is led to the king; her virgin companions are brought before you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 15, 'They are led in with joy and gladness; they enter the palace of the king.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 16, 'Your sons will succeed your fathers; you will make them princes throughout the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 45, 17, 'I will commemorate your name through all generations; therefore the nations will praise you forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 1, 'God is our refuge and strength, an ever-present help in times of trouble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 2, 'Therefore we will not fear, though the earth is transformed and the mountains are toppled into the depths of the seas,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 3, 'though their waters roar and foam and the mountains quake in the surge. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 4, 'There is a river whose streams delight the city of God, the holy place where the Most High dwells.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 5, 'God is within her; she will not be moved. God will help her when morning dawns.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 6, 'Nations rage, kingdoms crumble; the earth melts when He lifts His voice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 7, 'The LORD of Hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our fortress. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 8, 'Come, see the works of the LORD, who brings devastation upon the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 9, 'He makes wars to cease throughout the earth; He breaks the bow and shatters the spear; He burns the shields in the fire.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 10, '“Be still and know that I am God; I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted over the earth.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 46, 11, 'The LORD of Hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our fortress. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 1, 'Clap your hands, all you peoples; shout unto God with a voice of triumph.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 2, 'How awesome is the LORD Most High, the great King over all the earth!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 3, 'He subdues nations beneath us, and peoples under our feet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 4, 'He chooses our inheritance for us, the pride of Jacob, whom He loves. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 5, 'God has ascended amid shouts of joy, the LORD with the sound of the horn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 6, 'Sing praises to God, sing praises; sing praises to our King, sing praises!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 7, 'For God is King of all the earth; sing profound praises to Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 8, 'God reigns over the nations; God is seated on His holy throne.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 47, 9, 'The nobles of the nations have assembled as the people of the God of Abraham; for the shields of the earth belong to God; He is highly exalted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 1, 'Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, His holy mountain.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 2, 'Beautiful in loftiness, the joy of all the earth, like the peaks of Zaphon is Mount Zion, the city of the great King.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 3, 'God is in her citadels; He has shown Himself to be a fortress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 4, 'For behold, the kings assembled; they all advanced together.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 5, 'They saw and were astounded; they fled in terror.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 6, 'Trembling seized them there, anguish like a woman in labor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 7, 'With a wind from the east You wrecked the ships of Tarshish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 8, 'As we have heard, so we have seen in the city of the LORD of Hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish her forever. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 9, 'Within Your temple, O God, we contemplate Your loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 10, 'Your name, O God, like Your praise, reaches to the ends of the earth; Your right hand is full of righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 11, 'Mount Zion is glad, the daughters of Judah rejoice, on account of Your judgments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 12, 'March around Zion, encircle her, count her towers,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 13, 'consider her ramparts, tour her citadels, that you may tell the next generation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 48, 14, 'For this God is our God forever and ever; He will be our guide even till death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 1, 'Hear this, all you peoples; listen, all inhabitants of the world,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 2, 'both low and high, rich and poor alike.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 3, 'My mouth will impart wisdom, and the meditation of my heart will bring understanding.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 4, 'I will incline my ear to a proverb; I will express my riddle with the harp:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 5, 'Why should I fear in times of trouble, when wicked usurpers surround me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 6, 'They trust in their wealth and boast in their great riches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 7, 'No man can possibly redeem his brother or pay his ransom to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 8, 'For the redemption of his soul is costly, and never can payment suffice,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 9, 'that he should live on forever and not see decay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 10, 'For it is clear that wise men die, and the foolish and the senseless both perish and leave their wealth to others.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 11, 'Their graves are their eternal homes— their dwellings for endless generations— even though their lands were their namesakes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 12, 'But a man, despite his wealth, cannot endure; he is like the beasts that perish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 13, 'This is the fate of the self-confident and their followers who endorse their sayings. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 14, 'Like sheep they are destined for Sheol. Death will be their shepherd. The upright will rule them in the morning, and their form will decay in Sheol, far from their lofty abode.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 15, 'But God will redeem my life from Sheol, for He will surely take me to Himself. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 16, 'Do not be amazed when a man grows rich, when the splendor of his house increases.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 17, 'For when he dies, he will carry nothing away; his abundance will not follow him down.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 18, 'Though in his lifetime he blesses his soul— and men praise you when you prosper—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 19, 'he will join the generation of his fathers, who will never see the light of day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 49, 20, 'A man who has riches without understanding is like the beasts that perish.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 1, 'The Mighty One, God the LORD, speaks and summons the earth from where the sun rises to where it sets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 2, 'From Zion, perfect in beauty, God shines forth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 3, 'Our God approaches and will not be silent! Consuming fire precedes Him, and a tempest rages around Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 4, 'He summons the heavens above, and the earth, that He may judge His people:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 5, '“Gather to Me My saints, who made a covenant with Me by sacrifice.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 6, 'And the heavens proclaim His righteousness, for God Himself is Judge. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 7, '“Hear, O My people, and I will speak, O Israel, and I will testify against you: I am God, your God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 8, 'I do not rebuke you for your sacrifices, and your burnt offerings are ever before Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 9, 'I have no need for a bull from your stall or goats from your pens,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 10, 'for every beast of the forest is Mine— the cattle on a thousand hills.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 11, 'I know every bird in the mountains, and the creatures of the field are Mine.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 12, 'If I were hungry, I would not tell you, for the world is Mine, and the fullness thereof.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 13, 'Do I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 14, 'Sacrifice a thank offering to God, and fulfill your vows to the Most High.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 15, 'Call upon Me in the day of trouble; I will deliver you, and you will honor Me.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 16, 'To the wicked, however, God says, “What right have you to recite My statutes and to bear My covenant on your lips?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 17, 'For you hate My instruction and cast My words behind you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 18, 'When you see a thief, you befriend him, and throw in your lot with adulterers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 19, 'You unleash your mouth for evil and unharness your tongue for deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 20, 'You sit and malign your brother; you slander your own mother’s son.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 21, 'You have done these things, and I kept silent; you thought I was just like you. But now I rebuke you and accuse you to your face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 22, 'Now consider this, you who forget God, lest I tear you to pieces, with no one to rescue you:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 50, 23, 'He who sacrifices a thank offering honors Me, and to him who rights his way, I will show the salvation of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 1, 'Have mercy on me, O God, according to Your loving devotion; according to Your great compassion, blot out my transgressions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 2, 'Wash me clean of my iniquity and cleanse me from my sin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 3, 'For I know my transgressions, and my sin is always before me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 4, 'Against You, You only, have I sinned and done what is evil in Your sight, so that You may be proved right when You speak and blameless when You judge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 5, 'Surely I was brought forth in iniquity; I was sinful when my mother conceived me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 6, 'Surely You desire truth in the inmost being; You teach me wisdom in the inmost place.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 7, 'Purify me with hyssop, and I will be clean; wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 8, 'Let me hear joy and gladness; let the bones You have crushed rejoice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 9, 'Hide Your face from my sins and blot out all my iniquities.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 10, 'Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 11, 'Cast me not away from Your presence; take not Your Holy Spirit from me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 12, 'Restore to me the joy of Your salvation, and sustain me with a willing spirit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 13, 'Then I will teach transgressors Your ways, and sinners will return to You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 14, 'Deliver me from bloodguilt, O God, the God of my salvation, and my tongue will sing of Your righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 15, 'O Lord, open my lips, and my mouth will declare Your praise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 16, 'For You do not delight in sacrifice, or I would bring it; You take no pleasure in burnt offerings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 17, 'The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit; a broken and a contrite heart, O God, You will not despise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 18, 'In Your good pleasure, cause Zion to prosper; build up the walls of Jerusalem.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 51, 19, 'Then You will delight in righteous sacrifices, in whole burnt offerings; then bulls will be offered on Your altar.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 1, 'Why do you boast of evil, O mighty man? The loving devotion of God endures all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 2, 'Your tongue devises destruction like a sharpened razor, O worker of deceit.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 3, 'You love evil more than good, falsehood more than speaking truth. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 4, 'You love every word that devours, O deceitful tongue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 5, 'Surely God will bring you down to everlasting ruin; He will snatch you up and tear you away from your tent; He will uproot you from the land of the living. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 6, 'The righteous will see and fear; they will mock the evildoer, saying,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 7, '“Look at the man who did not make God his refuge, but trusted in the abundance of his wealth and strengthened himself by destruction.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 8, 'But I am like an olive tree flourishing in the house of God; I trust in the loving devotion of God forever and ever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 52, 9, 'I will praise You forever, because You have done it. I will wait on Your name— for it is good— in the presence of Your saints.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 53, 1, 'The fool says in his heart, “There is no God.” They are corrupt; their ways are vile. There is no one who does good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 53, 2, 'God looks down from heaven upon the sons of men to see if any understand, if any seek God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 53, 3, 'All have turned away, they have together become corrupt; there is no one who does good, not even one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 53, 4, 'Will the workers of iniquity never learn? They devour my people like bread; they refuse to call upon God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 53, 5, 'There they are, overwhelmed with dread, where there was nothing to fear. For God has scattered the bones of those who besieged you. You put them to shame, for God has despised them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 53, 6, 'Oh, that the salvation of Israel would come from Zion! When God restores His captive people, let Jacob rejoice, let Israel be glad!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 1, 'Save me, O God, by Your name, and vindicate me by Your might!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 2, 'Hear my prayer, O God; listen to the words of my mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 3, 'For strangers rise up against me, and ruthless men seek my life— men with no regard for God. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 4, 'Surely God is my helper; the Lord is the sustainer of my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 5, 'He will reward my enemies with evil. In Your faithfulness, destroy them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 6, 'Freely I will sacrifice to You; I will praise Your name, O LORD, for it is good.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 54, 7, 'For He has delivered me from every trouble, and my eyes have stared down my foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 1, 'Listen to my prayer, O God, and do not ignore my plea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 2, 'Attend to me and answer me. I am restless in my complaint, and distraught'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 3, 'at the voice of the enemy, at the pressure of the wicked. For they release disaster upon me and revile me in their anger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 4, 'My heart murmurs within me, and the terrors of death assail me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 5, 'Fear and trembling grip me, and horror has overwhelmed me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 6, 'I said, “Oh, that I had wings like a dove! I would fly away and find rest.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 7, 'How far away I would flee! In the wilderness I would remain. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 8, 'I would hurry to my shelter, far from this raging tempest.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 9, 'O Lord, confuse and confound their speech, for I see violence and strife in the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 10, 'Day and night they encircle the walls, while malice and trouble lie within.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 11, 'Destruction is within; oppression and deceit never leave the streets.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 12, 'For it is not an enemy who insults me; that I could endure. It is not a foe who rises against me; from him I could hide.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 13, 'But it is you, a man like myself, my companion and close friend.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 14, 'We shared sweet fellowship together; we walked with the crowd into the house of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 15, 'Let death seize them by surprise; let them go down to Sheol alive, for evil is with them in their homes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 16, 'But I call to God, and the LORD saves me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 17, 'Morning, noon, and night, I cry out in distress, and He hears my voice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 18, 'He redeems my soul in peace from the battle waged against me, even though many oppose me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 19, 'God will hear and humiliate them— the One enthroned for the ages— Selah because they do not change and they have no fear of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 20, 'My companion attacks his friends; he violates his covenant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 21, 'His speech is smooth as butter, but war is in his heart. His words are softer than oil, yet they are swords unsheathed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 22, 'Cast your burden upon the LORD and He will sustain you; He will never let the righteous be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 55, 23, 'But You, O God, will bring them down to the Pit of destruction; men of bloodshed and deceit will not live out half their days. But I will trust in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 1, 'Be merciful to me, O God, for men are hounding me; all day they press their attack.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 2, 'My enemies pursue me all day long, for many proudly assail me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 3, 'When I am afraid, I put my trust in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 4, 'In God, whose word I praise— in God I trust. I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 5, 'All day long they twist my words; all their thoughts are on my demise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 6, 'They conspire, they lurk, they watch my steps while they wait to take my life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 7, 'In spite of such sin, will they escape? In Your anger, O God, cast down the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 8, 'You have taken account of my wanderings. Put my tears in Your bottle— are they not in Your book?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 9, 'Then my enemies will retreat on the day I cry for help. By this I will know that God is on my side.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 10, 'In God, whose word I praise, in the LORD, whose word I praise,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 11, 'in God I trust; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 12, 'Your vows are upon me, O God; I will render thank offerings to You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 56, 13, 'For You have delivered my soul from death, and my feet from stumbling, that I may walk before God in the light of life.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 1, 'Have mercy on me, O God, have mercy, for in You my soul takes refuge. In the shadow of Your wings I will take shelter until the danger has passed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 2, 'I cry out to God Most High, to God who fulfills His purpose for me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 3, 'He reaches down from heaven and saves me; He rebukes those who trample me. Selah God sends forth His loving devotion and His truth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 4, 'My soul is among the lions; I lie down with ravenous beasts— with men whose teeth are spears and arrows, whose tongues are sharp swords.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 5, 'Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; may Your glory cover all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 6, 'They spread a net for my feet; my soul was despondent. They dug a pit before me, but they themselves have fallen into it! Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 7, 'My heart is steadfast, O God, my heart is steadfast. I will sing and make music.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 8, 'Awake, my glory! Awake, O harp and lyre! I will awaken the dawn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 9, 'I will praise You, O Lord, among the nations; I will sing Your praises among the peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 10, 'For Your loving devotion reaches to the heavens, and Your faithfulness to the clouds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 57, 11, 'Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; may Your glory cover all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 1, 'Do you indeed speak justly, O rulers? Do you judge uprightly, O sons of men?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 2, 'No, in your hearts you devise injustice; with your hands you mete out violence on the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 3, 'The wicked are estranged from the womb; the liars go astray from birth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 4, 'Their venom is like the venom of a snake, like a cobra that shuts its ears,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 5, 'refusing to hear the tune of the charmer who skillfully weaves his spell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 6, 'O God, shatter their teeth in their mouths; O LORD, tear out the fangs of the lions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 7, 'May they vanish like water that runs off; when they draw the bow, may their arrows be blunted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 8, 'Like a slug that dissolves in its slime, like a woman’s stillborn child, may they never see the sun.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 9, 'Before your pots can feel the burning thorns— whether green or dry— He will sweep them away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 10, 'The righteous will rejoice when they see they are avenged; they will wash their feet in the blood of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 58, 11, 'Then men will say, “There is surely a reward for the righteous! There is surely a God who judges the earth!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 1, 'Deliver me from my enemies, O my God; protect me from those who rise against me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 2, 'Deliver me from workers of iniquity, and save me from men of bloodshed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 3, 'See how they lie in wait for me. Fierce men conspire against me for no transgression or sin of my own, O LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 4, 'For no fault of my own, they move swiftly to attack me. Arise to help me, and take notice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 5, 'O LORD God of Hosts, the God of Israel, rouse Yourself to punish all the nations; show no mercy to the wicked traitors. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 6, 'They return in the evening, snarling like dogs and prowling around the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 7, 'See what they spew from their mouths— sharp words from their lips: “For who can hear us?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 8, 'But You, O LORD, laugh at them; You scoff at all the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 9, 'I will keep watch for You, O my strength, because You, O God, are my fortress.');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 10, 'My God of loving devotion will come to meet me; God will let me stare down my foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 11, 'Do not kill them, or my people will forget. Scatter them by Your power, and bring them down, O Lord, our shield.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 12, 'By the sins of their mouths and the words of their lips, let them be trapped in their pride, in the curses and lies they utter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 13, 'Consume them in wrath; consume them till they are no more, so it may be known to the ends of the earth that God rules over Jacob. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 14, 'They return in the evening, snarling like dogs and prowling around the city.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 15, 'They scavenge for food, and growl if they are not satisfied.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 16, 'But I will sing of Your strength and proclaim Your loving devotion in the morning. For You are my fortress, my refuge in times of trouble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 59, 17, 'To You, O my strength, I sing praises, for You, O God, are my fortress, my God of loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 1, 'You have rejected us, O God; You have broken us; You have been angry; restore us!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 2, 'You have shaken the land and torn it open. Heal its fractures, for it is quaking.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 3, 'You have shown Your people hardship; we are staggered from the wine You made us drink.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 4, 'You have raised a banner for those who fear You, that they may flee the bow. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 5, 'Respond and save us with Your right hand, that Your beloved may be delivered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 6, 'God has spoken from His sanctuary: “I will triumph! I will parcel out Shechem and apportion the Valley of Succoth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 7, 'Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine; Ephraim is My helmet, Judah is My scepter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 8, 'Moab is My washbasin; upon Edom I toss My sandal; over Philistia I shout in triumph.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 9, 'Who will bring me to the fortified city? Who will lead me to Edom?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 10, 'Have You not rejected us, O God? Will You no longer march out, O God, with our armies?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 11, 'Give us aid against the enemy, for the help of man is worthless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 60, 12, 'With God we will perform with valor, and He will trample our enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 1, 'Hear my cry, O God; attend to my prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 2, 'From the ends of the earth I call out to You whenever my heart is faint. Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 3, 'For You have been my refuge, a tower of strength against the enemy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 4, 'Let me dwell in Your tent forever and take refuge in the shelter of Your wings. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 5, 'For You have heard my vows, O God; You have given me the inheritance reserved for those who fear Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 6, 'Increase the days of the king’s life; may his years span many generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 7, 'May he sit enthroned in God’s presence forever; appoint Your loving devotion and Your faithfulness to guard him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 61, 8, 'Then I will ever sing praise to Your name and fulfill my vows day by day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 1, 'In God alone my soul finds rest; my salvation comes from Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 2, 'He alone is my rock and my salvation. He is my fortress; I will never be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 3, 'How long will you threaten a man? Will all of you throw him down like a leaning wall or a tottering fence?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 4, 'They fully intend to cast him down from his lofty perch; they delight in lies; with their mouths they bless, but inwardly they curse. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 5, 'Rest in God alone, O my soul, for my hope comes from Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 6, 'He alone is my rock and my salvation; He is my fortress; I will not be shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 7, 'My salvation and my honor rest on God, my strong rock; my refuge is in God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 8, 'Trust in Him at all times, O people; pour out your hearts before Him. God is our refuge. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 9, 'Lowborn men are but a vapor, the exalted but a lie. Weighed on the scale, they go up; together they are but a vapor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 10, 'Place no trust in extortion, or false hope in stolen goods. If your riches increase, do not set your heart upon them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 11, 'God has spoken once; I have heard this twice: that power belongs to God,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 62, 12, 'and loving devotion to You, O Lord. For You will repay each man according to his deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 1, 'O God, You are my God. Earnestly I seek You; my soul thirsts for You. My body yearns for You in a dry and weary land without water.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 2, 'So I have seen You in the sanctuary and beheld Your power and glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 3, 'Because Your loving devotion is better than life, my lips will glorify You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 4, 'So I will bless You as long as I live; in Your name I will lift my hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 5, 'My soul is satisfied as with the richest of foods; with joyful lips my mouth will praise You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 6, 'When I remember You on my bed, I think of You through the watches of the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 7, 'For You are my help; I will sing for joy in the shadow of Your wings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 8, 'My soul clings to You; Your right hand upholds me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 9, 'But those who seek my life to destroy it will go into the depths of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 10, 'They will fall to the power of the sword; they will become a portion for foxes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 63, 11, 'But the king will rejoice in God; all who swear by Him will exult, for the mouths of liars will be shut.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 1, 'Hear, O God, my voice of complaint; preserve my life from dread of the enemy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 2, 'Hide me from the scheming of the wicked, from the mob of workers of iniquity,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 3, 'who sharpen their tongues like swords and aim their bitter words like arrows,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 4, 'ambushing the innocent in seclusion, shooting suddenly, without fear.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 5, 'They hold fast to their evil purpose; they speak of hiding their snares. “Who will see them?” they say.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 6, 'They devise injustice and say, “We have perfected a secret plan.” For the inner man and the heart are mysterious.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 7, 'But God will shoot them with arrows; suddenly they will be wounded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 8, 'They will be made to stumble, their own tongues turned against them. All who see will shake their heads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 9, 'Then all mankind will fear and proclaim the work of God; so they will ponder what He has done.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 64, 10, 'Let the righteous rejoice in the LORD and take refuge in Him; let all the upright in heart exult.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 1, 'Praise awaits You, O God, in Zion; to You our vows will be fulfilled.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 2, 'O You who listen to prayer, all people will come to You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 3, 'When iniquities prevail against me, You atone for our transgressions.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 4, 'Blessed is the one You choose and bring near to dwell in Your courts! We are filled with the goodness of Your house, the holiness of Your temple.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 5, 'With awesome deeds of righteousness You answer us, O God of our salvation, the hope of all the ends of the earth and of the farthest seas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 6, 'You formed the mountains by Your power, having girded Yourself with might.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 7, 'You stilled the roaring of the seas, the pounding of their waves, and the tumult of the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 8, 'Those who live far away fear Your wonders; You make the dawn and sunset shout for joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 9, 'You attend to the earth and water it; with abundance You enrich it. The streams of God are full of water, for You prepare our grain by providing for the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 10, 'You soak its furrows and level its ridges; You soften it with showers and bless its growth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 11, 'You crown the year with Your bounty, and Your paths overflow with plenty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 12, 'The pastures of the wilderness overflow; the hills are robed with joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 65, 13, 'The pastures are clothed with flocks, and the valleys are decked with grain. They shout in triumph; indeed, they sing.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 1, 'Make a joyful noise to God, all the earth!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 2, 'Sing the glory of His name; make His praise glorious.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 3, 'Say to God, “How awesome are Your deeds! So great is Your power that Your enemies cower before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 4, 'All the earth bows down to You; they sing praise to You; they sing praise to Your name.” Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 5, 'Come and see the works of God; how awesome are His deeds toward mankind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 6, 'He turned the sea into dry land; they passed through the waters on foot; there we rejoiced in Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 7, 'He rules forever by His power; His eyes watch the nations. Do not let the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 8, 'Bless our God, O peoples; let the sound of His praise be heard.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 9, 'He preserves our lives and keeps our feet from slipping.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 10, 'For You, O God, have tested us; You have refined us like silver.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 11, 'You led us into the net; You laid burdens on our backs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 12, 'You let men ride over our heads; we went through fire and water, but You brought us into abundance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 13, 'I will enter Your house with burnt offerings; I will fulfill my vows to You—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 14, 'the vows that my lips promised and my mouth spoke in my distress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 15, 'I will offer You fatlings as burnt offerings, with the fragrant smoke of rams; I will offer bulls and goats. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 16, 'Come and listen, all you who fear God, and I will declare what He has done for me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 17, 'I cried out to Him with my mouth and praised Him with my tongue.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 18, 'If I had cherished iniquity in my heart, the Lord would not have listened.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 19, 'But God has surely heard; He has attended to the sound of my prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 66, 20, 'Blessed be God, who has not rejected my prayer or withheld from me His loving devotion!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 1, 'May God be gracious to us and bless us, and cause His face to shine upon us, Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 2, 'that Your ways may be known on earth, Your salvation among all nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 3, 'Let the peoples praise You, O God; let all the peoples praise You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 4, 'Let the nations be glad and sing for joy, for You judge the peoples justly and lead the nations of the earth. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 5, 'Let the peoples praise You, O God; let all the peoples praise You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 6, 'The earth has yielded its harvest; God, our God, blesses us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 67, 7, 'God blesses us, that all the ends of the earth shall fear Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 1, 'God arises. His enemies are scattered, and those who hate Him flee His presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 2, 'As smoke is blown away, You will drive them out; as wax melts before the fire, the wicked will perish in the presence of God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 3, 'But the righteous will be glad and rejoice before God; they will celebrate with joy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 4, 'Sing to God! Sing praises to His name. Exalt Him who rides on the clouds— His name is the LORD— and rejoice before Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 5, 'A father of the fatherless, and a defender of the widows, is God in His holy habitation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 6, 'God settles the lonely in families; He leads the prisoners out to prosperity, but the rebellious dwell in a sun-scorched land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 7, 'O God, when You went out before Your people, when You marched through the wasteland, Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 8, 'the earth shook and the heavens poured down rain before God, the One on Sinai, before God, the God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 9, 'You sent abundant rain, O God; You refreshed Your weary inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 10, 'Your flock settled therein; O God, from Your bounty You provided for the poor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 11, 'The Lord gives the command; a great company of women proclaim it:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 12, '“Kings and their armies flee in haste; she who waits at home divides the plunder.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 13, 'Though you lie down among the sheepfolds, the wings of the dove are covered with silver, and her feathers with shimmering gold.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 14, 'When the Almighty scattered the kings in the land, it was like the snow falling on Zalmon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 15, 'A mountain of God is Mount Bashan; a mountain of many peaks is Mount Bashan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 16, 'Why do you gaze in envy, O mountains of many peaks? This is the mountain God chose for His dwelling, where the LORD will surely dwell forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 17, 'The chariots of God are tens of thousands— thousands of thousands are they; the Lord is in His sanctuary as He was at Sinai.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 18, 'You have ascended on high; You have led captives away. You have received gifts from men, even from the rebellious, that the LORD God may dwell there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 19, 'Blessed be the Lord, who daily bears our burden, the God of our salvation. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 20, 'Our God is a God of deliverance; the Lord GOD is our rescuer from death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 21, 'Surely God will crush the heads of His enemies, the hairy crowns of those who persist in guilty ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 22, 'The Lord said, “I will retrieve them from Bashan, I will bring them up from the depths of the sea,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 23, 'that your foot may be dipped in the blood of your foes— the tongues of your dogs in the same.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 24, 'They have seen Your procession, O God— the march of my God and King into the sanctuary.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 25, 'The singers lead the way, the musicians follow after, among the maidens playing tambourines.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 26, 'Bless God in the great congregation; bless the LORD from the fountain of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 27, 'There is Benjamin, the youngest, ruling them, the princes of Judah in their company, the princes of Zebulun and of Naphtali.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 28, 'Summon Your power, O God; show Your strength, O God, which You have exerted on our behalf.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 29, 'Because of Your temple at Jerusalem kings will bring You gifts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 30, 'Rebuke the beast in the reeds, the herd of bulls among the calves of the nations, until it submits, bringing bars of silver. Scatter the nations who delight in war.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 31, 'Envoys will arrive from Egypt; Cush will stretch out her hands to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 32, 'Sing to God, O kingdoms of the earth; sing praises to the Lord— Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 33, 'to Him who rides upon the highest heavens of old; behold, His mighty voice resounds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 34, 'Ascribe the power to God, whose majesty is over Israel, whose strength is in the skies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 68, 35, 'O God, You are awesome in Your sanctuary; the God of Israel Himself gives strength and power to His people. Blessed be God!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 1, 'Save me, O God, for the waters are up to my neck.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 2, 'I have sunk into the miry depths, where there is no footing; I have drifted into deep waters, where the flood engulfs me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 3, 'I am weary from my crying; my throat is parched. My eyes fail, looking for my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 4, 'Those who hate me without cause outnumber the hairs of my head; many are those who would destroy me— my enemies for no reason. Though I did not steal, I must repay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 5, 'You know my folly, O God, and my guilt is not hidden from You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 6, 'May those who hope in You not be ashamed through me, O Lord GOD of Hosts; may those who seek You not be dishonored through me, O God of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 7, 'For I have endured scorn for Your sake, and shame has covered my face.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 8, 'I have become a stranger to my brothers and a foreigner to my mother’s sons,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 9, 'because zeal for Your house has consumed me, and the insults of those who insult You have fallen on me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 10, 'I wept and fasted, but it brought me reproach.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 11, 'I made sackcloth my clothing, and I was sport to them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 12, 'Those who sit at the gate mock me, and I am the song of drunkards.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 13, 'But my prayer to You, O LORD, is for a time of favor. In Your abundant loving devotion, O God, answer me with Your sure salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 14, 'Rescue me from the mire and do not let me sink; deliver me from my foes and out of the deep waters.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 15, 'Do not let the floods engulf me or the depths swallow me up; let not the Pit close its mouth over me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 16, 'Answer me, O LORD, for Your loving devotion is good; turn to me in keeping with Your great compassion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 17, 'Hide not Your face from Your servant, for I am in distress. Answer me quickly!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 18, 'Draw near to my soul and redeem me; ransom me because of my foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 19, 'You know my reproach, my shame and disgrace. All my adversaries are before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 20, 'Insults have broken my heart, and I am in despair. I looked for sympathy, but there was none, for comforters, but I found no one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 21, 'They poisoned my food with gall and gave me vinegar to quench my thirst.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 22, 'May their table become a snare; may it be a retribution and a trap.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 23, 'May their eyes be darkened so they cannot see, and their backs be bent forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 24, 'Pour out Your wrath upon them, and let Your burning anger overtake them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 25, 'May their place be deserted; let there be no one to dwell in their tents.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 26, 'For they persecute the one You struck and recount the pain of those You wounded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 27, 'Add iniquity to their iniquity; let them not share in Your righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 28, 'May they be blotted out of the Book of Life and not listed with the righteous.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 29, 'But I am in pain and distress; let Your salvation protect me, O God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 30, 'I will praise God’s name in song and exalt Him with thanksgiving.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 31, 'And this will please the LORD more than an ox, more than a bull with horns and hooves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 32, 'The humble will see and rejoice. You who seek God, let your hearts be revived!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 33, 'For the LORD listens to the needy and does not despise His captive people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 34, 'Let heaven and earth praise Him, the seas and everything that moves in them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 35, 'For God will save Zion and rebuild the cities of Judah, that they may dwell there and possess it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 69, 36, 'The descendants of His servants will inherit it, and those who love His name will settle in it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 70, 1, 'Make haste, O God, to deliver me! Hurry, O LORD, to help me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 70, 2, 'May those who seek my life be ashamed and confounded; may those who wish me harm be repelled and humiliated.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 70, 3, 'May those who say, “Aha, aha!” retreat because of their shame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 70, 4, 'May all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You; may those who love Your salvation always say, “Let God be magnified!”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 70, 5, 'But I am poor and needy; hurry to me, O God. You are my help and my deliverer; O LORD, do not delay.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 1, 'In You, O LORD, I have taken refuge; let me never be put to shame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 2, 'In Your justice, rescue and deliver me; incline Your ear and save me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 3, 'Be my rock of refuge, where I can always go. Give the command to save me, for You are my rock and my fortress.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 4, 'Deliver me, O my God, from the hand of the wicked, from the grasp of the unjust and ruthless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 5, 'For You are my hope, O Lord GOD, my confidence from my youth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 6, 'I have leaned on You since birth; You pulled me from my mother’s womb. My praise is always for You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 7, 'I have become a portent to many, but You are my strong refuge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 8, 'My mouth is filled with Your praise and with Your splendor all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 9, 'Do not discard me in my old age; do not forsake me when my strength fails.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 10, 'For my enemies speak against me, and those who lie in wait for my life conspire,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 11, 'saying, “God has forsaken him; pursue him and seize him, for there is no one to rescue him.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 12, 'Be not far from me, O God. Hurry, O my God, to help me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 13, 'May the accusers of my soul be ashamed and consumed; may those who seek my harm be covered with scorn and disgrace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 14, 'But I will always hope and will praise You more and more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 15, 'My mouth will declare Your righteousness and Your salvation all day long, though I cannot know their full measure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 16, 'I will enter in the strength of the Lord GOD; I will proclaim Your righteousness—Yours alone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 17, 'O God, You have taught me from my youth, and to this day I proclaim Your marvelous deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 18, 'Even when I am old and gray, do not forsake me, O God, until I proclaim Your power to the next generation, Your might to all who are to come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 19, 'Your righteousness reaches to the heavens, O God, You who have done great things. Who, O God, is like You?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 20, 'Though You have shown me many troubles and misfortunes, You will revive me once again. Even from the depths of the earth You will bring me back up.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 21, 'You will increase my honor and comfort me once again.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 22, 'So I will praise You with the harp for Your faithfulness, O my God; I will sing praise to You with the lyre, O Holy One of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 23, 'When I sing praise to You my lips will shout for joy, along with my soul, which You have redeemed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 71, 24, 'My tongue will indeed proclaim Your righteousness all day long, for those who seek my harm are disgraced and confounded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 1, 'Endow the king with Your justice, O God, and the son of the king with Your righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 2, 'May he judge Your people with righteousness and Your afflicted with justice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 3, 'May the mountains bring peace to the people, and the hills bring righteousness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 4, 'May he vindicate the afflicted among the people; may he save the children of the needy and crush the oppressor.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 5, 'May they fear him as long as the sun shines, as long as the moon remains, through all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 6, 'May he be like rain that falls on freshly cut grass, like spring showers that water the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 7, 'May the righteous flourish in his days and prosperity abound, until the moon is no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 8, 'May he rule from sea to sea, and from the Euphrates to the ends of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 9, 'May the nomads bow before him, and his enemies lick the dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 10, 'May the kings of Tarshish and distant shores bring tribute; may the kings of Sheba and Seba offer gifts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 11, 'May all kings bow down to him and all nations serve him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 12, 'For he will deliver the needy who cry out and the afflicted who have no helper.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 13, 'He will take pity on the poor and needy and save the lives of the oppressed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 14, 'He will redeem them from oppression and violence, for their blood is precious in his sight.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 15, 'Long may he live! May gold from Sheba be given him. May people ever pray for him; may they bless him all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 16, 'May there be an abundance of grain in the land; may it sway atop the hills. May its fruit trees flourish like the forests of Lebanon, and its people like the grass of the field.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 17, 'May his name endure forever; may his name continue as long as the sun shines. In him may all nations be blessed; may they call him blessed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 18, 'Blessed be the LORD God, the God of Israel, who alone does marvelous deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 19, 'And blessed be His glorious name forever; may all the earth be filled with His glory. Amen and amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 72, 20, 'Thus conclude the prayers of David son of Jesse.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 1, 'Surely God is good to Israel, to those who are pure in heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 2, 'But as for me, my feet had almost stumbled; my steps had nearly slipped.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 3, 'For I envied the arrogant when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 4, 'They have no struggle in their death; their bodies are well-fed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 5, 'They are free of the burdens others carry; they are not afflicted like other men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 6, 'Therefore pride is their necklace; a garment of violence covers them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 7, 'From their prosperity proceeds iniquity; the imaginations of their hearts run wild.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 8, 'They mock and speak with malice; with arrogance they threaten oppression.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 9, 'They set their mouths against the heavens, and their tongues strut across the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 10, 'So their people return to this place and drink up waters in abundance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 11, 'The wicked say, “How can God know? Does the Most High have knowledge?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 12, 'Behold, these are the wicked— always carefree as they increase their wealth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 13, 'Surely in vain I have kept my heart pure; in innocence I have washed my hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 14, 'For I am afflicted all day long and punished every morning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 15, 'If I had said, “I will speak this way,” then I would have betrayed Your children.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 16, 'When I tried to understand all this, it was troublesome in my sight'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 17, 'until I entered God’s sanctuary; then I discerned their end.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 18, 'Surely You set them on slick ground; You cast them down into ruin.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 19, 'How suddenly they are laid waste, completely swept away by terrors!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 20, 'Like one waking from a dream, so You, O Lord, awaken and despise their form.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 21, 'When my heart was grieved and I was pierced within,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 22, 'I was senseless and ignorant; I was a brute beast before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 23, 'Yet I am always with You; You hold my right hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 24, 'You guide me with Your counsel, and later receive me in glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 25, 'Whom have I in heaven but You? And on earth I desire no one besides You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 26, 'My flesh and my heart may fail, but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 27, 'Those far from You will surely perish; You destroy all who are unfaithful to You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 73, 28, 'But as for me, it is good to draw near to God. I have made the Lord GOD my refuge, that I may proclaim all Your works.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 1, 'Why have You rejected us forever, O God? Why does Your anger smolder against the sheep of Your pasture?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 2, 'Remember Your congregation, which You purchased long ago and redeemed as the tribe of Your inheritance— Mount Zion where You dwell.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 3, 'Turn Your steps to the everlasting ruins, to everything in the sanctuary the enemy has destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 4, 'Your foes have roared within Your meeting place; they have unfurled their banners as signs,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 5, 'like men wielding axes in a thicket of trees'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 6, 'and smashing all the carvings with hatchets and picks.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 7, 'They have burned Your sanctuary to the ground; they have defiled the dwelling place of Your Name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 8, 'They said in their hearts, “We will crush them completely.” They burned down every place where God met us in the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 9, 'There are no signs for us to see. There is no longer any prophet. And none of us knows how long this will last.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 10, 'How long, O God, will the enemy taunt You? Will the foe revile Your name forever?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 11, 'Why do You withdraw Your strong right hand? Stretch it out to destroy them!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 12, 'Yet God is my King from ancient times, working salvation on the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 13, 'You divided the sea by Your strength; You smashed the heads of the dragons of the sea;'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 14, 'You crushed the heads of Leviathan; You fed him to the creatures of the desert.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 15, 'You broke open the fountain and the flood; You dried up the ever-flowing rivers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 16, 'The day is Yours, and also the night; You established the moon and the sun.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 17, 'You set all the boundaries of the earth; You made the summer and winter.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 18, 'Remember how the enemy has mocked You, O LORD, how a foolish people has spurned Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 19, 'Do not deliver the soul of Your dove to beasts; do not forget the lives of Your afflicted forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 20, 'Consider Your covenant, for haunts of violence fill the dark places of the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 21, 'Do not let the oppressed retreat in shame; may the poor and needy praise Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 22, 'Rise up, O God; defend Your cause! Remember how the fool mocks You all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 74, 23, 'Do not disregard the clamor of Your adversaries, the uproar of Your enemies that ascends continually.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 1, 'We give thanks to You, O God; we give thanks, for Your Name is near. The people declare Your wondrous works.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 2, '“When I choose a time, I will judge fairly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 3, 'When the earth and all its dwellers quake, it is I who bear up its pillars. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 4, 'I say to the proud, ‘Do not boast,’ and to the wicked, ‘Do not lift up your horn.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 5, 'Do not lift up your horn against heaven or speak with an outstretched neck.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 6, 'For exaltation comes neither from east nor west, nor out of the desert,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 7, 'but it is God who judges; He brings down one and exalts another.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 8, 'For a cup is in the hand of the LORD, full of foaming wine mixed with spices. He pours from His cup, and all the wicked of the earth drink it down to the dregs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 9, 'But I will proclaim Him forever; I will sing praise to the God of Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 75, 10, '“All the horns of the wicked I will cut off, but the horns of the righteous will be exalted.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 1, 'God is known in Judah; His name is great in Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 2, 'His tent is in Salem, His dwelling place in Zion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 3, 'There He shattered the flaming arrows, the shield and sword and weapons of war. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 4, 'You are resplendent with light, more majestic than mountains filled with game.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 5, 'The valiant lie plundered; they sleep their last sleep. No men of might could lift a hand.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 6, 'At Your rebuke, O God of Jacob, both horse and rider lie stunned.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 7, 'You alone are to be feared. When You are angry, who can stand before You?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 8, 'From heaven You pronounced judgment, and the earth feared and was still'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 9, 'when God rose up to judge, to save all the lowly of the earth. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 10, 'Even the wrath of man shall praise You; with the survivors of wrath You will clothe Yourself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 11, 'Make and fulfill your vows to the LORD your God; let all the neighboring lands bring tribute to Him who is to be feared.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 76, 12, 'He breaks the spirits of princes; He is feared by the kings of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 1, 'I cried out to God; I cried aloud to God to hear me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 2, 'In the day of trouble I sought the Lord; through the night my outstretched hands did not grow weary; my soul refused to be comforted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 3, 'I remembered You, O God, and I groaned; I mused and my spirit grew faint. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 4, 'You have kept my eyes from closing; I am too troubled to speak.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 5, 'I considered the days of old, the years long in the past.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 6, 'At night I remembered my song; in my heart I mused, and my spirit pondered:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 7, '“Will the Lord spurn us forever and never show His favor again?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 8, 'Is His loving devotion gone forever? Has His promise failed for all time?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 9, 'Has God forgotten to be gracious? Has His anger shut off His compassion?” Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 10, 'So I said, “I am grieved that the right hand of the Most High has changed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 11, 'I will remember the works of the LORD; yes, I will remember Your wonders of old.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 12, 'I will reflect on all You have done and ponder Your mighty deeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 13, 'Your way, O God, is holy. What god is so great as our God?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 14, 'You are the God who works wonders; You display Your strength among the peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 15, 'With power You redeemed Your people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 16, 'The waters saw You, O God; the waters saw You and swirled; even the depths were shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 17, 'The clouds poured down water; the skies resounded with thunder; Your arrows flashed back and forth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 18, 'Your thunder resounded in the whirlwind; the lightning lit up the world; the earth trembled and quaked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 19, 'Your path led through the sea, Your way through the mighty waters, but Your footprints were not to be found.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 77, 20, 'You led Your people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 1, 'Give ear, O my people, to my instruction; listen to the words of my mouth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 2, 'I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things hidden from the beginning,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 3, 'that we have heard and known and our fathers have relayed to us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 4, 'We will not hide them from their children, but will declare to the next generation the praises of the LORD and His might, and the wonders He has performed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 5, 'For He established a testimony in Jacob and appointed a law in Israel, which He commanded our fathers to teach to their children,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 6, 'that the coming generation would know them— even children yet to be born— to arise and tell their own children'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 7, 'that they should put their confidence in God, not forgetting His works, but keeping His commandments.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 8, 'Then they will not be like their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation, whose heart was not loyal, whose spirit was not faithful to God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 9, 'The archers of Ephraim turned back on the day of battle.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 10, 'They failed to keep God’s covenant and refused to live by His law.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 11, 'They forgot what He had done, the wonders He had shown them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 12, 'He worked wonders before their fathers in the land of Egypt, in the region of Zoan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 13, 'He split the sea and brought them through; He set the waters upright like a wall.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 14, 'He led them with a cloud by day and with a light of fire all night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 15, 'He split the rocks in the wilderness and gave them drink as abundant as the seas.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 16, 'He brought streams from the stone and made water flow down like rivers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 17, 'But they continued to sin against Him, rebelling in the desert against the Most High.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 18, 'They willfully tested God by demanding the food they craved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 19, 'They spoke against God, saying, “Can God really prepare a table in the wilderness?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 20, 'When He struck the rock, water gushed out and torrents raged. But can He also give bread or supply His people with meat?”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 21, 'Therefore the LORD heard and was filled with wrath; so a fire was kindled against Jacob, and His anger flared against Israel,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 22, 'because they did not believe God or rely on His salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 23, 'Yet He commanded the clouds above and opened the doors of the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 24, 'He rained down manna for them to eat; He gave them grain from heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 25, 'Man ate the bread of angels; He sent them food in abundance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 26, 'He stirred the east wind from the heavens and drove the south wind by His might.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 27, 'He rained meat on them like dust, and winged birds like the sand of the sea.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 28, 'He felled them in the midst of their camp, all around their dwellings.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 29, 'So they ate and were well filled, for He gave them what they craved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 30, 'Yet before they had filled their desire, with the food still in their mouths,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 31, 'God’s anger flared against them, and He put to death their strongest and subdued the young men of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 32, 'In spite of all this, they kept on sinning; despite His wonderful works, they did not believe.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 33, 'So He ended their days in futility, and their years in sudden terror.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 34, 'When He slew them, they would seek Him; they repented and searched for God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 35, 'And they remembered that God was their Rock, that God Most High was their Redeemer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 36, 'But they deceived Him with their mouths, and lied to Him with their tongues.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 37, 'Their hearts were disloyal to Him, and they were unfaithful to His covenant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 38, 'And yet He was compassionate; He forgave their iniquity and did not destroy them. He often restrained His anger and did not unleash His full wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 39, 'He remembered that they were but flesh, a passing breeze that does not return.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 40, 'How often they disobeyed Him in the wilderness and grieved Him in the desert!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 41, 'Again and again they tested God and provoked the Holy One of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 42, 'They did not remember His power— the day He redeemed them from the adversary,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 43, 'when He performed His signs in Egypt and His wonders in the fields of Zoan.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 44, 'He turned their rivers to blood, and from their streams they could not drink.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 45, 'He sent swarms of flies that devoured them, and frogs that devastated them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 46, 'He gave their crops to the grasshopper, the fruit of their labor to the locust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 47, 'He killed their vines with hailstones and their sycamore-figs with sleet.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 48, 'He abandoned their cattle to the hail and their livestock to bolts of lightning.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 49, 'He unleashed His fury against them, wrath, indignation, and calamity— a band of destroying angels.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 50, 'He cleared a path for His anger; He did not spare them from death but delivered their lives to the plague.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 51, 'He struck all the firstborn of Egypt, the virility in the tents of Ham.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 52, 'He led out His people like sheep and guided them like a flock in the wilderness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 53, 'He led them safely, so they did not fear, but the sea engulfed their enemies.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 54, 'He brought them to His holy land, to the mountain His right hand had acquired.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 55, 'He drove out nations before them and apportioned their inheritance; He settled the tribes of Israel in their tents.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 56, 'But they tested and disobeyed God Most High, for they did not keep His decrees.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 57, 'They turned back and were faithless like their fathers, twisted like a faulty bow.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 58, 'They enraged Him with their high places and provoked His jealousy with their idols.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 59, 'On hearing it, God was furious and rejected Israel completely.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 60, 'He abandoned the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent He had pitched among men.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 61, 'He delivered His strength to captivity, and His splendor to the hand of the adversary.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 62, 'He surrendered His people to the sword because He was enraged by His heritage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 63, 'Fire consumed His young men, and their maidens were left without wedding songs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 64, 'His priests fell by the sword, but their widows could not lament.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 65, 'Then the Lord awoke as from sleep, like a mighty warrior overcome by wine.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 66, 'He beat back His foes; He put them to everlasting shame.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 67, 'He rejected the tent of Joseph and refused the tribe of Ephraim.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 68, 'But He chose the tribe of Judah, Mount Zion, which He loved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 69, 'He built His sanctuary like the heights, like the earth He has established forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 70, 'He chose David His servant and took him from the sheepfolds;'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 71, 'from tending the ewes He brought him to be shepherd of His people Jacob, of Israel His inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 78, 72, 'So David shepherded them with integrity of heart and guided them with skillful hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 1, 'The nations, O God, have invaded Your inheritance; they have defiled Your holy temple and reduced Jerusalem to rubble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 2, 'They have given the corpses of Your servants as food to the birds of the air, the flesh of Your saints to the beasts of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 3, 'They have poured out their blood like water all around Jerusalem, and there is no one to bury the dead.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 4, 'We have become a reproach to our neighbors, a scorn and derision to those around us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 5, 'How long, O LORD? Will You be angry forever? Will Your jealousy burn like fire?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 6, 'Pour out Your wrath on the nations that do not acknowledge You, on the kingdoms that refuse to call on Your name,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 7, 'for they have devoured Jacob and devastated his homeland.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 8, 'Do not hold past sins against us; let Your compassion come quickly, for we are brought low.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 9, 'Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of Your name; deliver us and atone for our sins, for the sake of Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 10, 'Why should the nations ask, “Where is their God?” Before our eyes, make known among the nations Your vengeance for the bloodshed of Your servants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 11, 'May the groans of the captives reach You; by the strength of Your arm preserve those condemned to death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 12, 'Pay back into the laps of our neighbors sevenfold the reproach they hurled at You, O Lord.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 79, 13, 'Then we Your people, the sheep of Your pasture, will thank You forever; from generation to generation we will declare Your praise.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 1, 'Hear us, O Shepherd of Israel, who leads Joseph like a flock; You who sit enthroned between the cherubim, shine forth');
insert into control_room_bible (version, book, book_num, chapter, verse, text) values
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 2, 'before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh. Rally Your mighty power and come to save us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 3, 'Restore us, O God, and cause Your face to shine upon us, that we may be saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 4, 'O LORD God of Hosts, how long will Your anger smolder against the prayers of Your people?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 5, 'You fed them with the bread of tears and made them drink the full measure of their tears.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 6, 'You make us contend with our neighbors; our enemies mock us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 7, 'Restore us, O God of Hosts, and cause Your face to shine upon us, that we may be saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 8, 'You uprooted a vine from Egypt; You drove out the nations and transplanted it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 9, 'You cleared the ground for it, and it took root and filled the land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 10, 'The mountains were covered by its shade, and the mighty cedars with its branches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 11, 'It sent out its branches to the Sea, and its shoots toward the River.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 12, 'Why have You broken down its walls, so that all who pass by pick its fruit?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 13, 'The boar from the forest ravages it, and the creatures of the field feed upon it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 14, 'Return, O God of Hosts, we pray! Look down from heaven and see! Attend to this vine—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 15, 'the root Your right hand has planted, the son You have raised up for Yourself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 16, 'Your vine has been cut down and burned; they perish at the rebuke of Your countenance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 17, 'Let Your hand be upon the man at Your right hand, on the son of man You have raised up for Yourself.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 18, 'Then we will not turn away from You; revive us, and we will call on Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 80, 19, 'Restore us, O LORD God of Hosts; cause Your face to shine upon us, that we may be saved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 1, 'Sing for joy to God our strength; make a joyful noise to the God of Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 2, 'Lift up a song, strike the tambourine, play the sweet-sounding harp and lyre.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 3, 'Sound the ram’s horn at the New Moon, and at the full moon on the day of our Feast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 4, 'For this is a statute for Israel, an ordinance of the God of Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 5, 'He ordained it as a testimony for Joseph when he went out over the land of Egypt, where I heard an unfamiliar language:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 6, '“I relieved his shoulder of the burden; his hands were freed from the basket.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 7, 'You called out in distress, and I rescued you; I answered you from the cloud of thunder; I tested you at the waters of Meribah. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 8, 'Hear, O My people, and I will warn you: O Israel, if only you would listen to Me!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 9, 'There must be no strange god among you, nor shall you bow to a foreign god.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 10, 'I am the LORD your God, who brought you up out of Egypt. Open wide your mouth, and I will fill it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 11, 'But My people would not listen to Me, and Israel would not obey Me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 12, 'So I gave them up to their stubborn hearts to follow their own devices.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 13, 'If only My people would listen to Me, if Israel would follow My ways,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 14, 'how soon I would subdue their enemies and turn My hand against their foes!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 15, 'Those who hate the LORD would feign obedience, and their doom would last forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 81, 16, 'But I would feed you the finest wheat; with honey from the rock I would satisfy you.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 1, 'God presides in the divine assembly; He renders judgment among the gods:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 2, '“How long will you judge unjustly and show partiality to the wicked? Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 3, 'Defend the cause of the weak and fatherless; uphold the rights of the afflicted and oppressed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 4, 'Rescue the weak and needy; save them from the hand of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 5, 'They do not know or understand; they wander in the darkness; all the foundations of the earth are shaken.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 6, 'I have said, ‘You are gods; you are all sons of the Most High.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 7, 'But like mortals you will die, and like rulers you will fall.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 82, 8, 'Arise, O God, judge the earth, for all the nations are Your inheritance.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 1, 'O God, be not silent; be not speechless; be not still, O God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 2, 'See how Your enemies rage, how Your foes have reared their heads.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 3, 'With cunning they scheme against Your people and conspire against those You cherish,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 4, 'saying, “Come, let us erase them as a nation; may the name of Israel be remembered no more.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 5, 'For with one mind they plot together, they form an alliance against You—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 6, 'the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites, of Moab and the Hagrites,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 7, 'of Gebal, Ammon, and Amalek, of Philistia with the people of Tyre.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 8, 'Even Assyria has joined them, lending strength to the sons of Lot. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 9, 'Do to them as You did to Midian, as to Sisera and Jabin at the River Kishon,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 10, 'who perished at Endor and became like dung on the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 11, 'Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb, and all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 12, 'who said, “Let us possess for ourselves the pastures of God.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 13, 'Make them like tumbleweed, O my God, like chaff before the wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 14, 'As fire consumes a forest, as a flame sets the mountains ablaze,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 15, 'so pursue them with Your tempest, and terrify them with Your storm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 16, 'Cover their faces with shame, that they may seek Your name, O LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 17, 'May they be ever ashamed and terrified; may they perish in disgrace.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 83, 18, 'May they know that You alone, whose name is the LORD, are Most High over all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 1, 'How lovely is Your dwelling place, O LORD of Hosts!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 2, 'My soul longs, even faints, for the courts of the LORD; my heart and my flesh cry out for the living God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 3, 'Even the sparrow has found a home, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she places her young near Your altars, O LORD of Hosts, my King and my God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 4, 'How blessed are those who dwell in Your house! They are ever praising You. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 5, 'Blessed are those whose strength is in You, whose hearts are set on pilgrimage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 6, 'As they pass through the Valley of Baca, they make it a place of springs; even the autumn rain covers it with pools.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 7, 'They go from strength to strength, until each appears before God in Zion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 8, 'O LORD God of Hosts, hear my prayer; give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 9, 'Take notice of our shield, O God, and look with favor on the face of Your anointed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 10, 'For better is one day in Your courts than a thousand elsewhere. I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God than dwell in the tents of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 11, 'For the LORD God is a sun and a shield; the LORD gives grace and glory; He withholds no good thing from those who walk with integrity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 84, 12, 'O LORD of Hosts, how blessed is the man who trusts in You!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 1, 'You showed favor to Your land, O LORD; You restored Jacob from captivity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 2, 'You forgave the iniquity of Your people; You covered all their sin. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 3, 'You withheld all Your fury; You turned from Your burning anger.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 4, 'Restore us, O God of our salvation, and put away Your displeasure toward us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 5, 'Will You be angry with us forever? Will You draw out Your anger to all generations?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 6, 'Will You not revive us again, that Your people may rejoice in You?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 7, 'Show us Your loving devotion, O LORD, and grant us Your salvation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 8, 'I will listen to what God the LORD will say; for He will surely speak peace to His people and His saints; He will not let them return to folly.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 9, 'Surely His salvation is near to those who fear Him, that His glory may dwell in our land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 10, 'Loving devotion and faithfulness have joined together; righteousness and peace have kissed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 11, 'Faithfulness sprouts from the earth, and righteousness looks down from heaven.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 12, 'The LORD will indeed provide what is good, and our land will yield its increase.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 85, 13, 'Righteousness will go before Him to prepare the way for His steps.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 1, 'Incline Your ear, O LORD, and answer me, for I am poor and needy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 2, 'Preserve my soul, for I am godly. You are my God; save Your servant who trusts in You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 3, 'Be merciful to me, O Lord, for I call to You all day long.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 4, 'Bring joy to Your servant, for to You, O Lord, I lift up my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 5, 'For You, O Lord, are kind and forgiving, rich in loving devotion to all who call on You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 6, 'Hear my prayer, O LORD, and attend to my plea for mercy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 7, 'In the day of my distress I call on You, because You answer me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 8, 'O Lord, there is none like You among the gods, nor any works like Yours.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 9, 'All the nations You have made will come and bow before You, O Lord, and they will glorify Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 10, 'For You are great and perform wonders; You alone are God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 11, 'Teach me Your way, O LORD, that I may walk in Your truth. Give me an undivided heart, that I may fear Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 12, 'I will praise You, O Lord my God, with all my heart; I will glorify Your name forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 13, 'For great is Your loving devotion to me; You have delivered me from the depths of Sheol.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 14, 'The arrogant rise against me, O God; a band of ruthless men seeks my life, with no regard for You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 15, 'But You, O Lord, are a compassionate and gracious God, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion and faithfulness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 16, 'Turn to me and have mercy; grant Your strength to Your servant; save the son of Your maidservant.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 86, 17, 'Show me a sign of Your goodness, that my enemies may see and be ashamed; for You, O LORD, have helped me and comforted me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 1, 'He has founded His city on the holy mountains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 2, 'The LORD loves the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 3, 'Glorious things are ascribed to you, O city of God. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 4, '“I will mention Rahab and Babylon among those who know Me— along with Philistia, Tyre, and Cush— when I say, ‘This one was born in Zion.’”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 5, 'And it will be said of Zion: “This one and that one were born in her, and the Most High Himself will establish her.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 6, 'The LORD will record in the register of the peoples: “This one was born in Zion.” Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 87, 7, 'Singers and pipers will proclaim, “All my springs of joy are in You.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 1, 'O LORD, the God of my salvation, day and night I cry out before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 2, 'May my prayer come before You; incline Your ear to my cry.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 3, 'For my soul is full of troubles, and my life draws near to Sheol.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 4, 'I am counted among those descending to the Pit. I am like a man without strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 5, 'I am forsaken among the dead, like the slain who lie in the grave, whom You remember no more, who are cut off from Your care.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 6, 'You have laid me in the lowest Pit, in the darkest of the depths.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 7, 'Your wrath weighs heavily upon me; all Your waves have submerged me. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 8, 'You have removed my friends from me; You have made me repulsive to them; I am confined and cannot escape.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 9, 'My eyes grow dim with grief. I call to You daily, O LORD; I spread out my hands to You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 10, 'Do You work wonders for the dead? Do departed spirits rise up to praise You? Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 11, 'Can Your loving devotion be proclaimed in the grave, Your faithfulness in Abaddon?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 12, 'Will Your wonders be known in the darkness, or Your righteousness in the land of oblivion?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 13, 'But to You, O LORD, I cry for help; in the morning my prayer comes before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 14, 'Why, O LORD, do You reject me? Why do You hide Your face from me?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 15, 'From my youth I was afflicted and near death. I have borne Your terrors; I am in despair.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 16, 'Your wrath has swept over me; Your terrors have destroyed me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 17, 'All day long they engulf me like water; they enclose me on every side.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 88, 18, 'You have removed my beloved and my friend; darkness is my closest companion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 1, 'I will sing of the loving devotion of the LORD forever; with my mouth I will proclaim Your faithfulness to all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 2, 'For I have said, “Loving devotion is built up forever; in the heavens You establish Your faithfulness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 3, 'You said, “I have made a covenant with My chosen one, I have sworn to David My servant:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 4, '‘I will establish your offspring forever and build up your throne for all generations.’” Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 5, 'The heavens praise Your wonders, O LORD— Your faithfulness as well— in the assembly of the holy ones.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 6, 'For who in the skies can compare with the LORD? Who among the heavenly beings is like the LORD?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 7, 'In the council of the holy ones, God is greatly feared, and awesome above all who surround Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 8, 'O LORD God of Hosts, who is like You? O mighty LORD, Your faithfulness surrounds You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 9, 'You rule the raging sea; when its waves mount up, You still them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 10, 'You crushed Rahab like a carcass; You scattered Your enemies with Your mighty arm.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 11, 'The heavens are Yours, and also the earth. The earth and its fullness You founded.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 12, 'North and south You created; Tabor and Hermon shout for joy at Your name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 13, 'Mighty is Your arm; strong is Your hand. Your right hand is exalted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 14, 'Righteousness and justice are the foundation of Your throne; loving devotion and faithfulness go before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 15, 'Blessed are those who know the joyful sound, who walk, O LORD, in the light of Your presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 16, 'They rejoice in Your name all day long, and in Your righteousness they exult.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 17, 'For You are the glory of their strength, and by Your favor our horn is exalted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 18, 'Surely our shield belongs to the LORD, and our king to the Holy One of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 19, 'You once spoke in a vision; to Your godly ones You said, “I have bestowed help on a warrior; I have exalted one chosen from the people.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 20, 'I have found My servant David; with My sacred oil I have anointed him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 21, 'My hand will sustain him; surely My arm will strengthen him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 22, 'No enemy will exact tribute; no wicked man will oppress him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 23, 'I will crush his foes before him and strike down those who hate him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 24, 'My faithfulness and loving devotion will be with him, and through My name his horn will be exalted.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 25, 'I will set his hand over the sea, and his right hand upon the rivers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 26, 'He will call to Me, ‘You are my Father, my God, the Rock of my salvation.’'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 27, 'I will indeed appoint him as My firstborn, the highest of the kings of the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 28, 'I will forever preserve My loving devotion for him, and My covenant with him will stand fast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 29, 'I will establish his line forever, his throne as long as the heavens endure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 30, 'If his sons forsake My law and do not walk in My judgments,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 31, 'if they violate My statutes and fail to keep My commandments,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 32, 'I will attend to their transgression with the rod, and to their iniquity with stripes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 33, 'But I will not withdraw My loving devotion from him, nor ever betray My faithfulness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 34, 'I will not violate My covenant or alter the utterance of My lips.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 35, 'Once and for all I have sworn by My holiness— I will not lie to David—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 36, 'his offspring shall endure forever, and his throne before Me like the sun,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 37, 'like the moon, established forever, a faithful witness in the sky.” Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 38, 'Now, however, You have spurned and rejected him; You are enraged by Your anointed one.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 39, 'You have renounced the covenant with Your servant and sullied his crown in the dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 40, 'You have broken down all his walls; You have reduced his strongholds to rubble.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 41, 'All who pass by plunder him; he has become a reproach to his neighbors.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 42, 'You have exalted the right hand of his foes; You have made all his enemies rejoice.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 43, 'You have bent the edge of his sword and have not sustained him in battle.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 44, 'You have ended his splendor and cast his throne to the ground.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 45, 'You have cut short the days of his youth; You have covered him with shame. Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 46, 'How long, O LORD? Will You hide Yourself forever? Will Your wrath keep burning like fire?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 47, 'Remember the briefness of my lifespan! For what futility You have created all men!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 48, 'What man can live and never see death? Can he deliver his soul from the power of Sheol? Selah'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 49, 'Where, O Lord, is Your loving devotion of old, which You faithfully swore to David?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 50, 'Remember, O Lord, the reproach of Your servants, which I bear in my heart from so many people—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 51, 'how Your enemies have taunted, O LORD, and have mocked every step of Your anointed one!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 89, 52, 'Blessed be the LORD forever! Amen and amen.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 1, 'Lord, You have been our dwelling place through all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 2, 'Before the mountains were born or You brought forth the earth and the world, from everlasting to everlasting You are God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 3, 'You return man to dust, saying, “Return, O sons of mortals.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 4, 'For in Your sight a thousand years are but a day that passes, or a watch of the night.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 5, 'You whisk them away in their sleep; they are like the new grass of the morning—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 6, 'in the morning it springs up new, but by evening it fades and withers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 7, 'For we are consumed by Your anger and terrified by Your wrath.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 8, 'You have set our iniquities before You, our secret sins in the light of Your presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 9, 'For all our days decline in Your fury; we finish our years with a sigh.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 10, 'The length of our days is seventy years— or eighty if we are strong— yet their pride is but labor and sorrow, for they quickly pass, and we fly away.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 11, 'Who knows the power of Your anger? Your wrath matches the fear You are due.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 12, 'So teach us to number our days, that we may present a heart of wisdom.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 13, 'Return, O LORD! How long will it be? Have compassion on Your servants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 14, 'Satisfy us in the morning with Your loving devotion, that we may sing for joy and be glad all our days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 15, 'Make us glad for as many days as You have afflicted us, for as many years as we have seen evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 16, 'May Your work be shown to Your servants, and Your splendor to their children.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 90, 17, 'May the favor of the Lord our God rest upon us; establish for us the work of our hands— yes, establish the work of our hands!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 1, 'He who dwells in the shelter of the Most High will abide in the shadow of the Almighty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 2, 'I will say to the LORD, “You are my refuge and my fortress, my God, in whom I trust.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 3, 'Surely He will deliver you from the snare of the fowler, and from the deadly plague.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 4, 'He will cover you with His feathers; under His wings you will find refuge; His faithfulness is a shield and rampart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 5, 'You will not fear the terror of the night, nor the arrow that flies by day,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 6, 'nor the pestilence that stalks in the darkness, nor the calamity that destroys at noon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 7, 'Though a thousand may fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand, no harm will come near you.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 8, 'You will only see it with your eyes and witness the punishment of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 9, 'Because you have made the LORD your dwelling— my refuge, the Most High—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 10, 'no evil will befall you, no plague will approach your tent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 11, 'For He will command His angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 12, 'They will lift you up in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 13, 'You will tread on the lion and cobra; you will trample the young lion and serpent.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 14, '“Because he loves Me, I will deliver him; because he knows My name, I will protect him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 15, 'When he calls out to Me, I will answer him; I will be with him in trouble. I will deliver him and honor him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 91, 16, 'With long life I will satisfy him and show him My salvation.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 1, 'It is good to praise the LORD, and to sing praises to Your name, O Most High,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 2, 'to proclaim Your loving devotion in the morning and Your faithfulness at night'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 3, 'with the ten-stringed harp and the melody of the lyre.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 4, 'For You, O LORD, have made me glad by Your deeds; I sing for joy at the works of Your hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 5, 'How great are Your works, O LORD, how deep are Your thoughts!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 6, 'A senseless man does not know, and a fool does not understand,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 7, 'that though the wicked sprout like grass, and all evildoers flourish, they will be forever destroyed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 8, 'But You, O LORD, are exalted forever!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 9, 'For surely Your enemies, O LORD, surely Your enemies will perish; all evildoers will be scattered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 10, 'But You have exalted my horn like that of a wild ox; with fine oil I have been anointed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 11, 'My eyes see the downfall of my enemies; my ears hear the wailing of my wicked foes.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 12, 'The righteous will flourish like a palm tree, and grow like a cedar in Lebanon.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 13, 'Planted in the house of the LORD, they will flourish in the courts of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 14, 'In old age they will still bear fruit; healthy and green they will remain,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 92, 15, 'to proclaim, “The LORD is upright; He is my Rock, and in Him there is no unrighteousness.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 93, 1, 'The LORD reigns! He is robed in majesty; the LORD has clothed and armed Himself with strength. The world indeed is firmly established; it cannot be moved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 93, 2, 'Your throne was established long ago; You are from all eternity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 93, 3, 'The floodwaters have risen, O LORD; the rivers have raised their voice; the seas lift up their pounding waves.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 93, 4, 'Above the roar of many waters— the mighty breakers of the sea— the LORD on high is majestic.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 93, 5, 'Your testimonies are fully confirmed; holiness adorns Your house, O LORD, for all the days to come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 1, 'O LORD, God of vengeance, O God of vengeance, shine forth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 2, 'Rise up, O Judge of the earth; render a reward to the proud.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 3, 'How long will the wicked, O LORD, how long will the wicked exult?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 4, 'They pour out arrogant words; all workers of iniquity boast.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 5, 'They crush Your people, O LORD; they oppress Your heritage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 6, 'They kill the widow and the foreigner; they murder the fatherless.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 7, 'They say, “The LORD does not see; the God of Jacob pays no heed.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 8, 'Take notice, O senseless among the people! O fools, when will you be wise?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 9, 'He who affixed the ear, can He not hear? He who formed the eye, can He not see?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 10, 'He who admonishes the nations, does He not discipline? He who teaches man, does He lack knowledge?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 11, 'The LORD knows the thoughts of man, that they are futile.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 12, 'Blessed is the man You discipline, O LORD, and teach from Your law,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 13, 'to grant him relief from days of trouble, until a pit is dug for the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 14, 'For the LORD will not forsake His people; He will never abandon His heritage.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 15, 'Surely judgment will again be righteous, and all the upright in heart will follow it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 16, 'Who will rise up for me against the wicked? Who will stand for me against the workers of iniquity?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 17, 'Unless the LORD had been my helper, I would soon have dwelt in the abode of silence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 18, 'If I say, “My foot is slipping,” Your loving devotion, O LORD, supports me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 19, 'When anxiety overwhelms me, Your consolation delights my soul.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 20, 'Can a corrupt throne be Your ally— one devising mischief by decree?'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 21, 'They band together against the righteous and condemn the innocent to death.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 22, 'But the LORD has been my stronghold, and my God is my rock of refuge.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 94, 23, 'He will bring upon them their own iniquity and destroy them for their wickedness. The LORD our God will destroy them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 1, 'Come, let us sing for joy to the LORD; let us shout to the Rock of our salvation!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 2, 'Let us enter His presence with thanksgiving; let us make a joyful noise to Him in song.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 3, 'For the LORD is a great God, a great King above all gods.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 4, 'In His hand are the depths of the earth, and the mountain peaks belong to Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 5, 'The sea is His, for He made it, and His hands formed the dry land.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 6, 'O come, let us worship and bow down; let us kneel before the LORD our Maker.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 7, 'For He is our God, and we are the people of His pasture, the sheep under His care. Today, if you hear His voice,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 8, 'do not harden your hearts as you did at Meribah, in the day at Massah in the wilderness,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 9, 'where your fathers tested and tried Me, though they had seen My work.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 10, 'For forty years I was angry with that generation, and I said, “They are a people whose hearts go astray, and they have not known My ways.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 95, 11, 'So I swore on oath in My anger, “They shall never enter My rest.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 1, 'Sing to the LORD a new song; sing to the LORD, all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 2, 'Sing to the LORD, bless His name; proclaim His salvation day after day.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 3, 'Declare His glory among the nations, His wonderful deeds among all peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 4, 'For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised; He is to be feared above all gods.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 5, 'For all the gods of the nations are idols, but it is the LORD who made the heavens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 6, 'Splendor and majesty are before Him; strength and beauty fill His sanctuary.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 7, 'Ascribe to the LORD, O families of the nations, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 8, 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due His name; bring an offering and enter His courts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 9, 'Worship the LORD in the splendor of His holiness; tremble before Him, all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 10, 'Declare among the nations: “The LORD reigns!” The world is firmly established; it cannot be moved; He will judge the peoples with equity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 11, 'Let the heavens be glad and the earth rejoice; let the sea resound, and all that fills it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 12, 'Let the fields exult, and all that is in them. Then all the trees of the forest will sing for joy'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 96, 13, 'before the LORD, for He is coming— He is coming to judge the earth. He will judge the world in righteousness and the peoples in His faithfulness.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 1, 'The LORD reigns, let the earth rejoice; let the distant shores be glad.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 2, 'Clouds and darkness surround Him; righteousness and justice are His throne’s foundation.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 3, 'Fire goes before Him and consumes His foes on every side.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 4, 'His lightning illuminates the world; the earth sees and trembles.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 5, 'The mountains melt like wax at the presence of the LORD, before the Lord of all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 6, 'The heavens proclaim His righteousness; all the peoples see His glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 7, 'All worshipers of images are put to shame— those who boast in idols. Worship Him, all you gods!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 8, 'Zion hears and rejoices, and the towns of Judah exult because of Your judgments, O LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 9, 'For You, O LORD, are Most High over all the earth; You are exalted far above all gods.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 10, 'Hate evil, O you who love the LORD! He preserves the souls of His saints; He delivers them from the hand of the wicked.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 11, 'Light shines on the righteous, gladness on the upright in heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 97, 12, 'Rejoice in the LORD, you righteous ones, and praise His holy name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 1, 'Sing to the LORD a new song, for He has done wonders; His right hand and holy arm have gained Him the victory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 2, 'The LORD has proclaimed His salvation and revealed His righteousness to the nations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 3, 'He has remembered His love and faithfulness to the house of Israel; all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 4, 'Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the earth; break forth—let your cry ring out, and sing praises!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 5, 'Sing praises to the LORD with the lyre, in melodious song with the harp.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 6, 'With trumpets and the blast of the ram’s horn shout for joy before the LORD, the King.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 7, 'Let the sea resound, and all that fills it, the world, and all who dwell in it.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 8, 'Let the rivers clap their hands, let the mountains sing together for joy'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 98, 9, 'before the LORD, for He comes to judge the earth. He will judge the world with righteousness and the peoples with equity.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 1, 'The LORD reigns; let the nations tremble! He is enthroned above the cherubim; let the earth quake!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 2, 'Great is the LORD in Zion; He is exalted above all the peoples.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 3, 'Let them praise Your great and awesome name— He is holy!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 4, 'The mighty King loves justice. You have established equity; You have exercised justice and righteousness in Jacob.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 5, 'Exalt the LORD our God, and worship at His footstool; He is holy!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 6, 'Moses and Aaron were among His priests; Samuel was among those who called on His name. They called to the LORD and He answered.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 7, 'He spoke to them from the pillar of cloud; they kept His decrees and the statutes He gave them.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 8, 'O LORD our God, You answered them. You were a forgiving God to them, yet an avenger of their misdeeds.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 99, 9, 'Exalt the LORD our God and worship at His holy mountain, for the LORD our God is holy.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 100, 1, 'Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 100, 2, 'Serve the LORD with gladness; come into His presence with joyful songs.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 100, 3, 'Know that the LORD is God. It is He who made us, and we are His; we are His people, and the sheep of His pasture.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 100, 4, 'Enter His gates with thanksgiving and His courts with praise; give thanks to Him and bless His name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 100, 5, 'For the LORD is good, and His loving devotion endures forever; His faithfulness continues to all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 1, 'I will sing of Your loving devotion and justice; to You, O LORD, I will sing praises.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 2, 'I will ponder the way that is blameless— when will You come to me? I will walk in my house with integrity of heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 3, 'I will set no worthless thing before my eyes. I hate the work of those who fall away; it shall not cling to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 4, 'A perverse heart shall depart from me; I will know nothing of evil.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 5, 'Whoever slanders his neighbor in secret, I will put to silence; the one with haughty eyes and a proud heart, I will not endure.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 6, 'My eyes favor the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me; he who walks in the way of integrity shall minister to me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 7, 'No one who practices deceit shall dwell in my house; no one who tells lies shall stand in my presence.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 101, 8, 'Every morning I will remove all the wicked of the land, that I may cut off every evildoer from the city of the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 1, 'Hear my prayer, O LORD; let my cry for help come before You.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 2, 'Do not hide Your face from me in my day of distress. Incline Your ear to me; answer me quickly when I call.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 3, 'For my days vanish like smoke, and my bones burn like glowing embers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 4, 'My heart is afflicted, and withered like grass; I even forget to eat my bread.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 5, 'Through my loud groaning my flesh clings to my bones.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 6, 'I am like a desert owl, like an owl among the ruins.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 7, 'I lie awake; I am like a lone bird on a housetop.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 8, 'All day long my enemies taunt me; they ridicule me and curse me.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 9, 'For I have eaten ashes like bread and mixed my drink with tears'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 10, 'because of Your indignation and wrath, for You have picked me up and cast me aside.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 11, 'My days are like lengthening shadows, and I wither away like grass.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 12, 'But You, O LORD, sit enthroned forever; Your renown endures to all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 13, 'You will rise up and have compassion on Zion, for it is time to show her favor— the appointed time has come.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 14, 'For Your servants delight in her stones and take pity on her dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 15, 'So the nations will fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth will fear Your glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 16, 'For the LORD will rebuild Zion; He has appeared in His glory.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 17, 'He will turn toward the prayer of the destitute; He will not despise their prayer.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 18, 'Let this be written for the generation to come, so that a people not yet created may praise the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 19, 'For He looked down from the heights of His sanctuary; the LORD gazed out from heaven to earth'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 20, 'to hear a prisoner’s groaning, to release those condemned to death,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 21, 'that they may proclaim the name of the LORD in Zion and praise Him in Jerusalem,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 22, 'when peoples and kingdoms assemble to serve the LORD.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 23, 'He has broken my strength on the way; He has cut short my days.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 24, 'I say: “O my God, do not take me in the midst of my days! Your years go on through all generations.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 25, 'In the beginning You laid the foundations of the earth, and the heavens are the work of Your hands.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 26, 'They will perish, but You remain; they will all wear out like a garment. Like clothing You will change them, and they will be passed on.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 27, 'But You remain the same, and Your years will never end.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 102, 28, 'The children of Your servants will dwell securely, and their descendants will be established before You.”'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 1, 'Bless the LORD, O my soul; all that is within me, bless His holy name.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 2, 'Bless the LORD, O my soul, and do not forget all His kind deeds—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 3, 'He who forgives all your iniquities and heals all your diseases,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 4, 'who redeems your life from the Pit and crowns you with loving devotion and compassion,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 5, 'who satisfies you with good things, so that your youth is renewed like the eagle’s.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 6, 'The LORD executes righteousness and justice for all the oppressed.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 7, 'He made known His ways to Moses, His deeds to the people of Israel.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 8, 'The LORD is compassionate and gracious, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 9, 'He will not always accuse us, nor harbor His anger forever.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 10, 'He has not dealt with us according to our sins or repaid us according to our iniquities.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 11, 'For as high as the heavens are above the earth, so great is His loving devotion for those who fear Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 12, 'As far as the east is from the west, so far has He removed our transgressions from us.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 13, 'As a father has compassion on his children, so the LORD has compassion on those who fear Him.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 14, 'For He knows our frame; He is mindful that we are dust.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 15, 'As for man, his days are like grass— he blooms like a flower of the field;'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 16, 'when the wind passes over, it vanishes, and its place remembers it no more.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 17, 'But from everlasting to everlasting the loving devotion of the LORD extends to those who fear Him, and His righteousness to their children’s children—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 18, 'to those who keep His covenant and remember to obey His precepts.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 19, 'The LORD has established His throne in heaven, and His kingdom rules over all.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 20, 'Bless the LORD, all His angels mighty in strength who carry out His word, who hearken to the voice of His command.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 21, 'Bless the LORD, all His hosts, you servants who do His will.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 103, 22, 'Bless the LORD, all His works in all places of His dominion. Bless the LORD, O my soul!'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 1, 'Bless the LORD, O my soul! O LORD my God, You are very great; You are clothed with splendor and majesty.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 2, 'He wraps Himself in light as with a garment; He stretches out the heavens like a tent,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 3, 'laying the beams of His chambers in the waters above, making the clouds His chariot, walking on the wings of the wind.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 4, 'He makes the winds His messengers, flames of fire His servants.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 5, 'He set the earth on its foundations, never to be moved.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 6, 'You covered it with the deep like a garment; the waters stood above the mountains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 7, 'At Your rebuke the waters fled; at the sound of Your thunder they hurried away—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 8, 'the mountains rose and the valleys sank to the place You assigned for them—'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 9, 'You set a boundary they cannot cross, that they may never again cover the earth.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 10, 'He sends forth springs in the valleys; they flow between the mountains.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 11, 'They give drink to every beast of the field; the wild donkeys quench their thirst.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 12, 'The birds of the air nest beside the springs; they sing among the branches.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 13, 'He waters the mountains from His chambers; the earth is satisfied by the fruit of His works.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 14, 'He makes the grass grow for the livestock and provides crops for man to cultivate, bringing forth food from the earth:'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 15, 'wine that gladdens the heart of man, oil that makes his face to shine, and bread that sustains his heart.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 16, 'The trees of the LORD have their fill, the cedars of Lebanon that He planted,'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 17, 'where the birds build their nests; the stork makes her home in the cypresses.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 18, 'The high mountains are for the wild goats, the cliffs a refuge for the rock badgers.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 19, 'He made the moon to mark the seasons; the sun knows when to set.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 20, 'You bring darkness, and it becomes night, when all the beasts of the forest prowl.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 21, 'The young lions roar for their prey and seek their food from God.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 22, 'The sun rises, and they withdraw; they lie down in their dens.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 23, 'Man goes forth to his work and to his labor until evening.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 24, 'How many are Your works, O LORD! In wisdom You have made them all; the earth is full of Your creatures.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 25, 'Here is the sea, vast and wide, teeming with creatures beyond number, living things both great and small.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 26, 'There the ships pass, and Leviathan, which You formed to frolic there.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 27, 'All creatures look to You to give them their food in due season.'),
  ('BSB', 'Psalms', 19, 104, 28, 'When You give it to them, they gather it up; when You open Your hand, they are satisfied with good things.');
